tachedPart`, `PoseHistory`, `socketMatrix`, `placeExtras`, `along`, `alongDirection`, `TipTrail`; types `LookAtOptions`, `BlinkOptions`, `HoveringOptions`, `OrbitOptions`, `DetachedOptions`, `HistoryOptions`, `Socket`, `SocketJoints`, `TrailOptions`, `TipSample`.\n\n**Reach and the rig contract (WP 10.1)**: an attack's reach measured off its animation; what a procedural rig names (its points, bones, feet and states) and the check it passes, as anim.check holds the humanoid.\n`measureReach`, `driveRig`, `rigCheck`, `rigClosed`; types `ReachPose`, `ReachOptions`, `Reach`, `ProcRig`, `ProcRigBody`, `RigRun`.\n\n**Footsteps (WP 13.22)**: which step a surface tag plays at a gait, sound data a scene's sound map reads sim-side.\n`footstepSound`, `stepGait`, `SURFACE_STEPS`, `STEP_GAITS`; types `StepGait`.\n\nPages only, from engine/index.ts:\n\n**Headless**: the engine without a page, and its inspector (window.__engine in a page).\n`createHeadless`; types `Headless`, `HeadlessOptions`, `Inspector`, `EngineInfo`, `EntitySummary`.\n\n**Materials and procedural textures (WP 2.3)**: materials as data with three.js's classic parameters, seeded tiling texture generators and their helpers, the CPU bake, and the page's material library.\n`defineMaterial`, `getMaterial`, `createMaterialLibrary`, `defineTexture`, `bakeTexture`, `cellHash`, `wrapIndex`, `palette`, `pickTone`, `runningBond`, `tileNoise`; types `MaterialEntry`, `MaterialSpec`, `MaterialLibrary`, `TextureEntry`, `Texel`, `TextureContext`, `TextureSpec`, `TextureLook`, `TextureBake`, `TextureRef`.\n\n**Input (WP 3.3)**: the devices of a page sampled into intents (keys by physical code, mouse with pointer lock and the wheel, gamepads in any slot), action maps and their presets, bindings players change and keep, prompts per device, the virtual device that __engine.input drives, and the scripted gamepad for tests.\n`createInput`, `defineActionMap`, `getActionMap`, `listActionMaps`, `SYSTEM_ACTIONS`, `RESERVED_CODES`, `createBindings`, `codeLabel`, `readKeyboardLayout`, `isCode`, `createVirtualDevice`, `connectVirtualDevice`, `createScriptedGamepad`; types `Input`, `InputOptions`, `CameraLike`, `CameraInputSample`, `ActionMap`, `ActionMapSpec`, `Bindings`, `BindingsOptions`, `BindingsStorage`, `BindingsFile`, `RebindResult`, `DeviceKind`, `VirtualDevice`, `ScriptedGamepad`, `GamepadLike`.\n\n**Aiming and look (WP 13.9)**: the point the intents' aim carries by a map's rule, and the look settings input.*.\n`aimPoint`, `screenRay`, `onFloor`, `AIM_RULES`, `AIM_RANGE`, `STICK_REACH`, `lookOptions`, `scaleLook`, `LOOK_SETTING_FIELDS`, `LOOK_SETTINGS`, `DEGREES_PER_COUNT`; types `AimRule`, `AimPose`, `AimView`, `AimDevices`, `AimRay`, `LookOptions`, `RawLook`, `ScaledLook`.\n\n**Held bindings (WP 13.20)**: a key or a button kept down for an action of its own (Apex's pad reload on X held), and the device a code is of.\n`holdCode`, `heldBase`, `HOLD_PREFIX`, `HOLD_TIME`, `deviceOf`.\n\n**Geometry kit and level meshes (WP 2.4)**: shapes standing on the ground with UVs in metres, the geometry registry (props and levels name geometry by id), their QA measures, and a compiled level drawn as meshes.\n`boxGeometry`, `roundedBoxGeometry`, `limbGeometry`, `rampGeometry`, `frustumGeometry`, `pillarGeometry`, `pillarParts`, `ringGeometry`, `sidesThenTops`, `mergeGeometries`, `defineGeometry`, `getGeometry`, `buildGeometry`, `inspectGeometry`, `createLevelMeshes`, `LEVEL_RECIPES`, `createTerrainMeshes`; types `BoxOptions`, `RoundedBoxOptions`, `LimbOptions`, `RampOptions`, `FrustumOptions`, `PillarOptions`, `PillarPart`, `RingOptions`, `GeometryEntry`, `GeometrySpec`, `GeometryRef`, `GeometryReport`, `LevelMeshes`, `LevelMeshesOptions`, `LevelMeshPart`, `LevelCell`, `LevelRecipe`, `LevelShape`, `TerrainMeshes`, `TerrainMeshesOptions`.\n\n**Sound data (WP 9.2)**: effects and songs as registry entries (voices, layers, variants; tracker-notation tracks), rendered offline by the DSP core into reproducible samples.\n`defineSfx`, `getSfx`, `renderSfx`, `sfxVoices`, `defineSong`, `getSong`, `renderSong`, `songVoices`, `songTiming`; types `Sfx`, `SfxSpec`, `SfxLayer`, `SfxBus`, `SfxRenderOptions`, `Song`, `SongSpec`, `SongTrack`, `SongTiming`, `SongRenderOptions`, `Voice`, `SoundDef`.\n\n**The audio runtime (WP 9.3)**: a page's sound through Web Audio, started by the first gesture: buses with ducking and voice limits, sounds placed in 3D and occluded through the QueryView, room reverb, and music in intensity layers that change on the beat and the bar line.\n`createAudio`, `BUS_VOLUMES`, `ROOMS`, `roomReverb`, `VOICE_LIMITS`; types `Audio`, `AudioOptions`, `AudioState`, `AudioInfo`, `PlayOptions`, `Sound`, `ListenerPose`, `GestureTarget`, `AudioBus`, `MixerInfo`, `MusicChange`, `MusicPosition`, `Quantize`, `RoomName`, `RoomSpec`, `VoiceLimits`.\n\n**Sound for places (WP 13.22)**: a room's reverb out of its size and what it is made of (Sabine's RT60), the walls between a sound and the listener counted, each muffling it more.\n`roomAcoustics`, `ABSORPTION`, `CONTENTS`, `wallsBetween`, `muffling`, `OCCLUSION`; types `RoomMake`.\n\n**The engine in a page (WP 2.7)**: createEngine reads the routes, starts the scene with its view, publishes window.__engine, warms up and runs the frame loop; createHeadless({ view: true }) builds the same view in Node.\n`createEngine`, `parseRoutes`, `routeQuery`; types `Engine`, `EngineOptions`, `Routes`, `CameraInfo`, `PlayResult`, `PlayIntoOptions`, `ViewChange`.\n\n**A page's own presentation (WP 9.5)**: createEngine's onFrame, once per drawn frame, with the run to read and the camera.\ntypes `EngineFrame`, `FrameWorld`, `CameraPose`.\n\n**Touch controls (WP 3.12; built, not tested, ADR-0021)**: a page's touch layout (the corner fan's buttons and the menu button) for createEngine's touchLayout and onMenu, the touch device on input.touch, and the touch codes it writes.\n`defineTouchLayout`, `getTouchLayout`, `touchCode`; types `TouchLayout`, `TouchLayoutSpec`, `TouchButtonSpec`, `TouchDevice`, `StickView`, `TouchSetting`.\n\n**Level meshes v2 and the cutaway (WP 4.4)**: galleries, stairs, the dais, pillars with plinths and capitals and brazier stands as recipe shapes; walls facing an outside camera cut low and pillars before the hero as stumps.\n`createCutaway`, `planCutaway`; types `Cutaway`, `CutawayReport`, `CutTarget`, `LevelCut`, `CutWhen`, `PartCut`.\n\n**Instancing and puppets (WP 3.8)**: batches of instanced copies in pages above r182's 1,000-slot uniform path; puppet bodies as data (one line per part on the humanoid skeleton's bones, mirrored parts, material slots), compiled per build and drawn as one rigid-skinned mesh per character or as instanced parts for crowds; blob shadows.\n`createInstancedBatch`, `defineBody`, `getBody`, `compileBody`, `recolor`, `createPuppet`, `createPuppetBatches`, `createBlobShadows`, `blobScale`; types `InstancedBatch`, `InstancedBatchOptions`, `InstancedBatchStats`, `InstanceColor`, `Body`, `BodySpec`, `BodyPart`, `BodyPoint`, `BodyLength`, `PartOptions`, `CompiledBody`, `BodyPiece`, `PieceShape`, `Puppet`, `PuppetMaterials`, `PuppetBatches`, `BlobShadows`.\n\n**The HTML/CSS overlay (WP 6.5)**: world-anchored labels and damage numbers placed from projected coordinates each frame (three.js's CSS2DRenderer pattern), HUD lines and a crosshair over the canvas; ui.state() for tests.\n`createOverlay`, `DAMAGE_NUMBERS`, `uiState`; types `Overlay`, `OverlayOptions`, `HudOptions`, `HudPlace`, `Label`, `LabelOptions`, `DamageOptions`, `WorldPoint`, `Anchor`, `OverlayCamera`, `UiState`, `UiElementState`.\n\n**The widgets (WP 10.6)**: bars, hearts and boxes, the dialog box and the menu as HTML/CSS over the overlay, reading the page's input (its system layer) and asking the page for sound cues; a gamepad's cursor over any panel. A menu sends the picks that change play as input (`send`), so replays hold them.\n`createBar`, `createHearts`, `createBox`, `createPadCursor`, `createDialog`, `createMenu`.\n\n**The store (WP 10.9)**: what a game keeps across sessions (high scores, progress, its settings) in the page's localStorage under the game's prefix, versioned and checked on load; memory in Node and in the isolated modes.\n`createStore`, `memoryBackend`.\n\n**Lights, shadows, atmosphere and sky (WP 7.1)**: light kinds for a level's light spots, a fixed pool of point lights near the focus with a shadow budget by quality tier, and sky presets (background, dome, backdrop, sun, ambient light, fog) that a sky puts on a scene.\n`defineLight`, `defineSky`, `createSky`; types `LightEntry`, `LightSource`, `SkyEntry`, `SkySpec`, `Sky`.\n\n**Materials v2 (WP 7.2)**: the same material data drawn in four styles (lambert, toon, flat, pbr), switched at run time with every style warmed; the toon look (bands and rim) as uniforms; outline shells for meshes and instanced batches.\n`createStyleSet`, `MATERIAL_STYLES`, `TOON_LOOK`, `createOutline`, `OUTLINE_MODES`; types `MaterialStyle`, `StyleSet`, `StyleSetOptions`, `ToonLook`, `ToonUniforms`, `Outline`, `OutlineMode`, `OutlineOptions`, `OutlineShells`.\n\n**Post-processing (WP 7.4, 13.32)**: one chain every frame draws through, every filter a uniform with an amount, scoped by part; looks as data (a material style, a filter chain, the sky, WP 7.8) that combine looks; objects tagged by part.\n`createPost`, `POST_SETTINGS`, `definePostSettings`, `setPart`, `PARTS`, `defineLook`, `FILTER_FIELDS`, `FILTER_NAMES`, `SCOPES`, `PALETTES`, `STYLIZE_KINDS`; types `Post`, `PostOptions`, `Part`, `PostTag`, `LookEntry`, `LookSpec`, `FilterName`, `Scope`, `FilterChain`, `FilterSpec`, `CombineLayer`, `PostShow`.\n\n**Props drawn (WP 4.5)**: every prop part a batch of the instancing service, posed by its body, the flames dancing on the visual streams, the light spots flickering, for the light pool; a part's geometry and where it stands (its matrix in the prop's frame), for a prop's tests.\n`createPropMeshes`, `FLICKER`, `buildPropPart`, `partMatrix`; types `PropMeshes`, `PropMeshesOptions`, `PropMeshPose`, `PropLight`.\n\n**Crowd rendering and pose LOD (WP 5.4)**: thousands of humanoids, blobs and floaters in a few dozen draw calls over the instancing service, each body seen through bands of detail by its distance (the animator's pose level, capes), culled by the view; the blob and floater bodies as data.\n`createCrowd`, `createCrowdLod`, `CROWD_LOD`, `BLOB_BODY`, `blobBody`, `FLOATER_BODY`, `QUADRUPED_BODY`; types `Crowd`, `CrowdDraw`, `CrowdRigDraw`, `CrowdStats`, `RigBody`, `RigPart`, `RigJoints`, `RigShape`, `CrowdLod`, `CrowdLodOptions`, `CrowdLodCounts`, `CrowdBand`, `CrowdBandSpec`, `BlobFeatures`.\n\n**Performance counters (WP 5.5)**: what `__engine.stats()` returns, means in ms and the renderer's counts, never fps.\ntypes `EngineStats`.\n\n**The texture library (v2, WP 7.3)**: a level's whole floor as a texture generator (define it under a game's id), with moss at the walls' feet, a rune circle on each dais and contact shadows along every block's foot.\n`levelFloorTexture`; types `LevelFloorOptions`, `ContactShadowOptions`, `FloorMossOptions`, `FloorRuneOptions`.\n\n**Clips in pages (WP 8.4)**: three.js's AnimationClip and AnimationMixer, for presentation only (a page plays a baked clip on a puppet with clipJSON and AnimationClip.parse); the sim samples the same tracks through the clip layer. The mannequin: the Quaternius figure the library was measured on, as a body and a build.\n`AnimationClip`, `AnimationMixer`, `defineMannequin`, `mannequinBody`, `MANNEQUIN_SLOTS`; types `MannequinData`.\n\n**Effects (WP 6.4)**: particles as data (emitters: shardfall's presets, the 2D engine's kinds, event effects), drawn with telegraphs on the floor, socket trails, bolts and camera shake by a view's effects; never part of the hash.\n`createEffects`, `FX_BUDGET`, `BOLT`, `defineEmitter`, `getEmitter`, `TRAIL_TINTS`, `ScreenShake`, `SHAKE`; types `Effects`, `EffectsOptions`, `FxEventPayload`, `FxStats`, `Emitter`, `EmitterSpec`, `EmitterLayer`, `ParticleFields`, `FxLight`, `BurstOptions`, `ParticleStats`, `TrailSampleLike`.\n\n**The feel kit (WP 13.4)**: courses, scripted runs of a scene and the numbers measured on them (`node x feel`); the runner and its verdicts; the owner's feel panel and copy as profile.\n`defineCourse`, `getCourse`, `listCourses`, `METRICS`, `runCourse`, `createFeelPanel`, `tunedSpec`, `profileText`; types `Course`, `Measure`, `Metric`, `CourseResult`, `CourseSample`, `MeasureResult`, `FeelPanel`, `FeelRow`, `FeelInspector`.\n\n**Camera modes (WP 2.5, WP 3.9, WP 13.8)**: a code to a camera, each mode's factory, and a game's own.\n`readCameraCode`, `createCamera`, `createShoulderCamera`, `SHOULDER`, `createFollowCamera`, `FOLLOW_RIG`, `createFirstCamera`, `createChaseCamera`, `createViewCamera`, `followCamera`, `defineCamera`, `makePose`, `poseForward`, `poseRight`, `poseUp`, `poseTarget`; types `AnyCamera`, `AnyCameraSpec`, `ShoulderInput`, `ShoulderSpec`, `FollowInput`, `FollowSpec`, `FollowCamera`, `FollowSteps`, `CameraKindSpec`, `Camera`, `CameraInput`.\n\n**The rig a view steps (WP 13.8)**: blends on live switches, the view effects, the view settings cam.*.\n`createCameraRig`, `rigOptions`, `CAMERA_SETTINGS`, `blendCameras`, `BLEND_TIME`, `createCameraEffects`, `applyEffects`, `cameraPlayer`, `apexFov`, `EFFECTS`; types `CameraRig`, `RigOptions`, `RigInput`, `CameraPlayer`, `EffectWeights`, `EffectsFrame`.\n<!-- api-map:end -->\n","numLines":479,"startLine":1,"totalLines":479}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NPJLtPPKfyrfTnjFQRRW8Q","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9JLbsZSxAAui538HFx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S2FGTYwQQmY9VyvYWnATim","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/.research/my-3dge/tools/game/new-game.mjs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3010,"cache_read_input_tokens":44208,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3010},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"04946840-99bd-4bf6-b110-36fc0972beea","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:43.201Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9JLNjFeTzRQCy1DeMt","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01S2FGTYwQQmY9VyvYWnATim":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/.research/my-3dge/tools/game/new-game.mjs"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S2FGTYwQQmY9VyvYWnATim","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env node\n2\t/**\n3\t * @file Makes a game from the my-3dge engine, and moves a game to a newer engine (PLAN.md WP 10.7, ADR-0024): the\n4\t * one command an agent runs to start a game. Plain JavaScript for any Node from 18 with nothing installed, since it\n5\t * runs straight after `git clone`, before setup. What a game gets, and whose each file is, is tools/game/files.mjs.\n6\t *\n7\t * Create: `node <engine>/tools/game/new-game.mjs <dir> [--name <name>]` writes a game into <dir> (made if missing;\n8\t * an empty folder, or a fresh repository's root): the engine's files, copied as they are and pinned by\n9\t * engine-lock.json; the starter game, labs/game/; the game's root files from tools/game/template/ (`TEMPLATES`); and\n10\t * package.json and package-lock.json with the engine's pins (`gamePackage`, `gameLockfile`, from tools/game/files.mjs).\n11\t * Then `git init` when the folder is in no repository. It never overwrites: a README.md or LICENSE already there is\n12\t * kept, a .gitignore gains the lines it lacks, an AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md or GEMINI.md gets the game's after its own\n13\t * text, and any other file in the way stops it before it writes anything.\n14\t *\n15\t * Update: `node <newer engine>/tools/game/new-game.mjs --update <dir>` (what `node x engine --update` runs) puts this\n16\t * checkout's engine files in place of the game's, removes those it dropped, moves package.json to its pins, brings\n17\t * the root files the game never edited to its templates (`refreshTemplates`) and writes the new lock. Nothing of the\n18\t * game's is replaced or removed: it stops, having written nothing, on an engine file the game changed without\n19\t * declaring it under \"Local engine patches\" in ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md (a declared one is kept), on a file of the game's\n20\t * where the newer engine adds one, and on a package.json entry of the game's that the newer engine sets otherwise\n21\t * (`npmClashes`); `--force` lets the engine's replace them. It names the package.json entries it drops, or sets back\n22\t * where the game had edited the engine's (`npmLost`): the engine's pins win, as its files do.\n23\t *\n24\t * `--verify <dir>` prints `verifyGame` (tools/game/files.mjs) as JSON. Exit codes: 0 done, 1 stopped (the message says\n25\t * why and what to do), 2 a usage error.\n26\t *\n27\t * @example\n28\t * // node /tmp/my-3dge/tools/game/new-game.mjs ../dragon-run → a game in ../dragon-run, named dragon-run\n29\t * // node /tmp/my-3dge/tools/game/new-game.mjs . --name dragon-run → in the current folder (a fresh repository)\n30\t * // node /tmp/my-3dge-new/tools/game/new-game.mjs --update . → the game in . on the newer engine\n31\t * gameName('/tmp/Dragon Run!'); // 'dragon-run'\n32\t * render('# {{name}}', { name: 'dragon-run' }); // '# dragon-run'\n33\t * @see tools/game/new-game.test.ts\n34\t */\n35\timport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\n36\timport { copyFileSync, existsSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, rmSync, statSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n37\timport { basename, dirname, join, relative, resolve, sep } from 'node:path';\n38\timport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n39\timport {\n40\t  engineIdentity,\n41\t  FEEDBACK_FILE,\n42\t  gameLockfile,\n43\t  gamePackage,\n44\t  hashFile,\n45\t  hashText,\n46\t  LOCK_FILE,\n47\t  lockFor,\n48\t  npmClashes,\n49\t  npmLost,\n50\t  plan,\n51\t  sameDependencies,\n52\t  SOURCE,\n53\t  verifyGame,\n54\t} from './files.mjs';\n55\t\n56\texport { gameLockfile, gamePackage, npmClashes };\n57\t\n58\t/** The game's root files: template (in tools/game/template/) → where it goes. */\n59\texport const TEMPLATES = Object.freeze([\n60\t  ['AGENTS.md.tmpl', 'AGENTS.md'],\n61\t  ['CLAUDE.md.tmpl', 'CLAUDE.md'],\n62\t  ['GEMINI.md.tmpl', 'GEMINI.md'],\n63\t  ['README.md.tmpl', 'README.md'],\n64\t  ['ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md.tmpl', FEEDBACK_FILE],\n65\t  ['gitignore.tmpl', '.gitignore'],\n66\t  ['index.html.tmpl', 'index.html'],\n67\t  ['claude-settings.json.tmpl', '.claude/settings.json'],\n68\t]);\n69\t\n70\t/** Files a target may hold: a README.md or LICENSE is kept; a .gitignore gains the template's lines it lacks. */\n71\tconst KEPT = new Set(['README.md', 'LICENSE', '.gitignore', 'AGENTS.md', 'CLAUDE.md', 'GEMINI.md']);\n72\t\n73\t/** Instruction files the agents read: one already there keeps its text, and the game's follows it (`appendOnce`). */\n74\tconst APPENDED = new Set(['AGENTS.md', 'CLAUDE.md', 'GEMINI.md']);\n75\t\n76\t/** A game's name: an npm package name, from the folder's name by default (`Dragon Run!` → `dragon-run`). */\n77\texport function gameName(target, name) {\n78\t  const folder = basename(resolve(target)).toLowerCase();\n79\t  const chosen = name ?? folder.replace(/[^a-z0-9._-]+/g, '-').replace(/^[-._]+|[-._]+$/g, '');\n80\t  if (!/^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{0,213}$/.test(chosen)) {\n81\t    throw new Error(`\"${chosen}\" cannot name a game: give --name with lower-case letters, digits, '-', '.' or '_'`);\n82\t  }\n83\t  return chosen;\n84\t}\n85\t\n86\t/** Fills a template's `{{name}}` and `{{engine.*}}`; any other placeholder is an error. */\n87\texport function render(text, values) {\n88\t  return text.replace(/\\{\\{([a-z.]+)\\}\\}/g, (whole, key) => {\n89\t    if (key in values) return values[key];\n90\t    throw new Error(`the template's ${whole} has no value: new-game.mjs fills ${Object.keys(values).join(', ')}`);\n91\t  });\n92\t}\n93\t\n94\t/** The values of the templates' placeholders for the game `game` on the engine `identity`. */\n95\tfunction templateValues(game, identity) {\n96\t  return {\n97\t    name: game,\n98\t    'engine.repository': identity.repository,\n99\t    'engine.commit': identity.commit,\n100\t    'engine.short': identity.commit.slice(0, 7),\n101\t    'engine.date': identity.date,\n102\t  };\n103\t}\n104\t\n105\t/** A template's text in the engine at `source`. */\n106\tconst templateText = (source, template) => readFileSync(join(source, 'tools/game/template', template), 'utf8');\n107\t\n108\t/** Reads a JSON file. */\n109\tconst readJson = (file) => JSON.parse(readFileSync(file, 'utf8'));\n110\t\n111\t/** Writes JSON with two spaces and a final newline (what Prettier keeps). */\n112\tfunction writeJson(file, value) {\n113\t  mkdirSync(dirname(file), { recursive: true });\n114\t  writeFileSync(file, `${JSON.stringify(value, null, 2)}\\n`);\n115\t}\n116\t\n117\t/** What writing `to` under `root` meets, if anything: the file itself, or a file where one of its folders goes. */\n118\tfunction inTheWay(root, to) {\n119\t  const parts = to.split('/');\n120\t  for (let i = 1; i <= parts.length; i++) {\n121\t    const path = join(root, ...parts.slice(0, i));\n122\t    if (existsSync(path) && (i === parts.length || !statSync(path).isDirectory())) return path;\n123\t  }\n124\t  return undefined;\n125\t}\n126\t\n127\t/** Copies one file, making its folder. */\n128\tfunction copyInto(source, from, root, to) {\n129\t  mkdirSync(dirname(join(root, to)), { recursive: true });\n130\t  copyFileSync(join(source, from), join(root, to));\n131\t}\n132\t\n133\t/** Makes a game in `target` from the engine at `source`; on a clash it throws, having written nothing. */\n134\texport function createGame({ target, name, source = SOURCE, git = true }) {\n135\t  const root = resolve(target);\n136\t  if (existsSync(root) && !statSync(root).isDirectory()) throw new Error(`${root} is a file: name a folder`);\n137\t  const game = gameName(root, name);\n138\t  const identity = engineIdentity(source);\n139\t  const items = plan(source);\n140\t  const writes = [\n141\t    ...items.map((item) => item.to),\n142\t    ...TEMPLATES.map(([, to]) => to),\n143\t    'package.json',\n144\t    'package-lock.json',\n145\t  ];\n146\t  const clashes = [...writes, LOCK_FILE].filter((to) => !KEPT.has(to) && inTheWay(root, to));\n147\t  if (clashes.length > 0) {\n148\t    const named = clashes.slice(0, 5).join(', ') + (clashes.length > 5 ? ` and ${clashes.length - 5} more` : '');\n149\t    throw new Error(\n150\t      `${root} already holds ${named}: make the game in an empty folder or a fresh repository's root (a README.md, ` +\n151\t        'LICENSE or .gitignore may be there), or move a game to a newer engine with --update',\n152\t    );\n153\t  }\n154\t  for (const { from, to } of items) copyInto(source, from, root, to);\n155\t  const values = templateValues(game, identity);\n156\t  const kept = [];\n157\t  const templates = {};\n158\t  for (const [template, to] of TEMPLATES) {\n159\t    const text = render(templateText(source, template), values);\n160\t    const file = join(root, to);\n161\t    templates[to] = existsSync(file) ? null : hashText(text);\n162\t    if (to === '.gitignore' && existsSync(file)) mergeLines(file, text);\n163\t    else if (APPENDED.has(to) && existsSync(file)) appendOnce(file, text);\n164\t    else if (existsSync(file)) kept.push(to);\n165\t    else {\n166\t      mkdirSync(dirname(file), { recursive: true });\n167\t      writeFileSync(file, text);\n168\t    }\n169\t  }\n170\t  const engine = readJson(join(source, 'package.json'));\n171\t  writeJson(join(root, 'package.json'), gamePackage(engine, game));\n172\t  writeJson(join(root, 'package-lock.json'), gameLockfile(readJson(join(source, 'package-lock.json')), game));\n173\t  const engineItems = items.filter((item) => item.owner === 'engine');\n174\t  writeJson(join(root, LOCK_FILE), lockFor(source, engineItems, identity, game, engine, templates));\n175\t  const initialized = git && initRepository(root);\n176\t  const starterFiles = items.length - engineItems.length;\n177\t  return { root, name: game, identity, engineFiles: engineItems.length, starterFiles, kept, initialized };\n178\t}\n179\t\n180\t/**\n181\t * Moves the game in `target` to the engine at `source`; returns what changed. Throws, having written nothing, on\n182\t * anything of the game's the update would replace (the file comment says what), unless `force`.\n183\t */\n184\texport function updateGame({ target, source = SOURCE, force = false }) {\n185\t  const root = resolve(target);\n186\t  const before = verifyGame(root);\n187\t  if (before.undeclared.length > 0 && !force) throw new Error(undeclaredMessage(before));\n188\t  const patched = [...before.changed, ...before.missing, ...before.added];\n189\t  const keep = new Set(force ? [] : before.declared.filter((path) => patched.includes(path)));\n190\t  const identity = engineIdentity(source);\n191\t  const items = plan(source).filter((item) => item.owner === 'engine');\n192\t  const old = before.lock.files;\n193\t  const added = items.filter((item) => !(item.to in old)).map((item) => item.to);\n194\t  const blocked = added.filter((path) => !keep.has(path) && inTheWay(root, path));\n195\t  const engine = readJson(join(source, 'package.json'));\n196\t  const previous = readJson(join(root, 'package.json'));\n197\t  const clashes = npmClashes(previous, engine, before.lock.npm);\n198\t  if (blocked.length + clashes.length > 0 && !force) throw new Error(clashMessage(blocked, clashes));\n199\t  const next = new Set(items.map((item) => item.to));\n200\t  const removed = Object.keys(old).filter((path) => !next.has(path) && !keep.has(path));\n201\t  for (const path of removed) rmSync(join(root, path), { force: true });\n202\t  for (const way of blocked.map((path) => inTheWay(root, path))) if (way) rmSync(way, { recursive: true, force: true });\n203\t  const replaced = items\n204\t    .filter((item) => item.to in old && !keep.has(item.to) && old[item.to] !== hashFile(join(source, item.from)))\n205\t    .map((item) => item.to);\n206\t  for (const { from, to } of items) if (!keep.has(to)) copyInto(source, from, root, to);\n207\t  const pkg = gamePackage(engine, previous.name, previous, before.lock.npm);\n208\t  writeJson(join(root, 'package.json'), pkg);\n209\t  const npm = npmLost(previous, pkg, before.lock.npm);\n210\t  const lockfileFits = sameDependencies(pkg, engine);\n211\t  if (lockfileFits) {\n212\t    writeJson(join(root, 'package-lock.json'), gameLockfile(readJson(join(source, 'package-lock.json')), pkg.name));\n213\t  }\n214\t  const { templates, refreshed, diverged } = refreshTemplates(root, source, before.lock, identity);\n215\t  writeJson(join(root, LOCK_FILE), lockFor(source, items, identity, before.lock.game, engine, templates));\n216\t  const forced = [...blocked, ...clashes];\n217\t  return { root, from: before.lock.engine, to: identity, added, removed, replaced, kept: [...keep], forced, npm, refreshed, diverged, lockfileFits }; // prettier-ignore\n218\t}\n219\t\n220\t/** Why an update stops on engine files the game changed or added without declaring them, with the fixes. */\n221\tfunction undeclaredMessage({ undeclared, added }) {\n222\t  const declare = `list it under \"Local engine patches\" in ${FEEDBACK_FILE} to keep it`;\n223\t  const edited = undeclared.filter((path) => !added.includes(path));\n224\t  const own = undeclared.filter((path) => added.includes(path));\n225\t  return [\n226\t    edited.length > 0 &&\n227\t      `the game changed engine files it does not declare: ${edited.join(', ')}. Undo each (git checkout -- <path>), ${declare}, or pass --force to replace it`, // prettier-ignore\n228\t    own.length > 0 &&\n229\t      `the game added files in the engine's folders: ${own.join(', ')}. Move each into labs/game/ (or delete it), or ${declare}`, // prettier-ignore\n230\t  ]\n231\t    .filter(Boolean)\n232\t    .join('; ');\n233\t}\n234\t\n235\t/** Why an update stops on the game's own files and package.json entries where the newer engine has its own. */\n236\tfunction clashMessage(blocked, clashes) {\n237\t  const parts = [\n238\t    blocked.length > 0 &&\n239\t      `the newer engine adds ${blocked.join(', ')}, where the game has files of its own: move or rename them`,\n240\t    clashes.length > 0 &&\n241\t      `the newer engine sets ${clashes.join(', ')} in package.json, where the game has its own: rename the game's (a script), or drop it (a dependency: the engine's pin then serves)`, // prettier-ignore\n242\t  ];\n243\t  return `${parts.filter(Boolean).join('; ')}; or pass --force to let the engine's replace them`;\n244\t}\n245\t\n246\t/**\n247\t * Brings the game's root files to the templates of the engine at `source` (`lock` is the game's, `identity` the new\n248\t * engine's). A file the game never edited (its hash is the lock's) gets the new template; one it edited is named when\n249\t * its template changed, to compare by hand; one it removed, or had before new-game.mjs, stays as it is; a template new\n250\t * to the game is written where no file is. Returns the lock's new `templates` and the paths refreshed and named.\n251\t */\n252\tfunction refreshTemplates(root, source, lock, identity) {\n253\t  const was = lock.templates ?? {};\n254\t  const [then, now] = [templateValues(lock.game, lock.engine), templateValues(lock.game, identity)];\n255\t  const templates = {};\n256\t  const refreshed = [];\n257\t  const diverged = [];\n258\t  for (const [template, to] of TEMPLATES) {\n259\t    const file = join(root, to);\n260\t    const text = templateText(source, template);\n261\t    const fresh = render(text, now);\n262\t    templates[to] = hashText(fresh);\n263\t    if (!(to in was) && !existsSync(file)) {\n264\t      mkdirSync(dirname(file), { recursive: true });\n265\t      writeFileSync(file, fresh);\n266\t      refreshed.push(to);\n267\t    } else if (!(to in was) || was[to] === null || !existsSync(file)) templates[to] = null;\n268\t    else if (hashFile(file) !== was[to]) {\n269\t      if (hashText(render(text, then)) !== was[to]) diverged.push(to);\n270\t    } else if (templates[to] !== was[to]) {\n271\t      writeFileSync(file, fresh);\n272\t      refreshed.push(to);\n273\t    }\n274\t  }\n275\t  return { templates, refreshed, diverged };\n276\t}\n277\t\n278\t/** Appends `text` after a file's own, once: a repository's instructions stay first, and the game's follow them. */\n279\tfunction appendOnce(file, text) {\n280\t  const had = readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n281\t  if (!had.includes(text.trim())) writeFileSync(file, `${had.replace(/\\n*$/, '\\n\\n')}${text}`);\n282\t}\n283\t\n284\t/** Appends the template's lines a file lacks. */\n285\tfunction mergeLines(file, text) {\n286\t  const had = readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n287\t  const have = new Set(had.split('\\n'));\n288\t  const lacking = text.split('\\n').filter((line) => line.trim() && !line.startsWith('#') && !have.has(line));\n289\t  if (lacking.length > 0) writeFileSync(file, `${had.replace(/\\n?$/, '\\n')}${lacking.join('\\n')}\\n`);\n290\t}\n291\t\n292\t/** Runs `git init` when `root` is in no repository and git is there; returns whether it did. */\n293\tfunction initRepository(root) {\n294\t  try {\n295\t    execFileSync('git', ['-C', root, 'rev-parse', '--is-inside-work-tree'], { stdio: 'ignore' });\n296\t    return false;\n297\t  } catch {\n298\t    try {\n299\t      execFileSync('git', ['init', '--quiet', root], { stdio: 'ignore' });\n300\t      return true;\n301\t    } catch {\n302\t      return false;\n303\t    }\n304\t  }\n305\t}\n306\t\n307\t/** The command line; returns the exit code. */\n308\texport function main(argv = process.argv.slice(2), out = console.log, err = console.error) {\n309\t  const usage = 'usage: node tools/game/new-game.mjs <dir> [--name <name>] | --update <dir> [--force] | --verify <dir>';\n310\t  const named = argv.indexOf('--name');\n311\t  const flags = argv.filter((arg) => arg.startsWith('--'));\n312\t  const positional = argv.filter((arg, i) => !arg.startsWith('--') && (named < 0 || i !== named + 1));\n313\t  const unknown = flags.find((flag) => !['--name', '--update', '--force', '--verify', '--help'].includes(flag));\n314\t  if (flags.includes('--help')) return (out(usage), 0);\n315\t  if (unknown || positional.length !== 1 || (named >= 0 && !argv[named + 1])) {\n316\t    return (err(`new-game: ${unknown ? `unknown flag ${unknown}` : 'name one folder'}\\n${usage}`), 2);\n317\t  }\n318\t  const [target] = positional;\n319\t  try {\n320\t    if (flags.includes('--verify')) return (out(JSON.stringify(verifyGame(target), null, 2)), 0);\n321\t    if (flags.includes('--update')) {\n322\t      const done = updateGame({ target, force: flags.includes('--force') });\n323\t      const patches = done.kept.length > 0 ? `, the local patches kept (${done.kept.join(', ')})` : '';\n324\t      const counts = `${done.replaced.length} engine files changed, ${done.added.length} added, ${done.removed.length} removed`; // prettier-ignore\n325\t      out(`new-game: moved from my-3dge@${done.from.commit.slice(0, 7)} to my-3dge@${done.to.commit.slice(0, 7)}: ${counts}${patches}`); // prettier-ignore\n326\t      if (done.forced.length > 0) out(`replaced the game's own (--force): ${done.forced.join(', ')}`);\n327\t      if (done.npm.length > 0) out(`package.json: the engine's entries win, so these went or are the engine's again: ${done.npm.join(', ')}; put back what the game needs under a name of its own`); // prettier-ignore\n328\t      if (done.refreshed.length > 0) out(`root files brought to the engine's templates: ${done.refreshed.join(', ')}`);\n329\t      const template = (to) => `${to} (tools/game/template/${TEMPLATES.find(([, path]) => path === to)[0]})`;\n330\t      if (done.diverged.length > 0) out(`the engine's templates changed for root files the game edited: compare ${done.diverged.map(template).join(', ')} and take what applies`); // prettier-ignore\n331\t      out(`next: ${done.lockfileFits ? 'npm ci' : 'npm install (the game has dependencies of its own)'}, then npm run check && npm test`); // prettier-ignore\n332\t      return 0;\n333\t    }\n334\t    const done = createGame({ target, name: named >= 0 ? argv[named + 1] : undefined });\n335\t    const near = relative(process.cwd(), done.root);\n336\t    const where = near.startsWith('..') ? done.root : (near || '.').split(sep).join('/');\n337\t    const extra = `${done.kept.length > 0 ? `; kept your ${done.kept.join(', ')}` : ''}${done.initialized ? '; git init' : ''}`; // prettier-ignore\n338\t    out(`new-game: made the game \"${done.name}\" in ${where}: the engine at my-3dge@${done.identity.commit.slice(0, 7)} (${done.engineFiles} files, read-only, pinned by ${LOCK_FILE}) and the starter game in labs/game/${extra}`); // prettier-ignore\n339\t    out(`next: ${where === '.' ? '' : `cd ${where} && `}bash scripts/setup.sh && npm test`);\n340\t    out('then: read AGENTS.md and docs/GAME-GUIDE.md, make the game in labs/game/, and commit as you go');\n341\t    return 0;\n342\t  } catch (error) {\n343\t    err(`new-game: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}`);\n344\t    return 1;\n345\t  }\n346\t}\n347\t\n348\tif (process.argv[1] && resolve(process.argv[1]) === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)) process.exitCode = main();\n349\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"b24d1829-6490-4537-8825-a8633b5747c2","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:43.225Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/.research/my-3dge/tools/game/new-game.mjs","content":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n/**\n * @file Makes a game from the my-3dge engine, and moves a game to a newer engine (PLAN.md WP 10.7, ADR-0024): the\n * one command an agent runs to start a game. Plain JavaScript for any Node from 18 with nothing installed, since it\n * runs straight after `git clone`, before setup. What a game gets, and whose each file is, is tools/game/files.mjs.\n *\n * Create: `node <engine>/tools/game/new-game.mjs <dir> [--name <name>]` writes a game into <dir> (made if missing;\n * an empty folder, or a fresh repository's root): the engine's files, copied as they are and pinned by\n * engine-lock.json; the starter game, labs/game/; the game's root files from tools/game/template/ (`TEMPLATES`); and\n * package.json and package-lock.json with the engine's pins (`gamePackage`, `gameLockfile`, from tools/game/files.mjs).\n * Then `git init` when the folder is in no repository. It never overwrites: a README.md or LICENSE already there is\n * kept, a .gitignore gains the lines it lacks, an AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md or GEMINI.md gets the game's after its own\n * text, and any other file in the way stops it before it writes anything.\n *\n * Update: `node <newer engine>/tools/game/new-game.mjs --update <dir>` (what `node x engine --update` runs) puts this\n * checkout's engine files in place of the game's, removes those it dropped, moves package.json to its pins, brings\n * the root files the game never edited to its templates (`refreshTemplates`) and writes the new lock. Nothing of the\n * game's is replaced or removed: it stops, having written nothing, on an engine file the game changed without\n * declaring it under \"Local engine patches\" in ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md (a declared one is kept), on a file of the game's\n * where the newer engine adds one, and on a package.json entry of the game's that the newer engine sets otherwise\n * (`npmClashes`); `--force` lets the engine's replace them. It names the package.json entries it drops, or sets back\n * where the game had edited the engine's (`npmLost`): the engine's pins win, as its files do.\n *\n * `--verify <dir>` prints `verifyGame` (tools/game/files.mjs) as JSON. Exit codes: 0 done, 1 stopped (the message says\n * why and what to do), 2 a usage error.\n *\n * @example\n * // node /tmp/my-3dge/tools/game/new-game.mjs ../dragon-run → a game in ../dragon-run, named dragon-run\n * // node /tmp/my-3dge/tools/game/new-game.mjs . --name dragon-run → in the current folder (a fresh repository)\n * // node /tmp/my-3dge-new/tools/game/new-game.mjs --update . → the game in . on the newer engine\n * gameName('/tmp/Dragon Run!'); // 'dragon-run'\n * render('# {{name}}', { name: 'dragon-run' }); // '# dragon-run'\n * @see tools/game/new-game.test.ts\n */\nimport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { copyFileSync, existsSync, mkdirSync, readFileSync, rmSync, statSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { basename, dirname, join, relative, resolve, sep } from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\nimport {\n  engineIdentity,\n  FEEDBACK_FILE,\n  gameLockfile,\n  gamePackage,\n  hashFile,\n  hashText,\n  LOCK_FILE,\n  lockFor,\n  npmClashes,\n  npmLost,\n  plan,\n  sameDependencies,\n  SOURCE,\n  verifyGame,\n} from './files.mjs';\n\nexport { gameLockfile, gamePackage, npmClashes };\n\n/** The game's root files: template (in tools/game/template/) → where it goes. */\nexport const TEMPLATES = Object.freeze([\n  ['AGENTS.md.tmpl', 'AGENTS.md'],\n  ['CLAUDE.md.tmpl', 'CLAUDE.md'],\n  ['GEMINI.md.tmpl', 'GEMINI.md'],\n  ['README.md.tmpl', 'README.md'],\n  ['ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md.tmpl', FEEDBACK_FILE],\n  ['gitignore.tmpl', '.gitignore'],\n  ['index.html.tmpl', 'index.html'],\n  ['claude-settings.json.tmpl', '.claude/settings.json'],\n]);\n\n/** Files a target may hold: a README.md or LICENSE is kept; a .gitignore gains the template's lines it lacks. */\nconst KEPT = new Set(['README.md', 'LICENSE', '.gitignore', 'AGENTS.md', 'CLAUDE.md', 'GEMINI.md']);\n\n/** Instruction files the agents read: one already there keeps its text, and the game's follows it (`appendOnce`). */\nconst APPENDED = new Set(['AGENTS.md', 'CLAUDE.md', 'GEMINI.md']);\n\n/** A game's name: an npm package name, from the folder's name by default (`Dragon Run!` → `dragon-run`). */\nexport function gameName(target, name) {\n  const folder = basename(resolve(target)).toLowerCase();\n  const chosen = name ?? folder.replace(/[^a-z0-9._-]+/g, '-').replace(/^[-._]+|[-._]+$/g, '');\n  if (!/^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{0,213}$/.test(chosen)) {\n    throw new Error(`\"${chosen}\" cannot name a game: give --name with lower-case letters, digits, '-', '.' or '_'`);\n  }\n  return chosen;\n}\n\n/** Fills a template's `{{name}}` and `{{engine.*}}`; any other placeholder is an error. */\nexport function render(text, values) {\n  return text.replace(/\\{\\{([a-z.]+)\\}\\}/g, (whole, key) => {\n    if (key in values) return values[key];\n    throw new Error(`the template's ${whole} has no value: new-game.mjs fills ${Object.keys(values).join(', ')}`);\n  });\n}\n\n/** The values of the templates' placeholders for the game `game` on the engine `identity`. */\nfunction templateValues(game, identity) {\n  return {\n    name: game,\n    'engine.repository': identity.repository,\n    'engine.commit': identity.commit,\n    'engine.short': identity.commit.slice(0, 7),\n    'engine.date': identity.date,\n  };\n}\n\n/** A template's text in the engine at `source`. */\nconst templateText = (source, template) => readFileSync(join(source, 'tools/game/template', template), 'utf8');\n\n/** Reads a JSON file. */\nconst readJson = (file) => JSON.parse(readFileSync(file, 'utf8'));\n\n/** Writes JSON with two spaces and a final newline (what Prettier keeps). */\nfunction writeJson(file, value) {\n  mkdirSync(dirname(file), { recursive: true });\n  writeFileSync(file, `${JSON.stringify(value, null, 2)}\\n`);\n}\n\n/** What writing `to` under `root` meets, if anything: the file itself, or a file where one of its folders goes. */\nfunction inTheWay(root, to) {\n  const parts = to.split('/');\n  for (let i = 1; i <= parts.length; i++) {\n    const path = join(root, ...parts.slice(0, i));\n    if (existsSync(path) && (i === parts.length || !statSync(path).isDirectory())) return path;\n  }\n  return undefined;\n}\n\n/** Copies one file, making its folder. */\nfunction copyInto(source, from, root, to) {\n  mkdirSync(dirname(join(root, to)), { recursive: true });\n  copyFileSync(join(source, from), join(root, to));\n}\n\n/** Makes a game in `target` from the engine at `source`; on a clash it throws, having written nothing. */\nexport function createGame({ target, name, source = SOURCE, git = true }) {\n  const root = resolve(target);\n  if (existsSync(root) && !statSync(root).isDirectory()) throw new Error(`${root} is a file: name a folder`);\n  const game = gameName(root, name);\n  const identity = engineIdentity(source);\n  const items = plan(source);\n  const writes = [\n    ...items.map((item) => item.to),\n    ...TEMPLATES.map(([, to]) => to),\n    'package.json',\n    'package-lock.json',\n  ];\n  const clashes = [...writes, LOCK_FILE].filter((to) => !KEPT.has(to) && inTheWay(root, to));\n  if (clashes.length > 0) {\n    const named = clashes.slice(0, 5).join(', ') + (clashes.length > 5 ? ` and ${clashes.length - 5} more` : '');\n    throw new Error(\n      `${root} already holds ${named}: make the game in an empty folder or a fresh repository's root (a README.md, ` +\n        'LICENSE or .gitignore may be there), or move a game to a newer engine with --update',\n    );\n  }\n  for (const { from, to } of items) copyInto(source, from, root, to);\n  const values = templateValues(game, identity);\n  const kept = [];\n  const templates = {};\n  for (const [template, to] of TEMPLATES) {\n    const text = render(templateText(source, template), values);\n    const file = join(root, to);\n    templates[to] = existsSync(file) ? null : hashText(text);\n    if (to === '.gitignore' && existsSync(file)) mergeLines(file, text);\n    else if (APPENDED.has(to) && existsSync(file)) appendOnce(file, text);\n    else if (existsSync(file)) kept.push(to);\n    else {\n      mkdirSync(dirname(file), { recursive: true });\n      writeFileSync(file, text);\n    }\n  }\n  const engine = readJson(join(source, 'package.json'));\n  writeJson(join(root, 'package.json'), gamePackage(engine, game));\n  writeJson(join(root, 'package-lock.json'), gameLockfile(readJson(join(source, 'package-lock.json')), game));\n  const engineItems = items.filter((item) => item.owner === 'engine');\n  writeJson(join(root, LOCK_FILE), lockFor(source, engineItems, identity, game, engine, templates));\n  const initialized = git && initRepository(root);\n  const starterFiles = items.length - engineItems.length;\n  return { root, name: game, identity, engineFiles: engineItems.length, starterFiles, kept, initialized };\n}\n\n/**\n * Moves the game in `target` to the engine at `source`; returns what changed. Throws, having written nothing, on\n * anything of the game's the update would replace (the file comment says what), unless `force`.\n */\nexport function updateGame({ target, source = SOURCE, force = false }) {\n  const root = resolve(target);\n  const before = verifyGame(root);\n  if (before.undeclared.length > 0 && !force) throw new Error(undeclaredMessage(before));\n  const patched = [...before.changed, ...before.missing, ...before.added];\n  const keep = new Set(force ? [] : before.declared.filter((path) => patched.includes(path)));\n  const identity = engineIdentity(source);\n  const items = plan(source).filter((item) => item.owner === 'engine');\n  const old = before.lock.files;\n  const added = items.filter((item) => !(item.to in old)).map((item) => item.to);\n  const blocked = added.filter((path) => !keep.has(path) && inTheWay(root, path));\n  const engine = readJson(join(source, 'package.json'));\n  const previous = readJson(join(root, 'package.json'));\n  const clashes = npmClashes(previous, engine, before.lock.npm);\n  if (blocked.length + clashes.length > 0 && !force) throw new Error(clashMessage(blocked, clashes));\n  const next = new Set(items.map((item) => item.to));\n  const removed = Object.keys(old).filter((path) => !next.has(path) && !keep.has(path));\n  for (const path of removed) rmSync(join(root, path), { force: true });\n  for (const way of blocked.map((path) => inTheWay(root, path))) if (way) rmSync(way, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  const replaced = items\n    .filter((item) => item.to in old && !keep.has(item.to) && old[item.to] !== hashFile(join(source, item.from)))\n    .map((item) => item.to);\n  for (const { from, to } of items) if (!keep.has(to)) copyInto(source, from, root, to);\n  const pkg = gamePackage(engine, previous.name, previous, before.lock.npm);\n  writeJson(join(root, 'package.json'), pkg);\n  const npm = npmLost(previous, pkg, before.lock.npm);\n  const lockfileFits = sameDependencies(pkg, engine);\n  if (lockfileFits) {\n    writeJson(join(root, 'package-lock.json'), gameLockfile(readJson(join(source, 'package-lock.json')), pkg.name));\n  }\n  const { templates, refreshed, diverged } = refreshTemplates(root, source, before.lock, identity);\n  writeJson(join(root, LOCK_FILE), lockFor(source, items, identity, before.lock.game, engine, templates));\n  const forced = [...blocked, ...clashes];\n  return { root, from: before.lock.engine, to: identity, added, removed, replaced, kept: [...keep], forced, npm, refreshed, diverged, lockfileFits }; // prettier-ignore\n}\n\n/** Why an update stops on engine files the game changed or added without declaring them, with the fixes. */\nfunction undeclaredMessage({ undeclared, added }) {\n  const declare = `list it under \"Local engine patches\" in ${FEEDBACK_FILE} to keep it`;\n  const edited = undeclared.filter((path) => !added.includes(path));\n  const own = undeclared.filter((path) => added.includes(path));\n  return [\n    edited.length > 0 &&\n      `the game changed engine files it does not declare: ${edited.join(', ')}. Undo each (git checkout -- <path>), ${declare}, or pass --force to replace it`, // prettier-ignore\n    own.length > 0 &&\n      `the game added files in the engine's folders: ${own.join(', ')}. Move each into labs/game/ (or delete it), or ${declare}`, // prettier-ignore\n  ]\n    .filter(Boolean)\n    .join('; ');\n}\n\n/** Why an update stops on the game's own files and package.json entries where the newer engine has its own. */\nfunction clashMessage(blocked, clashes) {\n  const parts = [\n    blocked.length > 0 &&\n      `the newer engine adds ${blocked.join(', ')}, where the game has files of its own: move or rename them`,\n    clashes.length > 0 &&\n      `the newer engine sets ${clashes.join(', ')} in package.json, where the game has its own: rename the game's (a script), or drop it (a dependency: the engine's pin then serves)`, // prettier-ignore\n  ];\n  return `${parts.filter(Boolean).join('; ')}; or pass --force to let the engine's replace them`;\n}\n\n/**\n * Brings the game's root files to the templates of the engine at `source` (`lock` is the game's, `identity` the new\n * engine's). A file the game never edited (its hash is the lock's) gets the new template; one it edited is named when\n * its template changed, to compare by hand; one it removed, or had before new-game.mjs, stays as it is; a template new\n * to the game is written where no file is. Returns the lock's new `templates` and the paths refreshed and named.\n */\nfunction refreshTemplates(root, source, lock, identity) {\n  const was = lock.templates ?? {};\n  const [then, now] = [templateValues(lock.game, lock.engine), templateValues(lock.game, identity)];\n  const templates = {};\n  const refreshed = [];\n  const diverged = [];\n  for (const [template, to] of TEMPLATES) {\n    const file = join(root, to);\n    const text = templateText(source, template);\n    const fresh = render(text, now);\n    templates[to] = hashText(fresh);\n    if (!(to in was) && !existsSync(file)) {\n      mkdirSync(dirname(file), { recursive: true });\n      writeFileSync(file, fresh);\n      refreshed.push(to);\n    } else if (!(to in was) || was[to] === null || !existsSync(file)) templates[to] = null;\n    else if (hashFile(file) !== was[to]) {\n      if (hashText(render(text, then)) !== was[to]) diverged.push(to);\n    } else if (templates[to] !== was[to]) {\n      writeFileSync(file, fresh);\n      refreshed.push(to);\n    }\n  }\n  return { templates, refreshed, diverged };\n}\n\n/** Appends `text` after a file's own, once: a repository's instructions stay first, and the game's follow them. */\nfunction appendOnce(file, text) {\n  const had = readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n  if (!had.includes(text.trim())) writeFileSync(file, `${had.replace(/\\n*$/, '\\n\\n')}${text}`);\n}\n\n/** Appends the template's lines a file lacks. */\nfunction mergeLines(file, text) {\n  const had = readFileSync(file, 'utf8');\n  const have = new Set(had.split('\\n'));\n  const lacking = text.split('\\n').filter((line) => line.trim() && !line.startsWith('#') && !have.has(line));\n  if (lacking.length > 0) writeFileSync(file, `${had.replace(/\\n?$/, '\\n')}${lacking.join('\\n')}\\n`);\n}\n\n/** Runs `git init` when `root` is in no repository and git is there; returns whether it did. */\nfunction initRepository(root) {\n  try {\n    execFileSync('git', ['-C', root, 'rev-parse', '--is-inside-work-tree'], { stdio: 'ignore' });\n    return false;\n  } catch {\n    try {\n      execFileSync('git', ['init', '--quiet', root], { stdio: 'ignore' });\n      return true;\n    } catch {\n      return false;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n/** The command line; returns the exit code. */\nexport function main(argv = process.argv.slice(2), out = console.log, err = console.error) {\n  const usage = 'usage: node tools/game/new-game.mjs <dir> [--name <name>] | --update <dir> [--force] | --verify <dir>';\n  const named = argv.indexOf('--name');\n  const flags = argv.filter((arg) => arg.startsWith('--'));\n  const positional = argv.filter((arg, i) => !arg.startsWith('--') && (named < 0 || i !== named + 1));\n  const unknown = flags.find((flag) => !['--name', '--update', '--force', '--verify', '--help'].includes(flag));\n  if (flags.includes('--help')) return (out(usage), 0);\n  if (unknown || positional.length !== 1 || (named >= 0 && !argv[named + 1])) {\n    return (err(`new-game: ${unknown ? `unknown flag ${unknown}` : 'name one folder'}\\n${usage}`), 2);\n  }\n  const [target] = positional;\n  try {\n    if (flags.includes('--verify')) return (out(JSON.stringify(verifyGame(target), null, 2)), 0);\n    if (flags.includes('--update')) {\n      const done = updateGame({ target, force: flags.includes('--force') });\n      const patches = done.kept.length > 0 ? `, the local patches kept (${done.kept.join(', ')})` : '';\n      const counts = `${done.replaced.length} engine files changed, ${done.added.length} added, ${done.removed.length} removed`; // prettier-ignore\n      out(`new-game: moved from my-3dge@${done.from.commit.slice(0, 7)} to my-3dge@${done.to.commit.slice(0, 7)}: ${counts}${patches}`); // prettier-ignore\n      if (done.forced.length > 0) out(`replaced the game's own (--force): ${done.forced.join(', ')}`);\n      if (done.npm.length > 0) out(`package.json: the engine's entries win, so these went or are the engine's again: ${done.npm.join(', ')}; put back what the game needs under a name of its own`); // prettier-ignore\n      if (done.refreshed.length > 0) out(`root files brought to the engine's templates: ${done.refreshed.join(', ')}`);\n      const template = (to) => `${to} (tools/game/template/${TEMPLATES.find(([, path]) => path === to)[0]})`;\n      if (done.diverged.length > 0) out(`the engine's templates changed for root files the game edited: compare ${done.diverged.map(template).join(', ')} and take what applies`); // prettier-ignore\n      out(`next: ${done.lockfileFits ? 'npm ci' : 'npm install (the game has dependencies of its own)'}, then npm run check && npm test`); // prettier-ignore\n      return 0;\n    }\n    const done = createGame({ target, name: named >= 0 ? argv[named + 1] : undefined });\n    const near = relative(process.cwd(), done.root);\n    const where = near.startsWith('..') ? done.root : (near || '.').split(sep).join('/');\n    const extra = `${done.kept.length > 0 ? `; kept your ${done.kept.join(', ')}` : ''}${done.initialized ? '; git init' : ''}`; // prettier-ignore\n    out(`new-game: made the game \"${done.name}\" in ${where}: the engine at my-3dge@${done.identity.commit.slice(0, 7)} (${done.engineFiles} files, read-only, pinned by ${LOCK_FILE}) and the starter game in labs/game/${extra}`); // prettier-ignore\n    out(`next: ${where === '.' ? '' : `cd ${where} && `}bash scripts/setup.sh && npm test`);\n    out('then: read AGENTS.md and docs/GAME-GUIDE.md, make the game in labs/game/, and commit as you go');\n    return 0;\n  } catch (error) {\n    err(`new-game: ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}`);\n    return 1;\n  }\n}\n\nif (process.argv[1] && resolve(process.argv[1]) === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)) process.exitCode = main();\n","numLines":349,"startLine":1,"totalLines":349}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01S2FGTYwQQmY9VyvYWnATim","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9JLbsZSxAAui538HFx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q2angrgYjeVJw55Z8i1Cyj","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/.research/my-3dge/docs/PROGRESS.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3010,"cache_read_input_tokens":44208,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3010},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"320f295b-f05d-4e88-82cd-4f42780a44ff","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:43.875Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9JLNjFeTzRQCy1DeMt","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Q2angrgYjeVJw55Z8i1Cyj":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/.research/my-3dge/docs/PROGRESS.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q2angrgYjeVJw55Z8i1Cyj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Progress\n2\t\n3\tRead this first: where things stand, what is next and the open issues, on one screen (`node x docs --check` fails it\n4\tpast 40 lines). The integrator rewrites it at each gate; every WP's status and notes are in the ledger, PLAN.md §14.\n5\t\n6\t## Next: nothing scheduled; the owner's playtest of the tech demo\n7\t\n8\t- Gate G13 (PR #34): Phase 13 is done, with every WP it fired: the front end (WP 13.25), the governor (7.5),\n9\t  GPU-driven crowds' stage 1 (11.4), templates and skills (12.1), the usability evals and mutation testing (12.2),\n10\t  `x mcp` (7.6), the tour with its attract mode and a film per look (13.26). What follows waits: upgrades U-2 to U-7\n11\t  from their dates (`node x deps --qualify`), on-demand WPs for their triggers (§9.1), Phase H for a game to ship.\n12\t- The owner's, all in the playground's Owner checks (start menu; WP 13.28), each in plain words with Go there: the\n13\t  playtest (docs/PLAYGROUND.md §9.3), the looks to judge (the clean default, clean and cel at full resolution, the\n14\t  accent weak from isometric, the cel look's dark night there, its near-black brick), the sound and a pad, and ESC-0002\n15\t  to ESC-0006's calls (the Quaternius GLBs, model access for the live evals, the crowd's CPU render, the mutants outside\n16\t  the sample), answered from Copy my answers. Their go-ahead (2026-10-22): a bot may play with infinite health and ammo.\n17\t\n18\t## Where things stand (2026-11-05)\n19\t\n20\t- Phases 0–9 and 13 are done (G10–G13: PR #22 to #34). The playground (`npm run dev`) is one map, the block, behind a\n21\t  splash and a start menu (WP 13.33), shut doors walls to its cameras (13.34), no z-fighting (13.35–13.37), the audit's\n22\t  gaps closed (13.38); the player moves as Apex in five cameras (doors, pickups, melee, guns, ragdolls, neighbours, a\n23\t  dog, sound, day and night, GPU rain; clean, cel and pixel looks); Watch the tour plays it all. Agents drive it through\n24\t  `node x`, `__engine` or `x mcp`. Games: lean/. Shipped as playground.html. Faster starts (ADR-0008 amendments 11, 12;\n25\t  Owner: a move still re-keys lit pipelines); Style Lab's filters in Tune the look.\n26\t\n27\t## What waits, and the open issues\n28\t\n29\t- Amendment 22 proposes triangle-mesh terrain. QA baselines: the timelines' knockdown slide, WP 8.8's. Owner:\n30\t  top-down's pixel look panned across a whole pixel changes 7–10 pixels of a soft shadow band (amendment 35). Clip\n31\t  contacts: hands read as holds in walks, idles and more (WP 8.8's row); no foot lock reads a clip's foot contacts yet.\n32\t  Not verifiable here: speakers, touch (ADR-0021), pads, real GPUs (`stats().gpuMs`: the rain's 1 ms; load times), the\n33\t  pixel look's glide, how the filters read, a desktop MCP client. A key pressed in a warm-up is lost (amendment 48).\n34\t- Mutation (WP 12.2, ESC-0006): the run's tenth catches 94.40%, the rest 74.3%; rotate its seed and redraw each gate.\n35\t- Near the size cap (390–397 lines), split on the next change: sim/world.ts, anim/{quadruped,clip/validate}.ts,\n36\t  tools/cmd/replay.ts, app/engine.ts; four tests at 399–400.\n37\t- The quick gate is over its 5 min (CI_BUDGET), its long pole the playground's soak and site tests; under load\n38\t  `npm test` can fail on RPC timeouts; audio.spec's spatial test hung once in an offline render on GitHub (e6f38ba).\n39\t- The tour's page goldens come from its spec (amendment 41). Random play lost the shooter's chest in 4–5% of frames\n40\t  (before WP 13.27). A shot's ID pass builds a pipeline again after each lambert–toon style switch (frames never do).\n41\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"f6b5c7b8-dd7e-47e7-a6cd-3ac0cecc7876","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:43.908Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/.research/my-3dge/docs/PROGRESS.md","content":"# Progress\n\nRead this first: where things stand, what is next and the open issues, on one screen (`node x docs --check` fails it\npast 40 lines). The integrator rewrites it at each gate; every WP's status and notes are in the ledger, PLAN.md §14.\n\n## Next: nothing scheduled; the owner's playtest of the tech demo\n\n- Gate G13 (PR #34): Phase 13 is done, with every WP it fired: the front end (WP 13.25), the governor (7.5),\n  GPU-driven crowds' stage 1 (11.4), templates and skills (12.1), the usability evals and mutation testing (12.2),\n  `x mcp` (7.6), the tour with its attract mode and a film per look (13.26). What follows waits: upgrades U-2 to U-7\n  from their dates (`node x deps --qualify`), on-demand WPs for their triggers (§9.1), Phase H for a game to ship.\n- The owner's, all in the playground's Owner checks (start menu; WP 13.28), each in plain words with Go there: the\n  playtest (docs/PLAYGROUND.md §9.3), the looks to judge (the clean default, clean and cel at full resolution, the\n  accent weak from isometric, the cel look's dark night there, its near-black brick), the sound and a pad, and ESC-0002\n  to ESC-0006's calls (the Quaternius GLBs, model access for the live evals, the crowd's CPU render, the mutants outside\n  the sample), answered from Copy my answers. Their go-ahead (2026-10-22): a bot may play with infinite health and ammo.\n\n## Where things stand (2026-11-05)\n\n- Phases 0–9 and 13 are done (G10–G13: PR #22 to #34). The playground (`npm run dev`) is one map, the block, behind a\n  splash and a start menu (WP 13.33), shut doors walls to its cameras (13.34), no z-fighting (13.35–13.37), the audit's\n  gaps closed (13.38); the player moves as Apex in five cameras (doors, pickups, melee, guns, ragdolls, neighbours, a\n  dog, sound, day and night, GPU rain; clean, cel and pixel looks); Watch the tour plays it all. Agents drive it through\n  `node x`, `__engine` or `x mcp`. Games: lean/. Shipped as playground.html. Faster starts (ADR-0008 amendments 11, 12;\n  Owner: a move still re-keys lit pipelines); Style Lab's filters in Tune the look.\n\n## What waits, and the open issues\n\n- Amendment 22 proposes triangle-mesh terrain. QA baselines: the timelines' knockdown slide, WP 8.8's. Owner:\n  top-down's pixel look panned across a whole pixel changes 7–10 pixels of a soft shadow band (amendment 35). Clip\n  contacts: hands read as holds in walks, idles and more (WP 8.8's row); no foot lock reads a clip's foot contacts yet.\n  Not verifiable here: speakers, touch (ADR-0021), pads, real GPUs (`stats().gpuMs`: the rain's 1 ms; load times), the\n  pixel look's glide, how the filters read, a desktop MCP client. A key pressed in a warm-up is lost (amendment 48).\n- Mutation (WP 12.2, ESC-0006): the run's tenth catches 94.40%, the rest 74.3%; rotate its seed and redraw each gate.\n- Near the size cap (390–397 lines), split on the next change: sim/world.ts, anim/{quadruped,clip/validate}.ts,\n  tools/cmd/replay.ts, app/engine.ts; four tests at 399–400.\n- The quick gate is over its 5 min (CI_BUDGET), its long pole the playground's soak and site tests; under load\n  `npm test` can fail on RPC timeouts; audio.spec's spatial test hung once in an offline render on GitHub (e6f38ba).\n- The tour's page goldens come from its spec (amendment 41). Random play lost the shooter's chest in 4–5% of frames\n  (before WP 13.27). A shot's ID pass builds a pipeline again after each lambert–toon style switch (frames never do).\n","numLines":41,"startLine":1,"totalLines":41}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Q2angrgYjeVJw55Z8i1Cyj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
