{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JLVJqkTCe9zBGyrt6FZC9b","type":"tool_result","content":"total 40\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha 4096 Nov  4 21:20 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha 4096 Nov  4 21:20 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 3591 Nov  4 21:20 AGENTS.md.tmpl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  273 Nov  4 21:20 CLAUDE.md.tmpl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  809 Nov  4 21:20 ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md.tmpl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   13 Nov  4 21:20 GEMINI.md.tmpl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  418 Nov  4 21:20 README.md.tmpl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  961 Nov  4 21:20 claude-settings.json.tmpl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  139 Nov  4 21:20 gitignore.tmpl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  981 Nov  4 21:20 index.html.tmpl\n# AGENTS.md: {{name}}\n\n{{name}} is a game made with my-3dge, a 3D web game engine built for AI coding agents: TypeScript, three.js on\nWebGPU, Rapier physics, gameplay reproducible on the CPU and checked without a screen, the UI in HTML/CSS. The engine\nis in this repository, pinned to the commit engine-lock.json names; you make the game.\n\nBefore your first change, read docs/GAME-GUIDE.md once: how a game is built on this engine, the commands that prove\nit works, and where to look things up. Then grow the game from the starter in labs/game/, which already plays, wins\nthrough its bot, and passes its tests.\n\n## Set up (once per machine)\n\n    bash scripts/setup.sh\n\nIt installs Node 24 when missing (Linux x64), Chromium for the browser commands when missing, then `npm ci`. Plain\n`npm ci` is enough for everything except `x shot`, `x film` and `x replay --browser`.\n\n## The loop\n\n1. Edit the game in labs/game/: sim-side code (the rules) in labs/game/scenes/ and labs/game/cast/, the page in\n   labs/game/main.ts.\n2. `npm run check`: types, lint, format, the asset rules, and the engine unchanged.\n3. `npm test`: the game's tests (its replay's golden hashes, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds).\n4. See it without a screen: `node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts` (the hash and the events), `node x shot labs/game`\n   (what the page draws, as numbers and a text thumbnail), `node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim` (the\n   goldens, in Node and Chromium). `node x help` lists every command; each prints its verdict first and writes\n   out/<cmd>/…/report.json.\n5. Commit, and keep labs/game/README.md current: what the game is, how it plays, the calls you made.\n\n`npm run dev` serves the game at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ for a person to play.\n\n## Rules\n\n- **The engine is read-only.** engine/, tools/, data/, labs/box/ (the engine's worked example), scripts/setup.sh, the\n  configs and the docs it shipped: engine-lock.json lists every one, and `npm run check` fails when one changes. When\n  the engine is in your way, work round it in the game and write what you needed in ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md. Only when no\n  workaround exists, patch the engine file and list it under \"Local engine patches\" there, with why.\n- **Only the public API.** Pages import engine/index.ts; sim-side code imports engine/sim-api.ts (lint enforces it).\n- **Reproducible play.** Sim-side code reads no clock, no `Math.random`, no DOM: randomness comes from named streams\n  (`w.rng('loot')`), time is whole 60 Hz steps. The same intents and seed give the same hashes, in Node and Chromium.\n- **Assets are code or text first**: geometry, textures, materials and sounds as data. A binary file only with the\n  owner's approval, listed in APPROVED-BINARIES.json with their answer (`npm run check` fails one unlisted); fonts are\n  approved, anywhere in labs/game/ with their license beside them.\n- SI units, +Y up, characters face +Z. Every file opens with a `@file` comment and stays under 400 lines.\n- **Ask the owner** before anything outward or costly: a binary asset, a new npm dependency, spending money,\n  publishing. No answer within 15 minutes: take the safer choice, note it in labs/game/README.md, carry on.\n- Update the engine only when the owner asks: `node x engine --update`.\n\n## Done means\n\n`npm run check` and `npm test` pass; the bot still wins (teach it each new rule); a change that alters play on\npurpose records the replay's goldens again (`node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim --update`) with the reason\nin the commit; labs/game/README.md says what the game is now.\n------README\n# {{name}}\n\nA game made with the [my-3dge]({{engine.repository}}) engine (at {{engine.short}}: engine-lock.json).\n\n```sh\nbash scripts/setup.sh   # once: Node 24 and Chromium when missing, then npm ci\nnpm run dev             # the game at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/\nnpm test                # its tests, headless\n```\n\nThe game is labs/game/: its README says what it is and how it plays. Agents start at AGENTS.md.\n------FEEDBACK\n# Engine feedback: {{name}}\n\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at {{engine.short}}) and did not get. The owner collects this file\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\n\n## Requests\n\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\n\n## Friction\n\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\n\n## Local engine patches\n\n<!--\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\n-->\n------index\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n    <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\" />\n    <title>{{name}}</title>\n    <!--\n      The landing page: it opens the game (labs/game/), passing on this URL's query and hash, so /?seed=3 reaches the\n      page that reads it. `npm run build` ships it with every labs/<name>/index.html.\n    -->\n    <script>\n      location.replace('labs/game/' + location.search + location.hash);\n    </script>\n    <style>\n      html,\n      body {\n        margin: 0;\n        height: 100%;\n        background: #15171c;\n      }\n      body {\n        display: flex;\n        align-items: center;\n        justify-content: center;\n        font:\n          18px system-ui,\n          sans-serif;\n        color: #c9ccd4;\n      }\n      a {\n        color: inherit;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <p><a href=\"labs/game/\">Play {{name}}</a></p>\n  </body>\n</html>\n----\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json\",\n  \"permissions\": {\n    \"allow\": [\n      \"Bash(node x *)\",\n      \"Bash(npm run *)\",\n      \"Bash(npm test*)\",\n      \"Bash(npm ci)\",\n      \"Bash(npx vitest *)\",\n      \"Bash(bash scripts/setup.sh)\",\n      \"Bash(git status*)\",\n      \"Bash(git diff*)\",\n      \"Bash(git log*)\",\n      \"Bash(git show*)\",\n      \"Bash(git add *)\",\n      \"Bash(git commit *)\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"SessionStart\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"bash \\\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/scripts/setup.sh\\\"\",\n            \"timeout\": 900\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"PostToolUse\": [\n      {\n        \"matcher\": \"Edit|Write|MultiEdit\",\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"node \\\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/post-tool-use.ts\\\"\",\n            \"timeout\": 60\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\nout/\ndist/\n.cache/\nnode_modules/\ntest-results/\n.env*\n.claude/settings.local.json\n\n# TypeScript build info (tsc -b writes it)\n*.tsbuildinfo","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"893f39ee-bcf3-4072-aece-47b181a31bea","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:50.720Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"total 40\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha 4096 Nov  4 21:20 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha 4096 Nov  4 21:20 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 3591 Nov  4 21:20 AGENTS.md.tmpl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  273 Nov  4 21:20 CLAUDE.md.tmpl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  809 Nov  4 21:20 ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md.tmpl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   13 Nov  4 21:20 GEMINI.md.tmpl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  418 Nov  4 21:20 README.md.tmpl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  961 Nov  4 21:20 claude-settings.json.tmpl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  139 Nov  4 21:20 gitignore.tmpl\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  981 Nov  4 21:20 index.html.tmpl\n# AGENTS.md: {{name}}\n\n{{name}} is a game made with my-3dge, a 3D web game engine built for AI coding agents: TypeScript, three.js on\nWebGPU, Rapier physics, gameplay reproducible on the CPU and checked without a screen, the UI in HTML/CSS. The engine\nis in this repository, pinned to the commit engine-lock.json names; you make the game.\n\nBefore your first change, read docs/GAME-GUIDE.md once: how a game is built on this engine, the commands that prove\nit works, and where to look things up. Then grow the game from the starter in labs/game/, which already plays, wins\nthrough its bot, and passes its tests.\n\n## Set up (once per machine)\n\n    bash scripts/setup.sh\n\nIt installs Node 24 when missing (Linux x64), Chromium for the browser commands when missing, then `npm ci`. Plain\n`npm ci` is enough for everything except `x shot`, `x film` and `x replay --browser`.\n\n## The loop\n\n1. Edit the game in labs/game/: sim-side code (the rules) in labs/game/scenes/ and labs/game/cast/, the page in\n   labs/game/main.ts.\n2. `npm run check`: types, lint, format, the asset rules, and the engine unchanged.\n3. `npm test`: the game's tests (its replay's golden hashes, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds).\n4. See it without a screen: `node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts` (the hash and the events), `node x shot labs/game`\n   (what the page draws, as numbers and a text thumbnail), `node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim` (the\n   goldens, in Node and Chromium). `node x help` lists every command; each prints its verdict first and writes\n   out/<cmd>/…/report.json.\n5. Commit, and keep labs/game/README.md current: what the game is, how it plays, the calls you made.\n\n`npm run dev` serves the game at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ for a person to play.\n\n## Rules\n\n- **The engine is read-only.** engine/, tools/, data/, labs/box/ (the engine's worked example), scripts/setup.sh, the\n  configs and the docs it shipped: engine-lock.json lists every one, and `npm run check` fails when one changes. When\n  the engine is in your way, work round it in the game and write what you needed in ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md. Only when no\n  workaround exists, patch the engine file and list it under \"Local engine patches\" there, with why.\n- **Only the public API.** Pages import engine/index.ts; sim-side code imports engine/sim-api.ts (lint enforces it).\n- **Reproducible play.** Sim-side code reads no clock, no `Math.random`, no DOM: randomness comes from named streams\n  (`w.rng('loot')`), time is whole 60 Hz steps. The same intents and seed give the same hashes, in Node and Chromium.\n- **Assets are code or text first**: geometry, textures, materials and sounds as data. A binary file only with the\n  owner's approval, listed in APPROVED-BINARIES.json with their answer (`npm run check` fails one unlisted); fonts are\n  approved, anywhere in labs/game/ with their license beside them.\n- SI units, +Y up, characters face +Z. Every file opens with a `@file` comment and stays under 400 lines.\n- **Ask the owner** before anything outward or costly: a binary asset, a new npm dependency, spending money,\n  publishing. No answer within 15 minutes: take the safer choice, note it in labs/game/README.md, carry on.\n- Update the engine only when the owner asks: `node x engine --update`.\n\n## Done means\n\n`npm run check` and `npm test` pass; the bot still wins (teach it each new rule); a change that alters play on\npurpose records the replay's goldens again (`node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim --update`) with the reason\nin the commit; labs/game/README.md says what the game is now.\n------README\n# {{name}}\n\nA game made with the [my-3dge]({{engine.repository}}) engine (at {{engine.short}}: engine-lock.json).\n\n```sh\nbash scripts/setup.sh   # once: Node 24 and Chromium when missing, then npm ci\nnpm run dev             # the game at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/\nnpm test                # its tests, headless\n```\n\nThe game is labs/game/: its README says what it is and how it plays. Agents start at AGENTS.md.\n------FEEDBACK\n# Engine feedback: {{name}}\n\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at {{engine.short}}) and did not get. The owner collects this file\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\n\n## Requests\n\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\n\n## Friction\n\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\n\n## Local engine patches\n\n<!--\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\n-->\n------index\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n    <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\" />\n    <title>{{name}}</title>\n    <!--\n      The landing page: it opens the game (labs/game/), passing on this URL's query and hash, so /?seed=3 reaches the\n      page that reads it. `npm run build` ships it with every labs/<name>/index.html.\n    -->\n    <script>\n      location.replace('labs/game/' + location.search + location.hash);\n    </script>\n    <style>\n      html,\n      body {\n        margin: 0;\n        height: 100%;\n        background: #15171c;\n      }\n      body {\n        display: flex;\n        align-items: center;\n        justify-content: center;\n        font:\n          18px system-ui,\n          sans-serif;\n        color: #c9ccd4;\n      }\n      a {\n        color: inherit;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <p><a href=\"labs/game/\">Play {{name}}</a></p>\n  </body>\n</html>\n----\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json\",\n  \"permissions\": {\n    \"allow\": [\n      \"Bash(node x *)\",\n      \"Bash(npm run *)\",\n      \"Bash(npm test*)\",\n      \"Bash(npm ci)\",\n      \"Bash(npx vitest *)\",\n      \"Bash(bash scripts/setup.sh)\",\n      \"Bash(git status*)\",\n      \"Bash(git diff*)\",\n      \"Bash(git log*)\",\n      \"Bash(git show*)\",\n      \"Bash(git add *)\",\n      \"Bash(git commit *)\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"SessionStart\": [\n      {\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"bash \\\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/scripts/setup.sh\\\"\",\n            \"timeout\": 900\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"PostToolUse\": [\n      {\n        \"matcher\": \"Edit|Write|MultiEdit\",\n        \"hooks\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"command\",\n            \"command\": \"node \\\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/post-tool-use.ts\\\"\",\n            \"timeout\": 60\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\nout/\ndist/\n.cache/\nnode_modules/\ntest-results/\n.env*\n.claude/settings.local.json\n\n# TypeScript build info (tsc -b writes it)\n*.tsbuildinfo","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JLVJqkTCe9zBGyrt6FZC9b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
