{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9KRSNKLYpLUNNbYSeL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019qtasC6TwKqjeuoADZhYUr","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-max-plan-v2--20261104-212002--x601dca-work/ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e/tool-results/bf5rgms82.txt","allow_large":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8609,"cache_read_input_tokens":85187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8609},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"028a68cb-9a87-47f4-bc44-88fb77c3b250","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:57.259Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9KRCEYsSxje7nToA6A","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019qtasC6TwKqjeuoADZhYUr":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-max-plan-v2--20261104-212002--x601dca-work/ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e/tool-results/bf5rgms82.txt","allow_large":true}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019qtasC6TwKqjeuoADZhYUr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# The starter game\n2\t\n3\tEvery game made with my-3dge starts as this one (`node tools/game/new-game.mjs`), then becomes its own: rewrite this\n4\tpage as the game grows. It is the game's page for the owner and the next agent: what the game is, how it plays, how to\n5\tsee it, and the calls made along the way.\n6\t\n7\t## The game\n8\t\n9\tRun round the arena collecting every gem before the clock runs out. WASD or the arrows run, Space jumps (over the low\n10\twalls), Shift dashes. All the gems: won. The clock at 0: lost. Enter starts a new round on the next seed.\n11\t\n12\t## Files\n13\t\n14\t| File                              | What it is                                                                    |\n15\t| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n16\t| labs/game/scenes/play.ts          | The rules, sim-side: the arena's text, the settings, the gems, the round, the systems |\n17\t| labs/game/cast/player.ts          | The player: its character (run, jump, dash) and the body it is drawn as        |\n18\t| labs/game/bot.ts                  | The bot: plays through intents, down the flow field to the nearest gem         |\n19\t| labs/game/main.ts, index.html     | The page: the engine, the HUD, Enter to play again, the chase camera           |\n20\t| labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts     | The tests: the golden replay, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds, the clock |\n21\t| labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json | The bot's play from seed 1, with its golden hashes                             |\n22\t\n23\t## Settings\n24\t\n25\t`game.gems` (10), `game.seconds` (30) and `game.speed` (6 m/s), read when the round starts: `?game.gems=20` in the\n26\tpage, `--set game.gems=20` for `node x sim` and `node x shot`.\n27\t\n28\t## See it\n29\t\n30\t```sh\n31\tnpm run dev                                         # http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (?replay=bot plays the bot's run)\n32\tnpm test                                            # the tests\n33\tnode x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --feel          # the rules in Node: hash, events, how the player handles\n34\tnode x shot labs/game                               # the page on WebGPU, as numbers\n35\tnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim       # the goldens, in Node and Chromium\n36\t```\n37\t\n38\t## Decisions\n39\t\n40\t<!-- The calls made without the owner, newest first: the date, what was decided, why. -->\n41\t-----\n42\t/**\n43\t * @file The starter game's page (labs/game/index.html): it starts the engine (`createEngine`, engine/app/engine.ts) on\n44\t * the scene `game:play` (labs/game/scenes/play.ts) with the arena's text registered for the view, offers the bot's\n45\t * replay to `?replay=bot`, and shows the round each drawn frame in the HTML/CSS overlay's HUD: the gems, the clock,\n46\t * the controls, the best round kept across sessions (labs/game/best.ts, through the engine's store) and, when the\n47\t * round ends, how it ended. Enter then starts a new round on the next seed. Escape (or the pad's Start) pauses the\n48\t * round under a menu (`createMenu`: Resume, New round), which keeps its keys out of play while it is open\n49\t * (`createEngine({ modal })`); the store keeps the best round and any keys rebound (`createEngine({ store })`). The\n50\t * camera is the chase camera unless the URL names one (`?cam=iso`, `?cam3=orbit`).\n51\t *\n52\t * Everything else a page does (routes, the renderer, the frame loop, the devices, `window.__engine`, the error\n53\t * overlay, the touch controls) is the engine's, so this file is the game's own presentation only. It reads the run\n54\t * and never changes it: the HUD cannot change the hash.\n55\t *\n56\t * Game code: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts) and the game's own files.\n57\t *\n58\t * Open it at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (`npm run dev`): `?seed=7&game.gems=20` plays another round,\n59\t * `?replay=bot` the bot's, `?cam=iso` another camera. Headless, `node x shot labs/game` reports what it draws.\n60\t */\n61\t/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />\n62\timport { createEngine, createMenu, createStore, type Engine, type EngineFrame, type Menu } from '../../engine';\n63\timport { bestOf, recordBest } from './best';\n64\timport { ARENA_TEXT, play, type Round } from './scenes/play';\n65\t\n66\t/** The page's query, with the chase camera when it names none: it follows the player round the arena. */\n67\tconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\n68\tif (!search.has('cam') && !search.has('cam3')) search.set('cam3', 'chase');\n69\t\n70\t/** The game's replays, by name (`?replay=bot`), as text loaded on demand. */\n71\tconst replays = { bot: () => import('./replays/bot.replay.json?raw').then((module) => module.default) };\n72\t\n73\t/** The started engine; null until `createEngine` resolves (its first frames are drawn before that). */\n74\tlet engine: Engine | null = null;\n75\t\n76\t/** Whether the round on screen has ended, so Enter starts the next. */\n77\tlet ended = false;\n78\t\n79\t/** The game's store: its best round across sessions; a replay's page plays in its demo mode, so it sets none. */\n80\tconst store = createStore({ prefix: 'my3dge-game:', mode: search.has('replay') ? 'demo' : 'play' });\n81\t\n82\t/** The fastest won round kept (s), and the run whose clock the page saw running, with the steps it started with. */\n83\tlet best = bestOf(store);\n84\tlet seen: { world: object; steps: number } | null = null;\n85\t\n86\t/** The pause menu while it is open; null while the round plays. */\n87\tlet paused: Menu | null = null;\n88\t\n89\t/** Opens the pause menu over the paused round, or reads it a frame: Resume (or Escape again), New round. */\n90\tfunction pauseMenu(dt: number): void {\n91\t  const [inspector, ui, input] = [engine?.inspector, engine?.ui, engine?.input];\n92\t  if (!inspector || !ui || !input) return;\n93\t  const close = () => {\n94\t    paused?.remove();\n95\t    paused = null;\n96\t    inspector.resume();\n97\t  };\n98\t  if (paused) return void paused.update(dt);\n99\t  if (!input.pressed('pause')) return;\n100\t  inspector.pause();\n101\t  const items = [\n102\t    { label: 'Resume', id: 'resume' },\n103\t    { label: 'New round', id: 'new' },\n104\t  ];\n105\t  paused = createMenu(ui.root, items, { input, id: 'pause', title: 'Paused', onCancel: close, onPick: (_i, item) => {\n106\t    if (typeof item === 'object' && item.id === 'new') inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\n107\t    close();\n108\t  } }); // prettier-ignore\n109\t}\n110\t\n111\t/** Shows the round in the HUD: the gems, the clock, the controls, and how the round ended. */\n112\tfunction showRound({ world }: EngineFrame): void {\n113\t  const ui = engine?.ui;\n114\t  const entity = world.query('round')[0] as unknown as { round: Round } | undefined;\n115\t  if (!ui || !entity) return;\n116\t  const { gems, collected, left, state } = entity.round;\n117\t  if (seen?.world !== world) seen = state === 'playing' ? { world, steps: left + world.tick } : null;\n118\t  const was = ended;\n119\t  ui.hud('gems', `Gems ${collected} / ${gems}`, { at: 'top-left' });\n120\t  ui.hud('clock', `${Math.ceil(left / world.hz)} s`, { at: 'top-right', color: left < 10 * world.hz ? '#ff8f6b' : '' });\n121\t  ui.hud('keys', 'WASD: run · Space: jump · Shift: dash · Esc: pause', { at: 'bottom', keys: true });\n122\t  ended = state !== 'playing';\n123\t  if (ended && !was && state === 'won' && seen) best = recordBest(store, (seen.steps - left) / world.hz);\n124\t  ui.hud('best', best === null ? null : `Best ${best.toFixed(1)} s`, { at: 'top-left' });\n125\t  const end = state === 'won' ? 'Every gem! Enter: play again' : 'Time! Enter: play again';\n126\t  ui.hud('end', ended ? end : null, { at: 'top' });\n127\t}\n128\t\n129\tengine = await createEngine({\n130\t  canvas: document.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('#view')!,\n131\t  scenes: [play.id],\n132\t  levels: { 'level:arena': { text: ARENA_TEXT, file: 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts' } },\n133\t  replays,\n134\t  search: `?${search}`,\n135\t  store,\n136\t  modal: () => paused !== null,\n137\t  onFrame: (frame) => {\n138\t    pauseMenu(frame.dt);\n139\t    showRound(frame);\n140\t  },\n141\t});\n142\t\n143\taddEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n144\t  const inspector = engine?.inspector;\n145\t  if (event.code === 'Enter' && ended && inspector) inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\n146\t});\n147\t-----\n148\t<!doctype html>\n149\t<html lang=\"en\">\n150\t  <head>\n151\t    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n152\t    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\" />\n153\t    <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#15171c\" />\n154\t    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../../engine/ui/touch.css\" />\n155\t    <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\" />\n156\t    <title>The starter game: my-3dge</title>\n157\t    <!--\n158\t      The starter game's page (labs/game/README.md): labs/game/main.ts starts the engine on the scene game:play and\n159\t      shows the round in the HUD. Ready or error: until the engine publishes window.__engine, the inline script below\n160\t      records a script that fails to load or throws, and shows it in #msg, so a broken page is one line of text,\n161\t      never a blank one; `node x shot labs/game` reports the same headless.\n162\t    -->\n163\t    <style>\n164\t      html,\n165\t      body {\n166\t        margin: 0;\n167\t        height: 100%;\n168\t        overflow: hidden;\n169\t        background: #15171c;\n170\t      }\n171\t      canvas {\n172\t        display: block;\n173\t        width: 100vw;\n174\t        height: 100vh;\n175\t        height: 100dvh;\n176\t        outline: none;\n177\t        touch-action: none;\n178\t      }\n179\t      #msg {\n180\t        position: fixed;\n181\t        inset: 0;\n182\t        display: flex;\n183\t        align-items: center;\n184\t        justify-content: center;\n185\t        padding: 24px;\n186\t        font:\n187\t          18px system-ui,\n188\t          sans-serif;\n189\t        color: #c9ccd4;\n190\t        text-align: center;\n191\t        white-space: pre-line;\n192\t        pointer-events: none;\n193\t      }\n194\t      #msg[hidden] {\n195\t        display: none;\n196\t      }\n197\t    </style>\n198\t    <script>\n199\t      window.__engine = { ready: false, errors: [] };\n200\t      function gameFailed(message) {\n201\t        if (!window.__engine || typeof window.__engine.help === 'function') return; // the engine reports now\n202\t        var fix = 'the console names the cause; node x shot labs/game reports it headless';\n203\t        var record = { code: 'APP_START', message: 'the page failed to start: ' + message, fix: fix };\n204\t        if (window.__engine.errors.length === 0) {\n205\t          var msg = document.getElementById('msg');\n206\t          if (msg) msg.textContent = record.code + ': ' + record.message + '\\nFix: ' + fix;\n207\t        }\n208\t        window.__engine.errors.push(record);\n209\t      }\n210\t      addEventListener('error', function (event) {\n211\t        gameFailed(event.message || 'a script failed');\n212\t      });\n213\t      addEventListener('unhandledrejection', function (event) {\n214\t        gameFailed(String((event.reason && event.reason.message) || event.reason));\n215\t      });\n216\t    </script>\n217\t  </head>\n218\t  <body>\n219\t    <canvas id=\"view\"></canvas>\n220\t    <div id=\"msg\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Loading…</div>\n221\t    <script type=\"module\" src=\"./main.ts\" onerror=\"gameFailed('labs/game/main.ts did not load')\"></script>\n222\t  </body>\n223\t</html>\n224\t----\n225\t/**\n226\t * @file The starter game's player: the character the keys move (the character controller's numbers: how it runs,\n227\t * jumps and dashes) and the body it is drawn as, and `spawnPlayer`, which stands it in a scene. A game keeps its\n228\t * cast here, one character a file, as the box keeps its hero, walkers, slimes and wisps (labs/box/cast/); its scenes\n229\t * spawn them. `node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --feel` measures how the player handles: response, top speed, the\n230\t * jump's height and air time, the dash's reach.\n231\t *\n232\t * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts.\n233\t *\n234\t * @example\n235\t * playerCharacter(6).speed; // 6: m/s\n236\t * playerCharacter(6).jumpSpeed; // 9: m/s at take-off, about 1.27 m up, over the arena's 0.75 m low walls\n237\t * @see labs/game/scenes/play.ts\n238\t */\n239\timport { createCharacter, spawnActor, type Character, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\n240\t\n241\t/** The player's take-off speed, m/s: about 1.27 m up under the controller's gravity, over a 0.75 m low wall. */\n242\texport const JUMP_SPEED = 9;\n243\t\n244\t/** The body the player is drawn as: the humanoid in the chibi build, empty-handed. */\n245\texport const PLAYER_BODY = Object.freeze({ build: 'build:chibi', weapon: 'none' });\n246\t\n247\t/** The player's character at `speed` m/s; createCharacter's defaults for the rest (its dash among them). */\n248\texport function playerCharacter(speed: number): Character {\n249\t  return createCharacter({ speed, jumpSpeed: JUMP_SPEED });\n250\t}\n251\t\n252\t/** Stands the player in `w` (a scene with physics) at `at`, facing `yaw`: an actor the step's intents move. */\n253\texport function spawnPlayer<C extends object>(\n254\t  w: World<C>,\n255\t  at: readonly [number, number, number],\n256\t  speed: number,\n257\t  yaw = 0,\n258\t): number {\n259\t  const character = playerCharacter(speed);\n260\t  return spawnActor(w, { at: [at[0], at[1], at[2]], character, player: true, yaw, anim: { ...PLAYER_BODY } });\n261\t}\n262\t----\n263\t/**\n264\t * @file The starter game's scene `game:play`: every new game begins as this one (tools/game/new-game.mjs copies\n265\t * labs/game/ into it), so it is small, plays, and shows the parts a game is made of. The player, a humanoid on the\n266\t * character controller, runs round the arena (`ARENA_TEXT` below: walls, two pillars, two low walls to jump) collecting\n267\t * the gems the seed scatters, before the clock runs out. All the gems: won; the clock at 0: lost.\n268\t *\n269\t * The parts: a level as text, compiled for its physics bodies; settings (`game.*`, read when the scene starts, so they\n270\t * change play and go in replays); components (`gem`, drawn as a small glowing box because it declares `x` and `z` in\n271\t * metres; `round`, the score and the clock); the player (labs/game/cast/player.ts, an actor that reads the step's\n272\t * intents: `move`, `jump`, `dash`); systems in the phase `rules`, after the actors' feet are read back; a named random\n273\t * stream (`gems`); events (`gem`, `won`, `lost`) that pages, sounds and tests hear. The page is labs/game/main.ts, the\n274\t * bot labs/game/bot.ts.\n275\t *\n276\t * The level's text lives here, not in a .txt file, since sim-side code reads no files; the page registers the same\n277\t * text for the view (labs/game/main.ts).\n278\t *\n279\t * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts, so `node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts` runs it in Node.\n280\t *\n281\t * @example\n282\t * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --steps 600\n283\t * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --set game.gems=3 --seed 7\n284\t * ARENA.spawns.find((spawn) => spawn.name === 'hero')?.position; // [3.5, 0, 2.5]\n285\t * @see labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\n286\t */\n287\timport {\n288\t  addLevelBodies,\n289\t  compileLevel,\n290\t  defineComponent,\n291\t  defineScene,\n292\t  defineSettings,\n293\t  physicsOf,\n294\t  type ActorComponent,\n295\t  type World,\n296\t} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\n297\timport { spawnPlayer } from '../cast/player';\n298\t\n299\t/** The arena: 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls (0.75 m) to jump, the spawn `@`. */\n300\texport const ARENA_TEXT = `---\n301\tdescription: The starter game's arena. 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls 0.75 m high that the player jumps, and the player's spawn.\n302\t---\n303\t##################\n304\t#................#\n305\t#..@.............#\n306\t#.......PP.......#\n307\t#.......PP.......#\n308\t#................#\n309\t#....w......w....#\n310\t#....w......w....#\n311\t#................#\n312\t#.......PP.......#\n313\t#.......PP.......#\n314\t#................#\n315\t#................#\n316\t##################\n317\t`;\n318\t\n319\t/** The arena, compiled: its colliders for physics, its tiles for the gems and the bot's paths. */\n320\texport const ARENA = compileLevel(ARENA_TEXT, { file: 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts', name: 'arena' });\n321\t\n322\t/** The game's settings: each is reachable through `x set`, URL parameters (`?game.gems=3`) and `__engine.set`. */\n323\texport const GAME_SETTINGS = defineSettings({\n324\t  'game.gems': {\n325\t    type: 'integer',\n326\t    default: 10,\n327\t    minimum: 1,\n328\t    maximum: 40,\n329\t    when: 'scene',\n330\t    description: 'How many gems the seed scatters.',\n331\t  },\n332\t  'game.seconds': {\n333\t    type: 'number',\n334\t    default: 30,\n335\t    minimum: 5,\n336\t    maximum: 600,\n337\t    unit: 's',\n338\t    when: 'scene',\n339\t    description: 'How long the player has to collect them all.',\n340\t  },\n341\t  'game.speed': {\n342\t    type: 'number',\n343\t    default: 6,\n344\t    minimum: 1,\n345\t    maximum: 20,\n346\t    unit: 'm/s',\n347\t    when: 'scene',\n348\t    description: 'How fast the player runs.',\n349\t  },\n350\t});\n351\t\n352\t/** A gem: where it floats and how it looks (the page draws a component that declares x and z in metres). */\n353\texport const GEM = defineComponent('gem', {\n354\t  description: 'A gem to collect: where it floats, its spin and how it is drawn.',\n355\t  fields: {\n356\t    x: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'm', description: 'East.' },\n357\t    y: { type: 'number', default: 0.5, unit: 'm', description: 'Up: the bottom of its box.' },\n358\t    z: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'm', description: 'South.' },\n359\t    yaw: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'rad', description: 'Its spin.' },\n360\t    size: { type: 'number', default: 0.4, unit: 'm', description: 'The side of its box.' },\n361\t    material: { type: 'string', default: 'material:glow', description: 'What it is drawn with.' },\n362\t  },\n363\t});\n364\t\n365\t/** The round: the score, the clock and how it ended. One entity holds it. */\n366\texport const ROUND = defineComponent('round', {\n367\t  description:\n368\t    'The round: gems collected of the total, the steps left on the clock, and whether it is playing, won or lost.',\n369\t  fields: {\n370\t    gems: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many gems the round scattered.' },\n371\t    collected: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many the player has collected.' },\n372\t    left: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'The sim steps left on the clock (60 a second).' },\n373\t    state: { type: 'string', default: 'playing', description: \"'playing', 'won' or 'lost'.\" },\n374\t  },\n375\t});\n376\t\n377\t/** The round, as the component holds it. */\n378\texport type Round = { gems: number; collected: number; left: number; state: 'playing' | 'won' | 'lost' };\n379\t\n380\t/** The scene's components, typed. */\n381\texport type GameComponents = {\n382\t  gem: { x: number; y: number; z: number; yaw: number; size: number; material: string };\n383\t  round: Round;\n384\t  actor: ActorComponent;\n385\t};\n386\t\n387\t/** How close the player's feet come to a gem to collect it, m (on the ground plane). */\n388\texport const REACH = 0.8;\n389\t\n390\t/** How far from the spawn the gems keep, m, so the first one is never collected without moving. */\n391\tconst CLEAR = 3;\n392\t\n393\t/** Where the player starts: the level's spawn `@`. */\n394\tconst START = ARENA.spawns.find((spawn) => spawn.name === 'hero')!.position;\n395\t\n396\t/** The floor tiles a gem may float over: open floor (`.`), at least `CLEAR` metres from the spawn, in reading order. */\n397\tfunction gemTiles(): number[] {\n398\t  const tiles: number[] = [];\n399\t  ARENA.tiles.forEach((char, i) => {\n400\t    const x = ((i % ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n401\t    const z = (Math.floor(i / ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n402\t    if (char === '.' && Math.hypot(x - START[0], z - START[2]) >= CLEAR) tiles.push(i);\n403\t  });\n404\t  return tiles;\n405\t}\n406\t\n407\t/** Scatters `count` gems over distinct floor tiles drawn from the stream `gems`: each seed lays them its own way. */\n408\tfunction scatterGems(w: World<GameComponents>, count: number): void {\n409\t  const tiles = gemTiles();\n410\t  const rng = w.rng('gems');\n411\t  for (let k = 0; k < count && tiles.length > 0; k++) {\n412\t    const [tile] = tiles.splice(rng.int(0, tiles.length - 1), 1);\n413\t    const x = ((tile % ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n414\t    const z = (Math.floor(tile / ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n415\t    w.spawn({ gem: { x, z, yaw: rng.range(0, Math.PI) } });\n416\t  }\n417\t}\n418\t\n419\t/** Ends the round: the player stops reading intents (and so stands still), and the event says how it ended. */\n420\tfunction endRound(w: World<GameComponents>, round: Round, state: 'won' | 'lost'): void {\n421\t  round.state = state;\n422\t  for (const e of w.query('actor')) {\n423\t    e.actor.player = false;\n424\t    e.actor.intents = {};\n425\t  }\n426\t  w.emit(state, { collected: round.collected, gems: round.gems, left: round.left });\n427\t}\n428\t\n429\t/**\n430\t * Spins the gems, collects those an actor's feet reach, and ends the round when the last one goes. A despawn waits for\n431\t * the end of the step, so a gem taken this step is remembered: two actors never count it twice.\n432\t */\n433\tfunction collect(w: World<GameComponents>): void {\n434\t  const [{ round }] = w.query('round');\n435\t  for (const gem of w.query('gem')) gem.gem.yaw += 2 * w.dt;\n436\t  if (round.state !== 'playing') return;\n437\t  const taken = new Set<number>();\n438\t  for (const { actor } of w.query('actor')) {\n439\t    for (const gem of w.query('gem')) {\n440\t      if (taken.has(gem.id) || Math.hypot(gem.gem.x - actor.x, gem.gem.z - actor.z) > REACH) continue;\n441\t      taken.add(gem.id);\n442\t      w.despawn(gem.id);\n443\t      round.collected += 1;\n444\t      w.emit('gem', { id: gem.id, x: gem.gem.x, z: gem.gem.z, collected: round.collected });\n445\t    }\n446\t  }\n447\t  if (round.collected >= round.gems) endRound(w, round, 'won');\n448\t}\n449\t\n450\t/** Runs the clock down a step at a time (game time is whole steps, never summed seconds); at 0 the round is lost. */\n451\tfunction clock(w: World<GameComponents>): void {\n452\t  const [{ round }] = w.query('round');\n453\t  if (round.state !== 'playing') return;\n454\t  round.left = Math.max(0, round.left - 1);\n455\t  if (round.left === 0) endRound(w, round, 'lost');\n456\t}\n457\t\n458\t/** The starter game: collect every gem before the clock runs out. */\n459\texport const play = defineScene<GameComponents>('game:play', {\n460\t  description: 'The starter game: run round the arena collecting the gems before the clock runs out.',\n461\t  level: 'level:arena',\n462\t  physics: true,\n463\t  setup(w) {\n464\t    addLevelBodies(physicsOf(w), ARENA);\n465\t    const gems = w.settings.get<number>('game.gems');\n466\t    w.spawn({ round: { gems, left: Math.round(w.settings.get<number>('game.seconds') * w.hz) } });\n467\t    scatterGems(w, gems);\n468\t    spawnPlayer(w, [START[0], START[1], START[2]], w.settings.get<number>('game.speed'));\n469\t    w.systems.add('game.collect', collect, { phase: 'rules' });\n470\t    w.systems.add('game.clock', clock, { phase: 'rules' });\n471\t  },\n472\t});\n473\t\n474\texport default play;\n475\t----\n476\t/**\n477\t * @file The starter game's bot: game code that plays `game:play` (labs/game/scenes/play.ts) through intents, the way\n478\t * a player's keys do, so a test or an agent plays the game with nobody at the keys. Each step it reads what a player\n479\t * would see (`viewOf`: the player's feet and the gems left) and answers with the step's intents (`botIntents`: run\n480\t * down the arena's flow field to the nearest gem, round the pillars and the low walls).\n481\t *\n482\t * The bot never reaches into the sim: it reads the engine's inspector (`state`) and writes intents through `step`, so\n483\t * what it plays is recorded like a person's play, and `input.record()` turns it into a replay\n484\t * (labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json). A game keeps its bot as the game grows: the tests ask it to win\n485\t * (labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts), which proves the game can be won, on every seed they try.\n486\t *\n487\t * Game code, page-side: it imports only engine/index.ts and the game's own modules.\n488\t *\n489\t * @example\n490\t * // import { createHeadless } from '../../engine';\n491\t * // const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play, seed: 3 });\n492\t * // const end = playBot(engine); // { state: 'won', steps: 1234 }\n493\t * botIntents({ player: { x: 3.5, z: 2.5 }, gems: [{ x: 3.5, z: 9.5 }] }).move; // [0, 1]: south, toward the gem\n494\t * @see labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\n495\t */\n496\timport { NavGrid, type Headless, type Intents } from '../../engine';\n497\timport { ARENA, type Round } from './scenes/play';\n498\t\n499\t/** A point on the ground, m: x east, z south. */\n500\texport interface GroundSpot {\n501\t  x: number;\n502\t  z: number;\n503\t}\n504\t\n505\t/** What the bot sees each step: the player's feet and the gems left. */\n506\texport interface BotView {\n507\t  player: GroundSpot;\n508\t  gems: readonly GroundSpot[];\n509\t}\n510\t\n511\t/** The arena's walkable grid: the flow fields the bot follows go round its pillars and low walls. */\n512\tconst GRID = new NavGrid(ARENA);\n513\t\n514\t/** How many headings the bot steers by: few, so its intents change seldom and its replays stay short. */\n515\texport const HEADINGS = 16;\n516\t\n517\t/** The intents for one step: run toward the nearest gem by walking distance; none when no gem is left. */\n518\texport function botIntents(view: BotView): Intents {\n519\t  if (view.gems.length === 0) return {};\n520\t  const goals = [...new Set(view.gems.map((gem) => GRID.nearestOpen(gem.x, gem.z)))].filter((tile) => tile >= 0);\n521\t  const way = goals.length > 0 ? GRID.flowField(goals).direction(view.player.x, view.player.z) : null;\n522\t  if (way) return { move: heading(way.x, way.z) };\n523\t  // On a gem's tile (or nowhere the field leads): straight at the nearest gem.\n524\t  const near = [...view.gems].sort((a, b) => distance(view.player, a) - distance(view.player, b))[0];\n525\t  const d = distance(view.player, near);\n526\t  return d < 1e-6 ? {} : { move: heading(near.x - view.player.x, near.z - view.player.z) };\n527\t}\n528\t\n529\t/** The nearest of the `HEADINGS` directions to (x, z), as `move` takes it: two decimals cut toward 0, never past 1. */\n530\tfunction heading(x: number, z: number): [number, number] {\n531\t  const step = (2 * Math.PI) / HEADINGS;\n532\t  const angle = Math.round(Math.atan2(x, z) / step) * step;\n533\t  return [Math.trunc(Math.sin(angle) * 100) / 100 || 0, Math.trunc(Math.cos(angle) * 100) / 100 || 0];\n534\t}\n535\t\n536\t/** The distance between two spots on the ground, m. */\n537\tfunction distance(a: GroundSpot, b: GroundSpot): number {\n538\t  return Math.hypot(b.x - a.x, b.z - a.z);\n539\t}\n540\t\n541\t/** What the bot sees in a running engine: the player's feet and the gems left, read through the inspector. */\n542\texport function viewOf(engine: Headless): BotView {\n543\t  const [player] = engine.state('actor').entities as unknown as { actor: GroundSpot }[];\n544\t  const gems = (engine.state('gem').entities as unknown as { gem: GroundSpot }[]).map(({ gem }) => ({\n545\t    x: gem.x,\n546\t    z: gem.z,\n547\t  }));\n548\t  return { player: { x: player.actor.x, z: player.actor.z }, gems };\n549\t}\n550\t\n551\t/** The round as it stands, read through the inspector. */\n552\texport function roundOf(engine: Headless): Round {\n553\t  const [entity] = engine.state('round').entities as unknown as { round: Round }[];\n554\t  return entity.round;\n555\t}\n556\t\n557\t/** Plays the bot until the round ends or `limit` steps pass; returns how the round stands and the steps it took. */\n558\texport function playBot(engine: Headless, limit = 60 * 600): { state: Round['state']; steps: number } {\n559\t  let steps = 0;\n560\t  while (roundOf(engine).state === 'playing' && steps < limit) {\n561\t    engine.step(1, botIntents(viewOf(engine)));\n562\t    steps += 1;\n563\t  }\n564\t  return { state: roundOf(engine).state, steps };\n565\t}\n566\t---\n567\t/**\n568\t * @file The starter game's tests (labs/game/scenes/play.ts): what every game made from it starts with, and keeps as it\n569\t * grows. They run headless in Node (`npm test`), in a few seconds:\n570\t * - its golden replay (labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json, the bot's play) gives its golden hashes, as `x replay`\n571\t *   checks it: on another platform than the one that recorded them, two runs agree instead;\n572\t * - a run continues exactly after a capture and a restore;\n573\t * - the bot (labs/game/bot.ts) wins on 10 seeds, so the game can be won, however the gems fall;\n574\t * - the clock runs out on a player who stands still, and the settings change play;\n575\t * - two actors that reach a gem in the same step take it once.\n576\t *\n577\t * When the game's play changes on purpose, record the goldens again: `node x replay labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json\n578\t * --browser sim --update` (in Node and Chromium), and say why in the commit.\n579\t * @see labs/game/scenes/play.ts\n580\t */\n581\timport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n582\timport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\n583\timport { createHeadless } from '../../../engine';\n584\timport { defineScene, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\n585\timport { botIntents, playBot, roundOf, viewOf } from '../bot';\n586\timport { spawnPlayer } from '../cast/player';\n587\timport { play, type GameComponents } from './play';\n588\t\n589\t/** The golden replay: the bot's play from seed 1, with the goldens `x replay --update` recorded. */\n590\tconst REPLAY = readFileSync(new URL('../replays/bot.replay.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\n591\t\n592\t/** This platform's golden key, as replays write it. */\n593\tconst PLATFORM = `${process.platform}-${process.arch}`;\n594\t\n595\t/** Plays `text` from step 0 in a fresh engine and returns its hashes at the replay's checkpoints. */\n596\tasync function replayed(text: string): Promise<Record<string, string>> {\n597\t  const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play });\n598\t  const result = await (engine.replay as (text: string) => Promise<{ hashes: Record<string, string> }>)(text);\n599\t  return result.hashes;\n600\t}\n601\t\n602\tdescribe('game:play', () => {\n603\t  it('replays the bot’s play to its golden hashes', async () => {\n604\t    const goldens = (JSON.parse(REPLAY) as { hashes: Record<string, Record<string, string>> }).hashes;\n605\t    const first = await replayed(REPLAY);\n606\t    if (goldens[PLATFORM]) expect(first).toEqual(goldens[PLATFORM]);\n607\t    else expect(await replayed(REPLAY)).toEqual(first); // recorded elsewhere: the runs agree, as x replay judges it\n608\t  });\n609\t\n610\t  it('continues exactly after a capture and a restore', async () => {\n611\t    const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play, seed: 4 });\n612\t    for (let k = 0; k < 120; k++) engine.step(1, botIntents(viewOf(engine)));\n613\t    const capture = engine.capture();\n614\t    for (let k = 0; k < 120; k++) engine.step(1, botIntents(viewOf(engine)));\n615\t    const straight = engine.hash();\n616\t    engine.restore(capture);\n617\t    for (let k = 0; k < 120; k++) engine.step(1, botIntents(viewOf(engine)));\n618\t    expect(engine.hash()).toBe(straight);\n619\t  });\n620\t\n621\t  it('is won by the bot on 10 seeds', async () => {\n622\t    for (let seed = 1; seed <= 10; seed++) {\n623\t      const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play, seed });\n624\t      expect({ seed, ...playBot(engine) }).toMatchObject({ seed, state: 'won' });\n625\t      expect(roundOf(engine).collected).toBe(roundOf(engine).gems);\n626\t    }\n627\t  });\n628\t\n629\t  it('is lost when the clock runs out, and its settings change play', async () => {\n630\t    const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play, settings: { 'game.seconds': 5, 'game.gems': 3 } });\n631\t    engine.step(5 * 60);\n632\t    expect(roundOf(engine)).toMatchObject({ gems: 3, collected: 0, left: 0, state: 'lost' });\n633\t    expect(viewOf(engine).gems).toHaveLength(3);\n634\t  });\n635\t\n636\t  it('counts a gem once when two actors reach it in the same step', async () => {\n637\t    const twin = defineScene<GameComponents>('game:twin', {\n638\t      description: 'The starter, and two more players put on its gem in the first step: both reach it in the next.',\n639\t      level: 'level:arena',\n640\t      physics: true,\n641\t      setup(w) {\n642\t        play.setup(w);\n643\t        const twins = (world: World<GameComponents>) => {\n644\t          if ([...world.query('actor')].length > 1) return;\n645\t          const [{ gem }] = world.query('gem');\n646\t          for (const dx of [-0.3, 0.3]) spawnPlayer(world, [gem.x + dx, 0, gem.z], 6);\n647\t        };\n648\t        w.systems.add('test.twins', twins, { phase: 'rules' });\n649\t      },\n650\t    });\n651\t    const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: twin, settings: { 'game.gems': 1 } }); // no neighbour within reach\n652\t    engine.step(2);\n653\t    expect([roundOf(engine).collected, roundOf(engine).state, engine.state('gem').entities.length]).toEqual([1, 'won', 0]); // prettier-ignore\n654\t  });\n655\t});\n656\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"9c8e9dec-ed78-46f3-bfb0-a7e0ed45e09f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:57.289Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-max-plan-v2--20261104-212002--x601dca-work/ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e/tool-results/bf5rgms82.txt","content":"# The starter game\n\nEvery game made with my-3dge starts as this one (`node tools/game/new-game.mjs`), then becomes its own: rewrite this\npage as the game grows. It is the game's page for the owner and the next agent: what the game is, how it plays, how to\nsee it, and the calls made along the way.\n\n## The game\n\nRun round the arena collecting every gem before the clock runs out. WASD or the arrows run, Space jumps (over the low\nwalls), Shift dashes. All the gems: won. The clock at 0: lost. Enter starts a new round on the next seed.\n\n## Files\n\n| File                              | What it is                                                                    |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| labs/game/scenes/play.ts          | The rules, sim-side: the arena's text, the settings, the gems, the round, the systems |\n| labs/game/cast/player.ts          | The player: its character (run, jump, dash) and the body it is drawn as        |\n| labs/game/bot.ts                  | The bot: plays through intents, down the flow field to the nearest gem         |\n| labs/game/main.ts, index.html     | The page: the engine, the HUD, Enter to play again, the chase camera           |\n| labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts     | The tests: the golden replay, capture and restore, the bot wins on 10 seeds, the clock |\n| labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json | The bot's play from seed 1, with its golden hashes                             |\n\n## Settings\n\n`game.gems` (10), `game.seconds` (30) and `game.speed` (6 m/s), read when the round starts: `?game.gems=20` in the\npage, `--set game.gems=20` for `node x sim` and `node x shot`.\n\n## See it\n\n```sh\nnpm run dev                                         # http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (?replay=bot plays the bot's run)\nnpm test                                            # the tests\nnode x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --feel          # the rules in Node: hash, events, how the player handles\nnode x shot labs/game                               # the page on WebGPU, as numbers\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim       # the goldens, in Node and Chromium\n```\n\n## Decisions\n\n<!-- The calls made without the owner, newest first: the date, what was decided, why. -->\n-----\n/**\n * @file The starter game's page (labs/game/index.html): it starts the engine (`createEngine`, engine/app/engine.ts) on\n * the scene `game:play` (labs/game/scenes/play.ts) with the arena's text registered for the view, offers the bot's\n * replay to `?replay=bot`, and shows the round each drawn frame in the HTML/CSS overlay's HUD: the gems, the clock,\n * the controls, the best round kept across sessions (labs/game/best.ts, through the engine's store) and, when the\n * round ends, how it ended. Enter then starts a new round on the next seed. Escape (or the pad's Start) pauses the\n * round under a menu (`createMenu`: Resume, New round), which keeps its keys out of play while it is open\n * (`createEngine({ modal })`); the store keeps the best round and any keys rebound (`createEngine({ store })`). The\n * camera is the chase camera unless the URL names one (`?cam=iso`, `?cam3=orbit`).\n *\n * Everything else a page does (routes, the renderer, the frame loop, the devices, `window.__engine`, the error\n * overlay, the touch controls) is the engine's, so this file is the game's own presentation only. It reads the run\n * and never changes it: the HUD cannot change the hash.\n *\n * Game code: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts) and the game's own files.\n *\n * Open it at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (`npm run dev`): `?seed=7&game.gems=20` plays another round,\n * `?replay=bot` the bot's, `?cam=iso` another camera. Headless, `node x shot labs/game` reports what it draws.\n */\n/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />\nimport { createEngine, createMenu, createStore, type Engine, type EngineFrame, type Menu } from '../../engine';\nimport { bestOf, recordBest } from './best';\nimport { ARENA_TEXT, play, type Round } from './scenes/play';\n\n/** The page's query, with the chase camera when it names none: it follows the player round the arena. */\nconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\nif (!search.has('cam') && !search.has('cam3')) search.set('cam3', 'chase');\n\n/** The game's replays, by name (`?replay=bot`), as text loaded on demand. */\nconst replays = { bot: () => import('./replays/bot.replay.json?raw').then((module) => module.default) };\n\n/** The started engine; null until `createEngine` resolves (its first frames are drawn before that). */\nlet engine: Engine | null = null;\n\n/** Whether the round on screen has ended, so Enter starts the next. */\nlet ended = false;\n\n/** The game's store: its best round across sessions; a replay's page plays in its demo mode, so it sets none. */\nconst store = createStore({ prefix: 'my3dge-game:', mode: search.has('replay') ? 'demo' : 'play' });\n\n/** The fastest won round kept (s), and the run whose clock the page saw running, with the steps it started with. */\nlet best = bestOf(store);\nlet seen: { world: object; steps: number } | null = null;\n\n/** The pause menu while it is open; null while the round plays. */\nlet paused: Menu | null = null;\n\n/** Opens the pause menu over the paused round, or reads it a frame: Resume (or Escape again), New round. */\nfunction pauseMenu(dt: number): void {\n  const [inspector, ui, input] = [engine?.inspector, engine?.ui, engine?.input];\n  if (!inspector || !ui || !input) return;\n  const close = () => {\n    paused?.remove();\n    paused = null;\n    inspector.resume();\n  };\n  if (paused) return void paused.update(dt);\n  if (!input.pressed('pause')) return;\n  inspector.pause();\n  const items = [\n    { label: 'Resume', id: 'resume' },\n    { label: 'New round', id: 'new' },\n  ];\n  paused = createMenu(ui.root, items, { input, id: 'pause', title: 'Paused', onCancel: close, onPick: (_i, item) => {\n    if (typeof item === 'object' && item.id === 'new') inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\n    close();\n  } }); // prettier-ignore\n}\n\n/** Shows the round in the HUD: the gems, the clock, the controls, and how the round ended. */\nfunction showRound({ world }: EngineFrame): void {\n  const ui = engine?.ui;\n  const entity = world.query('round')[0] as unknown as { round: Round } | undefined;\n  if (!ui || !entity) return;\n  const { gems, collected, left, state } = entity.round;\n  if (seen?.world !== world) seen = state === 'playing' ? { world, steps: left + world.tick } : null;\n  const was = ended;\n  ui.hud('gems', `Gems ${collected} / ${gems}`, { at: 'top-left' });\n  ui.hud('clock', `${Math.ceil(left / world.hz)} s`, { at: 'top-right', color: left < 10 * world.hz ? '#ff8f6b' : '' });\n  ui.hud('keys', 'WASD: run · Space: jump · Shift: dash · Esc: pause', { at: 'bottom', keys: true });\n  ended = state !== 'playing';\n  if (ended && !was && state === 'won' && seen) best = recordBest(store, (seen.steps - left) / world.hz);\n  ui.hud('best', best === null ? null : `Best ${best.toFixed(1)} s`, { at: 'top-left' });\n  const end = state === 'won' ? 'Every gem! Enter: play again' : 'Time! Enter: play again';\n  ui.hud('end', ended ? end : null, { at: 'top' });\n}\n\nengine = await createEngine({\n  canvas: document.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('#view')!,\n  scenes: [play.id],\n  levels: { 'level:arena': { text: ARENA_TEXT, file: 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts' } },\n  replays,\n  search: `?${search}`,\n  store,\n  modal: () => paused !== null,\n  onFrame: (frame) => {\n    pauseMenu(frame.dt);\n    showRound(frame);\n  },\n});\n\naddEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n  const inspector = engine?.inspector;\n  if (event.code === 'Enter' && ended && inspector) inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\n});\n-----\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\" />\n    <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#15171c\" />\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../../engine/ui/touch.css\" />\n    <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\" />\n    <title>The starter game: my-3dge</title>\n    <!--\n      The starter game's page (labs/game/README.md): labs/game/main.ts starts the engine on the scene game:play and\n      shows the round in the HUD. Ready or error: until the engine publishes window.__engine, the inline script below\n      records a script that fails to load or throws, and shows it in #msg, so a broken page is one line of text,\n      never a blank one; `node x shot labs/game` reports the same headless.\n    -->\n    <style>\n      html,\n      body {\n        margin: 0;\n        height: 100%;\n        overflow: hidden;\n        background: #15171c;\n      }\n      canvas {\n        display: block;\n        width: 100vw;\n        height: 100vh;\n        height: 100dvh;\n        outline: none;\n        touch-action: none;\n      }\n      #msg {\n        position: fixed;\n        inset: 0;\n        display: flex;\n        align-items: center;\n        justify-content: center;\n        padding: 24px;\n        font:\n          18px system-ui,\n          sans-serif;\n        color: #c9ccd4;\n        text-align: center;\n        white-space: pre-line;\n        pointer-events: none;\n      }\n      #msg[hidden] {\n        display: none;\n      }\n    </style>\n    <script>\n      window.__engine = { ready: false, errors: [] };\n      function gameFailed(message) {\n        if (!window.__engine || typeof window.__engine.help === 'function') return; // the engine reports now\n        var fix = 'the console names the cause; node x shot labs/game reports it headless';\n        var record = { code: 'APP_START', message: 'the page failed to start: ' + message, fix: fix };\n        if (window.__engine.errors.length === 0) {\n          var msg = document.getElementById('msg');\n          if (msg) msg.textContent = record.code + ': ' + record.message + '\\nFix: ' + fix;\n        }\n        window.__engine.errors.push(record);\n      }\n      addEventListener('error', function (event) {\n        gameFailed(event.message || 'a script failed');\n      });\n      addEventListener('unhandledrejection', function (event) {\n        gameFailed(String((event.reason && event.reason.message) || event.reason));\n      });\n    </script>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <canvas id=\"view\"></canvas>\n    <div id=\"msg\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Loading…</div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"./main.ts\" onerror=\"gameFailed('labs/game/main.ts did not load')\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n----\n/**\n * @file The starter game's player: the character the keys move (the character controller's numbers: how it runs,\n * jumps and dashes) and the body it is drawn as, and `spawnPlayer`, which stands it in a scene. A game keeps its\n * cast here, one character a file, as the box keeps its hero, walkers, slimes and wisps (labs/box/cast/); its scenes\n * spawn them. `node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --feel` measures how the player handles: response, top speed, the\n * jump's height and air time, the dash's reach.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts.\n *\n * @example\n * playerCharacter(6).speed; // 6: m/s\n * playerCharacter(6).jumpSpeed; // 9: m/s at take-off, about 1.27 m up, over the arena's 0.75 m low walls\n * @see labs/game/scenes/play.ts\n */\nimport { createCharacter, spawnActor, type Character, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\n\n/** The player's take-off speed, m/s: about 1.27 m up under the controller's gravity, over a 0.75 m low wall. */\nexport const JUMP_SPEED = 9;\n\n/** The body the player is drawn as: the humanoid in the chibi build, empty-handed. */\nexport const PLAYER_BODY = Object.freeze({ build: 'build:chibi', weapon: 'none' });\n\n/** The player's character at `speed` m/s; createCharacter's defaults for the rest (its dash among them). */\nexport function playerCharacter(speed: number): Character {\n  return createCharacter({ speed, jumpSpeed: JUMP_SPEED });\n}\n\n/** Stands the player in `w` (a scene with physics) at `at`, facing `yaw`: an actor the step's intents move. */\nexport function spawnPlayer<C extends object>(\n  w: World<C>,\n  at: readonly [number, number, number],\n  speed: number,\n  yaw = 0,\n): number {\n  const character = playerCharacter(speed);\n  return spawnActor(w, { at: [at[0], at[1], at[2]], character, player: true, yaw, anim: { ...PLAYER_BODY } });\n}\n----\n/**\n * @file The starter game's scene `game:play`: every new game begins as this one (tools/game/new-game.mjs copies\n * labs/game/ into it), so it is small, plays, and shows the parts a game is made of. The player, a humanoid on the\n * character controller, runs round the arena (`ARENA_TEXT` below: walls, two pillars, two low walls to jump) collecting\n * the gems the seed scatters, before the clock runs out. All the gems: won; the clock at 0: lost.\n *\n * The parts: a level as text, compiled for its physics bodies; settings (`game.*`, read when the scene starts, so they\n * change play and go in replays); components (`gem`, drawn as a small glowing box because it declares `x` and `z` in\n * metres; `round`, the score and the clock); the player (labs/game/cast/player.ts, an actor that reads the step's\n * intents: `move`, `jump`, `dash`); systems in the phase `rules`, after the actors' feet are read back; a named random\n * stream (`gems`); events (`gem`, `won`, `lost`) that pages, sounds and tests hear. The page is labs/game/main.ts, the\n * bot labs/game/bot.ts.\n *\n * The level's text lives here, not in a .txt file, since sim-side code reads no files; the page registers the same\n * text for the view (labs/game/main.ts).\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts, so `node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts` runs it in Node.\n *\n * @example\n * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --steps 600\n * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --set game.gems=3 --seed 7\n * ARENA.spawns.find((spawn) => spawn.name === 'hero')?.position; // [3.5, 0, 2.5]\n * @see labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\n */\nimport {\n  addLevelBodies,\n  compileLevel,\n  defineComponent,\n  defineScene,\n  defineSettings,\n  physicsOf,\n  type ActorComponent,\n  type World,\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { spawnPlayer } from '../cast/player';\n\n/** The arena: 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls (0.75 m) to jump, the spawn `@`. */\nexport const ARENA_TEXT = `---\ndescription: The starter game's arena. 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls 0.75 m high that the player jumps, and the player's spawn.\n---\n##################\n#................#\n#..@.............#\n#.......PP.......#\n#.......PP.......#\n#................#\n#....w......w....#\n#....w......w....#\n#................#\n#.......PP.......#\n#.......PP.......#\n#................#\n#................#\n##################\n`;\n\n/** The arena, compiled: its colliders for physics, its tiles for the gems and the bot's paths. */\nexport const ARENA = compileLevel(ARENA_TEXT, { file: 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts', name: 'arena' });\n\n/** The game's settings: each is reachable through `x set`, URL parameters (`?game.gems=3`) and `__engine.set`. */\nexport const GAME_SETTINGS = defineSettings({\n  'game.gems': {\n    type: 'integer',\n    default: 10,\n    minimum: 1,\n    maximum: 40,\n    when: 'scene',\n    description: 'How many gems the seed scatters.',\n  },\n  'game.seconds': {\n    type: 'number',\n    default: 30,\n    minimum: 5,\n    maximum: 600,\n    unit: 's',\n    when: 'scene',\n    description: 'How long the player has to collect them all.',\n  },\n  'game.speed': {\n    type: 'number',\n    default: 6,\n    minimum: 1,\n    maximum: 20,\n    unit: 'm/s',\n    when: 'scene',\n    description: 'How fast the player runs.',\n  },\n});\n\n/** A gem: where it floats and how it looks (the page draws a component that declares x and z in metres). */\nexport const GEM = defineComponent('gem', {\n  description: 'A gem to collect: where it floats, its spin and how it is drawn.',\n  fields: {\n    x: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'm', description: 'East.' },\n    y: { type: 'number', default: 0.5, unit: 'm', description: 'Up: the bottom of its box.' },\n    z: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'm', description: 'South.' },\n    yaw: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'rad', description: 'Its spin.' },\n    size: { type: 'number', default: 0.4, unit: 'm', description: 'The side of its box.' },\n    material: { type: 'string', default: 'material:glow', description: 'What it is drawn with.' },\n  },\n});\n\n/** The round: the score, the clock and how it ended. One entity holds it. */\nexport const ROUND = defineComponent('round', {\n  description:\n    'The round: gems collected of the total, the steps left on the clock, and whether it is playing, won or lost.',\n  fields: {\n    gems: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many gems the round scattered.' },\n    collected: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many the player has collected.' },\n    left: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'The sim steps left on the clock (60 a second).' },\n    state: { type: 'string', default: 'playing', description: \"'playing', 'won' or 'lost'.\" },\n  },\n});\n\n/** The round, as the component holds it. */\nexport type Round = { gems: number; collected: number; left: number; state: 'playing' | 'won' | 'lost' };\n\n/** The scene's components, typed. */\nexport type GameComponents = {\n  gem: { x: number; y: number; z: number; yaw: number; size: number; material: string };\n  round: Round;\n  actor: ActorComponent;\n};\n\n/** How close the player's feet come to a gem to collect it, m (on the ground plane). */\nexport const REACH = 0.8;\n\n/** How far from the spawn the gems keep, m, so the first one is never collected without moving. */\nconst CLEAR = 3;\n\n/** Where the player starts: the level's spawn `@`. */\nconst START = ARENA.spawns.find((spawn) => spawn.name === 'hero')!.position;\n\n/** The floor tiles a gem may float over: open floor (`.`), at least `CLEAR` metres from the spawn, in reading order. */\nfunction gemTiles(): number[] {\n  const tiles: number[] = [];\n  ARENA.tiles.forEach((char, i) => {\n    const x = ((i % ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    const z = (Math.floor(i / ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    if (char === '.' && Math.hypot(x - START[0], z - START[2]) >= CLEAR) tiles.push(i);\n  });\n  return tiles;\n}\n\n/** Scatters `count` gems over distinct floor tiles drawn from the stream `gems`: each seed lays them its own way. */\nfunction scatterGems(w: World<GameComponents>, count: number): void {\n  const tiles = gemTiles();\n  const rng = w.rng('gems');\n  for (let k = 0; k < count && tiles.length > 0; k++) {\n    const [tile] = tiles.splice(rng.int(0, tiles.length - 1), 1);\n    const x = ((tile % ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    const z = (Math.floor(tile / ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    w.spawn({ gem: { x, z, yaw: rng.range(0, Math.PI) } });\n  }\n}\n\n/** Ends the round: the player stops reading intents (and so stands still), and the event says how it ended. */\nfunction endRound(w: World<GameComponents>, round: Round, state: 'won' | 'lost'): void {\n  round.state = state;\n  for (const e of w.query('actor')) {\n    e.actor.player = false;\n    e.actor.intents = {};\n  }\n  w.emit(state, { collected: round.collected, gems: round.gems, left: round.left });\n}\n\n/**\n * Spins the gems, collects those an actor's feet reach, and ends the round when the last one goes. A despawn waits for\n * the end of the step, so a gem taken this step is remembered: two actors never count it twice.\n */\nfunction collect(w: World<GameComponents>): void {\n  const [{ round }] = w.query('round');\n  for (const gem of w.query('gem')) gem.gem.yaw += 2 * w.dt;\n  if (round.state !== 'playing') return;\n  const taken = new Set<number>();\n  for (const { actor } of w.query('actor')) {\n    for (const gem of w.query('gem')) {\n      if (taken.has(gem.id) || Math.hypot(gem.gem.x - actor.x, gem.gem.z - actor.z) > REACH) continue;\n      taken.add(gem.id);\n      w.despawn(gem.id);\n      round.collected += 1;\n      w.emit('gem', { id: gem.id, x: gem.gem.x, z: gem.gem.z, collected: round.collected });\n    }\n  }\n  if (round.collected >= round.gems) endRound(w, round, 'won');\n}\n\n/** Runs the clock down a step at a time (game time is whole steps, never summed seconds); at 0 the round is lost. */\nfunction clock(w: World<GameComponents>): void {\n  const [{ round }] = w.query('round');\n  if (round.state !== 'playing') return;\n  round.left = Math.max(0, round.left - 1);\n  if (round.left === 0) endRound(w, round, 'lost');\n}\n\n/** The starter game: collect every gem before the clock runs out. */\nexport const play = defineScene<GameComponents>('game:play', {\n  description: 'The starter game: run round the arena collecting the gems before the clock runs out.',\n  level: 'level:arena',\n  physics: true,\n  setup(w) {\n    addLevelBodies(physicsOf(w), ARENA);\n    const gems = w.settings.get<number>('game.gems');\n    w.spawn({ round: { gems, left: Math.round(w.settings.get<number>('game.seconds') * w.hz) } });\n    scatterGems(w, gems);\n    spawnPlayer(w, [START[0], START[1], START[2]], w.settings.get<number>('game.speed'));\n    w.systems.add('game.collect', collect, { phase: 'rules' });\n    w.systems.add('game.clock', clock, { phase: 'rules' });\n  },\n});\n\nexport default play;\n----\n/**\n * @file The starter game's bot: game code that plays `game:play` (labs/game/scenes/play.ts) through intents, the way\n * a player's keys do, so a test or an agent plays the game with nobody at the keys. Each step it reads what a player\n * would see (`viewOf`: the player's feet and the gems left) and answers with the step's intents (`botIntents`: run\n * down the arena's flow field to the nearest gem, round the pillars and the low walls).\n *\n * The bot never reaches into the sim: it reads the engine's inspector (`state`) and writes intents through `step`, so\n * what it plays is recorded like a person's play, and `input.record()` turns it into a replay\n * (labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json). A game keeps its bot as the game grows: the tests ask it to win\n * (labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts), which proves the game can be won, on every seed they try.\n *\n * Game code, page-side: it imports only engine/index.ts and the game's own modules.\n *\n * @example\n * // import { createHeadless } from '../../engine';\n * // const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play, seed: 3 });\n * // const end = playBot(engine); // { state: 'won', steps: 1234 }\n * botIntents({ player: { x: 3.5, z: 2.5 }, gems: [{ x: 3.5, z: 9.5 }] }).move; // [0, 1]: south, toward the gem\n * @see labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\n */\nimport { NavGrid, type Headless, type Intents } from '../../engine';\nimport { ARENA, type Round } from './scenes/play';\n\n/** A point on the ground, m: x east, z south. */\nexport interface GroundSpot {\n  x: number;\n  z: number;\n}\n\n/** What the bot sees each step: the player's feet and the gems left. */\nexport interface BotView {\n  player: GroundSpot;\n  gems: readonly GroundSpot[];\n}\n\n/** The arena's walkable grid: the flow fields the bot follows go round its pillars and low walls. */\nconst GRID = new NavGrid(ARENA);\n\n/** How many headings the bot steers by: few, so its intents change seldom and its replays stay short. */\nexport const HEADINGS = 16;\n\n/** The intents for one step: run toward the nearest gem by walking distance; none when no gem is left. */\nexport function botIntents(view: BotView): Intents {\n  if (view.gems.length === 0) return {};\n  const goals = [...new Set(view.gems.map((gem) => GRID.nearestOpen(gem.x, gem.z)))].filter((tile) => tile >= 0);\n  const way = goals.length > 0 ? GRID.flowField(goals).direction(view.player.x, view.player.z) : null;\n  if (way) return { move: heading(way.x, way.z) };\n  // On a gem's tile (or nowhere the field leads): straight at the nearest gem.\n  const near = [...view.gems].sort((a, b) => distance(view.player, a) - distance(view.player, b))[0];\n  const d = distance(view.player, near);\n  return d < 1e-6 ? {} : { move: heading(near.x - view.player.x, near.z - view.player.z) };\n}\n\n/** The nearest of the `HEADINGS` directions to (x, z), as `move` takes it: two decimals cut toward 0, never past 1. */\nfunction heading(x: number, z: number): [number, number] {\n  const step = (2 * Math.PI) / HEADINGS;\n  const angle = Math.round(Math.atan2(x, z) / step) * step;\n  return [Math.trunc(Math.sin(angle) * 100) / 100 || 0, Math.trunc(Math.cos(angle) * 100) / 100 || 0];\n}\n\n/** The distance between two spots on the ground, m. */\nfunction distance(a: GroundSpot, b: GroundSpot): number {\n  return Math.hypot(b.x - a.x, b.z - a.z);\n}\n\n/** What the bot sees in a running engine: the player's feet and the gems left, read through the inspector. */\nexport function viewOf(engine: Headless): BotView {\n  const [player] = engine.state('actor').entities as unknown as { actor: GroundSpot }[];\n  const gems = (engine.state('gem').entities as unknown as { gem: GroundSpot }[]).map(({ gem }) => ({\n    x: gem.x,\n    z: gem.z,\n  }));\n  return { player: { x: player.actor.x, z: player.actor.z }, gems };\n}\n\n/** The round as it stands, read through the inspector. */\nexport function roundOf(engine: Headless): Round {\n  const [entity] = engine.state('round').entities as unknown as { round: Round }[];\n  return entity.round;\n}\n\n/** Plays the bot until the round ends or `limit` steps pass; returns how the round stands and the steps it took. */\nexport function playBot(engine: Headless, limit = 60 * 600): { state: Round['state']; steps: number } {\n  let steps = 0;\n  while (roundOf(engine).state === 'playing' && steps < limit) {\n    engine.step(1, botIntents(viewOf(engine)));\n    steps += 1;\n  }\n  return { state: roundOf(engine).state, steps };\n}\n---\n/**\n * @file The starter game's tests (labs/game/scenes/play.ts): what every game made from it starts with, and keeps as it\n * grows. They run headless in Node (`npm test`), in a few seconds:\n * - its golden replay (labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json, the bot's play) gives its golden hashes, as `x replay`\n *   checks it: on another platform than the one that recorded them, two runs agree instead;\n * - a run continues exactly after a capture and a restore;\n * - the bot (labs/game/bot.ts) wins on 10 seeds, so the game can be won, however the gems fall;\n * - the clock runs out on a player who stands still, and the settings change play;\n * - two actors that reach a gem in the same step take it once.\n *\n * When the game's play changes on purpose, record the goldens again: `node x replay labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json\n * --browser sim --update` (in Node and Chromium), and say why in the commit.\n * @see labs/game/scenes/play.ts\n */\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport { createHeadless } from '../../../engine';\nimport { defineScene, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { botIntents, playBot, roundOf, viewOf } from '../bot';\nimport { spawnPlayer } from '../cast/player';\nimport { play, type GameComponents } from './play';\n\n/** The golden replay: the bot's play from seed 1, with the goldens `x replay --update` recorded. */\nconst REPLAY = readFileSync(new URL('../replays/bot.replay.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\n\n/** This platform's golden key, as replays write it. */\nconst PLATFORM = `${process.platform}-${process.arch}`;\n\n/** Plays `text` from step 0 in a fresh engine and returns its hashes at the replay's checkpoints. */\nasync function replayed(text: string): Promise<Record<string, string>> {\n  const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play });\n  const result = await (engine.replay as (text: string) => Promise<{ hashes: Record<string, string> }>)(text);\n  return result.hashes;\n}\n\ndescribe('game:play', () => {\n  it('replays the bot’s play to its golden hashes', async () => {\n    const goldens = (JSON.parse(REPLAY) as { hashes: Record<string, Record<string, string>> }).hashes;\n    const first = await replayed(REPLAY);\n    if (goldens[PLATFORM]) expect(first).toEqual(goldens[PLATFORM]);\n    else expect(await replayed(REPLAY)).toEqual(first); // recorded elsewhere: the runs agree, as x replay judges it\n  });\n\n  it('continues exactly after a capture and a restore', async () => {\n    const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play, seed: 4 });\n    for (let k = 0; k < 120; k++) engine.step(1, botIntents(viewOf(engine)));\n    const capture = engine.capture();\n    for (let k = 0; k < 120; k++) engine.step(1, botIntents(viewOf(engine)));\n    const straight = engine.hash();\n    engine.restore(capture);\n    for (let k = 0; k < 120; k++) engine.step(1, botIntents(viewOf(engine)));\n    expect(engine.hash()).toBe(straight);\n  });\n\n  it('is won by the bot on 10 seeds', async () => {\n    for (let seed = 1; seed <= 10; seed++) {\n      const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play, seed });\n      expect({ seed, ...playBot(engine) }).toMatchObject({ seed, state: 'won' });\n      expect(roundOf(engine).collected).toBe(roundOf(engine).gems);\n    }\n  });\n\n  it('is lost when the clock runs out, and its settings change play', async () => {\n    const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play, settings: { 'game.seconds': 5, 'game.gems': 3 } });\n    engine.step(5 * 60);\n    expect(roundOf(engine)).toMatchObject({ gems: 3, collected: 0, left: 0, state: 'lost' });\n    expect(viewOf(engine).gems).toHaveLength(3);\n  });\n\n  it('counts a gem once when two actors reach it in the same step', async () => {\n    const twin = defineScene<GameComponents>('game:twin', {\n      description: 'The starter, and two more players put on its gem in the first step: both reach it in the next.',\n      level: 'level:arena',\n      physics: true,\n      setup(w) {\n        play.setup(w);\n        const twins = (world: World<GameComponents>) => {\n          if ([...world.query('actor')].length > 1) return;\n          const [{ gem }] = world.query('gem');\n          for (const dx of [-0.3, 0.3]) spawnPlayer(world, [gem.x + dx, 0, gem.z], 6);\n        };\n        w.systems.add('test.twins', twins, { phase: 'rules' });\n      },\n    });\n    const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: twin, settings: { 'game.gems': 1 } }); // no neighbour within reach\n    engine.step(2);\n    expect([roundOf(engine).collected, roundOf(engine).state, engine.state('gem').entities.length]).toEqual([1, 'won', 0]); // prettier-ignore\n  });\n});\n","numLines":656,"startLine":1,"totalLines":656}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019qtasC6TwKqjeuoADZhYUr","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgj9KRSNKLYpLUNNbYSeL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015oTWfQEhdQehkuQaZchfUg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/.research/ai-hub/lib/hub && cat retrofit.md && echo ------- && sed -n 1,200p examples/arena.html && echo ---- && wc -l examples/* session.js harness.html round.js bridge.js && sed -n 1,60p round.js","description":"Print hub retrofit guide and shared-world example"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8609,"cache_read_input_tokens":85187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8609},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"26407d8e-aa18-400a-a9cd-e1c3d04c9b54","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:59.123Z","request_id":"req_011Cgj9KRCEYsSxje7nToA6A","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015oTWfQEhdQehkuQaZchfUg":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/.research/ai-hub/lib/hub && cat retrofit.md && echo ------- && sed -n 1,200p examples/arena.html && echo ---- && wc -l examples/* session.js harness.html round.js bridge.js && sed -n 1,60p round.js","description":"Print hub retrofit guide and shared-world example"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015oTWfQEhdQehkuQaZchfUg","type":"tool_result","content":"# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n\n---\n\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\n\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\nagainst it:\n\n<protocol>\n{{contract}}\n</protocol>\n\nDo only this:\n\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\n   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press\n   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\n   `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })` once. In\n   `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current score at once if the run is\n   still going.\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\n\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\nlike). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the\ngame an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for\neither. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol\ndescribes; you need not run them, the hub does.\n\nIf the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one\nline: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.\n\nOtherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line\nyou changed.\n\n{{notes}}\n-------\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Star Arena — AI Hub session example (shared world)</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"A minimal shared-world game for the AI Hub Session Protocol: every copy moves its own player, the host runs the stars and the scores, first to ten wins.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1b1530\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Tech demo\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"2\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"First to ten stars wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: arrows, WASD or a stick · sprint: Space or Cross · or hold a finger\">\n<style>\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #1b1530; color: #f3eef7; font: 16px system-ui, sans-serif; overflow: hidden; }\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; touch-action: none; }\n</style>\n<script>\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\n      },\n    };\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\n    return new Proxy(api, {\n      get: function (t, k) {\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\n      },\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\n        return true;\n      },\n      has: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data || k in t;\n      },\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\n        delete data[k];\n        return true;\n      },\n      ownKeys: function () {\n        return Object.keys(data);\n      },\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\n  function generator(a) {\n    return function () {\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n      var t = a;\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n    };\n  }\n\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\n  if (hub.active) {\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\n      try {\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\n      } catch (e) {\n        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\n  var seededRandom = null;\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\n    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\n    hub.seeded = true;\n  }\n\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\n    var asks = function (on) {\n      return function () {\n        post('fullscreen', { on: on });\n        return Promise.resolve();\n      };\n    };\n    var proto = root.Element.prototype;\n    proto.requestFullscreen = proto.webkitRequestFullscreen = asks(true);\n    root.document.exitFullscreen = root.document.webkitExitFullscreen = asks(false);\n    var shown = function () {\n      return fullscreenOn ? root.document.documentElement || null : null;\n    };\n    try {\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'fullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'webkitFullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n    } catch (e) {}\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\n   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\n   * must never land on the player's real saves.\n   */\n  function standAlone() {\n    hub.active = false;\n    if (seededRandom && Math.random === seededRandom) Math.random = realRandom;\n    hub.seeded = false;\n  }\n\n  var origin = '*';\n  var welcomed = false;\n  var ended = false;\n  var connecting = null;\n  var goAt = null;\n  var sentReady = false;\n  var reported = false;\n  var handlers = {};\n  var pending = {};\n  var tokens = limits.burst;\n  var refilled = now();\n  var probeFn = null;\n  var lastProgress = -Infinity;\n  var nextProgress = null;\n  var progressTimer = null;\n\n  function now() {\n    return root.performance && root.performance.now ? root.performance.now() : Date.now();\n  }\n\n  function warn(text) {\n----\n   882 examples/arena.html\n   798 examples/ghost.html\n   878 examples/parallel.html\n   488 session.js\n   548 harness.html\n   533 round.js\n   339 bridge.js\n  4466 total\n/**\n * round.js — one round of an AI Hub session, run by the hub that coordinates\n * it (the harness page, or the session host's tab).\n *\n * It never touches the network or a frame itself: every message for a game\n * goes out through `deliver(key, msg)`, and everything the games report comes\n * in through `receive(key, msg)` and `leave(key, reason)`. The clock is\n * injected, so `scripts/hub.test.mjs` can walk a round through every timeout\n * without waiting for one.\n *\n * Players are known by `key` (whatever the session calls them); games see\n * contiguous ids 0..N-1 in slot order.\n */\n\nexport const TIMINGS = Object.freeze({\n  helloMs: 10_000,\n  readyMs: 45_000,\n  /** Gated rounds: a game still loading when the hub releases the round gets this long more. */\n  loadGraceMs: 20_000,\n  countdownMs: 3_000,\n  graceMs: 5_000,\n  hiddenMs: 20_000,\n  maxRoundMs: 15 * 60_000,\n});\n\n/** P1 red, P2 blue, P3 green, P4 yellow: the colour follows the seat. */\nexport const SLOT_COLORS = Object.freeze(['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700']);\n\nexport const MODES = Object.freeze(['parallel', 'ghost', 'shared-world']);\n\n/** Each mode's name on screen. */\nexport const MODE_NAMES = Object.freeze({ parallel: 'Parallel', ghost: 'Ghost', 'shared-world': 'Shared world' });\n\n/** Older tags, still played: race as ghost, co-op and versus as a shared world. */\nconst MODE_ALIASES = Object.freeze({ race: 'ghost', 'co-op': 'shared-world', versus: 'shared-world' });\n\n/** The mode a tag or a hello names, older tags included; null for anything else. */\nexport function modeOf(word) {\n  const w = String(word ?? '').trim().toLowerCase();\n  return MODES.includes(w) ? w : (MODE_ALIASES[w] ?? null);\n}\n\n/** Modes where every copy runs its own world: each reports its own result, and nothing depends on a host. */\nexport const SELF_REPORTED = Object.freeze(['parallel', 'ghost']);\n\n/**\n * Whether a game's round carries the seed in its address, so the client seeds\n * Math.random and every copy starts the same: read from the game's own tag,\n * parallel or ghost. A game still tagged race was built for an unseeded start\n * (ids it makes from Math.random must differ between its copies), so it keeps one.\n */\nexport const seedsRandom = (tag) => ['parallel', 'ghost'].includes(String(tag ?? '').trim().toLowerCase());\n\nconst REAL_CLOCK = {\n  now: () => Date.now(),\n  setTimeout: (fn, ms) => setTimeout(fn, ms),\n  clearTimeout: (handle) => clearTimeout(handle),\n};\n\n/** A round's hard cap: half again its declared length, never past 15 minutes; the longest when it declares none. */","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"10c4c5c5-db32-4521-84d9-817a40e5f39b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:59.216Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n\n---\n\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\n\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\nagainst it:\n\n<protocol>\n{{contract}}\n</protocol>\n\nDo only this:\n\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\n   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press\n   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\n   `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })` once. In\n   `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current score at once if the run is\n   still going.\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\n\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\nlike). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the\ngame an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for\neither. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol\ndescribes; you need not run them, the hub does.\n\nIf the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one\nline: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.\n\nOtherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line\nyou changed.\n\n{{notes}}\n-------\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Star Arena — AI Hub session example (shared world)</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"A minimal shared-world game for the AI Hub Session Protocol: every copy moves its own player, the host runs the stars and the scores, first to ten wins.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1b1530\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Tech demo\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"2\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"First to ten stars wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: arrows, WASD or a stick · sprint: Space or Cross · or hold a finger\">\n<style>\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #1b1530; color: #f3eef7; font: 16px system-ui, sans-serif; overflow: hidden; }\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; touch-action: none; }\n</style>\n<script>\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\n      },\n    };\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\n    return new Proxy(api, {\n      get: function (t, k) {\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\n      },\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\n        return true;\n      },\n      has: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data || k in t;\n      },\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\n        delete data[k];\n        return true;\n      },\n      ownKeys: function () {\n        return Object.keys(data);\n      },\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\n  function generator(a) {\n    return function () {\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n      var t = a;\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n    };\n  }\n\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\n  if (hub.active) {\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\n      try {\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\n      } catch (e) {\n        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\n  var seededRandom = null;\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\n    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\n    hub.seeded = true;\n  }\n\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\n    var asks = function (on) {\n      return function () {\n        post('fullscreen', { on: on });\n        return Promise.resolve();\n      };\n    };\n    var proto = root.Element.prototype;\n    proto.requestFullscreen = proto.webkitRequestFullscreen = asks(true);\n    root.document.exitFullscreen = root.document.webkitExitFullscreen = asks(false);\n    var shown = function () {\n      return fullscreenOn ? root.document.documentElement || null : null;\n    };\n    try {\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'fullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'webkitFullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n    } catch (e) {}\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\n   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\n   * must never land on the player's real saves.\n   */\n  function standAlone() {\n    hub.active = false;\n    if (seededRandom && Math.random === seededRandom) Math.random = realRandom;\n    hub.seeded = false;\n  }\n\n  var origin = '*';\n  var welcomed = false;\n  var ended = false;\n  var connecting = null;\n  var goAt = null;\n  var sentReady = false;\n  var reported = false;\n  var handlers = {};\n  var pending = {};\n  var tokens = limits.burst;\n  var refilled = now();\n  var probeFn = null;\n  var lastProgress = -Infinity;\n  var nextProgress = null;\n  var progressTimer = null;\n\n  function now() {\n    return root.performance && root.performance.now ? root.performance.now() : Date.now();\n  }\n\n  function warn(text) {\n----\n   882 examples/arena.html\n   798 examples/ghost.html\n   878 examples/parallel.html\n   488 session.js\n   548 harness.html\n   533 round.js\n   339 bridge.js\n  4466 total\n/**\n * round.js — one round of an AI Hub session, run by the hub that coordinates\n * it (the harness page, or the session host's tab).\n *\n * It never touches the network or a frame itself: every message for a game\n * goes out through `deliver(key, msg)`, and everything the games report comes\n * in through `receive(key, msg)` and `leave(key, reason)`. The clock is\n * injected, so `scripts/hub.test.mjs` can walk a round through every timeout\n * without waiting for one.\n *\n * Players are known by `key` (whatever the session calls them); games see\n * contiguous ids 0..N-1 in slot order.\n */\n\nexport const TIMINGS = Object.freeze({\n  helloMs: 10_000,\n  readyMs: 45_000,\n  /** Gated rounds: a game still loading when the hub releases the round gets this long more. */\n  loadGraceMs: 20_000,\n  countdownMs: 3_000,\n  graceMs: 5_000,\n  hiddenMs: 20_000,\n  maxRoundMs: 15 * 60_000,\n});\n\n/** P1 red, P2 blue, P3 green, P4 yellow: the colour follows the seat. */\nexport const SLOT_COLORS = Object.freeze(['#e8443a', '#3b82f6', '#22c55e', '#f5b700']);\n\nexport const MODES = Object.freeze(['parallel', 'ghost', 'shared-world']);\n\n/** Each mode's name on screen. */\nexport const MODE_NAMES = Object.freeze({ parallel: 'Parallel', ghost: 'Ghost', 'shared-world': 'Shared world' });\n\n/** Older tags, still played: race as ghost, co-op and versus as a shared world. */\nconst MODE_ALIASES = Object.freeze({ race: 'ghost', 'co-op': 'shared-world', versus: 'shared-world' });\n\n/** The mode a tag or a hello names, older tags included; null for anything else. */\nexport function modeOf(word) {\n  const w = String(word ?? '').trim().toLowerCase();\n  return MODES.includes(w) ? w : (MODE_ALIASES[w] ?? null);\n}\n\n/** Modes where every copy runs its own world: each reports its own result, and nothing depends on a host. */\nexport const SELF_REPORTED = Object.freeze(['parallel', 'ghost']);\n\n/**\n * Whether a game's round carries the seed in its address, so the client seeds\n * Math.random and every copy starts the same: read from the game's own tag,\n * parallel or ghost. A game still tagged race was built for an unseeded start\n * (ids it makes from Math.random must differ between its copies), so it keeps one.\n */\nexport const seedsRandom = (tag) => ['parallel', 'ghost'].includes(String(tag ?? '').trim().toLowerCase());\n\nconst REAL_CLOCK = {\n  now: () => Date.now(),\n  setTimeout: (fn, ms) => setTimeout(fn, ms),\n  clearTimeout: (handle) => clearTimeout(handle),\n};\n\n/** A round's hard cap: half again its declared length, never past 15 minutes; the longest when it declares none. */","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015oTWfQEhdQehkuQaZchfUg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
