{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013A3Qq1wBfPaThUgrMKmpgL","type":"tool_result","content":"24:  if (c) return `<style>${find(c)}</style>`;\nbytes 6721143 html-comment-in-script false\nready after 6.2 s\nerrors []\nhash ff144f43a34d1d64\ngpu True secure True\nhelp \"actions.list()                                                  Lists the run's dev actions: the scene's own, then the engine's (god, freeze, spawn, travel, timeScale).\\nactions.run(name, args?)                                        Runs a dev action between steps, recorded in the replay: actions.run('travel', { at: [3, 0, 5] }).\\nadvice                                                          The advice records (warn-once, each with its code), latest last.\\nanim(id?)                                                       An animated actor's animator: its weights, the layer stack slot by slot, effectors, sockets, events, trail.\\nbot(plan = {})                                                  Plays the player with the bot: to goals, a tour, back; until, steps, trace; with seeds, a sweep of fresh runs.\\ncamera.advance(n = 60)                                          Moves the camera on by n frames of 1/60 s, drawing nothing and never stepping, as a page's frames move it: headless, where no frames run, it catches up with a player a dev action moved and a follow camera swings out; view only, never recorded; returns camera.get().\\ncamera.get()                                                    The camera: its code (cam=iso), what it shows in words, its type, heading and pose.\\ncamera.set(code, options = {})                                  Switches to the camera a code names (cam=topdown, cam=iso,45,2, cam3=shoulder, cam3=fly) at once, or blending over cam.blend seconds with { blend: true } as the page's live switches do; view only, never recorded; returns camera.get().\\ncapture()                                                       The whole sim, copied, to restore later in this run.\\ndescribe(kind?, id?)                                            The registries, as x describe lists them: every kind, one kind with its fields and ids, or one entry.\\nentities(query?)                                                The live entities the query matches, in id order: each id and the components it holds.\\nerrors                                                          The structured error records, latest last.\\neye(options = {})                                               What the camera, as last placed, sees of the bodies, with no GPU (the agent eye), passing where the view draws nothing: the raster as text with a legend, and each thing it sees with its cells.\\nfeel(id?)                                                       An actor's feel measured on a flat course: response, acceleration, stop, turn, jump apex, air time, reach; the shooter model's gaits, sprint, fatigue, strafe and lurch.\\nfx.stats()                                                      The effects' counts: the CPU pool's particles (live, born, dropped), the GPU's ring's while it has one (WP 11.3: its recycled too), sprites, decals, ribbons, draw calls and events played.\\ngallery.frames(kind, id)                                        An entry’s gallery frames: what each stages, holds a\nstats {\"simMs\":20.5714,\"physicsMs\":15.7571,\"animMs\":3.8429,\"renderMs\":11.275,\"gpuMs\":46.1868,\"steps\":7,\"frames\":4,\"drawCalls\":55,\"triangles\":8939,\"computeCalls\":1,\"textures\":43,\"geometries\":29,\"pipelines\":52,\"pipelinesAfterWarmUp\":0,\"warmUps\":2}\nhud Gems 0 / 10\n29 s\nWASD: run · Space: jump · Shift: dash · Esc: pause\npageerrors []","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"07a8c814-1c62-4d13-b512-99f0cbac7916","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:27:04.065Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"24:  if (c) return `<style>${find(c)}</style>`;\nbytes 6721143 html-comment-in-script false\nready 