{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014aGxpiwNRHXE2hZFNB5bgf","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file The intents vocabulary (PLAN.md §6.4, §6.5 item 3, §8.4, WP 1.5; doctrine: Reproducible): everything the sim\n * reads from outside arrives once per step as plain data, recorded by replays. `move` is a world-space direction\n * `[x, z]` (`fromCamera` turns a stick or keys into one, so W walks away from the camera), `cam` the camera heading,\n * `aim` a world-space aim point, `look` a view direction, `b` the buttons held and `p` the buttons pressed this step,\n * and game code adds its own keys, namespaced (`'game:charge'`). Devices (WP 3.3) make intents; the sim only reads them.\n *\n * Invariants: `normalizeIntents` checks every key and value (an unknown key names the closest; numbers are finite;\n * custom values are plain data) and returns a frozen object with keys in a fixed order, buttons sorted and unique, and\n * absent or empty entries left out. `p` is the union of the presses given and the edges of `b` (held now, not held the\n * step before), so a press is never lost and a hold presses once; when one frame runs several steps, the frame loop\n * passes its taps to the first step only (§6.4). `diffIntents` and `applyIntents` are the replay encoding (§8.4): held\n * state repeats until a change-point changes it (`null` clears a key), `p` belongs to its step and is written only for\n * presses the edges of `b` do not explain, so `applyIntents(prev, diffIntents(prev, next))` is `next` again. `-0` is\n * kept (`Object.is`), since replays must give the sim the very bits live play gave it.\n *\n * `cam` is the yaw of the camera's horizontal view direction, forward(ψ) = (sin ψ, 0, cos ψ) (§6.3), not three.js's\n * `camera.rotation.y`, which is ψ − π since a camera looks down its −Z.\n *\n * Edges, buffering and `consume` in sim time (WP 3.3): an `InputBuffer` is what a body remembers of its buttons across\n * steps, plain data in a component field, so the world hashes, captures and restores it. `updateInputBuffer(buffer,\n * intents, w.tick)` runs once per step (a system in the phase `intents`); then `released` says a button went up this\n * step (a tap shorter than a step is pressed and released on the same one), `buffered` that it was pressed within the\n * last `BUFFER_STEPS` steps and not yet used up by `consume` (a jump pressed just before landing still jumps), and\n * `repeated` that a held button repeats, as a menu cursor does. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:564-583`\n * (`released`, `repeat`, `buffered`, `consume`, `consumeAll`), counted in steps instead of seconds.\n *\n * @example\n * const step1 = normalizeIntents({ move: fromCamera(Math.PI / 2, [0, 1]), b: ['jump'] }); // move ≈ [1, 0]: +X\n * pressed(step1, 'jump'); // true: an edge of b\n * const step2 = normalizeIntents({ move: step1.move, b: ['jump'] }, step1);\n * [held(step2, 'jump'), pressed(step2, 'jump')]; // [true, false]\n * diffIntents(step1, normalizeIntents({}, step1)); // { b: null, move: null }\n * const buffer = updateInputBuffer(createInputBuffer(), step1, 1);\n * buffered(buffer, 'jump'); // true for 9 steps, or until consume(buffer, 'jump')\n * @see engine/input/intents.test.ts\n * @see engine/input/buffer.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, didYouMean } from '../core/log';\nimport { isPlainObject, show } from '../core/schema';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const INTENT_CODES = defineCodes('input', {\n  INPUT_BAD_INTENTS: {\n    template: '{where}: {problems}',\n    fix: 'give intents as { move: [x, z], cam, aim: [x, y, z], look: [yaw, pitch], b: [held buttons], p: [pressed buttons] } with finite numbers, plus custom keys namespaced \"game:key\" holding plain data (engine/input/intents.ts); null or a missing key means not given',\n    doc: 'Raised by `normalizeIntents`, `applyIntents` and the replay checks (engine/input/intents.ts, engine/sim/replay.ts) for an unknown key (named with the closest), a non-finite or misshapen number, a button that is not a non-empty string, or a custom value that is not plain data. Every problem is listed at once.',\n  },\n});\n\n/** A custom intent's value: plain data, as a replay file holds it. */\nexport type IntentValue = number | string | boolean | readonly IntentValue[] | { readonly [key: string]: IntentValue };\n\n/** A namespaced key for game code's own intents: `'game:charge'`. */\nexport type CustomIntentKey = `${string}:${string}`;\n\n/** One step's intents, as the sim reads them (systems get them as their second argument). */\nexport type Intents = {\n  /** The direction to move in, world space `[x, z]`, length 1 at most from `fromCamera`. */\n  readonly move?: readonly [number, number];\n  /** The camera heading: the yaw of its horizontal view direction, rad (see the file comment). */\n  readonly cam?: number;\n  /** The point aimed at, world space `[x, y, z]`, m. */\n  readonly aim?: readonly [number, number, number];\n  /** The view direction `[yaw, pitch]`, rad (first-person look). */\n  readonly look?: readonly [number, number];\n  /** The buttons held this step, sorted. */\n  readonly b?: readonly string[];\n  /** The buttons pressed this step (edges of `b` plus taps released within the step), sorted. */\n  readonly p?: readonly string[];\n} & { readonly [key: CustomIntentKey]: IntentValue | undefined };\n\n/** A replay change-point's intent part: the keys that changed, `null` for a key cleared, `p` for unexplained presses. */\nexport type IntentChanges = { -readonly [K in keyof Intents]?: Intents[K] | null };\n\n/** The built-in keys, in the order a normalized object holds them, each with what it means. */\nexport const INTENT_KEYS = {\n  move: 'the direction to move in, world space [x, z]',\n  cam: 'the camera heading (yaw of its view direction), rad',\n  aim: 'the point aimed at, world space [x, y, z], m',\n  look: 'the view direction [yaw, pitch], rad',\n  b: 'the buttons held, sorted',\n  p: 'the buttons pressed this step, sorted',\n} as const;\n\n/** A built-in key. */\nexport type IntentKey = keyof typeof INTENT_KEYS;\n\n/** No intents: what a step gets when nothing is given. */\nexport const NO_INTENTS: Intents = Object.freeze({});\n\n/** A namespaced key: a lower-case word, a colon, a name. */\nconst CUSTOM = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/;\n\n/** The namespaced key a bad one most likely means: `'Game:x'` → `'game:x'`, `'charge'` → `'game:charge'`. */\nfunction customKey(key: string): string {\n  const at = key.indexOf(':');\n  const space = (at < 0 ? '' : key.slice(0, at)).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9]/g, '').replace(/^[^A-Za-z]+/, '');\n  const name = (at < 0 ? key : key.slice(at + 1)).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_.-]/g, '');\n  return `${space ? space[0].toLowerCase() + space.slice(1) : 'game'}:${name || 'key'}`;\n}\n\n/** How many numbers each vector key holds. */\nconst VECTORS: Partial<Record<IntentKey, number>> = { move: 2, aim: 3, look: 2 };\n/** Code-unit order, so sorting never depends on the locale. */\nconst byText = (a: string, b: string) => (a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0);\n/** Deepest nesting a custom value may have. */\nconst MAX_DEPTH = 32;\n\n/** A frozen copy of plain data, or a problem pushed for the first value that is not. */\nfunction plainData(value: unknown, path: string, problems: string[], depth = 0): IntentValue | undefined {\n  if (typeof value === 'number') {\n    if (Number.isFinite(value)) return value;\n    problems.push(`${path} is ${show(value)}; numbers must be finite`);\n  } else if (typeof value === 'string' || typeof value === 'boolean') {\n    return value;\n  } else if (depth >= MAX_DEPTH) {\n    problems.push(`${path} nests deeper than ${MAX_DEPTH} levels`);\n  } else if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n    const out = value.map((item, i) => plainData(item, `${path}[${i}]`, problems, depth + 1));\n    return Object.freeze(out) as IntentValue;\n  } else if (isPlainObject(value)) {\n    const out: Record<string, IntentValue | undefined> = {};\n    for (const key of Object.keys(value).sort(byText))\n      out[key] = plainData(value[key], `${path}.${key}`, problems, depth + 1);\n    return Object.freeze(out) as IntentValue;\n  } else {\n    problems.push(`${path} is ${value === null ? 'null inside a value' : show(value)}; custom intents hold plain data`);\n  }\n  return undefined;\n}\n\n/** A sorted, unique, frozen copy of a button list, or problems. */\nfunction buttons(value: unknown, path: string, problems: string[]): readonly string[] | undefined {\n  if (!Array.isArray(value)) return void problems.push(`${path} is ${show(value)}; it must be a list of button names`);\n  const bad = value.find((name) => typeof name !== 'string' || name === '');\n  if (bad !== undefined) return void problems.push(`${path} holds ${show(bad)}; button names are non-empty strings`);\n  return Object.freeze([...new Set(value as string[])].sort(byText));\n}\n\n=====INPUT\n/**\n * @file The input (PLAN.md §6.4, WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Reproducible): the devices of a page (keyboard, mouse,\n * gamepads, touch, the virtual device) turned into one step's intents through bindings (engine/input/bindings.ts).\n * The frame loop calls `sample(camera, now)` once per rendered frame, before the clock hands out steps, and gives the\n * result to the frame's first step (its later steps get it without `p`, PLAN.md §6.4); the session records it, so\n * touch play replays like any other (WP 3.12, `sample`).\n *\n * What a sample holds: `b`, the map's actions held, sorted; `p`, those pressed since the last sample (a code that went\n * down, so a tap shorter than a frame still presses); `move`, the map's four move actions as `[right − left, forward −\n * back]` turned by `fromCamera(camera.yaw(), …)`, so W walks away from the camera; `cam`, the camera's heading; `look`\n * (its yaw and pitch) for maps with `look`; `aim`, the camera's point for the map's `aimWith` rule from the free\n * pointer and the right stick (engine/input/aim.ts); the map's `values` as custom intents. The move actions, the map's\n * `view` actions and the system layer (pause, menus) are never buttons in it: `held`, `pressed` and `strength` give\n * every action to the app and the UI, and `onView` hears a view action as it is pressed (a key at once, a pad button at\n * its poll, the virtual device's at the sample). `camera()` gives what the camera takes each frame (mouse look under\n * pointer lock and the right stick, scaled by the view settings `input.*`, engine/input/look.ts; the wheel; a map that\n * aims with the pointer keeps the stick for aiming). `prompt(action)` labels a binding on the device used last;\n * `use(map)` switches the map live (one per camera mode, WP 13.9), what is held read through it from the next sample;\n * `bindingsFor(map)`, another map's bindings, unswitched, for a controls screen (WP 13.25). A code a held binding waits\n * on (WP 13.20) is held back as it goes down, until it is a tap or a hold (`sample`).\n *\n * Clearing: a page blur, the page going hidden and `clear()` let go of every held code and drop pending presses, so\n * nothing stays held after alt-tab; a gamepad that disconnects lets go of its own. `listen(device)` serves rebinding.\n *\n * Invariants: nothing here reads a clock; edges are counted per sample; a code is held only between its press and\n * release reports. In Node (no `window`, `document`), only the gamepad source given and the virtual device feed it.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:482-512, 542-555, 594-622` (the input object, blur, `move`, `tick`),\n * sampled per frame; shardfall's short taps and prompts (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:590-610`).\n *\n * @example\n * const window = new EventTarget();\n * const input = createInput({ window, document: new EventTarget(), element: new EventTarget() });\n * const key = (type: string, code: string) => window.dispatchEvent(Object.assign(new Event(type), { code }));\n * ['KeyW', 'Space'].forEach((code) => key('keydown', code)), key('keyup', 'Space'); // a tap between two frames\n * input.sample({ yaw: () => Math.PI / 2 }); // { move: [1, 6.1e-17], cam: 1.5707963267948966, p: ['jump'] }\n * input.prompt('jump'); // 'Space'\n * input.sample({ yaw: () => 0 }).move; // [0, 1]: still held; the camera turned, so W walks +Z now\n * @see engine/input/input.test.ts\n */\nimport type { Log } from '../core/log';\nimport type { Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { SYSTEM_ACTIONS } from './actionMaps';\nimport { createBindings, pickLabel, type Bindings, type BindingsStorage } from './bindings';\nimport { deviceOf, heldBase, HOLD_TIME, holdCode, PAD_BUTTONS, touchCode, type DeviceKind, type InputSink } from './codes'; // prettier-ignore\nimport { createGamepadDevice, type GamepadDevice, type GamepadSource } from './devices/gamepad';\nimport { attachKeyboard } from './devices/keyboard';\nimport type { AimDevices, AimRule } from './aim';\nimport { attachMouse, type MouseDevice, type MouseTargets } from './devices/mouse';\nimport { attachTouch, type TouchDevice, type TouchSetting } from './devices/touch';\nimport { createVirtualDevice, type VirtualDevice } from './devices/virtual';\nimport { fromCamera } from './intents';\nimport { lookOptions, scaleLook, type LookOptions } from './look';\n\n/** A camera as the input reads it (the app's, over its view): its heading, its pitch for the look, and the aim. */\nexport interface CameraLike {\n  yaw(): number;\n  pose?(): { readonly pitch: number };\n  /** The point `rule` aims at this frame from the devices' pointer and stick (engine/input/aim.ts), or undefined. */\n  aim?(rule: AimRule, devices: AimDevices): readonly [number, number, number] | undefined;\n3: * gamepads, touch, the virtual device) turned into one step's intents through bindings (engine/input/bindings.ts).\n15: * its poll, the virtual device's at the sample). `camera()` gives what the camera takes each frame (mouse look under\n17: * aims with the pointer keeps the stick for aiming). `prompt(action)` labels a binding on the device used last;\n19: * `bindingsFor(map)`, another map's bindings, unswitched, for a controls screen (WP 13.25). A code a held binding waits\n23: * nothing stays held after alt-tab; a gamepad that disconnects lets go of its own. `listen(device)` serves rebinding.\n26: * release reports. In Node (no `window`, `document`), only the gamepad source given and the virtual device feed it.\n29: * sampled per frame; shardfall's short taps and prompts (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:590-610`).\n37: * input.prompt('jump'); // 'Space'\n51:import { createVirtualDevice, type VirtualDevice } from './devices/virtual';\n83:  /** The keyboard layout for prompts (`readKeyboardLayout()`). */\n104:  /** The bindings of the map in use: rebind, reset, labels. */\n109:  bindingsFor(map: string): Bindings;\n110:  /** The virtual device, merged into every sample (`__engine.input` drives it). */\n111:  readonly virtual: VirtualDevice;\n116:  /** The device used last: prompts follow it. */\n117:  readonly lastDevice: DeviceKind;\n130:  pressed(action: string): boolean;\n136:  prompt(action: string): string;\n137:  /** The next code pressed on `device`'s family, swallowed; null when Escape cancels or another listen starts. */\n138:  listen(device: 'keyboard' | 'gamepad'): Promise<string | null>;\n141:  /** Removes every listener. */\n166:  let listening: { family: 'keyboard' | 'gamepad'; resolve: (code: string | null) => void } | null = null;\n185:  /** The view actions told as their codes went down since the last sample, which tells only the others (virtual). */\n196:    const wait = listening;\n197:    listening = null;\n204:      if (listening && code === 'Escape') return hear(null);\n207:      if (listening?.family === family && (family === 'keyboard' || PAD_BUTTONS.includes(code as never))) {\n241:  const virtual = createVirtualDevice();\n285:    bindingsFor(map) {\n290:    virtual,\n293:    get lastDevice() {\n299:      if (virtual.touched) last = 'virtual';\n313:      const own = virtual.take();\n371:    prompt(action) {\n375:    listen(device) {\n377:      return new Promise((resolve) => (listening = { family: device, resolve }));\n=====\n44:export function connectVirtualDevice(host: object, device: VirtualDevice): void {\n49:export function virtualDeviceOf(host: object): VirtualDevice {\n/**\n * @file `__engine.input` (PLAN.md §8.3, WP 3.3; doctrine: Agent-operable): the inspector members that drive the virtual\n * device (engine/input/devices/virtual.ts) and record the run, registered from this file as entries of the registry\n * kind `inspectorMember` (engine/dev/members.ts), so no layer imports `dev/` and no other WP edits the inspector.\n *\n * - `input.press(action)`, `input.hold(action, down)`, `input.axis(name, value)`: change what the virtual device holds.\n *   A page's input merges it into every frame's intents; headless, `input.play` runs the steps.\n * - `input.play(script)`: runs a script one sim step at a time through the session (each step recorded), on top of\n *   what the device holds; returns the steps run and the tick after them. `input.play('30')` steps 30 times with it.\n * - `input.record()`: the run's intents from step 0 as a replay (PLAN.md §8.4), what `x replay` plays.\n * - `input.state()`: what the virtual device holds.\n *\n * Each engine has its own virtual device: the page's input when the app connects it (`connectVirtualDevice(host,\n * input.virtual)`), else one made on first use. Members change the sim only through `host.step`, which records.\n *\n * Invariants: this module registers on the shared registry when it loads, so `inspectorMember` must be declared first\n * (engine/dev/members.ts: the app and createHeadless load it before this module; a test imports it first).\n *\n * @example\n * import '../../dev/members';\n * import { createHeadless } from '../../app/headless';\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\n * import { defineScene } from '../../sim/scene';\n * const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: defineScene('walk', { setup: () => {} }, createRegistry()) });\n * const input = engine.input as Record<string, (...args: unknown[]) => unknown>;\n * input.axis('move', [0, 1]);\n * input.play('2 tap=jump'); // { steps: 2, tick: 2 }\n * (input.record() as { inputs: unknown[] }).inputs; // [[0, { move: [0, 1], p: ['jump'] }]]\n * @see engine/input/devices/virtual.test.ts\n */\nimport { def } from '../../core/registry';\nimport { createVirtualDevice, playScript, type VirtualDevice } from './virtual';\n\n/** What the input members use of an inspector host (engine/dev/members.ts `InspectorHost`). */\ninterface InputHost {\n  step(n: number, intents: unknown): void;\n  readonly session: { readonly world: { readonly tick: number }; record(): unknown };\n}\n\n/** Each host's virtual device. */\nconst devices = new WeakMap<object, VirtualDevice>();\n\n/** Gives `host` (the app's inspector host) the page input's virtual device, so `__engine.input` drives the page. */\nexport function connectVirtualDevice(host: object, device: VirtualDevice): void {\n  devices.set(host, device);\n}\n\n/** The virtual device of `host`, made on first use. */\nexport function virtualDeviceOf(host: object): VirtualDevice {\n  let device = devices.get(host);","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"ae30a204-e21f-495e-824c-56d0c6c7db40","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:34:56.872Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file The intents vocabulary (PLAN.md §6.4, §6.5 item 3, §8.4, WP 1.5; doctrine: Reproducible): everything the sim\n * reads from outside arrives once per step as plain data, recorded by replays. `move` is a world-space direction\n * `[x, z]` (`fromCamera` turns a stick or keys into one, so W walks away from the camera), `cam` the camera heading,\n * `aim` a world-space aim point, `look` a view direction, `b` the buttons held and `p` the buttons pressed this step,\n * and game code adds its own keys, namespaced (`'game:charge'`). Devices (WP 3.3) make intents; the sim only reads them.\n *\n * Invariants: `normalizeIntents` checks every key and value (an unknown key names the closest; numbers are finite;\n * custom values are plain data) and returns a frozen object with keys in a fixed order, buttons sorted and unique, and\n * absent or empty entries left out. `p` is the union of the presses given and the edges of `b` (held now, not held the\n * step before), so a press is never lost and a hold presses once; when one frame runs several steps, the frame loop\n * passes its taps to the first step only (§6.4). `diffIntents` and `applyIntents` are the replay encoding (§8.4): held\n * state repeats until a change-point changes it (`null` clears a key), `p` belongs to its step and is written only for\n * presses the edges of `b` do not explain, so `applyIntents(prev, diffIntents(prev, next))` is `next` again. `-0` is\n * kept (`Object.is`), since replays must give the sim the very bits live play gave it.\n *\n * `cam` is the yaw of the camera's horizontal view direction, forward(ψ) = (sin ψ, 0, cos ψ) (§6.3), not three.js's\n * `camera.rotation.y`, which is ψ − π since a camera looks down its −Z.\n *\n * Edges, buffering and `consume` in sim time (WP 3.3): an `InputBuffer` is what a body remembers of its buttons across\n * steps, plain data in a component field, so the world hashes, captures and restores it. `updateInputBuffer(buffer,\n * intents, w.tick)` runs once per step (a system in the phase `intents`); then `released` says a button went up this\n * step (a tap shorter than a step is pressed and released on the same one), `buffered` that it was pressed within the\n * last `BUFFER_STEPS` steps and not yet used up by `consume` (a jump pressed just before landing still jumps), and\n * `repeated` that a held button repeats, as a menu cursor does. Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:564-583`\n * (`released`, `repeat`, `buffered`, `consume`, `consumeAll`), counted in steps instead of seconds.\n *\n * @example\n * const step1 = normalizeIntents({ move: fromCamera(Math.PI / 2, [0, 1]), b: ['jump'] }); // move ≈ [1, 0]: +X\n * pressed(step1, 'jump'); // true: an edge of b\n * const step2 = normalizeIntents({ move: step1.move, b: ['jump'] }, step1);\n * [held(step2, 'jump'), pressed(step2, 'jump')]; // [true, false]\n * diffIntents(step1, normalizeIntents({}, step1)); // { b: null, move: null }\n * const buffer = updateInputBuffer(createInputBuffer(), step1, 1);\n * buffered(buffer, 'jump'); // true for 9 steps, or until consume(buffer, 'jump')\n * @see engine/input/intents.test.ts\n * @see engine/input/buffer.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError, defineCodes, didYouMean } from '../core/log';\nimport { isPlainObject, show } from '../core/schema';\n\n/** The codes this module raises, with their fixes. */\nexport const INTENT_CODES = defineCodes('input', {\n  INPUT_BAD_INTENTS: {\n    template: '{where}: {problems}',\n    fix: 'give intents as { move: [x, z], cam, aim: [x, y, z], look: [yaw, pitch], b: [held buttons], p: [pressed buttons] } with finite numbers, plus custom keys namespaced \"game:key\" holding plain data (engine/input/intents.ts); null or a missing key means not given',\n    doc: 'Raised by `normalizeIntents`, `applyIntents` and the replay checks (engine/input/intents.ts, engine/sim/replay.ts) for an unknown key (named with the closest), a non-finite or misshapen number, a button that is not a non-empty string, or a custom value that is not plain data. Every problem is listed at once.',\n  },\n});\n\n/** A custom intent's value: plain data, as a replay file holds it. */\nexport type IntentValue = number | string | boolean | readonly IntentValue[] | { readonly [key: string]: IntentValue };\n\n/** A namespaced key for game code's own intents: `'game:charge'`. */\nexport type CustomIntentKey = `${string}:${string}`;\n\n/** One step's intents, as the sim reads them (systems get them as their second argument). */\nexport type Intents = {\n  /** The direction to move in, world space `[x, z]`, length 1 at most from `fromCamera`. */\n  readonly move?: readonly [number, number];\n  /** The camera heading: the yaw of its horizontal view direction, rad (see the file comment). */\n  readonly cam?: number;\n  /** The point aimed at, world space `[x, y, z]`, m. */\n  readonly aim?: readonly [number, number, number];\n  /** The view direction `[yaw, pitch]`, rad (first-person look). */\n  readonly look?: readonly [number, number];\n  /** The buttons held this step, sorted. */\n  readonly b?: readonly string[];\n  /** The buttons pressed this step (edges of `b` plus taps released within the step), sorted. */\n  readonly p?: readonly string[];\n} & { readonly [key: CustomIntentKey]: IntentValue | undefined };\n\n/** A replay change-point's intent part: the keys that changed, `null` for a key cleared, `p` for unexplained presses. */\nexport type IntentChanges = { -readonly [K in keyof Intents]?: Intents[K] | null };\n\n/** The built-in keys, in the order a normalized object holds them, each with what it means. */\nexport const INTENT_KEYS = {\n  move: 'the direction to move in, world space [x, z]',\n  cam: 'the camera heading (yaw of its view direction), rad',\n  aim: 'the point aimed at, world space [x, y, z], m',\n  look: 'the view direction [yaw, pitch], rad',\n  b: 'the buttons held, sorted',\n  p: 'the buttons pressed this step, sorted',\n} as const;\n\n/** A built-in key. */\nexport type IntentKey = keyof typeof INTENT_KEYS;\n\n/** No intents: what a step gets when nothing is given. */\nexport const NO_INTENTS: Intents = Object.freeze({});\n\n/** A namespaced key: a lower-case word, a colon, a name. */\nconst CUSTOM = /^[a-z][A-Za-z0-9]*:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]+$/;\n\n/** The namespaced key a bad one most likely means: `'Game:x'` → `'game:x'`, `'charge'` → `'game:charge'`. */\nfunction customKey(key: string): string {\n  const at = key.indexOf(':');\n  const space = (at < 0 ? '' : key.slice(0, at)).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9]/g, '').replace(/^[^A-Za-z]+/, '');\n  const name = (at < 0 ? key : key.slice(at + 1)).replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9_.-]/g, '');\n  return `${space ? space[0].toLowerCase() + space.slice(1) : 'game'}:${name || 'key'}`;\n}\n\n/** How many numbers each vector key holds. */\nconst VECTORS: Partial<Record<IntentKey, number>> = { move: 2, aim: 3, look: 2 };\n/** Code-unit order, so sorting never depends on the locale. */\nconst byText = (a: string, b: string) => (a < b ? -1 : a > b ? 1 : 0);\n/** Deepest nesting a custom value may have. */\nconst MAX_DEPTH = 32;\n\n/** A frozen copy of plain data, or a problem pushed for the first value that is not. */\nfunction plainData(value: unknown, path: string, problems: string[], depth = 0): IntentValue | undefined {\n  if (typeof value === 'number') {\n    if (Number.isFinite(value)) return value;\n    problems.push(`${path} is ${show(value)}; numbers must be finite`);\n  } else if (typeof value === 'string' || typeof value === 'boolean') {\n    return value;\n  } else if (depth >= MAX_DEPTH) {\n    problems.push(`${path} nests deeper than ${MAX_DEPTH} levels`);\n  } else if (Array.isArray(value)) {\n    const out = value.map((item, i) => plainData(item, `${path}[${i}]`, problems, depth + 1));\n    return Object.freeze(out) as IntentValue;\n  } else if (isPlainObject(value)) {\n    const out: Record<string, IntentValue | undefined> = {};\n    for (const key of Object.keys(value).sort(byText))\n      out[key] = plainData(value[key], `${path}.${key}`, problems, depth + 1);\n    return Object.freeze(out) as IntentValue;\n  } else {\n    problems.push(`${path} is ${value === null ? 'null inside a value' : show(value)}; custom intents hold plain data`);\n  }\n  return undefined;\n}\n\n/** A sorted, unique, frozen copy of a button list, or problems. */\nfunction buttons(value: unknown, path: string, problems: string[]): readonly string[] | undefined {\n  if (!Array.isArray(value)) return void problems.push(`${path} is ${show(value)}; it must be a list of button names`);\n  const bad = value.find((name) => typeof name !== 'string' || name === '');\n  if (bad !== undefined) return void problems.push(`${path} holds ${show(bad)}; button names are non-empty strings`);\n  return Object.freeze([...new Set(value as string[])].sort(byText));\n}\n\n=====INPUT\n/**\n * @file The input (PLAN.md §6.4, WP 3.3, I-24; doctrine: Reproducible): the devices of a page (keyboard, mouse,\n * gamepads, touch, the virtual device) turned into one step's intents through bindings (engine/input/bindings.ts).\n * The frame loop calls `sample(camera, now)` once per rendered frame, before the clock hands out steps, and gives the\n * result to the frame's first step (its later steps get it without `p`, PLAN.md §6.4); the session records it, so\n * touch play replays like any other (WP 3.12, `sample`).\n *\n * What a sample holds: `b`, the map's actions held, sorted; `p`, those pressed since the last sample (a code that went\n * down, so a tap shorter than a frame still presses); `move`, the map's four move actions as `[right − left, forward −\n * back]` turned by `fromCamera(camera.yaw(), …)`, so W walks away from the camera; `cam`, the camera's heading; `look`\n * (its yaw and pitch) for maps with `look`; `aim`, the camera's point for the map's `aimWith` rule from the free\n * pointer and the right stick (engine/input/aim.ts); the map's `values` as custom intents. The move actions, the map's\n * `view` actions and the system layer (pause, menus) are never buttons in it: `held`, `pressed` and `strength` give\n * every action to the app and the UI, and `onView` hears a view action as it is pressed (a key at once, a pad button at\n * its poll, the virtual device's at the sample). `camera()` gives what the camera takes each frame (mouse look under\n * pointer lock and the right stick, scaled by the view settings `input.*`, engine/input/look.ts; the wheel; a map that\n * aims with the pointer keeps the stick for aiming). `prompt(action)` labels a binding on the device used last;\n * `use(map)` switches the map live (one per camera mode, WP 13.9), what is held read through it from the next sample;\n * `bindingsFor(map)`, another map's bindings, unswitched, for a controls screen (WP 13.25). A code a held binding waits\n * on (WP 13.20) is held back as it goes down, until it is a tap or a hold (`sample`).\n *\n * Clearing: a page blur, the page going hidden and `clear()` let go of every held code and drop pending presses, so\n * nothing stays held after alt-tab; a gamepad that disconnects lets go of its own. `listen(device)` serves rebinding.\n *\n * Invariants: nothing here reads a clock; edges are counted per sample; a code is held only between its press and\n * release reports. In Node (no `window`, `document`), only the gamepad source given and the virtual device feed it.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:482-512, 542-555, 594-622` (the input object, blur, `move`, `tick`),\n * sampled per frame; shardfall's short taps and prompts (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:590-610`).\n *\n * @example\n * const window = new EventTarget();\n * const input = createInput({ window, document: new EventTarget(), element: new EventTarget() });\n * const key = (type: string, code: string) => window.dispatchEvent(Object.assign(new Event(type), { code }));\n * ['KeyW', 'Space'].forEach((code) => key('keydown', code)), key('keyup', 'Space'); // a tap between two frames\n * input.sample({ yaw: () => Math.PI / 2 }); // { move: [1, 6.1e-17], cam: 1.5707963267948966, p: ['jump'] }\n * input.prompt('jump'); // 'Space'\n * input.sample({ yaw: () => 0 }).move; // [0, 1]: still held; the camera turned, so W walks +Z now\n * @see engine/input/input.test.ts\n */\nimport type { Log } from '../core/log';\nimport type { Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { SYSTEM_ACTIONS } from './actionMaps';\nimport { createBindings, pickLabel, type Bindings, type BindingsStorage } from './bindings';\nimport { deviceOf, heldBase, HOLD_TIME, holdCode, PAD_BUTTONS, touchCode, type DeviceKind, type InputSink } from './codes'; // prettier-ignore\nimport { createGamepadDevice, type GamepadDevice, type GamepadSource } from './devices/gamepad';\nimport { attachKeyboard } from './devices/keyboard';\nimport type { AimDevices, AimRule } from './aim';\nimport { attachMouse, type MouseDevice, type MouseTargets } from './devices/mouse';\nimport { attachTouch, type TouchDevice, type TouchSetting } from './devices/touch';\nimport { createVirtualDevice, type VirtualDevice } from './devices/virtual';\nimport { fromCamera } from './intents';\nimport { lookOptions, scaleLook, type LookOptions } from './look';\n\n/** A camera as the input reads it (the app's, over its view): its heading, its pitch for the look, and the aim. */\nexport interface CameraLike {\n  yaw(): number;\n  pose?(): { readonly pitch: number };\n  /** The point `rule` aims at this frame from the devices' pointer and stick (engine/input/aim.ts), or undefined. */\n  aim?(rule: AimRule, devices: AimDevices): readonly [number, number, number] | undefined;\n3: * gamepads, touch, the virtual device) turned into one step's intents through bindings (engine/input/bindings.ts).\n15: * its poll, the virtual device's at the sample). `camera()` gives what the camera takes each frame (mouse look under\n17: * aims with the pointer keeps the stick for aiming). `prompt(action)` labels a binding on the device used last;\n19: * `bindingsFor(map)`, another map's bindings, unswitched, for a controls screen (WP 13.25). A code a held binding waits\n23: * nothing stays held after alt-tab; a gamepad that disconnects lets go of its own. `listen(device)` serves rebinding.\n26: * release reports. In Node (no `window`, `document`), only the gamepad source given and the virtual device feed it.\n29: * sampled per frame; shardfall's short taps and prompts (`shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/input.rs:590-610`).\n37: * input.prompt('jump'); // 'Space'\n51:import { createVirtualDevice, type VirtualDevice } from './devices/virtual';\n83:  /** The keyboard layout for prompts (`readKeyboardLayout()`). */\n104:  /** The bindings of the map in use: rebind, reset, labels. */\n109:  bindingsFor(map: string): Bindings;\n110:  /** The virtual device, merged into every sample (`__engine.input` drives it). */\n111:  readonly virtual: VirtualDevice;\n116:  /** The device used last: prompts follow it. */\n117:  readonly lastDevice: DeviceKind;\n130:  pressed(action: string): boolean;\n136:  prompt(action: string): string;\n137:  /** The next code pressed on `device`'s family, swallowed; null when Escape cancels or another listen starts. */\n138:  listen(device: 'keyboard' | 'gamepad'): Promise<string | null>;\n141:  /** Removes every listener. */\n166:  let listening: { family: 'keyboard' | 'gamepad'; resolve: (code: string | null) => void } | null = null;\n185:  /** The view actions told as their codes went down since the last sample, which tells only the others (virtual). */\n196:    const wait = listening;\n197:    listening = null;\n204:      if (listening && code === 'Escape') return hear(null);\n207:      if (listening?.family === family && (family === 'keyboard' || PAD_BUTTONS.includes(code as never))) {\n241:  const virtual = createVirtualDevice();\n285:    bindingsFor(map) {\n290:    virtual,\n293:    get lastDevice() {\n299:      if (virtual.touched) last = 'virtual';\n313:      const own = virtual.take();\n371:    prompt(action) {\n375:    listen(device) {\n377:      return new Promise((resolve) => (listening = { family: device, resolve }));\n=====\n44:export function connectVirtualDevice(host: object, device: VirtualDevice): void {\n49:export function virtualDeviceOf(host: object): VirtualDevice {\n/**\n * @file `__engine.input` (PLAN.md §8.3, WP 3.3; doctrine: Agent-operable): the inspector members that drive the virtual\n * device (engine/input/devices/virtual.ts) and record the run, registered from this file as entries of the registry\n * kind `inspectorMember` (engine/dev/members.ts), so no layer imports `dev/` and no other WP edits the inspector.\n *\n * - `input.press(action)`, `input.hold(action, down)`, `input.axis(name, value)`: change what the virtual device holds.\n *   A page's input merges it into every frame's intents; headless, `input.play` runs the steps.\n * - `input.play(script)`: runs a script one sim step at a time through the session (each step recorded), on top of\n *   what the device holds; returns the steps run and the tick after them. `input.play('30')` steps 30 times with it.\n * - `input.record()`: the run's intents from step 0 as a replay (PLAN.md §8.4), what `x replay` plays.\n * - `input.state()`: what the virtual device holds.\n *\n * Each engine has its own virtual device: the page's input when the app connects it (`connectVirtualDevice(host,\n * input.virtual)`), else one made on first use. Members change the sim only through `host.step`, which records.\n *\n * Invariants: this module registers on the shared registry when it loads, so `inspectorMember` must be declared first\n * (engine/dev/members.ts: the app and createHeadless load it before this module; a test imports it first).\n *\n * @example\n * import '../../dev/members';\n * import { createHeadless } from '../../app/headless';\n * import { createRegistry } from '../../core/registry';\n * import { defineScene } from '../../sim/scene';\n * const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: defineScene('walk', { setup: () => {} }, createRegistry()) });\n * const input = engine.input as Record<string, (...args: unknown[]) => unknown>;\n * input.axis('move', [0, 1]);\n * input.play('2 tap=jump'); // { steps: 2, tick: 2 }\n * (input.record() as { inputs: unknown[] }).inputs; // [[0, { move: [0, 1], p: ['jump'] }]]\n * @see engine/input/devices/virtual.test.ts\n */\nimport { def } from '../../core/registry';\nimport { createVirtualDevice, playScript, type VirtualDevice } from './virtual';\n\n/** What the input members use of an inspector host (engine/dev/members.ts `InspectorHost`). */\ninterface InputHost {\n  step(n: number, intents: unknown): void;\n  readonly session: { readonly world: { readonly tick: number }; record(): unknown };\n}\n\n/** Each host's virtual device. */\nconst devices = new WeakMap<object, VirtualDevice>();\n\n/** Gives `host` (the app's inspector host) the page input's virtual device, so `__engine.input` drives the page. */\nexport function connectVirtualDevice(host: object, device: VirtualDevice): void {\n  devices.set(host, device);\n}\n\n/** The virtual device of `host`, made on first use. */\nexport function virtualDeviceOf(host: object): VirtualDevice {\n  let device = devices.get(host);","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014aGxpiwNRHXE2hZFNB5bgf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
