{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TzGzpg9xjRVKhxvBtG7oQe","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file The ring's sparring partners (docs/PLAYGROUND.md §2.2, §7.3; PLAN.md WP 10.2): two people on the ring's canvas\n * (`RING_PARTNERS`: actors on `build:adult` in its south corners, either side of the top of its steps, turned toward\n * them) who take the player's\n * blows. A punch or a shot flinches one along the blow (its reactions, engine/sim/reactions.ts); a kick or the\n * uppercut hands it off to its ragdoll (engine/sim/ragdolls.ts `handOff`, `PARTNER_BLOWS`: the kick drives it back\n * off its feet, the uppercut lifts it), and it gets up the way it lies once it lies still. Their hit points come back\n * at every blow (the component `health`, labs/playground/cast/health.ts), so they never die.\n * `standPartners(w)` stands them and adds the systems `ragdolls` and `partners` (phase `rules`, after the step's blows\n * landed), last in a scene's setup.\n *\n * Invariants: everything a partner is lives in its components; partners step in id order; no random stream.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts and the playground's own files.\n *\n * @example\n * // in a scene's setup, after the dummies: standPartners(w);\n * // a kick from the south: the partner flies north off its feet, lies still, then gets up from its back\n * @see labs/playground/cast/partners.test.ts\n */\nimport { addRagdolls, createCharacter, defineComponent, handOff, reactTo, spawnActor, Vector3, type Health, type MeleeState, type RagdollState, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api'; // prettier-ignore\nimport { CAST_HP, castHealth } from './health';\n\n/** Where the partners stand (m, on the canvas 1 m up) and face: the canvas's south corners, toward the steps. */\nexport const RING_PARTNERS: readonly { readonly at: readonly [number, number, number]; readonly yaw: number }[] = [\n  { at: [64, 1, 8], yaw: 0.6 },\n  { at: [68, 1, 8], yaw: -0.6 },\n];\n\n/** What each hard blow does, by its move: its push along the blow and up (m/s). A blow not here flinches. */\nexport const PARTNER_BLOWS: Readonly<Record<string, { along: number; up: number }>> = {\n  'move:kick': { along: 4, up: 1.5 },\n  'move:uppercut': { along: 1.5, up: 4 },\n};\n\ndefineComponent('sparringPartner', { description: 'One of the ring’s sparring partners (WP 10.2).', fields: {} });\n\n/** A partner and a player as this module reads them. */\ntype Partner = { id: number; actor: { x: number; z: number; yaw: number }; health: Health; ragdoll?: RagdollState };\ntype Player = { id: number; actor: { x: number; z: number }; melee?: MeleeState };\n\nconst along = new Vector3();\n\n/** The system `partners`: each partner a blow landed on this step flinches or falls (see the file comment). */\nfunction spar(w: World): void {\n  const players = w.query('melee', 'actor') as unknown as Player[];\n  for (const p of w.query('sparringPartner', 'health', 'actor') as unknown as Partner[]) {\n    if (p.health.hitAt !== w.tick) continue;\n    p.health.hp = CAST_HP;\n    const striker = players.find((player) => player.melee?.hitAt === w.tick && player.melee.struck === p.id);\n    const from = striker ?? (w.get(p.health.hitBy) as unknown as Player | undefined);\n    if (!from?.actor) continue;\n    along.set(p.actor.x - from.actor.x, 0, p.actor.z - from.actor.z);\n    if (along.lengthSq() < 1e-12) along.set(Math.sin(p.actor.yaw), 0, Math.cos(p.actor.yaw)).negate();\n    along.normalize();\n    const hard = striker ? PARTNER_BLOWS[striker.melee!.move] : undefined;\n    if (hard) handOff(w, p.id, { push: [along.x * hard.along, hard.up, along.z * hard.along] });\n    else if (!p.ragdoll) reactTo(w, p.id, (r) => r.hit(along, p.actor.yaw, striker ? 1 : 0.6));\n  }\n}\n======\n/**\n * @file The neighbours (docs/PLAYGROUND.md §7.4; PLAN.md WP 13.21): four people about the block, each on a route of\n * stops kept on a schedule (`NEIGHBOURS`: the north sidewalk end to end, the porch and the front path, the garden\n * bench and the backyard, the bus stop's bench and the south sidewalk; engine/world/aiRoutes.ts `followRoute`),\n * strolling between them over the site's navigation round its props (a flow field a stop: ways.ts beside it). Each\n * knows the player by WP 10.4's awareness (`sense`: in sight within `NEIGHBOUR.sight` m, nothing\n * of the world between their eyes; a shot or a kick it hears) and reacts:\n * - it looks at him (its head along `intents.look`) while he is within `NEIGHBOUR.look` m and in sight, and for a\n *   moment at a noise it heard;\n * - it steps aside, to its right, when he stands in its way (`stepAside`);\n * - it flinches when he shoves into it (he comes within `NEIGHBOUR.shove` m, moving at it);\n * - it startles at a shot or a kick it hears (a flinch away from it, and a look);\n * - a hard blow (a kick or the uppercut, `PARTNER_BLOWS`) hands it off to its ragdoll (WP 10.2), and it gets up the\n *   way it lies; a punch or a shot flinches it. Its hit points come back at every blow (health.ts beside it).\n * Each reaction emits `neighbour` `{ id, what }` (`look`, `aside`, `shoved`, `startle`, `flinch`, `fall`), as do its\n * sitting down and rising (`sit`, `rise`: `action:sit`, a seat behind it, on the benches' stops). Each is\n * drawn as `body:neighbour<k>` (labs/playground/bodies/neighbours.ts: the player's slots varied by a seed of its own,\n * which the page registers); the sim names it by id only. `standNeighbours(w)` stands them and adds the systems\n * `ragdolls` and `neighbours` (phase `ai`, after the step's blows and shots: engine/sim/melee.ts, weapons.ts).\n *\n * Invariants: everything a neighbour is lives in its components (`neighbour`, `route`, `awareness`, `health`);\n * neighbours step in id order; no random stream.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts and the playground's own files.\n *\n * @example\n * // in the site's setup, after the player: standNeighbours(w);\n * NEIGHBOURS.map((n) => n.name); // ['walker', 'porch', 'gardener', 'commuter']\n * @see labs/playground/cast/neighbours.test.ts\n */\nimport { actOn, addRagdolls, AWARENESS_FIELDS, createCharacter, defineAction, defineComponent, followRoute, handOff, physicsOf, reactTo, ROUTE_FIELDS, sense, spawnActor, stepAside, Vector3, type Awareness, type Health, type MeleeState, type Noise, type RagdollState, type RouteState, type RouteStop, type WeaponsState, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api'; // prettier-ignore\nimport { CAST_HP, castHealth } from './health';\nimport { PARTNER_BLOWS } from './partners';\nimport { wayTo } from './ways';\n\n/** A neighbour: its name, its body's index (`body:neighbour<k>`) and its route. */\nexport interface Neighbour {\n  readonly name: string;\n  readonly body: number;\n  readonly stops: readonly RouteStop[];\n}\n\n/** The north sidewalk's and the south's walking line (m, south), and their floor (m up). */\nconst [NORTH, SOUTH, KERB] = [84.75, 93.75, 0.15];\n\n/** The neighbours and their rounds (see the file comment): stops in world metres, stays in seconds. */\nexport const NEIGHBOURS: readonly Neighbour[] = [\n  {\n    name: 'walker',\n    body: 0,\n====\nlabs/playground/bodies:\nneighbours.test.ts\nneighbours.ts\nplayer.test.ts\nplayer.ts\n\nlabs/playground/levels:\ngym.ts\nhouse.test.ts\nhouse.ts\nplan.ts\nsite.ts\nstreet.ts\nyard.ts\n\nlabs/playground/looks:\ncel.ts\nclean.ts\nlooks.test.ts\npixel.ts\npixelPerspective.ts\n\nlabs/playground/props:\nhouse.ts\noutdoors.ts\nprops.test.ts\n\nlabs/playground/sounds:\neffects.ts\nevents.test.ts\nevents.ts\nground.test.ts\nground.ts\npage.test.ts\npage.ts\n/**\n * @file Unit tests for the neighbours' bodies (labs/playground/bodies/neighbours.ts, PLAN.md WP 13.21): each compiles\n * on build:adult wearing the player's slots, no two dressed alike, none in the player's accent, and the same seed\n * dresses them the same every time.\n * @see labs/playground/bodies/neighbours.ts\n */\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport { compileBody } from '../../../engine/gfx/puppets/compile';\nimport { NEIGHBOUR_BODIES, neighbourBody } from './neighbours';\nimport { PLAYER_BODY } from './player';\n\ndescribe('the neighbours’ bodies', () => {\n  it('compile on build:adult, wearing the player’s slots in clothes of their own', () => {\n    NEIGHBOUR_BODIES.forEach((body, k) => {\n      const worn = [...new Set(compileBody(`body:neighbour${k}`, 'build:adult').pieces.map((piece) => piece.slot))];\n      expect(worn.sort()).toEqual(Object.keys(PLAYER_BODY.slots!).sort());\n      expect(body.slots!.accent).not.toBe(PLAYER_BODY.slots!.accent); // he stays the one marked\n      expect([body.slots!.glove, body.slots!.cuff]).toEqual([body.slots!.skin, body.slots!.jacket]); // bare hands\n    });\n    const dress = (body: (typeof NEIGHBOUR_BODIES)[number]) => JSON.stringify([body.slots!.jacket, body.slots!.pants, body.slots!.accent]); // prettier-ignore\n    expect(new Set(NEIGHBOUR_BODIES.map(dress)).size).toBe(NEIGHBOUR_BODIES.length);\n  });\n\n  it('dresses each the same from its seed every time', () => {\n    expect(neighbourBody(2)).toEqual(NEIGHBOUR_BODIES[2]);\n  });\n});\n/**\n * @file The neighbours' bodies, `body:neighbour0` to `body:neighbour3` (docs/PLAYGROUND.md §7.4, §3.1; PLAN.md WP\n * 13.21): the player's body (labs/playground/bodies/player.ts), its parts as they are, in other clothes: each\n * neighbour's slots drawn from the palettes below by a seed of its own (`Rng(NEIGHBOUR_SEED + k)`): a skin and a hair,\n * a jacket and trousers each with its darker tone, boots and their soles, a pack, and an accent of its own (never the\n * player's orange, so he stays the one marked from every camera); bare hands: the gloves its skin, the cuffs its\n * jacket's.\n *\n * Invariants: data, drawn once at load from fixed seeds, so every run and every page dresses them alike; each body\n * names exactly the player's slots. The page registers them with its bodies (labs/playground/main.ts); the sim names\n * them by id only (labs/playground/cast/neighbours.ts).\n *\n * Game code, a page's: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts).\n *\n * @example\n * import { PLAYER_BODY } from './player';\n * NEIGHBOUR_BODIES.length; // 4\n * NEIGHBOUR_BODIES[0].slots?.accent === PLAYER_BODY.slots?.accent; // false\n * @see labs/playground/bodies/neighbours.test.ts\n */\nimport { defineBody, Rng, type BodySpec } from '../../../engine';\nimport { PLAYER_BODY } from './player';\n\n/** The first neighbour's seed; the k-th's is this plus k. */\nconst NEIGHBOUR_SEED = 2113;\n\n/** The palettes a neighbour is dressed from: single colours, or a garment's two tones. */\nconst PALETTES = {\n  skin: ['#f1c9a5', '#e3b48f', '#d1a07a', '#c68642', '#a46b45', '#8d5524', '#5c3a21'],\n  hair: ['#2b1d16', '#090806', '#71635a', '#b7a69e', '#a7856a', '#dcd0ba', '#8a3b1d'],\n  jacket: [['#7a3b3b', '#4e2424'], ['#3b5a7a', '#24394e'], ['#6b6b3b', '#45452a'], ['#4a7a4a', '#2e4e2e'], ['#7a5a8a', '#4b3756'], ['#8a6a3b', '#584326'], ['#c8c4b8', '#8e8a80']], // prettier-ignore\n  pants: [['#3a3f4d', '#24272f'], ['#5a4a3a', '#3a3026'], ['#2f4f6f', '#1d3245'], ['#6a6a6a', '#444444'], ['#2b2b2b', '#1a1a1a'], ['#4d5a3a', '#323b26']], // prettier-ignore\n  boot: [","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"fc52bd65-7c99-40b1-a147-0af61ce923de","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:35:46.355Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file The ring's sparring partners (docs/PLAYGROUND.md §2.2, §7.3; PLAN.md WP 10.2): two people on the ring's canvas\n * (`RING_PARTNERS`: actors on `build:adult` in its south corners, either side of the top of its steps, turned toward\n * them) who take the player's\n * blows. A punch or a shot flinches one along the blow (its reactions, engine/sim/reactions.ts); a kick or the\n * uppercut hands it off to its ragdoll (engine/sim/ragdolls.ts `ha