{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SDfvxvjMg8eoduEuSYuC8E","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/session-hub.md:176:| game | `answer` | `answer`: `ready` or `more` | on its own card, after the welcome, until `start` |\nlib/hub/README.md:3:An **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\nlib/hub/README.md:113:  the game runs as it does on its own.\nlib/hub/README.md:353:checks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:153:| 4 Natural multiplayer | A shared world, in whatever form the game's own multiplayer takes |\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:226:   progress and a seeded start expected; and the game on its own compared\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:398:  agent on its own copy of the game, spend capped, every failure put back);\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:475:- **Games on their own origin.** Every game shares the hub's origin today,\nREADME.md:267:If a game misbehaves in a frame, *Open on its own page* in its Details drawer\nREADME.md:422:record, **F** favourites, **O** opens a game on its own page, **/** writes a\nREADME.md:464:Every game can be played with up to three friends, each on their own device,\nREADME.md:491:awards, and outside a session the game plays exactly as it always would. What\nREADME.md:518:each with a player leaving, then the game on its own. `--record` writes the\nREADME.md:564:  on its own compared with the original.\n\n# AI Hub sessions: the hub's side\n\nWhat the hub does around a round, and how a round travels between the\ndevices. Games never need this page: the protocol a game follows is\n`lib/hub/README.md` (served at\n<https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md>), and that is the only\nthing the game factory is given. This page is for whoever changes the hub:\n`lib/hub/` (client, bridge, round, harness) and `assets/js/session/` (the\nsession page).\n\n## Around a round\n\nA game only plays its round. Everything around it belongs to the hub and is\nthe same for every game, so players learn it once.\n\n### Points and wins\n\n- Each round, a player scores **one point for every player they beat**. A\n  player who left or sat out without reporting counts as beaten; one who\n  reported and then left keeps their place. Tied players share a place. Every\n  round of four is worth three points to its winner, whatever the game.\n- **First place is a win**; in a team result (a shared world's `finish` with\n  `won`) only when the team won.\n- The **table** orders players by points, then wins, then the better average\n  place (`assets/js/session/score.js`).\n\n### Awards\n\n- **Game awards** come from a game's `result()` or `finish()`. The hub shows\n  them on the results, in the player's colour, and counts them for the\n  session.\n- **Session awards** are the hub's, given when a session ends:\n  **Showstopper** (most game awards), **Hot streak** (most wins in a row, at\n  least two) and **Steady hand** (best average place).\n\n### Ways to win a session\n\nThe host picks a format in the lobby:\n\n| Format | Ends | Winner |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Party** (default) | after 8 rounds | most points, after the three session awards add **3 bonus points** each, so the last word is never certain |\n| **Sprint** | after 5 rounds | most points |\n| **First to 12** | when someone has 12 points after a round | that player |\n| **Endless** | when the host ends it | most points |\n\nTies go to more wins, then the better average place, and otherwise stay ties.\n\n### The deal\n\n\nindex.html\n353:  computer*, and *Practise alone* in the hub's player. A couch co-op game has\n356:### The Couch — `/couch`\n800:couch/            the Couch: a page of its own, over the same library\n821:  couch/          rails, pad and keys, the game page, search (logic tested)\n\n489:In short: the `hub:session` metas in the head, the small `session.js` client\n592:After the picks, **Random Mode** deals. The hub deals every game that declares `hub:session` and\n623:  the browser, as `localStorage['ai-hub:relay-only']`).\n624:- While no game in the library declares `hub:session`, the reference games\n734:own, with `<meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"…\">` in its head. A field whose\n741:an override, or a `hub:collection` meta, replaces it.\n757:checks. A game can name its own source with `<meta name=\"hub:source\">`\n758:(`hub:inspired-by`, the older name, still works). Source leads the rail strip.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"059dfd23-02a8-4e8f-a766-5b697ac31ab7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:40:38.497Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"docs/session-hub.md:176:| game | `answer` | `answer`: `ready` or `more` | on its own card, after the welcome, until `start` |\nlib/hub/README.md:3:An **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\nlib/hub/README.md:113:  the game runs as it does on its own.\nlib/hub/README.md:353:checks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:153:| 4 Natural multiplayer | A shared world, in whatever form the game's own multiplayer takes |\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:226:   progress and a seeded start expected; and the game on its own compared\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:398:  agent on its own copy of the game, spend capped, every failure put back);\ndocs/multiplayer-plan.md:475:- **Games on their own origin.** Every game shares the hub's origin today,\nREADME.md:267:If a game misbehaves in a frame, *Open on its own page* in its Details drawer\nREADME.md:422:record, **F** favourites, **O** opens a game on its own page, **/** writes a\nREADME.md:464:Every game can be played with up to three friends, each on their own device,\nREADME.md:491:awards, and outside a session the game plays exactly as it always would. What\nREADME.md:518:each with a player leaving, then the game on its own. `--record` writes the\nREADME.md:564:  on its own compared with the original.\n\n# AI Hub sessions: the hub's side\n\nWhat the hub does around a round, and how a round travels between the\ndevices. Games never need this page: the protocol a game follows is\n`lib/hub/README.md` (served at\n<https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md>), and that is the only\nthing the game factory is given. This page is for whoever changes the hub:\n`lib/hub/` (client, bridge, round, harness) and `assets/js/session/` (the\nsession page).\n\n## Around a round\n\nA game only plays its round. Everything around it belongs to the hub and is\nthe same for every game, so players learn it once.\n\n### Points and wins\n\n- Each round, a player scores **one point for every player they beat**. A\n  player who left or sat out without reporting counts as beaten; one who\n  reported and then left keeps their place. Tied players share a place. Every\n  round of four is worth three points to its winner, whatever the game.\n- **First place is a win**; in a team result (a shared world's `finish` with\n  `won`) only when the team won.\n- The **table** orders players by points, then wins, then the better average\n  place (`assets/js/session/score.js`).\n\n### Awards\n\n- **Game awards** come from a game's `result()` or `finish()`. The hub shows\n  them on the results, in the player's colour, and counts them for the\n  session.\n- **Session awards** are the hub's, given when a session ends:\n  **Showstopper** (most game awards), **Hot streak** (most wins in a row, at\n  least two) and **Steady hand** (best average place).\n\n### Ways to win a session\n\nThe host picks a format in the lobby:\n\n| Format | Ends | Winner |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Party** (default) | after 8 rounds | most points, after the three session awards add **3 bonus points** each, so the last word is never certain |\n| **Sprint** | after 5 rounds | most points |\n| **First to 12** | when someone has 12 points after a round | that player |\n| **Endless** | when the host ends it | most points |\n\nTies go to more wins, then the better average place, and otherwise stay ties.\n\n### The deal\n\n\nindex.html\n353:  computer*, and *Practise alone* in the hub's player. A couch co-op game has\n356:### The Couch — `/couch`\n800:couch/            the Couch: a page of its own, over the same library\n821:  couch/          rails, pad and keys, the game page, search (logic tested)\n\n489:In short: the `hub:session` metas in the head, the small `session.js` client\n592:After the picks, **Random Mode** deals. The hub deals every game that declares `hub:session` and\n623:  the browser, as `localStorage['ai-hub:relay-only']`).\n624:- While no game in the library declares `hub:session`, the reference games\n734:own, with `<meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"…\">` in its head. A field whose\n741:an override, or a `hub:collection` meta, replaces it.\n757:checks. A game can name its own source with `<meta name=\"hub:source\">`\n758:(`hub:inspired-by`, the older name, still works). Source leads the rail strip.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SDfvxvjMg8eoduEuSYuC8E","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjAYuczTiSpbqsxZ5CpQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011A4rz1kfjeCa1EFMFmxMXM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"R=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/.research/ai-hub; sed -n 690,882p $R/lib/hub/examples/arena.html | cut -c1-170","description":"Read the shared-world example game's session wiring"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1915,"cache_read_input_tokens":357635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1915},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"a3370ff9-0cb1-4adc-9b07-a3911b1dba97","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:40:39.989Z","request_id":"req_011CgjAYuLNgahLKAh3JdpDc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011A4rz1kfjeCa1EFMFmxMXM":{"command":"R=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/.research/ai-hub; sed -n 690,882p $R/lib/hub/examples/arena.html | cut -c1-170","description":"Read the shared-world example game's session wiring"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011A4rz1kfjeCa1EFMFmxMXM","type":"tool_result","content":"    if (p) p.gone = true;\n    if (hub.isHost && game.phase === 'playing' && game.players.filter((q) => !q.gone).length < 2) finish();\n  });\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (hub.isHost) finish(); });\n  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\n    game.phase = 'over';\n    game.standings = standings;\n    game.message = reason === 'finished' ? 'Round over' : reason === 'sat-out' ? 'You sat this one out' : 'Round cancelled';\n  });\n}\nconst inside = (v, max) => Math.max(R, Math.min(max - R, Number(v) || 0));\n\n/** Host: a player says where it is, and there it is, unless an older report arrived late. */\nfunction heard(id, m) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (!p || !(m.at > p.at)) return;\n  p.at = m.at; p.tx = inside(m.x, W); p.ty = inside(m.y, H);\n}\n\n/** Host: player id touched star n. It scores, unless someone else got there first. */\nfunction take(id, n) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (game.phase !== 'playing' || !p || p.gone || n !== game.star.n) return;\n  p.score++;\n  newStar();\n  beep(id === hub.me ? 660 : 330);\n  AIHub.send({ t: 'pick', id, n });\n  if (p.score >= TARGET) finish();\n}\n\n/** Host: one snapshot for everyone: every player still here with its score, and the star. */\nfunction snapshot() {\n  const spot = (p) => (p.id === hub.me ? [p.x, p.y] : [p.tx, p.ty]);   // the others: where they said\n  return {\n    t: 's',\n    at: Math.round(AIHub.time()),\n    p: game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).map((p) => [p.id, ...spot(p).map(Math.round), p.score]),\n    s: [Math.round(game.star.x), Math.round(game.star.y), game.star.n],\n  };\n}\n\n/** Not the host: take the scores, the star and the other players from the snapshot, never your own player. */\nfunction applySnapshot(s) {\n  if (s.at < lastSnap) return;   // unreliable: an older one that arrived late\n  lastSnap = s.at;\n  for (const [id, x, y, score] of s.p) {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (!p) continue;\n    p.score = score;\n    if (id !== hub.me) { p.tx = x; p.ty = y; }\n  }\n  game.star = { x: s.s[0], y: s.s[1], n: s.s[2] };\n  if (s.over) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = 'Round over'; }\n}\n\n/** Host: standings by score, ties together, best first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends every copy on the same scores. */\nfunction finish() {\n  if (game.phase === 'over') return;\n  AIHub.send({ ...snapshot(), over: 1 });\n  const live = game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);\n  const standings = [];\n  for (const p of live) {\n    const last = standings[standings.length - 1];\n    if (last && last.score === p.score) last.ids.push(p.id);\n    else standings.push({ score: p.score, ids: [p.id] });\n  }\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(game.players.map((p) => [p.id, p.score]));\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: standings.map((g) => g.ids), scores });\n  game.phase = 'over';\n  game.message = 'Round over';\n}\n\nfunction unlockAudio() {\n  if (!audio) {\n    try { audio = new AudioContext(); } catch { audio = null; }\n  }\n  audio?.resume?.().catch(() => {});\n}\n\nfunction gesture() {\n  unlockAudio();\n  if (!hub && (game.phase === 'title' || game.phase === 'over')) {\n    solo();\n    game.phase = 'playing';\n    soloEnds = performance.now() + 60_000;\n  }\n}\n\n// ---- the loop: advance by elapsed time, never pause\nlet last = performance.now();\nfunction frame(now) {\n  const dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25);\n  last = now;\n  readPad();\n  const me = game.players.find((p) => p.id === (hub ? hub.me : 0));\n  felt = stick(me);\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && (!hub || AIHub.time() >= 0)) {\n    if (me) move(me, felt, dt);   // now, on every copy: your controls never wait for the network\n    if (hub) play(now, dt, me);\n    else {\n      if (touching(me)) { me.score++; newStar(); beep(660); }\n      if (now > soloEnds) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = `Time! ${me.score} stars — press to play again`; }\n    }\n  }\n  if (!hub?.server) draw(now);   // a server runs the world and needs no picture of it\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\n\n/** A session frame, after your own move: the star, what this copy sends, and the others eased toward where they are. */\nfunction play(now, dt, me) {\n  if (me && touching(me)) {\n    if (hub.isHost) take(hub.me, game.star.n);\n    else if (claimed !== game.star.n) {\n      // Predict the contact: claim the star once, hide it and cheer now. The host decides the point.\n      claimed = game.star.n;\n      AIHub.send({ t: 'claim', n: claimed }, { to: hub.host });\n      beep(660);\n    }\n  }\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && now - lastSent > 66) {\n    lastSent = now;\n    if (hub.isHost) AIHub.send(snapshot(), { reliable: false });\n    else AIHub.send({ t: 'me', at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), x: Math.round(me.x), y: Math.round(me.y) }, { to: hub.host, reliable: false });\n  }\n  const k = 1 - Math.pow(0.001, dt);\n  for (const p of game.players) if (p !== me) { p.x += (p.tx - p.x) * k; p.y += (p.ty - p.y) * k; }\n}\n\nfunction draw(now) {\n  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\n  const dpr = devicePixelRatio || 1;\n  if (canvas.width !== Math.round(r.width * dpr) || canvas.height !== Math.round(r.height * dpr)) {\n    canvas.width = Math.round(r.width * dpr); canvas.height = Math.round(r.height * dpr);\n  }\n  const s = Math.min(canvas.width / W, canvas.height / H);\n  ctx.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#120e22'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  ctx.setTransform(s, 0, 0, s, (canvas.width - W * s) / 2, (canvas.height - H * s) / 2);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#1b1530'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n\n  if (game.star.n !== claimed) {   // a star you claimed is gone here until the host's next one arrives\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#ffd34d';\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(game.star.x, game.star.y, 10 + Math.sin(now / 150) * 2, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n  }\n\n  ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n  for (const p of game.players) {\n    if (p.gone) continue;\n    ctx.fillStyle = p.color;\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(p.x, p.y, R, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7'; ctx.font = '14px system-ui';\n    ctx.fillText(`${p.name} ${p.score}`, p.x, p.y - R - 8);\n  }\n\n  ctx.font = '22px system-ui';\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7';\n  if (hub && game.phase === 'playing' && AIHub.time() < 0) {\n    ctx.font = 'bold 96px system-ui';\n    ctx.fillText(String(Math.ceil(-AIHub.time() / 1000)), W / 2, H / 2 + 32);\n  } else if (game.phase !== 'playing') {\n    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(0,0,0,.55)'; ctx.fillRect(0, H / 2 - 120, W, 240);\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7';\n    ctx.fillText(game.message, W / 2, H / 2 - 70);\n    const rows = game.standings\n      ? game.standings.flatMap((ids, place) => ids.map((id) => [place + 1, game.players.find((p) => p.id === id)]))\n      : game.players.map((p) => [null, p]);\n    ctx.font = '18px system-ui';\n    rows.slice(0, 4).forEach(([place, p], i) => {\n      if (!p) return;\n      ctx.fillStyle = p.color;\n      ctx.fillText(`${place ? place + '. ' : ''}${p.name}${hub && p.id === hub.me ? ' (you)' : ''} — ${p.score}`, W / 2, H / 2 - 30 + i * 28);\n    });\n  }\n  if (menu.open) drawMenu();\n}\n\nfunction drawMenu() {\n  ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(10,8,20,.82)'; ctx.fillRect(W / 2 - 170, 150, 340, 70 + menu.items.length * 40);\n  ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7'; ctx.font = 'bold 22px system-ui';\n  ctx.fillText('Settings', W / 2, 186);\n  ctx.font = '18px system-ui';\n  menu.items.forEach((item, i) => {\n    ctx.fillStyle = i === menu.at ? '#ffd34d' : '#f3eef7';\n    ctx.fillText(`${i === menu.at ? '▸ ' : ''}${item.label()}`, W / 2, 226 + i * 40);\n  });\n}\n\nconnect();\nrequestAnimationFrame(frame);\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"be617815-97d9-49fa-a117-d21c99b5025a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:40:40.011Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"    if (p) p.gone = true;\n    if (hub.isHost && game.phase === 'playing' && game.players.filter((q) => !q.gone).length < 2) finish();\n  });\n  AIHub.on('time-up', () => { if (hub.isHost) finish(); });\n  AIHub.on('end', ({ reason, standings }) => {\n    game.phase = 'over';\n    game.standings = standings;\n    game.message = reason === 'finished' ? 'Round over' : reason === 'sat-out' ? 'You sat this one out' : 'Round cancelled';\n  });\n}\nconst inside = (v, max) => Math.max(R, Math.min(max - R, Number(v) || 0));\n\n/** Host: a player says where it is, and there it is, unless an older report arrived late. */\nfunction heard(id, m) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (!p || !(m.at > p.at)) return;\n  p.at = m.at; p.tx = inside(m.x, W); p.ty = inside(m.y, H);\n}\n\n/** Host: player id touched star n. It scores, unless someone else got there first. */\nfunction take(id, n) {\n  const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n  if (game.phase !== 'playing' || !p || p.gone || n !== game.star.n) return;\n  p.score++;\n  newStar();\n  beep(id === hub.me ? 660 : 330);\n  AIHub.send({ t: 'pick', id, n });\n  if (p.score >= TARGET) finish();\n}\n\n/** Host: one snapshot for everyone: every player still here with its score, and the star. */\nfunction snapshot() {\n  const spot = (p) => (p.id === hub.me ? [p.x, p.y] : [p.tx, p.ty]);   // the others: where they said\n  return {\n    t: 's',\n    at: Math.round(AIHub.time()),\n    p: game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).map((p) => [p.id, ...spot(p).map(Math.round), p.score]),\n    s: [Math.round(game.star.x), Math.round(game.star.y), game.star.n],\n  };\n}\n\n/** Not the host: take the scores, the star and the other players from the snapshot, never your own player. */\nfunction applySnapshot(s) {\n  if (s.at < lastSnap) return;   // unreliable: an older one that arrived late\n  lastSnap = s.at;\n  for (const [id, x, y, score] of s.p) {\n    const p = game.players.find((q) => q.id === id);\n    if (!p) continue;\n    p.score = score;\n    if (id !== hub.me) { p.tx = x; p.ty = y; }\n  }\n  game.star = { x: s.s[0], y: s.s[1], n: s.s[2] };\n  if (s.over) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = 'Round over'; }\n}\n\n/** Host: standings by score, ties together, best first. A last snapshot, reliable, ends every copy on the same scores. */\nfunction finish() {\n  if (game.phase === 'over') return;\n  AIHub.send({ ...snapshot(), over: 1 });\n  const live = game.players.filter((p) => !p.gone).sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);\n  const standings = [];\n  for (const p of live) {\n    const last = standings[standings.length - 1];\n    if (last && last.score === p.score) last.ids.push(p.id);\n    else standings.push({ score: p.score, ids: [p.id] });\n  }\n  const scores = Object.fromEntries(game.players.map((p) => [p.id, p.score]));\n  AIHub.finish({ standings: standings.map((g) => g.ids), scores });\n  game.phase = 'over';\n  game.message = 'Round over';\n}\n\nfunction unlockAudio() {\n  if (!audio) {\n    try { audio = new AudioContext(); } catch { audio = null; }\n  }\n  audio?.resume?.().catch(() => {});\n}\n\nfunction gesture() {\n  unlockAudio();\n  if (!hub && (game.phase === 'title' || game.phase === 'over')) {\n    solo();\n    game.phase = 'playing';\n    soloEnds = performance.now() + 60_000;\n  }\n}\n\n// ---- the loop: advance by elapsed time, never pause\nlet last = performance.now();\nfunction frame(now) {\n  const dt = Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.25);\n  last = now;\n  readPad();\n  const me = game.players.find((p) => p.id === (hub ? hub.me : 0));\n  felt = stick(me);\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && (!hub || AIHub.time() >= 0)) {\n    if (me) move(me, felt, dt);   // now, on every copy: your controls never wait for the network\n    if (hub) play(now, dt, me);\n    else {\n      if (touching(me)) { me.score++; newStar(); beep(660); }\n      if (now > soloEnds) { game.phase = 'over'; game.message = `Time! ${me.score} stars — press to play again`; }\n    }\n  }\n  if (!hub?.server) draw(now);   // a server runs the world and needs no picture of it\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\n\n/** A session frame, after your own move: the star, what this copy sends, and the others eased toward where they are. */\nfunction play(now, dt, me) {\n  if (me && touching(me)) {\n    if (hub.isHost) take(hub.me, game.star.n);\n    else if (claimed !== game.star.n) {\n      // Predict the contact: claim the star once, hide it and cheer now. The host decides the point.\n      claimed = game.star.n;\n      AIHub.send({ t: 'claim', n: claimed }, { to: hub.host });\n      beep(660);\n    }\n  }\n  if (game.phase === 'playing' && now - lastSent > 66) {\n    lastSent = now;\n    if (hub.isHost) AIHub.send(snapshot(), { reliable: false });\n    else AIHub.send({ t: 'me', at: Math.round(AIHub.time()), x: Math.round(me.x), y: Math.round(me.y) }, { to: hub.host, reliable: false });\n  }\n  const k = 1 - Math.pow(0.001, dt);\n  for (const p of game.players) if (p !== me) { p.x += (p.tx - p.x) * k; p.y += (p.ty - p.y) * k; }\n}\n\nfunction draw(now) {\n  const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\n  const dpr = devicePixelRatio || 1;\n  if (canvas.width !== Math.round(r.width * dpr) || canvas.height !== Math.round(r.height * dpr)) {\n    canvas.width = Math.round(r.width * dpr); canvas.height = Math.round(r.height * dpr);\n  }\n  const s = Math.min(canvas.width / W, canvas.height / H);\n  ctx.setTransform(1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#120e22'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);\n  ctx.setTransform(s, 0, 0, s, (canvas.width - W * s) / 2, (canvas.height - H * s) / 2);\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#1b1530'; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);\n\n  if (game.star.n !== claimed) {   // a star you claimed is gone here until the host's next one arrives\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#ffd34d';\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(game.star.x, game.star.y, 10 + Math.sin(now / 150) * 2, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n  }\n\n  ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n  for (const p of game.players) {\n    if (p.gone) continue;\n    ctx.fillStyle = p.color;\n    ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(p.x, p.y, R, 0, Math.PI * 2); ctx.fill();\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7'; ctx.font = '14px system-ui';\n    ctx.fillText(`${p.name} ${p.score}`, p.x, p.y - R - 8);\n  }\n\n  ctx.font = '22px system-ui';\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7';\n  if (hub && game.phase === 'playing' && AIHub.time() < 0) {\n    ctx.font = 'bold 96px system-ui';\n    ctx.fillText(String(Math.ceil(-AIHub.time() / 1000)), W / 2, H / 2 + 32);\n  } else if (game.phase !== 'playing') {\n    ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(0,0,0,.55)'; ctx.fillRect(0, H / 2 - 120, W, 240);\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7';\n    ctx.fillText(game.message, W / 2, H / 2 - 70);\n    const rows = game.standings\n      ? game.standings.flatMap((ids, place) => ids.map((id) => [place + 1, game.players.find((p) => p.id === id)]))\n      : game.players.map((p) => [null, p]);\n    ctx.font = '18px system-ui';\n    rows.slice(0, 4).forEach(([place, p], i) => {\n      if (!p) return;\n      ctx.fillStyle = p.color;\n      ctx.fillText(`${place ? place + '. ' : ''}${p.name}${hub && p.id === hub.me ? ' (you)' : ''} — ${p.score}`, W / 2, H / 2 - 30 + i * 28);\n    });\n  }\n  if (menu.open) drawMenu();\n}\n\nfunction drawMenu() {\n  ctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(10,8,20,.82)'; ctx.fillRect(W / 2 - 170, 150, 340, 70 + menu.items.length * 40);\n  ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#f3eef7'; ctx.font = 'bold 22px system-ui';\n  ctx.fillText('Settings', W / 2, 186);\n  ctx.font = '18px system-ui';\n  menu.items.forEach((item, i) => {\n    ctx.fillStyle = i === menu.at ? '#ffd34d' : '#f3eef7';\n    ctx.fillText(`${i === menu.at ? '▸ ' : ''}${item.label()}`, W / 2, 226 + i * 40);\n  });\n}\n\nconnect();\nrequestAnimationFrame(frame);\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"is