{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HKW3C6raLuhLo1KbTipcBv","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file Clip mode, the animation library in the box (PLAN.md §10, WP 8.9; the Mocap Lab's clip mode,\n * `my-3d2dge:src/mocap.game.js`): the room (labs/box/levels/room.txt) as a physics level, the hero at its spawn and the\n * mannequin beside him, both playing a clip of the library through the clip layer in their animators (engine/sim\n * actorClips.ts), over the procedural rig. The mannequin is the figure the Quaternius clips were measured on\n * (`body:mannequin` on `build:mannequin`); the hero plays the clip retargeted to his build, and stays the player: he\n * walks under it (`box.clips.mask=upper` keeps his legs' own walk).\n *\n * Settings (`box.clips.*`, read every step, so a change plays at once and goes in replays): the clip, named\n * `<set>/<clip>` as `node x anim show` and `node x anim find` name it (a change crossfades to it from the pose on\n * screen); its rate; frame stepping (`box.clips.frame`, a frame of its bake at 30 a second, as `x anim bake` counts\n * them, held; -1 plays); the mirror and the mask. A one-shot holds its end 0.8 s, then plays again, as the Lab's did.\n * When the scene starts: who plays (`box.clips.cast`) and contact IK (`box.clips.ik`).\n *\n * The library's sets come from the registry (`defineClipSet`, the kind `clipset`): the box page registers every set\n * under data/anim/sets/ before it opens this scene (labs/box/main.ts), and so do tests/pages/replay.ts and the Node\n * hosts, `x sim`, `x replay` and tests (tools/anim/library.ts `defineLibrary`). Without them the setup fails with\n * `CORE_NO_ENTRY`, naming `defineClipSet`. Clips that travel play in place (their root motion is the layer's `root`,\n * which a game moves the body by). Its machine interface: `node x anim show <set>/<clip>` prints the clip this plays,\n * `__engine.describe('clipset')` and `node x describe clipset` list the sets, and the inspector shows each figure's\n * component `clips` (what plays, its time and weight) and its animator's layers (`__engine.anim(id)`).\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts and the box's own files.\n *\n * Tests: labs/box/scenes/clips.test.ts (every clip on the mannequin headless; `x anim show` and the setting select the\n * same clip, frame for frame; tests/replays/box-8-clips.replay.json's goldens), tests/e2e/box-clips.spec.ts (one clip\n * of each set in the page; `BOX_CLIPS=all` plays them all, a long run), tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts (the replay's\n * goldens while the page renders; live play replayed in Node).\n *\n * @example\n * // labs/box/?scene=clips&box.clips.clip=cmu/Cartwheel&cam=threequarter\n * // __engine.set('box.clips.clip', 'style100/Old_Walk'); __engine.set('box.clips.frame', 12)\n * // node x set box.clips.clip quaternius/Sword_Attack (in an x inspect session)\n * CLIPS_START; // [3.5, 0, 2.5]: the hero's spawn in the room; the mannequin stands 1.5 m east of him\n */\nimport {\n  addLevelBodies,\n  BAKE_FPS,\n  clipLayerOf,\n  clipSetIds,\n  createCharacter,\n  defineComponent,\n  defineScene,\n  defineSetBuild,\n  defineSettings,\n  getClipSet,\n  physicsOf,\n  playClip,\n  seekClip,\n  spawnActor,\nlabs/box/library.ts:2: * @file The animation library on the box page (PLAN.md §10, WP 8.9): `loadLibrary(files)` registers every set of\nlabs/box/library.ts:5: * `clipset` entry (engine/anim/clip/clipsets.ts: its `_set.json` and its clip files joined, `clipSetFromFiles`), then\nlabs/box/library.ts:13: * Invariants: the sets register sorted by directory, each once (`defineClipSet` keeps a set registered already); the\nlabs/box/library.ts:19: * // await loadLibrary((await import('./clipFiles')).CLIP_FILES); // __engine.describe('clipset').ids: ['clipset:cmu', …]\nlabs/box/library.ts:21:import { clipSetFromFiles, defineClipSet, defineMannequin, getClipSet, parseClip } from '../../engine';\nlabs/box/library.ts:24:export async function loadLibrary(files: Readonly<Record<string, () => Promise<string>>>): Promise<string[]> {\nlabs/box/library.ts:33:    .map((dir) => defineClipSet(clipSetFromFiles(dirs[dir], `data/anim/sets/${dir}`)).id);\nlabs/box/library.ts:48:  defineClipSet({ set, sources: getClipSet(from).sources, clips: { [name]: parseClip(text, name) } });\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts:6: * are the same text, and compress better together. `CLIP_FILES` is what `loadLibrary` (labs/box/library.ts) takes:\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts:17: * typeof JSON.parse(await read()); // 'object': the file, as loadLibrary reads it\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts:18: * // labs/box/main.ts, clip mode: await loadLibrary((await import('./clipFiles')).CLIP_FILES);\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts:25:/** The library's files as `loadLibrary` takes them: each path, and its text. */\nhero.ts\nslime.ts\nwalker.ts\nwisp.ts\n/**\n * @file The box's walker (PLAN.md §9.0, WP 5.7): the crowd's foot soldier from Box 4 on, a capsule that walks after\n * the hero. `WALKER` holds its numbers, `CROWD_WALKER` its own component (`crowdWalker`: its speed, heading and sway\n * phase, beside the crowd agent the scene keeps), `makeWalker` draws one, and `steerWalker` gives the velocity it\n * wants each step, for `setVelocity` (engine/physics/crowd.ts), whose acceleration limit and the solver do the rest.\n * `Chase` is what every member of the cast steers by (the slime and the wisp take it too).\n *\n * Its steering, the prototype's swarm: level with the hero (within `WALKER.level` of his height) it waits on a ring\n * round him (`approachRing`): in by the flow field from beyond it, backing off inside it, drifting round it on it as\n * its sway turns; anywhere else (on the floor below his gallery, on the stairs) it follows the flow field toward his\n * tile (`followFlow`), up the stairs when he is up. It faces where it walks, turning at `WALKER.turn`, and him while\n * it waits.\n *\n * Its numbers are the stress test's husk walker (`my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/20-sim.js:73-74, 196-199, 371-385`), in\n * SI units (PLAN.md Appendix C: 16 units a metre), as starting values (§9.0: similar, not identical):\n * - the capsule: radius 5 units → 0.3125 m, a straight middle of 16 → 1 m (the crowd agent's own make), 1.625 m tall;\n * - walking at 28 units/s plus up to 12 more, drawn per walker → 1.75 to 2.5 m/s, at 500 units/s² (the agent's\n *   31.25 m/s²);\n * - the ring: the hero's reach plus 10 units → 1.5 m, a band of 3 units either side, backing off at half speed and\n *   drifting round at 0.4 of it, the sway's phase drawn per walker at 0.9 rad/s; level within 14 units → 0.875 m;\n * - turning at 5 rad/s.\n *\n * Its attack (Box 5, WP 6.7): `WALKER_ATTACK`. Waiting on its ring, cooled down and granted one of the hero's attack\n * tokens (engine/world/ai.ts), it winds one of its fists' moves up (`moves`, drawn per swing; the prototype's husk's\n * claw, haymaker and hook), its wind-up at least `wind` s and twice the move's, its recovery `recover` s longer. While\n * it winds it turns to him at `turn` rad/s and walks to `stand` m from him, its arc telegraph (`telegraph:boxSwing`)\n * filling on the floor before it; as it strikes it lunges in when he stepped back, and what the arc holds as its hit\n * window opens is hit: `damage` hit points. Then it gives the token back and cools down for `cool` s plus up to\n * `coolSpread`. A hit on it breaks its swing off. It has `health` hit points.\n *\n * Its body is drawn as the neutral humanoid (a crowd body, engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts) in one of `WALKER.looks`: the\n * prototype's mixed husks, knights and skeletons, as builds.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts.\n *\n * @example\n * WALKER.speed.min; // 1.75: m/s\n * // const out = steerWalker(agent, walker, chase, new Vector3()); setVelocity(physics, agent, out, w);\n * @see labs/box/cast/crowd.test.ts\n */\nls: cannot access 'tests/replays': No such file or directory\ntests:\nbaselines\npages\nsetup\n\ntests/baselines:\nREADME.md\nadvice\nanim-clips.json\nperf\nqa-anim-adult.json\nqa-anim-library.json\nqa-anim.json\nqa-audio.json\nqa-geo-hall.json\nqa-geo.json\nqa-level.json\nqa-tex.json\nt2-minutes.json\nthumbs","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"c5533439-e80b-4298-b123-da72c4b768d9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:41:44.199Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file Clip mode, the animation library in the box (PLAN.md §10, WP 8.9; the Mocap Lab's clip mode,\n * `my-3d2dge:src/mocap.game.js`): the room (labs/box/levels/room.txt) as a physics level, the hero at its spawn and the\n * mannequin beside him, both playing a clip of the library through the clip layer in their animators (engine/sim\n * actorClips.ts), over the procedural rig. The mannequin is the figure the Quaternius clips were measured on\n * (`body:mannequin` on `build:mannequin`); the hero plays the clip retargeted to his build, and stays the player: he\n * walks under it (`box.clips.mask=upper` keeps his legs' own walk).\n *\n * Settings (`box.clips.*`, read every step, so a change plays at once and goes in replays): the clip, named\n * `<set>/<clip>` as `node x anim show` and `node x anim find` name it (a change crossfades to it from the pose on\n * screen); its rate; frame stepping (`box.clips.frame`, a frame of its bake at 30 a second, as `x anim bake` counts\n * them, held; -1 plays); the mirror and the mask. A one-shot holds its end 0.8 s, then plays again, as the Lab's did.\n * When the scene starts: who plays (`box.clips.cast`) and contact IK (`box.clips.ik`).\n *\n * The library's sets come from the registry (`defineClipSet`, the kind `clipset`): the box page registers every set\n * under data/anim/sets/ before it opens this scene (labs/box/main.ts), and so do tests/pages/replay.ts and the Node\n * hosts, `x sim`, `x replay` and tests (tools/anim/library.ts `defineLibrary`). Without them the setup fails with\n * `CORE_NO_ENTRY`, naming `defineClipSet`. Clips that travel play in place (their root motion is the layer's `root`,\n * which a game moves the body by). Its machine interface: `node x anim show <set>/<clip>` prints the clip this plays,\n * `__engine.describe('clipset')` and `node x describe clipset` list the sets, and the inspector shows each figure's\n * component `clips` (what plays, its time and weight) and its animator's layers (`__engine.anim(id)`).\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts and the box's own files.\n *\n * Tests: labs/box/scenes/clips.test.ts (every clip on the mannequin headless; `x anim show` and the setting select the\n * same clip, frame for frame; tests/replays/box-8-clips.replay.json's goldens), tests/e2e/box-clips.spec.ts (one clip\n * of each set in the page; `BOX_CLIPS=all` plays them all, a long run), tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts (the replay's\n * goldens while the page renders; live play replayed in Node).\n *\n * @example\n * // labs/box/?scene=clips&box.clips.clip=cmu/Cartwheel&cam=threequarter\n * // __engine.set('box.clips.clip', 'style100/Old_Walk'); __engine.set('box.clips.frame', 12)\n * // node x set box.clips.clip quaternius/Sword_Attack (in an x inspect session)\n * CLIPS_START; // [3.5, 0, 2.5]: the hero's spawn in the room; the mannequin stands 1.5 m east of him\n */\nimport {\n  addLevelBodies,\n  BAKE_FPS,\n  clipLayerOf,\n  clipSetIds,\n  createCharacter,\n  defineComponent,\n  defineScene,\n  defineSetBuild,\n  defineSettings,\n  getClipSet,\n  physicsOf,\n  playClip,\n  seekClip,\n  spawnActor,\nlabs/box/library.ts:2: * @file The animation library on the box page (PLAN.md §10, WP 8.9): `loadLibrary(files)` registers every set of\nlabs/box/library.ts:5: * `clipset` entry (engine/anim/clip/clipsets.ts: its `_set.json` and its clip files joined, `clipSetFromFiles`), then\nlabs/box/library.ts:13: * Invariants: the sets register sorted by directory, each once (`defineClipSet` keeps a set registered already); the\nlabs/box/library.ts:19: * // await loadLibrary((await import('./clipFiles')).CLIP_FILES); // __engine.describe('clipset').ids: ['clipset:cmu', …]\nlabs/box/library.ts:21:import { clipSetFromFiles, defineClipSet, defineMannequin, getClipSet, parseClip } from '../../engine';\nlabs/box/library.ts:24:export async function loadLibrary(files: Readonly<Record<string, () => Promise<string>>>): Promise<string[]> {\nlabs/box/library.ts:33:    .map((dir) => defineClipSet(clipSetFromFiles(dirs[dir], `data/anim/sets/${dir}`)).id);\nlabs/box/library.ts:48:  defineClipSet({ set, sources: getClipSet(from).sources, clips: { [name]: parseClip(text, name) } });\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts:6: * are the same text, and compress better together. `CLIP_FILES` is what `loadLibrary` (labs/box/library.ts) takes:\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts:17: * typeof JSON.parse(await read()); // 'object': the file, as loadLibrary reads it\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts:18: * // labs/box/main.ts, clip mode: await loadLibrary((await import('./clipFiles')).CLIP_FILES);\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts:25:/** The library's files as `loadLibrary` takes them: each path, and its text. */\nhero.ts\nslime.ts\nwalker.ts\nwisp.ts\n/**\n * @file The box's walker (PLAN.md §9.0, WP 5.7): the crowd's foot soldier from Box 4 on, a capsule that walks after\n * the hero. `WALKER` holds its numbers, `CROWD_WALKER` its own component (`crowdWalker`: its speed, heading and sway\n * phase, beside the crowd agent the scene keeps), `makeWalker` draws one, and `steerWalker` gives the velocity it\n * wants each step, for `setVelocity` (engine/physics/crowd.ts), whose acceleration limit and the solver do the rest.\n * `Chase` is what every member of the cast steers by (the slime and the wisp take it too).\n *\n * Its steering, the prototype's swarm: level with the hero (within `WALKER.level` of his height) it waits on a ring\n * round him (`approachRing`): in by the flow field from beyond it, backing off inside it, drifting round it on it as\n * its sway turns; anywhere else (on the floor below his gallery, on the stairs) it follows the flow field toward his\n * tile (`followFlow`), up the stairs when he is up. It faces where it walks, turning at `WALKER.turn`, and him while\n * it waits.\n *\n * Its numbers are the stress test's husk walker (`my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/20-sim.js:73-74, 196-199, 371-385`), in\n * SI units (PLAN.md Appendix C: 16 units a metre), as starting values (§9.0: similar, not identical):\n * - the capsule: radius 5 units → 0.3125 m, a straight middle of 16 → 1 m (the crowd agent's own make), 1.625 m tall;\n * - walking at 28 units/s plus up to 12 more, drawn per walker → 1.75 to 2.5 m/s, at 500 units/s² (the agent's\n *   31.25 m/s²);\n * - the ring: the hero's reach plus 10 units → 1.5 m, a band of 3 units either side, backing off at half speed and\n *   drifting round at 0.4 of it, the sway's phase drawn per walker at 0.9 rad/s; level within 14 units → 0.875 m;\n * - turning at 5 rad/s.\n *\n * Its attack (Box 5, WP 6.7): `WALKER_ATTACK`. Waiting on its ring, cooled down and granted one of the hero's attack\n * tokens (engine/world/ai.ts), it winds one of its fists' moves up (`moves`, drawn per swing; the prototype's husk's\n * claw, haymaker and hook), its wind-up at least `wind` s and twice the move's, its recovery `recover` s longer. While\n * it winds it turns to him at `turn` rad/s and walks to `stand` m from him, its arc telegraph (`telegraph:boxSwing`)\n * filling on the floor before it; as it strikes it lunges in when he stepped back, and what the arc holds as its hit\n * window opens is hit: `damage` hit points. Then it gives the token back and cools down for `cool` s plus up to\n * `coolSpread`. A hit on it breaks its swing off. It has `health` hit points.\n *\n * Its body is drawn as the neutral humanoid (a crowd body, engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts) in one of `WALKER.looks`: the\n * prototype's mixed husks, knights and skeletons, as builds.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts.\n *\n * @example\n * WALKER.speed.min; // 1.75: m/s\n * // const out = steerWalker(agent, walker, chase, new Vector3()); setVelocity(physics, agent, out, w);\n * @see labs/box/cast/crowd.test.ts\n */\nls: cannot access 'tests/replays': No such file or directory\ntests:\nbaselines\npages\nsetup\n\ntests/baselines:\nREADME.md\nadvice\nanim-clips.json\nperf\nqa-anim-adult.json\nqa-anim-library.json\nqa-anim.json\nqa-audio.json\nqa-geo-hall.json\nqa-geo.json\nqa-level.json\nqa-tex.json\nt2-minutes.json\nthumbs","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HKW3C6raLuhLo1KbTipcBv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
