{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BE4Xt4dPRWbJ44eGj4RhUj","type":"tool_result","content":"/**\n * @file Terrain (PLAN.md WP 10.5, §5.8; docs/PLAYGROUND.md §2.2, §6.3): outdoor ground as plain data, a heightfield\n * made from a seeded spec, and the queries on it. `defineTerrain(id, spec)` registers a spec (the registry kind\n * `terrain`); `getTerrain(id)` makes it (`makeTerrain`): a grid of `cols` × `rows` cells `cell` metres wide from its\n * north-west corner `origin`, a height at every cell corner. The physics stands it as a heightfield\n * (engine/sim/levelBodies.ts's `addTerrainBody`, engine/physics/heightfield.ts), the view draws it in chunks\n * (engine/gfx/terrain.ts), navigation walks it (engine/world/terrainNav.ts).\n *\n * A height is shardfall's: fbm value noise of `height` metres' range at the `scale` of its features, plus a ridged\n * fbm (`ridges` of it), then the `hills` (smooth domes, each `height` high and `radius` across from `at`) added, then\n * rounded to `terrace` steps when that is set, then pulled to each of the `flats` (a footprint flattened to its\n * `height`, blending back over `margin` metres round it), all over `origin`'s height. Cells split as Rapier splits a\n * heightfield's: along the diagonal from the north-east corner to the south-west one, so `terrainHeight` is the\n * collider's surface, the triangle under the point interpolated, and `terrainNormal` that triangle's normal.\n *\n * `surface` is the tag underfoot, `steepSurface` where the ground rises `steep` metres a metre or more (0.7: 35°);\n * `materials` (presentation only, as a level's) are the drawing's layers: the ground, the steep and, from `high`\n * metres over the origin up (0: none), the high one. `scatterTerrain` places trees and rocks by hashes of the cells\n * (shardfall's stateless placement).\n *\n * Invariants: pure: equal specs give equal terrains in Node and Chromium (int32 hashing, polynomial blends, no trig);\n * heights are float32, as the collider keeps them; outside the grid nothing stands (`terrainHeight` is null).\n *\n * Carried from shardfall@fa2dab6 `crates/pav_core/src/terrain.rs:93-153` (`raw_height`: fbm of 5 octaves at\n * lacunarity 2.03, the ridge term, the flattened footprints' smoothstep, `cell`'s terraces; `decor`'s hashed cells),\n * as a concept: on a heightfield's corners rather than in terraced tiles.\n *\n * @example\n * import { createRegistry } from '../core/registry';\n * const reg = createRegistry();\n * defineTerrain('terrain:knoll', { size: [16, 16], hills: [{ at: [8, 8], radius: 8, height: 2 }] }, reg);\n * const knoll = getTerrain('terrain:knoll', reg);\n * [knoll.cols, terrainHeight(knoll, 8, 8), terrainHeight(knoll, 0, 0), terrainHeight(knoll, -1, 0)]; // [16, 2, 0, null]\n * @see engine/world/terrain.test.ts\n */\nimport { mix32 } from '../core/hash';\nimport { codeError } from '../core/log';\nimport { registry as sharedRegistry, type Entry, type Registry } from '../core/registry';\nimport { createNoise2D } from '../core/noise';\nimport { Vector3 } from '../core/math';\n4: * `terrain`); `getTerrain(id)` makes it (`makeTerrain`): a grid of `cols` × `rows` cells `cell` metres wide from its\n5: * north-west corner `origin`, a height at every cell corner. The physics stands it as a heightfield\n18: * metres over the origin up (0: none), the high one. `scatterTerrain` places trees and rocks by hashes of the cells\n25: * lacunarity 2.03, the ridge term, the flattened footprints' smoothstep, `cell`'s terraces; `decor`'s hashed cells),\n49:  size: pair('Its extent along x and along z, each a whole number of cells: [24, 96].', true),\n50:  cell: { type: 'number', default: 1, minimum: 0.25, maximum: 8, unit: 'm', description: 'The grid’s spacing: a height stands at every cell’s corners.' }, // prettier-\n90:  /** Cells along x and along z, and a cell's side (m). */\n93:  readonly cell: number;\n119:  /** The chance a cell holds one, 0 to 1. */\n140:  const { size = [0, 0], cell, origin, hills, flats, materials } = { ...defaults(), ...spec } as Required<TerrainSpec>;\n148:      const cells = extent / cell;\n149:      if (Math.abs(cells - Math.round(cells)) > 1e-9) problems.push(`size along ${axis}, ${extent} m, is no whole number of ${cell} m cells`); // prettier-ignore\napi.ts\nblend.ts\nboost.ts\nchase.ts\ncodes.ts\ncollide.ts\ndefine.ts\neffects.ts\nfirst.ts\nfixed.ts\nfly.ts\nfollow.ts\norbit.ts\nplace.ts\npose.ts\npresets.ts\nrail.ts\nrig.ts\nshoulder.ts\n/**\n * @file The depth rail (PLAN.md WP 3.9; doctrine: Common ground): side scrolling with depth, a perspective camera on\n * a rail beside the hero, the 2D engine's Mode 7 side view. It follows him along the rail and keeps him between a\n * `near` and a `far` distance in depth, so he shrinks walking away into the level and grows coming back. `stepRail`\n * and `railPose` are the pure steps; `createRailCamera` wraps them in a camera.\n *\n * The rail stands on the `azimuth` side of the hero (round him from +Z toward +X, as the views' azimuth; 0, the side\n * view's side, by default), `RAIL_HEIGHT` above him, and looks straight across, tilted `RAIL_TILT` down. Along the rail\n * and in height it follows `input.follow` with a time constant of `RAIL_LAG` real seconds; in depth it stays put while\n * he is between `near` and `far` from it, and otherwise moves, twice as fast, only as far as brings him back within\n * them. `input.zoom` steps the zoom through the views' steps (`VIEW_ZOOMS`). Its yaw never turns, so W walks into the\n * depth and D along the rail, to the right of the picture.\n *\n * Invariants: it starts `RAIL_START` out from the hero; settled, his depth from the rail is within [near, far]. Pure:\n * each step returns a new state.\n *\n * Codes: `cam3=rail[,<azimuth>,<near>,<far>[,<zoom>]]` (degrees, metres). The reader and the camera wrapper are\n * engine/gfx/cameras/chase.ts's, shared by WP 3.9's cameras.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/40-cameras.js:71-81` (`railPose`: the follow along, the clamp in depth)\n * and `:42` (`DEPTH`: height, tilt, lens, near and far), in metres and +Y up.\n *\n * @example\n * const rail = createRailCamera();\n * rail.update({ follow: [2, 0, 0] }, 1 / 60).position; // [2, 4.375, 10]: RAIL_START out on +Z, RAIL_HEIGHT up\n * rail.yaw(); // π: it looks along −Z, into the depth\n * rail.code(); // 'cam3=rail,0,6.875,16.25'\n * @see engine/gfx/cameras/rail.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError } from '../../core/log';\n/**\n * @file Unit tests for the build `build:{{name}}` ({{id}}.ts): it is defined, its rest pose stands on the floor, and\n * anim.check passes it.\n * @see {{id}}.ts\n */\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport { animCheck, createSkeleton, forwardKinematics, jointPosition, Pose } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { {{name}} } from './{{name}}';\n\ndescribe('build:{{name}}', () => {\n  it('is defined, stands on the floor at rest, and passes anim.check', () => {\n    expect({{name}}.id).toBe('build:{{name}}');\n    const skeleton = createSkeleton({{name}});\n    const world = forwardKinematics(skeleton, new Pose());\n    expect(jointPosition(world, 'pelvis').y).toBeCloseTo(({{name}}.legUpper + {{name}}.legLower) * {{name}}.size, 9);\n    expect(animCheck({ poses: [new Pose()], skeleton }).problems).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n/**\n * @file The build `build:{{name}}`: whose body it is (replace this text; `x docs` puts the first sentence in INDEX).\n *\n * Invariants: lengths in metres before `size`, which scales them all; a field left out keeps `build:chibi`'s value\n * (node x describe build lists the fields with their defaults); hipHeight is at most legUpper + legLower.\n *\n * @example\n/**\n * @file The cast's ways about the block (docs/PLAYGROUND.md §7.4; PLAN.md WP 13.21): one navigation of the site a\n * world, round its props (engine/world/siteNav.ts `createSiteNav`, engine/sim/propBlocks.ts `propObstacles`), and flow\n * fields over it: `wayTo(w, key, goal)` keeps one a key (a neighbour's stop, the dog's goal), made again only when the\n * goal lies on another node, and lazy: flooded only as far as `direction` reads it, which answers as on a full field\n * (engine/world/siteNavGraph.ts), so the dog following the player across tiles floods a few metres, not the block. `plainWays()` is the site's alone, without a scene's props, for placing th\n * scene's setup, whose props no query sees yet.\n *\n * - The navigation is made the first time a step asks (`waysOf`), round the props as they stand then (the scene's\n *   setup can see none of them); a walker held by what its way does not know (a door opened onto it) has it made\n *   again round them as they stand now (`replanWays`), as the bot does. The boxes each went round are kept in the\n *   world with a count of the remakes (the component `siteWays`), so a world restored from a capture makes the very\n *   same ways the run had then, whatever the props did since.\n *\n * Invariants: derived data, apart from `siteWays`'s boxes (plain numbers, hashed and captured with the world); a field's\n * answers are a pure function of the navigation and its goal's node.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts and the playground's own files.\n *\n * @example\n * // stepping: const { nav, field } = wayTo(w, stop, stop.at); nav.direction(field, x, y, z);\n * @see labs/playground/cast/neighbours.test.ts\n */\nimport { createSiteNav, defineComponent, propObstacles, type NavBlock, type SiteNav, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api'; // prettier-ignore\nimport { SITE } from '../levels/site';\n\ndefineComponent('siteWays', {\n  description: 'The boxes of the props the cast’s ways go round, as a step last found them (WP 13.21).',\n  fields: {\n    blocks: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Each box’s min, then max (m).' }, // prettier-ignore\n    version: { type: 'integer', default: 0, minimum: 0, description: 'How many times the ways were made again.' },\n  },\n});\n\n/** A world's navigation, the remake it is and the step it was made in, and its fields by key with the node each leads to. */ // prettier-ignore\ninterface Ways {\n  readonly nav: SiteNav;\n  readonly version: number;\n  readonly tick: number;\n  readonly fields: Map<unknown, { node: number; field: Float64Array }>;\n}\ntype Kept = { siteWays: { blocks: number[]; version: number } };\nconst WAYS = new WeakMap<object, Ways>();\nlet plain: SiteNav | undefined;\n\n/** How far up a walker of the cast steps between tiles (m): a kerb, a porch's step. */\nconst CLIMB = 0.4;\n\n/** The site's navigation without a scene's props, made once (a pure function of the site): for placing in a setup. */\nexport function plainWays(): SiteNav {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"dc5de530-c5e7-462e-97b1-3823f7be8876","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:54:05.013Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/**\n * @file Terrain (PLAN.md WP 10.5, §5.8; docs/PLAYGROUND.md §2.2, §6.3): outdoor ground as plain data, a heightfield\n * made from a seeded spec, and the queries on it. `defineTerrain(id, spec)` registers a spec (the registry kind\n * `terrain`); `getTerrain(id)` makes it (`makeTerrain`): a grid of `cols` × `rows` cells `cell` metres wide from its\n * north-west corner `origin`, a height at every cell corner. The physics stands it as a heightfield\n * (engine/sim/levelBodies.ts's `addTerrainBody`, engine/physics/heightfield.ts), the view draws it in chunks\n * (engine/gfx/terrain.ts), navigation walks it (engine/world/terrainNav.ts).\n *\n * A height is shardfall's: fbm value noise of `height` metres' range at the `scale` of its features, plus a ridged\n * fbm (`ridges` of it), then the `hills` (smooth domes, each `height` high and `radius` across from `at`) added, then\n * rounded to `terrace` steps when that is set, then pulled to each of the `flats` (a fo