`RAIL_HEIGHT` above him, and looks straight across, tilted `RAIL_TILT` down. Along the rail\n * and in height it follows `input.follow` with a time constant of `RAIL_LAG` real seconds; in depth it stays put while\n * he is between `near` and `far` from it, and otherwise moves, twice as fast, only as far as brings him back within\n * them. `input.zoom` steps the zoom through the views' steps (`VIEW_ZOOMS`). Its yaw never turns, so W walks into the\n * depth and D along the rail, to the right of the picture.\n *\n * Invariants: it starts `RAIL_START` out from the hero; settled, his depth from the rail is within [near, far]. Pure:\n * each step returns a new state.\n *\n * Codes: `cam3=rail[,<azimuth>,<near>,<far>[,<zoom>]]` (degrees, metres). The reader and the camera wrapper are\n * engine/gfx/cameras/chase.ts's, shared by WP 3.9's cameras.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/40-cameras.js:71-81` (`railPose`: the follow along, the clamp in depth)\n * and `:42` (`DEPTH`: height, tilt, lens, near and far), in metres and +Y up.\n *\n * @example\n * const rail = createRailCamera();\n * rail.update({ follow: [2, 0, 0] }, 1 / 60).position; // [2, 4.375, 10]: RAIL_START out on +Z, RAIL_HEIGHT up\n * rail.yaw(); // π: it looks along −Z, into the depth\n * rail.code(); // 'cam3=rail,0,6.875,16.25'\n * @see engine/gfx/cameras/rail.test.ts\n */\nimport { codeError } from '../../core/log';\n/**\n * @file Unit tests for the build `build:{{name}}` ({{id}}.ts): it is defined, its rest pose stands on the floor, and\n * anim.check passes it.\n * @see {{id}}.ts\n */\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport { animCheck, createSkeleton, forwardKinematics, jointPosition, Pose } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { {{name}} } from './{{name}}';\n\ndescribe('build:{{name}}', () => {\n  it('is defined, stands on the floor at rest, and passes anim.check', () => {\n    expect({{name}}.id).toBe('build:{{name}}');\n    const skeleton = createSkeleton({{name}});\n    const world = forwardKinematics(skeleton, new Pose());\n    expect(jointPosition(world, 'pelvis').y).toBeCloseTo(({{name}}.legUpper + {{name}}.legLower) * {{name}}.size, 9);\n    expect(animCheck({ poses: [new Pose()], skeleton }).problems).toEqual([]);\n  });\n});\n/**\n * @file The build `build:{{name}}`: whose body it is (replace this text; `x docs` puts the first sentence in INDEX).\n *\n * Invariants: lengths in metres before `size`, which scales them all; a field left out keeps `build:chibi`'s value\n * (node x describe build lists the fields with their defaults); hipHeight is at most legUpper + legLower.\n *\n * @example\n/**\n * @file The cast's ways about the block (docs/PLAYGROUND.md §7.4; PLAN.md WP 13.21): one navigation of the site a\n * world, round its props (engine/world/siteNav.ts `createSiteNav`, engine/sim/propBlocks.ts `propObstacles`), and flow\n * fields over it: `wayTo(w, key, goal)` keeps one a key (a neighbour's stop, the dog's goal), made again only when the\n * goal lies on another node, and lazy: flooded only as far as `direction` reads it, which answers as on a full field\n * (engine/world/siteNavGraph.ts), so the dog following the player across tiles floods a few metres, not the block. `plainWays()` is the site's alone, without a scene's props, for placing th\n * scene's setup, whose props no query sees yet.\n *\n * - The navigation is made the first time a step asks (`waysOf`), round the props as they stand then (the scene's\n *   setup can see none of them); a walker held by what its way does not know (a door opened onto it) has it made\n *   again round them as they stand now (`replanWays`), as the bot does. The boxes each went round are kept in the\n *   world with a count of the remakes (the component `siteWays`), so a world restored from a capture makes the very\n *   same ways the run had then, whatever the props did since.\n *\n * Invariants: derived data, apart from `siteWays`'s boxes (plain numbers, hashed and captured with the world); a field's\n * answers are a pure function of the navigation and its goal's node.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts and the playground's own files.\n *\n * @example\n * // stepping: const { nav, field } = wayTo(w, stop, stop.at); nav.direction(field, x, y, z);\n * @see labs/playground/cast/neighbours.test.ts\n */\nimport { createSiteNav, defineComponent, propObstacles, type NavBlock, type SiteNav, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api'; // prettier-ignore\nimport { SITE } from '../levels/site';\n\ndefineComponent('siteWays', {\n  description: 'The boxes of the props the cast’s ways go round, as a step last found them (WP 13.21).',\n  fields: {\n    blocks: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'number' }, default: [], description: 'Each box’s min, then max (m).' }, // prettier-ignore\n    version: { type: 'integer', default: 0, minimum: 0, description: 'How many times the ways were made again.' },\n  },\n});\n\n/** A world's navigation, the remake it is and the step it was made in, and its fields by key with the node each leads to. */ // prettier-ignore\ninterface Ways {\n  readonly nav: SiteNav;\n  readonly version: number;\n  readonly tick: number;\n  readonly fields: Map<unknown, { node: number; field: Float64Array }>;\n}\ntype Kept = { siteWays: { blocks: number[]; version: number } };\nconst WAYS = new WeakMap<object, Ways>();\nlet plain: SiteNav | undefined;\n\n/** How far up a walker of the cast steps between tiles (m): a kerb, a porch's step. */\nconst CLIMB = 0.4;\n\n/** The site's navigation without a scene's props, made once (a pure function of the site): for placing in a setup. */\nexport function plainWays(): SiteNav {","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BE4Xt4dPRWbJ44eGj4RhUj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
