{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TWGwvWLnehdcH4J5e3NkNA","type":"tool_result","content":"3: * an entity with the components `actor` and `animator`) drawn as a puppet (engine/gfx/puppets/draw.ts) of the neutral\n4: * humanoid (`ACTOR_BODY`) or the body its component `puppet` names (`body:mannequin`, WP 8.9), in its animator's build,\n10: * animator's data; `draw(alpha)` poses each puppet `alpha` of the way from the one before to the last. `player()` is\n11: * the first player actor (in id order) as the last draw put it: its feet and, with a puppet, its skeleton, world pose\n15: * each puppet's trail as its last pose sampled it (WP 6.7, oldest first), which the stage's effects draw as ribbons.\n19: * WP 6.2 in the box (WP 7.8): an actor's `reactions` (engine/sim/reactions.ts) are a `Reactions` layer on its puppet's\n22: * chains hang under the puppet (engine/gfx/puppets/chains.ts: `actor#<id>/cape`…), and its `post` slot ends with a\n29: * animator's own invariant, engine/anim/character.test.ts); one puppet per actor, its layers made again when its\n30: * animator or their components do; every object it draws is under `root`, and a puppet given up waits as a spare for\n31: * the next actor of its build and body (`createActorPuppets` says why). A puppet is a skinned mesh of two draw calls:\n104:/** A puppet's part of the warm-up's key: its build, and its body when not `ACTOR_BODY`. */\n112:  /** With a puppet: its skeleton and world pose, and its eye (the head socket), m. */\n189:export function codeLabel(code: string, options: LabelOptions = {}): string {\n190-  const base = heldBase(code);\n191-  if (base !== null) return `Hold ${codeLabel(base, options)}`;\n192-  const button = PAD_BUTTONS.indexOf(code as (typeof PAD_BUTTONS)[number]);\n193-  if (button >= 0) return PAD_LABELS[options.pad ?? 'xbox'][button];\n194-  const stick = /^Pad(Left|Right)Stick(Up|Down|Left|Right)$/.exec(code);\n195-  if (stick) return `${stick[1][0]}