fp":{"command":"R=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/.research; cd $R/proto2; grep -n \"labs\" eslint.config.js tools/eslint/layers.ts | cut -c1-200 | head -30; sed -n 1,30p tools/eslint/layers.ts | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"400\\|600\\|maxLines\\|max-lines\" eslint.config.js tools/eslint/*.ts tools/cmd/check.ts tools/lib/*.ts 2>/dev/null | head -10 | cut -c1-200; cd $R/my-3dge; grep -n \"materials\" labs/playground/levels/house.ts | head -8 | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"materials\\|recipes\\|rooms:\" labs/playground/levels/street.ts | head -8 | cut -c1-200; sed -n 1,12p labs/playground/levels/plan.ts | cut -c1-200; cd $R/proto2; grep -n \"when\" engine/core/settings.ts | head -14 | cut -c1-210; grep -n \"reset\" engine/dev/inspector.ts engine/core/settings.ts | head -8 | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"movers\\|MOVER\\b\" engine/physics/*.ts | head -5 | cut -c1-200; sed -n 1,25p engine/physics/bodies.ts 2>/dev/null | cut -c1-200; ls engine/physics | head -30","description":"Check lint layers, level materials, settings semantics"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TasVDXSxP8c7oN6X1zCrfp","type":"tool_result","content":"tools/eslint/layers.ts:59:  regex: climb('labs', 'fixtures', 'tests', 'tools'),\ntools/eslint/layers.ts:61:    'engine code never imports labs/, fixtures/, tests/ or tools/: game content and test helpers stay outside the engine; pass what the engine needs in through its API (PLAN.\neslint.config.js:39:  'labs/**/*.{ts,js,mjs}',\n/**\n * @file The layer rules (PLAN.md §6.1; doctrines: WebGPU only, Reproducible): one `no-restricted-imports` block per\n * engine layer, naming what the layer may import, so a forbidden edge fails T0 with the rule and the way round it.\n *\n * Imports inside the engine are relative, so each pattern matches where an import climbs to: from\n * `engine/gfx/level/meshes.ts`, `../../physics/world` climbs into `physics`. The rule sees each relative source in its\n * shortest spelling from the importing file (`resolvingImports`, family.ts), so `../../../engine/physics/world` and\n * `./../../physics/world` are the same edge. Packages have single owners: only `physics/` imports Rapier, only `gfx/`\n * imports three.js, and `core/math.ts` alone takes three.js's math classes (`allowImportNames`). The sim-side\n * three.js ban itself is in simSide.ts, which also bans dynamic `import()`, a form these rules do not see. No engine\n * module imports the public barrels (`../index`, `../sim-api`, `..`): they are for game code, and re-export the\n * engine, so such an import is a cycle (WP 1.6). Tests (`*.test.ts`) may import anything.\n *\n * Invariants: every block lists its layer's whole policy (flat config keeps the last block that matches a file, so\n * the specific blocks, such as `core/math.ts` and `dev/bot.ts`, come after their layer's); the rule id is\n * `layer/no-restricted-imports`.\n *\n * @example\n * // engine/core/a.ts: import { World } from '../sim/world';\n * // → layer/no-restricted-imports: engine/core imports nothing from the other layers: …\n * @see tools/eslint/layers.test.ts\n */\nimport type { ESLint, Linter } from 'eslint';\nimport { family, resolvingImports } from './family';\n\n/** The plugin the layer blocks use: core's `no-restricted-imports`, resolving, as `layer/no-restricted-imports`. */\nexport const layerPlugin: ESLint.Plugin = resolvingImports(family('layer', 'no-restricted-imports'));\n\n/**\n * three.js's math classes, the only names `core/math.ts` takes from `three/webgpu` (§6.1); `Color` (from three.js's\ntools/lib/ciSummary.ts:5: * (`toResult`: the timing table and one finding per problem). Split from tools/cmd/ci.ts to keep each under 400 lines\ntools/lib/scenes.ts:6: * module that defines several). `x sim`, `x perf`, `x replay`, `x set` and `x audio` find scenes through it. Split from tools/cmd/sim.ts to keep each under 400 lines (ADR-0014 a\ntools/lib/ciShards.ts:101:    [...ms].sort(([a], [b]) => a.localeCompare(b)).map(([file, total]) => [file, Math.round(total / 6000) / 10]),\ntools/lib/perfBudget.ts:10: * 400 lines (ADR-0014 amendment 16).\ntools/lib/perfBudget.ts:38:export const DEFAULT_STEPS = { node: 600, ladder: 300, page: 120 } as const;\neslint.config.js:35:/** Code under these directories opens with a `@file` comment and stays under 400 lines (hard cap 600). */\neslint.config.js:71:      plugins: { jsdoc, 'hard-cap': families.family('hard-cap', 'max-lines') },\neslint.config.js:74:        'max-lines': ['warn', { max: 400 }],\neslint.config.js:75:        'hard-cap/max-lines': ['error', { max: 600 }],\ntools/lib/portVectors.ts:8: * tools/cmd/port.ts to keep each under 400 lines (ADR-0014 amendment 16).\n193:const block = (sides: string, tops: string, when: 'either' | 'blocking' = 'either') => ({ shape: 'block', materials: [sides, tops], castShadow: true, receiveShadow: true, cut: { height: 0.4375, wh\n195:const one = (shape: string, ...materials: string[]) => ({ shape, materials, castShadow: true, receiveShadow: true });\n3: * labs/playground/levels/site.ts lays on the block, each drawn in its own surface (their entries' recipes):\n50:const floor = (material: string) => ({ shape: 'surface', materials: [material], castShadow: false, receiveShadow: true }) as const; // prettier-ignore\n56:  recipes: {\n59:    gallery: { shape: 'slab', materials: ['material:concrete', 'material:concrete'], castShadow: false, receiveShadow: true }, // prettier-ignore\n62:defineLevel('level:driveway', { text: DRIVEWAY_TEXT, file: FILE, recipes: { floor: floor('material:concrete') } });\n63:defineLevel('level:path', { text: PATH_TEXT, file: FILE, recipes: { floor: floor('material:flagstone') } });\n/**\n * @file Storey plans (PLAN.md WP 13.18): how the playground writes its buildings as storeys (level format 2,\n * engine/world/level/parse.ts) from rectangles in metres, not character by character. `new Plan(width, depth, tile)`\n * is one storey's map, every tile void (`~`) until painted; `fill(rect, char)` paints a rectangle's tiles, `box(rect,\n * edge, inside)` its edge one tile thick and its inside, `line(rect, char)` a run along a wall (a door, a window, a\n * railing); `levelText(header, storeys)` writes the level's text: its front matter, then each storey's block (its keys:\n * `storey`, `base`, `height` or a roof's) and map, bottom first. A rectangle is `[x0, z0, x1, z1]` in the map's metres,\n * its north-west corner at 0, 0, +X east and +Z south (PLAN.md §6.3), on whole tiles.\n *\n * Invariants: pure; a rectangle off whole tiles or outside the map is refused, naming it and the fix; later paint\n * covers earlier, so a plan reads as the order a builder works in: walls, then rooms, then doors and windows.\n *\n14: * nothing when anything is wrong. Values are plain data, stored frozen all the way down, defaults included (each a\n18: * `when` says when a change takes effect; `set` reports it.\n28: * settings.set('crowd', 400).when; // 'now'\n74:/** What `set` reports: the new and previous values, and when the change takes effect. */\n79:  when: When;\n93:  when: When;\n104:  /** Validates and sets a value; returns what changed and when it takes effect. */\n108:  /** Back to the default: one setting, or every setting (overrides included) when no path is given. */\n154:  when: {\n158:    description: 'When a change takes effect: at once, for what spawns next, or when the scene next starts.',\n164:      'True when it changes only how the game looks or performs: kept out of the hash, captures and replays.',\n196:/** Text from a URL or the command line as a value of `field`'s type; undefined when it cannot be. */\n258:      return { path, value, previous, when: field.when ?? 'now', view: field.view ?? false };\n363:          when: field.when ?? 'now',\nengine/core/settings.ts:4: * `createSettings` makes a store with a validated `get` and `set`, URL parameters, JSON export (`toJSON`, a preset)\nengine/core/settings.ts:8: * A preset is path → value JSON. A scene or variant overrides settings for its lifetime with `override(values)`;\nengine/core/settings.ts:12: * Invariants: an unknown path is an error naming the closest: `CORE_UNKNOWN_SETTING` from `get`, `set` and `reset`,\nengine/core/settings.ts:13: * and one of the problems of `CORE_BAD_SETTING` (a bad value) from presets, URL parameters and overrides, which apply\nengine/core/settings.ts:21: * shardfall's presets and scoped overrides (`shardfall:crates/pav_core/src/params.rs:63-259`).\nengine/core/settings.ts:58:    doc: 'Raised by the settings store (engine/core/settings.ts) for an unknown path in `get`, `set`, `setText`, `reset` or `sim.get`. Presets, URL parameters and overrides \nengine/core/settings.ts:63:    doc: 'Raised by `set`, `setText`, `load`, `fromUrl` and `override` (engine/core/settings.ts). A preset or a URL with any problem applies nothing, and every problem is li\nengine/core/settings.ts:109:  reset(path?: string): void;\nengine/physics/bodies.ts:2: * @file Bodies and props (PLAN.md WP 4.1; doctrines: Common ground, Reproducible): what scenes build props, movers\nengine/physics/bodies.ts:3: * and triggers with, on the physics world (engine/physics/world.ts), in plain terms. Scenes keep the state (movers,\nengine/physics/bodies.ts:28: * `crates/pav_core/src/behaviors.rs:14-75` (`drive`, movers) and `entity.rs:118-150` (`MoverDef::amount`).\nengine/physics/bodies.ts:36: * moverPose({ ...MOVER, origin: [0, 0, 0], offset: [6, 0, 0], period: 4 }, 2).position.x; // 6: the far end\nengine/physics/bodies.ts:199:export const MOVER: Readonly<Mover> = freezeValue(\n/**\n * @file Bodies and props (PLAN.md WP 4.1; doctrines: Common ground, Reproducible): what scenes build props, movers\n * and triggers with, on the physics world (engine/physics/world.ts), in plain terms. Scenes keep the state (movers,\n * what a trigger holds) in components and call these from systems; fixtures/scenes/physics-props is the worked example.\n *\n * - **Props.** `addBox(physics, size, spec)`, `addBall`, `addCapsule` and `addCylinder` add a dynamic body of one\n *   shape, sized as three.js sizes its geometries, made of `PROP_MATERIAL` (the prototype's crates and barrels) unless\n *   the spec says otherwise. Stacks stand; bodies at rest fall asleep (a settled stack within a second) and wake when\n *   touched, and `readBody(id).sleeping` says which. `applyTorqueImpulse` turns a body (N·m·s); `knock(physics, id,\n *   from)` is the prototype's knock: a push away from `from` across the ground and up, the same for every mass, and a\n *   tip toward the push with a twist.\n * - **Movers** (shardfall's): kinematic bodies whose pose is a function of time, `moverPose(mover, t)`: back and forth\n *   along `offset` (waiting `hold` at the ends, eased when `smooth`), turning about +Y at `spin`. `driveMover` sets\n *   the velocities that bring the body there when the world steps, so the character controller carries riders, and\n *   reads only the component and the body's pose, so a restore continues exactly. Call it in the phase `ai`, before\n *   the actors move, with the world (`w.time` in step k is k·dt, the step's end: shardfall's `pose((tick + 1) · dt)`).\n * - **Triggers.** `addSensor(physics, shape, spec)` adds a fixed (or kinematic) body whose collider blocks nothing and\n *   detects every dynamic and kinematic body it overlaps; `sensorHits` lists those as of the last step, and\n *   `updateTrigger(physics, trigger)` compares them with `trigger.inside` and returns who entered and left, for the\n *   scene to emit as events. Fixed bodies (the level) never trip one.\n * The lost-body rescue is engine/physics/rescue.ts's (split from here at its cap, WP 13.16).\n *\n * Invariants: no state beside Rapier's and the caller's (`trigger.inside`, the mover's fields); lists are in id order.\n * A mover's colliders sit on its body's origin.\n *\nbinding.ts\nbodies.ts\ncapture.ts\ncarry.ts\ncharacter.ts\ncharacterBody.ts\ncrowd.ts\nfeel.ts\ngroups.ts\nheightfield.ts\nhull.ts\njoints.ts\nledge.ts\nmove.ts\nmovement\nparams.ts\nqueries.ts\nragdoll.ts\nrescue.ts\nroom.ts\ntrimesh.ts\nworld.ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"5dc994e2-1d9f-44f2-a6e6-dbccb1679e9f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:00:58.001Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"tools/eslint/layers.ts:59:  regex: climb('labs', 'fixtures', 'tests', 'tools'),\ntools/eslint/layers.ts:61:    'engine code never imports labs/, fixtures/, tests/ or tools/: game content and test helpers stay outside the engine; pass what the engine needs in through its API (PLAN.\neslint.config.js:39:  'labs/**/*.{ts,js,mjs}',\n/**\n * @file The layer rules (PLAN.md §6.1; doctrines: WebGPU only, Reproducible): one `no-restricted-imports` block per\n * engine layer, naming what the layer may import, so a forbidden edge fails T0 with the rule and the way round it.\n *\n * Imports inside the engine are relative, so each pattern matches where an import climbs to: from\n * `engine/gfx