ds) in components and call these from systems; fixtures/scenes/physics-props is the worked example.\n *\n * - **Props.** `addBox(physics, size, spec)`, `addBall`, `addCapsule` and `addCylinder` add a dynamic body of one\n *   shape, sized as three.js sizes its geometries, made of `PROP_MATERIAL` (the prototype's crates and barrels) unless\n *   the spec says otherwise. Stacks stand; bodies at rest fall asleep (a settled stack within a second) and wake when\n *   touched, and `readBody(id).sleeping` says which. `applyTorqueImpulse` turns a body (N·m·s); `knock(physics, id,\n *   from)` is the prototype's knock: a push away from `from` across the ground and up, the same for every mass, and a\n *   tip toward the push with a twist.\n * - **Movers** (shardfall's): kinematic bodies whose pose is a function of time, `moverPose(mover, t)`: back and forth\n *   along `offset` (waiting `hold` at the ends, eased when `smooth`), turning about +Y at `spin`. `driveMover` sets\n *   the velocities that bring the body there when the world steps, so the character controller carries riders, and\n *   reads only the component and the body's pose, so a restore continues exactly. Call it in the phase `ai`, before\n *   the actors move, with the world (`w.time` in step k is k·dt, the step's end: shardfall's `pose((tick + 1) · dt)`).\n * - **Triggers.** `addSensor(physics, shape, spec)` adds a fixed (or kinematic) body whose collider blocks nothing and\n *   detects every dynamic and kinematic body it overlaps; `sensorHits` lists those as of the last step, and\n *   `updateTrigger(physics, trigger)` compares them with `trigger.inside` and returns who entered and left, for the\n *   scene to emit as events. Fixed bodies (the level) never trip one.\n * The lost-body rescue is engine/physics/rescue.ts's (split from here at its cap, WP 13.16).\n *\n * Invariants: no state beside Rapier's and the caller's (`trigger.inside`, the mover's fields); lists are in id order.\n * A mover's colliders sit on its body's origin.\n *\nbinding.ts\nbodies.ts\ncapture.ts\ncarry.ts\ncharacter.ts\ncharacterBody.ts\ncrowd.ts\nfeel.ts\ngroups.ts\nheightfield.ts\nhull.ts\njoints.ts\nledge.ts\nmove.ts\nmovement\nparams.ts\nqueries.ts\nragdoll.ts\nrescue.ts\nroom.ts\ntrimesh.ts\nworld.ts","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TasVDXSxP8c7oN6X1zCrfp","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBzrAEFCLcBbguFsQ7V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EDS722sbbqDeh7NbQ14top","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"R=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/.research; cd $R/proto; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='labs/game/vis/world.ts'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    w.systems.add('game.foes', (world: World<any>) => {\"\"\",\"\"\"    w.spawn({ netProbe: { last: -1, count: 0 } } as never);\n    w.systems.add('game.netProbe', (world: World<any>, intents: any) => {\n      const net = intents['game:net'];\n      const [e] = world.query('netProbe') as any[];\n      if (net && net.seq !== e.netProbe.last) { e.netProbe.last = net.seq; e.netProbe.count += 1; }\n    }, { phase: 'intents' });\n    w.systems.add('game.foes', (world: World<any>) => {\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"defineComponent('health',\",\"defineComponent('netProbe', { description: 'probe', fields: { last: { type: 'integer', default: -1, description: 'x' }, count: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'y' } } });\\ndefineComponent('health',\")\ns=s.replace(\"size: [320, 320], seed: 7\",\"size: [120, 120], seed: 7\")\ns=s.replace(\"...Array.from({ length: 36 }\",\"...Array.from({ length: 0 }\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode $R/probe/bvis.mjs $R/probe/vis.html 2>&1 | tail -1; cat > $R/probe/nettest.py <<'EOF'\nimport sys, json, time\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nARGS = ['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-angle=swiftshader']\npath = sys.argv[1]\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n    b = p.chromium.launch(args=ARGS)\n    pg = b.new_page(viewport={'width':640,'height':360})\n    errs=[]\n    pg.on('pageerror', lambda e: errs.append(str(e)[:400]))\n    pg.goto('file://'+path+'?gfx.governor=false&quality=low')\n    pg.wait_for_function('window.__engine && window.__engine.ready === true', timeout=170000)\n    pg.wait_for_function('window.__game', timeout=60000)\n    # the page-side path: the page input's virtual device holds a custom intent for the next steps\n    for seq in range(1,6):\n        payload = {'seq': seq, 'foes': [[i, 10.5+i, 3.25, 1.5, 2] for i in range(30)]}\n        pg.evaluate(\"(p)=>window.__game.input.virtual.axis('game:net', p)\", payload)\n        pg.wait_for_timeout(1500)\n    print('probe', pg.evaluate(\"JSON.stringify(window.__engine.state('netProbe').entities[0].netProbe)\"))\n    print('tick', pg.evaluate(\"window.__engine.info().run ? JSON.stringify(window.__engine.info().run) : ''\"))\n    # restart with a sim setting kept, the page stays\n    h0 = pg.evaluate(\"window.__engine.hash()\")\n    pg.evaluate(\"window.__engine.seed(5)\")\n    pg.wait_for_timeout(1500)\n    print('after seed', pg.evaluate(\"window.__engine.seed()\"), 'ready', pg.evaluate(\"window.__engine.ready\"), 'errs', pg.evaluate(\"JSON.stringify(window.__engine.errors)\")[:300])\n    print('lastDevice', pg.evaluate(\"window.__game.input.lastDevice\"), 'codes', pg.evaluate(\"JSON.stringify(window.__game.input.bindings.codes('fire'))\"), 'prompt', pg.evaluate(\"window.__game.input.prompt('fire')\"))\n    print('pageerrs', errs[:4])\n    b.close()\nEOF\ncd $R/probe && timeout 200 python3 nettest.py $R/probe/vis.html 2>&1 | cut -c1-500","description":"Test custom intents and restart from a running page","timeout":280000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4890,"cache_read_input_tokens":478903,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4890},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5