{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YBoErH9oFRtHSpFo5LgDJa","type":"tool_result","content":"  publicApi: true,\n  /** \"Ask the entry, never the id\" (tools/eslint/askTheEntry.ts): on since WP 1.2, with the registry. */\n  askTheEntry: true,\n};\n\n/** Code under these directories opens with a `@file` comment and stays under 400 lines (hard cap 600). */\nconst AGENT_READABLE = [\n  'engine/**/*.{ts,js,mjs}',\n  'tools/**/*.{ts,js,mjs}',\n  'labs/**/*.{ts,js,mjs}',\n  'tests/**/*.{ts,js,mjs}',\n  '.claude/hooks/**/*.ts',\n];\n\n/** Builds the whole config; `switches` defaults to `SWITCHES` (tests turn every switch on). */\nexport function configure(switches = SWITCHES) {\n  return [\n    {\n      name: 'ignores',\n      ignores: ['out/**', 'dist/**', '.cache/**', 'test-results/**', 'lean/**', '.claude/worktrees/**'],\n    },\n    ...tseslint.configs.recommended,\n    {\n      name: 'typescript: unused names',\n      rules: {\n        // The usual exceptions: a leading underscore marks a name unused on purpose; `{ dropped, ...rest }` omits a key.\n        '@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars': [\n          'error',\n          {\n            argsIgnorePattern: '^_',\n            varsIgnorePattern: '^_',\n            caughtErrorsIgnorePattern: '^_',\n            ignoreRestSiblings: true,\n          },\n        ],\n      },\n    },\n    { name: 'globals', languageOptions: { globals: { ...globals.browser, ...globals.node } } },\n    {\n      name: 'agent-readable: file comments and size (PLAN.md §6.8)',\n      files: AGENT_READABLE,\n7: * `engine/dev/bot.ts` and the gallery's scene (`engine/dev/galleryScene.ts`), every lab's scenes and cast (the box's,\n8: * the starter game's, a game's own), the box's and the playground's sound events (labs/box/sounds/events.ts,\n9: * labs/playground/sounds/{events,ground}.ts: the scenes' `sounds`), and the fixture scenes; `*.test.ts` files are\n54:  'labs/*/scenes/**',\n55:  'labs/*/cast/**',\n56:  'labs/box/sounds/events.ts',\n57:  'labs/playground/sounds/events.ts',\n58:  'labs/playground/sounds/ground.ts',\n59:  'fixtures/scenes/**',\ntools/eslint/index.ts:6: * Families: layers.ts (the layer rules), publicApi.ts (game code sees only the barrels), simSide.ts (the\ntools/eslint/index.ts:24:export { publicApiBlocks } from './publicApi';\ntools/eslint/layers.ts:11: * module imports the public barrels (`../index`, `../sim-api`, `..`): they are for game code, and re-export the\ntools/eslint/layers.ts:78:/** The public barrels from inside the engine: `../index`, `../sim-api`, or `..` (engine/ itself, its index). */\ntools/eslint/layers.ts:80:  regex: '^(?:(?:\\\\.\\\\./)+(?:index|sim-api)(?:\\\\.ts)?|\\\\.\\\\.(?:/\\\\.\\\\.)*)$',\ntools/eslint/layers.ts:82:    'engine code never imports the public barrels (engine/index.ts, engine/sim-api.ts): they re-export the engine, so the import makes a cycle; import the module that declare\ntools/eslint/layers.ts:267:    name: 'sim-api.ts',\ntools/eslint/layers.ts:268:    files: ['engine/sim-api.ts'],\ntools/eslint/publicApi.ts:3: * only through its barrels, `engine/index.ts` (pages) and `engine/sim-api.ts` (sim-side code), and never three.js or\ntools/eslint/publicApi.ts:8: * code (every lab's `scenes/` and `cast/`, `fixtures/scenes/`) takes only `engine/sim-api.ts`, so `x sim` runs it in\ntools/eslint/publicApi.ts:16: * is engine/index.ts); sim-side game code may not.\ntools/eslint/publicApi.ts:18: * Invariants: switched on by WP 1.6 with the barrels (`SWITCHES.publicApi` in eslint.config.js); switched off, the\ntools/eslint/publicApi.ts:23: * // → public-api/no-restricted-imports: 'Vector3' import from … Import it from engine/sim-api.ts …\ntools/eslint/publicApi.ts:24: * @see tools/eslint/publicApi.test.ts\n5: * `MouseMiddle`, `MouseBack`, `MouseForward`, `WheelUp` and `WheelDown`; gamepad buttons follow the W3C standard\n20: * Invariants: `isCode` accepts exactly the codes above, touch codes aside; `deviceOf` is `gamepad` for `Pad…`, `mouse`\n24: * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/emberdeep/61-controls.js:28-116` (`bindingCode`, `PAD_LABELS`, `codeLabel`), with\n28: * deviceOf('PadSouth'); // 'gamepad'\n38:export type DeviceKind = 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch' | 'virtual';\n54:/** A gamepad family, for labels. */\n57:/** The W3C standard gamepad buttons by index, named by position. */\n143:  if (code.startsWith('Pad')) return 'gamepad';\n148:const PAD_LABELS: Record<PadStyle, readonly string[]> = {\n173:/** The family of a gamepad, from its `Gamepad.id` (vendor 054c is Sony, 057e Nintendo). */\n65:  readonly style: PadStyle;\n75:  let style: PadStyle = 'xbox';\n92:    get style() {\n93:      return style;\n116:        style = padStyle(pad.id);\n11: * - `bot(plan)`: plays the player with the bot (engine/dev/bot.ts) over the scene's level: the goals `to`, a `tour`,\n12- *   `back`, the stop condition `until` (`component.field`), `steps`, a `trace`, its options; through `step`, so each\n13- *   step is recorded (`input.record()` replays it). With `seeds` (`1-20`, `5`, `3,7,9`), a sweep from fresh sessions\n14- *   of the scene with this run's recorded settings instead, the run itself left alone: one row, a run per seed.\n--\n93:    if (!scene.level && !scene.site) throw codeError('SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT', { where: '__engine.bot()', value: scene.id, expected: 'a scene with a level or a site for the bot to read (defineScene({ lev\n94-    const level = scene.site ? getSite(scene.site, h.registry) : getLevel(scene.level!, h.registry);\n95-    if (seeds !== undefined) {\n96-      const settings = h.session.settings.values({ view: false });\n/**\n * @file The bot (PLAN.md WP 5.6, §5.6, I-38; doctrines: Agent-operable, Reproducible): plays a scene's player through\n * intents, as a virtual device would, for play longer and more varied than a scripted replay (soaks, navigation smoke).\n * It is sim-side: it reads the world and writes intents through the session's step, so its play is recorded and\n * replays as anyone's does; its own sums run under the sim's math (engine/core/simMath.ts), alike in Node and a page.\n *\n * - **Navigation** (`Bot`): toward its goal down the level's flow field (engine/world/nav.ts, to the goal's nearest\n *   open tile) or a site's (engine/dev/botNav.ts), the last `near` metres straight at it, as one of `headings`\n *   directions (few, so its intents change seldom); there within `reach` (on a site, and 1 m of its height). A closed\n *   door its way runs into it opens as a player does (`runBot` presses use: `closedDoorAhead`, WP 13.18). On a site\n *   it walks round the scene's props, and held by one its way does not know (a door left open), finds it again.\n *   With `look` its view turns the way it walks (`LOOK_TURN`), its keys' frame (`cam`) the heading.\n * - **Stuck, measured along the wanted direction**: each step, how far the feet went along the way it asked for, or up\n *   (a ladder). Under `progress` m/s while it asks to move, the held time grows (else it falls at twice the pace):\n *   pressed against a wall, a body jitters back and forth faster than \"not moving\" allows, so only the way it wants\n *   counts. Held 0.45 s, it sidesteps 1.3 rad to one side; 0.9 s, 2.2 rad; 1.5 s, it jumps and tries the other side.\n *   Held `stuck` seconds in all on one goal, it is `stuck` (`held`).\n * - **Watchdog**: a goal whose walking distance has not fallen by `gain` in `patience` seconds is given up (`stuck`,\n *   `no progress`); one no route leads to, at once (`no route`).\n * - **Runs** (`runBot`): the goals `to` in order, or a tour of `tour` open tiles both ways reachable from the start\n *   (drawn from the bot's own stream, `derive(seed, 'bot')`, never the world's), then `back` to the start; it stops\n *   when all are reached (`arrived`), stuck, at the stop condition `until` (`stopped`: a function of the world, or\n *   `component.field`, true on some entity) or at the budget of `steps` (`timeout`). The report: