{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RuvtmSXbFT5cZyLN4HFcJ4","type":"tool_result","content":"x describe: ok: material: 18 fields, 29 entries\nMaterials as data with three.js's classic parameters (color, map, roughness, emissive, flags); the engine decides how to draw them.\nfallback: material:default\nids: material:asphalt, material:barrel, material:barrelLid, material:barrelStaves, material:blobShadow, material:brick, material:carpet, material:checker, material:cloth,\n  description: string, = \"\": What it is for, in plain sentences.\n  color: string, = \"#ffffff\": The base colour, hex; it multiplies the map (three.js's color).\n  map: any, = null: The texture generator that fills the maps: a texture id ('texture:brick'), or { texture, seed, params, size, look, re...\n  roughness: number, = 1, 0..1: Microfacet roughness, 0 (mirror) to 1 (matte), for the styles that shade with it (pbr, WP 7.2).\n  metalness: number, = 0, 0..1: How metallic, 0 to 1, for the styles that shade with it (pbr, WP 7.2).\n  emissive: string, = \"#000000\": The colour it glows with, hex, unaffected by light; it multiplies the map's emissive, as three.js's emis...\n  emissiveIntensity: number, = 1, 0..inf: A multiplier on emissive.\n  normalScale: number, = 1, 0..8: How deep the map's relief looks: scales the normal map from its height (0 turns it off).\n  unlit: boolean, = false: Drawn without lights (glTF unlit, three.js MeshBasicMaterial): color × map as it is; for glows, skies and mark...\n  transparent: boolean, = false: Blended with what is behind it, by opacity.\n  opacity: number, = 1, 0..1: Its opacity when transparent.\n  alphaTest: number, = 0, 0..1: Texels with alpha below this are not drawn (cut-outs).\n  side: string, = \"front\", one of \"front\"|\"back\"|\"double\": Which faces are drawn.\n  flatShading: boolean, = false: Faceted: one normal per triangle.\n… 5 more in out/describe/material/output.txt\nreport: out/describe/material/report.json\n145: * cape (`secondary`: the component the view hangs on his puppet, engine/sim/reactions.ts; the cape WP 6.2 carried\n186:  /** His cape, the component `secondary` (engine/sim/reactions.ts): the view hangs it on his puppet and swings it. */\n187:  secondary: Object.freeze({ cape: true, color: '#7a2430' }),\n9: * hides no switch). It keeps that thing and its prompt in the actor's `interactor` component, which the page shows with\n12: * Usable things are asked of their entries, never their ids: `defineUsable(component, { prompt, use })` says how an\n14: * its own `use` has a `prompt`, or when a player can carry it (dynamic, at most `CARRY_MASS`). Its `use` hook gets the\n59:  prompt(w: World, id: number, user: number): string | null;\n63:/** The component `interactor`: what a player would use, its prompt, what it carries, and when it last used. */\n66:  prompt: string;\n75:    description: 'How an entity holding a component is used (doors, switches): its prompt and its use (WP 13.16).',\n77:      prompt: { type: 'function', default: () => null, description: '(w, id, user) => the HUD’s words, or null.' },\n9: * hides no switch). It keeps that thing and its prompt in the actor's `interactor` component, which the page shows with\n22: * A use takes its press: `interactor.usedAt` is the step, and the actors' input leaves it out of the rides'\n26: * Invariants: everything is in components (the interactor, the props', the doors'); candidates in id order, the\n63:/** The component `interactor`: what a player would use, its prompt, what it carries, and when it last used. */\n71:/** Declares the kinds `usable` and `strikable` and the component `interactor` on `registry` (once). */\n101:  defineComponent('interactor', { description: 'A player’s use (WP 13.16).', fields }, registry);","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"1facdb04-528d-47f0-8927-fc3a17837df1","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:11:21.509Z","tool_