{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDaar3axQyuLzhXfoHY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Those checks confirmed L1/R1 map to the shoulder buttons, the secondary chains are only hair, cape and tail, the iPhone WebKit profile lacks WebGPU so the touch gate can't depend on the engine, and the harness's Enter poke needs a direct listener. I'll fold these into the plan, along with the cutscene, dialogue, side-activity and shared-machine gaps.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2111,"cache_read_input_tokens":613804,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2111},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"d4ded452-16c0-43ea-85ab-05c6c9cd362b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:20:06.051Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDaaWCHQd59jqEVbjaw","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDaar3axQyuLzhXfoHY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JAozbJUrjmEKN7WYstCMzP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,count)\n\n# small side activities after the funicular section\nrep(\"\"\"top the cable snaps: a large jump prompt, then a scramble up a ladder with the car falling away behind you. Failing the\nprompt costs a checkpoint, not much else.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"top the cable snaps: a large jump prompt, then a scramble up a ladder with the car falling away behind you. Failing the\nprompt costs a checkpoint, not much else.\n\n### 4.4 Small things\n\n- **Claims Practice** (Shingle): a coin-op gallery on a rotten pier, the Salvor's pride. 60 s, cardboard claimants on tracks\n  (`defineThing`, `spawnThing`), hit the frauds, spare the widows. Score pays shillings, and beating it gives a free\n  Firepower level. Enter and leave through a prompt, in the same world.\n- **Glass floats:** 12 blue glass net floats hung about the island. They shatter when shot (`addBreakables`). All 12: the Salvor\n  gives you a rare gem worth 5,000. Progress shows in the Claim File.\n- **The ledger dials** (Vault): three big number wheels, one on screen at a time. The numbers are in the 3 required ledger pages,\n  which Wren reads aloud on request. Left and right pick a wheel, up and down turn it, mouse clicks and wheel too.\n- **The seal:** a grey blob-rig seal in a net on the Shingle. Shoot the net rope to free it, and it barks and flops off. Payoff in §7.3.\n\"\"\")\n\n# pad codes under controls table\nrep(\"\"\"With keyboard and mouse, when not aiming, a left click on a thing whose prompt is showing uses it.\"\"\",\"\"\"Engine codes: Cross `PadSouth`, Circle `PadEast`, Square `PadWest`, Triangle `PadNorth`, L1 `PadLeftShoulder`, R1 `PadRightShoulder`, L2\n`PadLeftTrigger`, R2 `PadRightTrigger`, L3 `PadLeftStick`, R3 `PadRightStick`, D-pad `PadUp PadDown PadLeft PadRight`, Create `PadSelect`,\nOptions `PadStart` (the system `pause`), sticks `PadLeftStickUp` and so on, wheel `WheelUp` `WheelDown`, mouse `MouseLeft` `MouseRight`.\n\nWith keyboard and mouse, when not aiming, a left click on a thing whose prompt is showing uses it.\"\"\")\n\n# saves verified\nrep(\"\"\"kept with\n  `createStore` (localStorage, which works on `file://`).\"\"\",\"\"\"kept with\n  `createStore` (localStorage, which survives a reload on `file://` [verified]).\"\"\")\n\n# Last stand wording\nrep(\"\"\"Menu entry \"Last Stand\" plays it solo, with up to 3 AI \"temps\" you may hire (a simple bot on the same replica path,\nwhich also serves attract mode).\"\"\",\"\"\"Menu entry \"Last Stand\" plays it solo in `game:world` with no reload, with up to 3 AI \"temps\" you may hire (a simple bot on the same\nreplica path, which also serves attract mode).\"\"\")\n\n# curl base and client\nrep(\"\"\"repository (it is over 5 GB); `curl` these three into a folder under `out/`, plus the client:\n`lib/hub/session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`. Keep `session.js` as `labs/game/net/session.client.txt` so lint leaves it alone.\"\"\",\"\"\"repository (it is over 5 GB). `curl -fsSO` what you need from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`:\n`harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into a folder under `out/`; `examples/arena.html`, a small shared-world game, to read; and\n`session.js`, saved as `labs/game/net/session.client.txt` so lint leaves it alone. (The hub replaces an unmodified client with each new version.)\"\"\")\n\n# card input direct\nrep(\"\"\"controls, the countdown from the `card` event. Cross or Enter is `AIHub.answer('ready')`, Triangle or T is `AIHub.answer('more')`. It changes nothing in the round.\"\"\",\"\"\"controls, the countdown from the `card` event. Cross or Enter is `AIHub.answer('ready')`, Triangle or T is `AIHub.answer('more')`, and a tap or click on the card works too. It changes nothing in the round. **Listen for Enter with a plain `window` `keydown` listener added right after `connect()`, not through frame-sampled input:** the harness pokes Enter into the frame and allows 3 s, and frames are slow on the software renderer. Poll the pad in `requestAnimationFrame` here too.\"\"\")\n\n# gate\nrep(\"\"\"- **Touch-only devices** (`matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` with no pad connected): no touch controls at all. Always pass `touch=off`. Show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button. Attract mode runs behind it. A pad connecting or a key pressed dismisses the gate.\n- **No WebGPU:** a styled message saying which browsers have it. No WebGL fallback.\"\"\",\"\"\"- **Touch-only devices** (`matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` with no pad connected): no touch controls at all. Always pass `touch=off` [verified: no touch UI appears]. Show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button. Attract mode runs behind it. A pad connecting or a key pressed dismisses the gate. **Build the gate in plain DOM, created before `createEngine`,** since `engine.ui` is null when the renderer can't start. A Chromium phone profile on `file://` has WebGPU and runs attract [verified]; the WebKit iPhone profile has no WebGPU at all [verified], so there the gate shows over a dark page with no attract, and the engine's own error overlay stays hidden.\n- **No WebGPU, not touch:** a styled message saying which browsers have it (Chrome or Edge, recent Safari). No WebGL fallback.\n- **Dialogue and cutscenes.** `createDialog`: `modal: false` with `auto` for radio, Tannoy and barks, so play goes on; modal for the shop patter and story talk. Cutscenes run in the world, with own cameras (`node x new camera`, `camera.set(code, { blend: true })`), `modal: () => true`, a letterbox through `post.combine`, and always skippable (hold Circle or Esc). Keep them short: 20 s at most, and most are under 10.\"\"\")\n\n# burst fix\nrep(\"\"\"`removeActor`, then `spawnActor` on the spot with `body:parishionerBurst` (head parts removed, a neck stump, a `Chain` from `secondary`), with a splash of brine to hide the swap.\"\"\",\"\"\"`removeActor`, then `spawnActor` on the spot with `body:parishionerBurst` (head parts removed, a neck stump, and for the lamprey the `secondary` component's hair chain, `{ hair: 'ponytail', color: '#5ff0c4' }`, the only chain that hangs at head height), with a splash of brine to hide the swap.\"\"\")\n\n# lights\nrep(\"\"\"- **Effects (`defineEmitter`).**\"\"\",\"\"\"- **Light.** Lanterns and braziers (`prop:lantern`, `prop:brazier`, your own props with light spots) make the night; the engine's pool picks the nearest. Group them with `switchGroup` for scripted blackouts. Every interior needs an amber pool to walk toward.\n- **Effects (`defineEmitter`).**\"\"\")\n\n# shared machine\nrep(\"\"\"- **Don't `git init` or commit.** The dev folder already sits inside the harness's repository. Skip the commit steps in AGENTS.md.\"\"\",\"\"\"- **Don't `git init` or commit.** The dev folder already sits inside the harness's repository. Skip the commit steps in AGENTS.md.\n- **You share this machine.** Keep every file you make inside your folder, not in `/tmp` or a parent; don't read the folders beside yours. Prefer `file://` and the engine's headless tools. A server only for the hub harness (§17), on a port the OS picks. Stop only what you started, by PID: never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`.\"\"\")\n\n# iPhone + tally in tests\nrep(\"\"\"- A phone profile (`devices['Pixel 7']`, touch) shows the gate with the Settings button, with attract running, and no touch controls.\"\"\",\"\"\"- A Chromium phone profile (`devices['Pixel 7']`) shows the gate with the Settings button, with attract running, and no touch controls. WebKit's iPhone profile shows the gate with no WebGPU and no error text.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Visual checks:** a few `--png` shots at 1920×1080 (the look, the Case, a boss, the HUD from far away), `node x gallery` for bodies and props, `node x qa geo tex audio`, `npm run check`.\"\"\",\"\"\"**Visual checks:** a few `--png` shots at 1920×1080 (the look, the Case, a boss, the HUD from far away), `node x gallery` for bodies and props, `node x qa geo tex audio`, `npm run check`.\n\n**Keep a tally as you go** in `labs/game/README.md`: issues testing caught, how many were critical, the most and least helpful tests. TASK.md's Testing Feedback asks for exactly that, and it's hard to reconstruct at the end.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint(len(s))\nEOF\ngrep -n \"exit-interview\\|GameTitle\\|claude-opus\\|20261104\\|TODO\" PLAN.md | head; grep -c \"\" PLAN.md; awk 'length > 400' PLAN.md | wc -l","description":"Apply the verified corrections to the plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2111,"cache_read_input_tokens":613804,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2111},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"ba1f84fe-3f97-4d69-9225-4dc819690164","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:20:33.392Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDaaWCHQd59jqEVbjaw","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JAozbJUrjmEKN7WYstCMzP":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,count)\n\n# small side activities after the funicular section\nrep(\"\"\"top the cable snaps: a large jump prompt, then a scramble up a ladder with the car falling away behind you. Failing the\nprompt costs a checkpoint, not much else.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"top the cable snaps: a large jump prompt, then a scramble up a ladder with the car falling away behind you. Failing the\nprompt costs a checkpoint, not much else.\n\n### 4.4 Small things\n\n- **Claims Practice** (Shingle): a coin-op gallery on a rotten pier, the Salvor's pride. 60 s, cardboard claimants on tracks\n  (`defineThing`, `spawnThing`), hit the frauds, spare the widows. Score pays shillings, and beating it gives a free\n  Firepower level. Enter and leave through a prompt, in the same world.\n- **Glass floats:** 12 blue glass net floats hung about the island. They shatter when shot (`addBreakables`). All 12: the Salvor\n  gives you a rare gem worth 5,000. Progress shows in the Claim File.\n- **The ledger dials** (Vault): three big number wheels, one on screen at a time. The numbers are in the 3 required ledger pages,\n  which Wren reads aloud on request. Left and right pick a wheel, up and down turn it, mouse clicks and wheel too.\n- **The seal:** a grey blob-rig seal in a net on the Shingle. Shoot the net rope to free it, and it barks and flops off. Payoff in §7.3.\n\"\"\")\n\n# pad codes under controls table\nrep(\"\"\"With keyboard and mouse, when not aiming, a left click on a thing whose prompt is showing uses it.\"\"\",\"\"\"Engine codes: Cross `PadSouth`, Circle `PadEast`, Square `PadWest`, Triangle `PadNorth`, L1 `PadLeftShoulder`, R1 `PadRightShoulder`, L2\n`PadLeftTrigger`, R2 `PadRightTrigger`, L3 `PadLeftStick`, R3 `PadRightStick`, D-pad `PadUp PadDown PadLeft PadRight`, Create `PadSelect`,\nOptions `PadStart` (the system `pause`), sticks `PadLeftStickUp` and so on, wheel `WheelUp` `WheelDown`, mouse `MouseLeft` `MouseRight`.\n\nWith keyboard and mouse, when not aiming, a left click on a thing whose prompt is showing uses it.\"\"\")\n\n# saves verified\nrep(\"\"\"kept with\n  `createStore` (localStorage, which works on `file://`).\"\"\",\"\"\"kept with\n  `createStore` (localStorage, which survives a reload on `file://` [verified]).\"\"\")\n\n# Last stand wording\nrep(\"\"\"Menu entry \"Last Stand\" plays it solo, with up to 3 AI \"temps\" you may hire (a simple bot on the same replica path,\nwhich also serves attract mode).\"\"\",\"\"\"Menu entry \"Last Stand\" plays it solo in `game:world` with no reload, with up to 3 AI \"temps\" you may hire (a simple bot on the same\nreplica path, which also serves attract mode).\"\"\")\n\n# curl base and client\nrep(\"\"\"repository (it is over 5 GB); `curl` these three into a folder under `out/`, plus the client:\n`lib/hub/session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js`. Keep `session.js` as `labs/game/net/session.client.txt` so lint leaves it alone.\"\"\",\"\"\"repository (it is over 5 GB). `curl -fsSO` what you need from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`:\n`harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into a folder under `out/`; `examples/arena.html`, a small shared-world game, to read; and\n`session.js`, saved as `labs/game/net/session.client.txt` so lint leaves it alone. (The hub replaces an unmodified client with each new version.)\"\"\")\n\n# card input direct\nrep(\"\"\"controls, the countdown from the `card` event. Cross or Enter is `AIHub.answer('ready')`, Triangle or T is `AIHub.answer('more')`. It changes nothing in the round.\"\"\",\"\"\"controls, the countdown from the `card` event. Cross or Enter is `AIHub.answer('ready')`, Triangle or T is `AIHub.answer('more')`, and a tap or click on the card works too. It changes nothing in the round. **Listen for Enter with a plain `window` `keydown` listener added right after `connect()`, not through frame-sampled input:** the harness pokes Enter into the frame and allows 3 s, and frames are slow on the software renderer. Poll the pad in `requestAnimationFrame` here too.\"\"\")\n\n# gate\nrep(\"\"\"- **Touch-only devices** (`matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` with no pad connected): no touch controls at all. Always pass `touch=off`. Show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button. Attract mode runs behind it. A pad connecting or a key pressed dismisses the gate.\n- **No WebGPU:** a styled message saying which browsers have it. No WebGL fallback.\"\"\",\"\"\"- **Touch-only devices** (`matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` with no pad connected): no touch controls at all. Always pass `touch=off` [verified: no touch UI appears]. Show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button. Attract mode runs behind it. A pad connecting or a key pressed dismisses the gate. **Build the gate in plain DOM, created before `createEngine`,** since `engine.ui` is null when the renderer can't start. A Chromium phone profile on `file://` has WebGPU and runs attract [verified]; the WebKit iPhone profile has no WebGPU at all [verified], so there the gate shows over a dark page with no attract, and the engine's own error overlay stays hidden.\n- **No WebGPU, not touch:** a styled message saying which browsers have it (Chrome or Edge, recent Safari). No WebGL fallback.\n- **Dialogue and cutscenes.** `createDialog`: `modal: false` with `auto` for radio, Tannoy and barks, so play goes on; modal for the shop patter and story talk. Cutscenes run in the world, with own cameras (`node x new camera`, `camera.set(code, { blend: true })`), `modal: () => true`, a letterbox through `post.combine`, and always skippable (hold Circle or Esc). Keep them short: 20 s at most, and most are under 10.\"\"\")\n\n# burst fix\nrep(\"\"\"`removeActor`, then `spawnActor` on the spot with `body:parishionerBurst` (head parts removed, a neck stump, a `Chain` from `secondary`), with a splash of brine to hide the swap.\"\"\",\"\"\"`removeActor`, then `spawnActor` on the spot with `body:parishionerBurst`