{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDeHmFAHN7u3fG7vsQM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GThcTsHnkcXv2wk1Ps74KA","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/PLAN.md","offset":330,"limit":300},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10819,"cache_read_input_tokens":621491,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10819},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"0dd1881e-c743-4b20-874b-ed21c83e2097","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:20:43.447Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDeHUspBjfdHSJFLgaD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GThcTsHnkcXv2wk1Ps74KA":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/PLAN.md","offset":330,"limit":300}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GThcTsHnkcXv2wk1Ps74KA","type":"tool_result","content":"330\t| **Bog Hound** (quadruped rig) | 60 | 5.5 | Leap bite 12 | Packs of 3 to 5. One shot staggers. | Marsh |\n331\t| **Lodger Whip** (a burst Parishioner: headless, a lamprey lashing from the neck) | 140 | 1.4 | Lash 25 at 4.5 m, telegraphed | Body shots ×0.5. Flare or flash kills at once. | Chapel |\n332\t| **Leech** (blob rig) | 8 | 3.0 | Latches on, 3 a second | Comes from dead Whips; mash to shake off. | Cannery |\n333\t| **Deacon** (hooded robe, lantern) | 150 | 1.0 | Staff 12 | Chanting speeds foes within 12 m by 30%. Runs from you. Kill him first. | Chapel |\n334\t| **Hatchman** (hatch-cover shield) | 130 | 1.1 | Shove 20 | Shield blocks the front torso. Knees and head are open; flank him. | Line Floor |\n335\t\n336\t### 7.2 Foe behaviour\n337\t\n338\tStates: `idle` (work or pray), `alert` (a shout, 0.5 s), `approach`, `windUp`, `strike`, `recover`, `reel`, `kneel`, `down` (ragdoll),\n339\t`getUp`, `grabbing`, `carrying` (Wren), `vault`, `dead`.\n340\t\n341\t- **Pressure, not swarm.** A ring round the player (`approachRing`) with an assigned angle each, so they flank. At most 2\n342\t  melee attackers at a time, through attack tokens (`takeToken`, `releaseToken`), scaled by `game.risk`. The others shuffle and\n343\t  close, so the crowd looks hungry but the player stays fair.\n344\t- **Add separation steering** (a spatial hash, repulsion within 0.9 m): actors do not push each other.\n345\t- **Awareness** through `sense` and `Noise`: gunshots alert within 30 m; sight 25 m in a 110° cone; fog is no excuse.\n346\t- **Paths** through `createSiteNav` flow fields (§16.5). Doors: foes bash and break them (`strikeDoor`). Windows and low walls:\n347\t  scripted vaults with `ClimbUp_1m`.\n348\t- **Telegraph everything that hurts:** an arm raised and a grunt at least 0.6 s before any swing. Big attacks also draw an\n349\t  engine floor telegraph (`telegraph:arc`, `ring`, `line`).\n350\t- **Corpses:** keep 30 ragdolls, then remove the oldest out of view (`removeActor`).\n351\t\n352\t### 7.3 Bosses and the duel\n353\t\n354\t**Harbourmaster Brack (The Gutting Floor).** 3,200 HP, a 30 × 30 m open floor under the sky. `build:giant`-style, 5 m tall\n355\t(size 2.7 worked) [verified].\n356\t- Attacks: anchor throw and drag along a line, 45; chain sweep in an arc, 45; slam in a ring, 35. All telegraphed.\n357\t- Weak point: when he roars, the anglerfish lure on his chest opens for 2.5 s. Hits on it are ×3. Three hits and he kneels;\n358\t  a kick prompt tears at it for 200.\n359\t- Hazards: four hanging oil lamps. Shoot one when he stands under it: 300 damage and a stagger.\n360\t- At 50% he summons four Parishioners and speeds up. At 30%, if you freed the seal, it bursts in and bites his leg for a\n361\t  3 s stun (blob rig, grey). Reward: the gun you do not yet own, and \"Harbour dues. Paid.\"\n362\t\n363\t**Mr. Sedge (The Audit).** 1,100 HP in the Records Vault, a maze of shelf lanes, paper blowing. He deflects bullets with his cane\n364\tunless stunned. He hides, lunges in 2 to 4 hit combos; each lunge is a parry prompt. Three clean parries stun him for\n365\t2 s: shoot or kick now. Miss a parry: 22 damage. He also taunts on the Tannoy line, having cut in. It is the exam for the\n366\tparry system, so make the parry feel wonderful.\n367\t\n368\t**Prior Goole, then the Undertow (The Causeway).**\n369\t- *Phase 1, 1,500 HP, the Prior.* A long stone causeway with the tide rising to the ankles (slower run). He walks through fog\n370\t  (vanishing and reappearing) and calls up Whips. Monologue over the Tannoy throughout.\n371\t- *Phase 2, 5,000 HP, the Undertow.* He falls into the sea and rises 6 m tall, on a giant build with hanging tendril chains.\n372\t  Wave slam (line telegraphs across the causeway), tendril sweep, brine spit (`SHOT_EMITTER` volleys). Wren turns the lighthouse\n373\t  lens from the tower; the beam sweeps the causeway. When it hits him he recoils and his heart opens for 4 s (×2.5). Leeches\n374\t  go for Wren: if she stops, the beam stops.\n375\t- *Phase 3, below 25%.* The Salvor rows up mid-battle: \"Special offer, friend!\" He sells you the **Whaling Gun for 1 shilling**. It takes\n376\t  a planted aim and one harpoon. Hit the open heart to finish, with a mash prompt to reel him in. Miss, and the next\n377\t  harpoon costs twice as much. \"That'll be dear.\" Then the pun, the explosion, the rowboat.\n378\t\n379\t## 8. The briefcase economy\n380\t\n381\t### 8.1 The Case\n382\t\n383\tA grid inventory, played on a TV. The game pauses while it's open.\n384\t\n385\t- **Grid:** 10 × 6, buying 12 × 7, then 14 × 8. Items have footprints and rotate. Weapons, ammo, heals and throwables go in the grid.\n386\t  Salvage and keys go in a separate File tab and take no room.\n387\t- **Controls:** D-pad or left stick moves a big cursor. Cross lifts and places, Triangle rotates, Square uses or equips, Circle backs out.\n388\t  **Mouse:** hover moves the cursor, click lifts and places, right click or wheel rotates. Keys: arrows or WASD, Enter, R, Esc.\n389\t- **Combining:** lift one item and place it on another to mix. Rum + Kelp = Grog. Grog + Samphire = Tonic. Gems into salvage.\n390\t- **Autosort** button. A pickup that doesn't fit opens the Case with the item on the cursor: fit it, or leave it.\n391\t- **Cells are at least 64 px at 1080p.** One info pane, three lines, big type. Never a data table.\n392\t\n393\tKeep the grid logic in a pure, tested module (`labs/game/scenes/caseGrid.ts`). The state lives in a component on the player;\n394\teach change is a scene dev action (`__engine.actions.run('case', op)`), so replays hold it.\n395\t\n396\t### 8.2 Items\n397\t\n398\t| Item | Cells | Effect |\n399\t|---|---|---|\n400\t| Rum | 1×2 | +25 HP |\n401\t| Kelp | 1×1 | +35 HP |\n402\t| Grog (Rum + Kelp) | 1×2 | Full heal |\n403\t| Samphire | 1×1 | Alone, nothing. Mixed into Grog: Tonic |\n404\t| Tonic | 1×2 | Full heal, max HP +10 |\n405\t| Pistol rounds ×10, flare ×3, rifle ×5 | 1×1 | |\n406\t| Shells ×6, trench rounds ×30 | 2×1 | |\n407\t| Salvage | File tab | Sells for 300 to 5,000 shillings |\n408\t\n409\t### 8.3 The Salvor's stall\n410\t\n411\tA lantern-lit stall of crates and wreckage in three places (Shingle, Loading bay, Abbey steps), each with a filing cabinet near\n412\tby. **Buy, Sell, Service, Organise.** Shows one item at a time with a large model-free card: name, price, one line of patter.\n413\t\n414\t- **Currency:** shillings. Income across a campaign should be about 25,000.\n415\t- **Service (upgrades):** Firepower, Reload, Capacity, Handling, four levels a weapon, rising 800 to 5,000. Fully serviced\n416\t  weapons earn one perk each (pistol: head shots sometimes crit ×5; pump gun: wider push; rifle: higher pierce; trench gun: no climb).\n417\t- **Larger Case:** 2,500, 6,000. **Chart:** 500.\n418\t\n419\t### 8.4 Adaptive drops\n420\t\n421\tCrates and fallen foes drop what you lack. Each drop rolls an item or shillings, then weights by need: ammo for your equipped\n422\tgun when under 1.5 mags, heals when HP is under 50%, shillings otherwise. Never drop ammo for a gun you don't own. Named stream\n423\t`drops`. Keep one rule: the player should feel lucky, and always be one bad decision from ruin.\n424\t\n425\t### 8.5 Saves\n426\t\n427\t- **Filing cabinets** in each zone: \"File your report\" (three manual slots). The room is safe and quiet, with its own music.\n428\t- **Autosave checkpoints** at zone gates and boss doors. Game over offers Retry from checkpoint, Last filed report, Main menu.\n429\t- A save is compact JSON (version, beat, flags, HP, Case, shillings, service levels, collected sets, stats, seed), kept with\n430\t  `createStore` (localStorage, which survives a reload on `file://` [verified]). Load is `inspector.seed(n)` and then a `load` dev action. Captures are\n431\t  not saves: `restore` refuses foreign ones.\n432\t\n433\t**Results screen** at the end: big single numbers, one at a time: time, accuracy, kicks, head shots, deaths, salvage, rank (A to D,\n434\twith a stamp), Risk Rating.\n435\t\n436\t## 9. Wren\n437\t\n438\tAn actor with `player: false`, 60 HP, who follows at 2 m through the nav. Shots pass through her; she ducks when your laser\n439\tcrosses her and says \"Oi.\" Hurt or carried, she shows on a small name bar top right.\n440\t\n441\t- **Commands (L1/G):** tap toggles *Stay close* and *Wait here*. Held near a locker, barrel or hatch: *Hide*, and she climbs in,\n442\t  safe, muffled commentary. Tap to call her out. In waits and hides she's a problem you've parked, and you must come back.\n443\t- **Grabbed and carried.** A foe near her lifts her (`Walk_Carry_Loop`) and walks toward the nearest exit or chute at 1.4 m/s.\n444\t  A marker shows. Hit him enough and she drops. If he reaches it, or she dies: **CLAIM DENIED. Cause of loss: beneficiary mislaid.**\n445\t- **She helps.** Calls flanks with odds and an on-screen ping. Boosts you up marked ledges (prompt for both). Cranks the hoist and\n446\t  the lens. Reads the ledgers. She finds ammo sometimes: \"Ninety percent sure this is yours.\"\n447\t- **Fair:** she must never stand in a doorway you need. When you back into her, swap places. Foes prefer her only if you've\n448\t  left her alone over 10 m away.\n449\t\n450\t## 10. Last Stand: co-op and the hub\n451\t\n452\t**A 5-minute co-op survival round on the Mary Constance**, for 1 to 4 players, and the game's AI Hub session mode. It reuses the\n453\tSquare. Menu entry \"Last Stand\" plays it solo in `game:world` with no reload, with up to 3 AI \"temps\" you may hire (a simple bot on the same\n454\treplica path, which also serves attract mode). There is no network outside a session: that's what \"the game on its own\" means in the hub's\n455\tprotocol (`connect()` answers `null` and the game plays alone).\n456\t\n457\t### 10.1 The round\n458\t\n459\t- **Five waves over 300 s**, ending with the foghorn: everyone standing wins. Budgets: 14; 22 with Netwives; 26 with Hounds; 30 with Whips;\n460\t  34 with the Gutter. Multiply by `0.7 + 0.3 × players`. At most `14 + 4 × players`, capped at 24 on the field.\n461\t- **Loadout:** pistol, pump gun, 2 rum. Supply crates land in each 15 s lull. Planks and winch nets work as in the campaign.\n462\t- **Downed, not dead:** at 0 HP you crawl for 30 s; a teammate holds Cross for 2.5 s to revive you at 40 HP. Bled out: back next wave at 50 HP. All down at\n463\t  once: the round is lost. Solo gets one second wind.\n464\t- **Score:** kill 100, head shot +50, kick kill +75, revive +150, multiplied by a streak (×1 + 0.1 a kill, lapsing after 6 s).\n465\t- **Each player's coat trim and armband** take the seat's colour (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`), and a name label floats\n466\t  over each. Names come from the hub and go in as text, never HTML.\n467\t\n468\t### 10.2 The hub protocol: exact requirements\n469\t\n470\tRead the protocol itself once: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Don't clone that\n471\trepository (it is over 5 GB). `curl -fsSO` what you need from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`:\n472\t`harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into a folder under `out/`; `examples/arena.html`, a small shared-world game, to read; and\n473\t`session.js`, saved as `labs/game/net/session.client.txt` so lint leaves it alone. (The hub replaces an unmodified client with each new version.)\n474\t\n475\t```html\n476\t<!-- right after <meta charset>, first script in <head>, pasted unmodified: the bundler does this (§16.6) -->\n477\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n478\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n479\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n480\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n481\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Hold the square together until the foghorn\">\n482\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: stick/WASD. Aim: L2/RMB. Fire: R2/LMB. Kick: X/E. Reload: Square/R\">\n483\t<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n484\t```\n485\t\n486\t- `AIHub.active` true: **no title, menu or attract**. Straight into the round. `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`.\n487\t- **Own card**, in the world: slow orbit of the trawler at dusk, the title, each player in their colour with a ready tick, how to win, this player's\n488\t  controls, the countdown from the `card` event. Cross or Enter is `AIHub.answer('ready')`, Triangle or T is `AIHub.answer('more')`, and a tap or click on the card works too. It changes nothing in the round. **Listen for Enter with a plain `window` `keydown` listener added right after `connect()`, not through frame-sampled input:** the harness pokes Enter into the frame and allows 3 s, and frames are slow on the software renderer. Poll the pad in `requestAnimationFrame` here too.\n489\t- `AIHub.ready()` once `createEngine` resolves, with no key press. **The harness waits only 20 s for this** (§16.7).\n490\t- Play starts when `AIHub.time() >= 0`. A shared world finishes through the host: `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won, stats, awards })`, with a last reliable\n491\t  snapshot first. `time-up` means finish now, within `graceMs`.\n492\t- `end`: stop input, stop sound, stop the engine. `leave`: remove that player's actor. If no WebGPU: `AIHub.fail('WebGPU required')`.\n493\t- **No** `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open`, navigation, sockets, `fetch` or chat. Options opens a small Settings overlay only; the round keeps running.\n494\t- `AIHub.server` true (host with no player): run the world, no local player, input or card, and no heavy drawing beyond what the engine does.\n495\t\n496\t### 10.3 Netcode\n497\t\n498\tHost-authoritative for the world, client-authoritative for each player's own body. It is the pattern of the protocol's `examples/arena.html`.\n499\t\n500\t```text\n501\tClient -> host  {t:'me', at, x,y,z, yaw,pitch, st, w}          12 Hz, unreliable, to the host\n502\tClient -> host  {t:'shot'|'kick'|'use'|'rev', at, ...}         reliable, as they happen, at most 8/s\n503\tHost  -> all    {t:'s', at, wave, left, p:[...], f:[...]}      10 Hz, unreliable, at most 1,200 bytes\n504\tHost  -> all    {t:'e', ev:[[code, ...args], ...]}             reliable batches, at most 8/s\n505\t```\n506\t\n507\t- **Budget:** at most 20 messages a second leave a copy, 16 KB each. An unreliable message over 1,200 bytes is lost whole if any packet is. A foe is about\n508\t  28 bytes (`[nid, x·100, z·100, yaw·10, hp%, state, kind]`), so 24 foes fit. Past that, send alternate foes in alternate snapshots.\n509\t- **Your controls never wait.** Your own actor moves locally. Your shot raycasts locally against what you see, with instant tracer, sound and hit marker; the host\n510\t  applies damage from the `shot` message. In co-op, trust the client: no anti-cheat.\n511\t- **Replicas are actors on both sides:** spawned from events, moved by steering. Each step: `move` toward the latest snapshot position, scaled by distance; a snap past 1.5 m. Foes' states\n512\t  pick clips and reactions. Ragdolls may differ between copies; nobody will mind.\n513\t- **Sim boundary [verified].** The sim never touches the network. Page code gathers each frame's messages and hands them over as a custom intent:\n514\t  `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:net', { seq, msgs })`. A `net` system in phase `intents` applies each `seq` once (axes hold until changed). The same page reads\n515\t  outgoing sim events from `frame.world.events.trace()` and sends them. This keeps \"the page never writes the sim\" and makes host runs replayable.\n516\t- **Roles** come in as a setting: `game.role` = `solo`, `host`, `server` or `client`. On a client, AI, spawning and hazards do not run; `net` drives everything but the local player.\n517\t- **Use a transport interface** (`send`, `on`, `me`, `players`, `isHost`, `time`), with `AIHub` behind one implementation and an in-memory one with seeded latency and loss behind another, so\n518\t  host and client sims can be tested together in Vitest with no browser (§17).\n519\t\n520\t## 11. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n521\t\n522\tDesigned for a DualSense on a TV at 10 feet. Keyboard and mouse get the same screens and feel native on them.\n523\t\n524\t- **Look: a claims department in a storm.** Manila folders, carbon paper, typewriter text, red rubber stamps. Pause is a folder. Game over is a stamp. The shop is chalk on a crate lid.\n525\t  Fonts are CSS stacks only: `\"Courier New\", monospace` for forms, `Georgia, serif` small caps for headings. No font files.\n526\t- **Scale.** All UI sizes come from one scale, `min(innerWidth / 1920, innerHeight / 1080)`. At 1080p: body text at least 34 px, smallest text 28 px, subtitle 40 px, menu rows at least 56 px tall, at most 7 rows showing. 5% safe margin all round.\n527\t- **No dense screens.** One column of choices, one detail pane, big single numbers. If a screen looks like a web page, redo it.\n528\t- **HUD.** Bottom right: ammo as `10 / 42`, 96 px, with a weapon silhouette. Bottom left: health as a large stamped word and bar: **INSURED** (teal, 60%+), **UNDERINSURED** (amber), **UNINSURABLE** (red, pulsing, under 30%).\n529\t  Top left: objective for 6 s when it changes. Centre: the prompt, at 64 px glyph and 44 px text. Top right: Wren. Direction arcs when hit. It fades in calm moments.\n530\t- **Prompts follow the last input used.** PlayStation glyphs for a pad by default, with a Settings option for Xbox (A B X Y), keycaps and mouse icons otherwise. Draw the glyphs as inline SVG. Write `glyphFor(action)`: `input.bindings.codes(action)`, filtered with\n531\t  `deviceOf`, by **your own** last-device tracker, from keydown, pointer and a poll of `navigator.getGamepads()`. Don't use `input.lastDevice`: it reads `virtual` whenever the game feeds the virtual device (netcode, attract), and prompts fall back to the keyboard [verified].\n532\t- **Menus.** `createMenu` for lists (hover moves focus and a click picks, built in), themed with CSS over `.ui-panel` and `.ui-menu`. Add W and S to its arrows. `createPadCursor` is available for odd panels. While a menu is up: `inspector.pause()`, `modal: () => true`; the mouse cursor shows and pointer lock is released. Starting play shows \"Click to aim\" until the lock is taken.\n533\t- **Touch-only devices** (`matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` with no pad connected): no touch controls at all. Always pass `touch=off` [verified: no touch UI appears]. Show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button. Attract mode runs behind it. A pad connecting or a key pressed dismisses the gate. **Build the gate in plain DOM, created before `createEngine`,** since `engine.ui` is null when the renderer can't start. A Chromium phone profile on `file://` has WebGPU and runs attract [verified]; the WebKit iPhone profile has no WebGPU at all [verified], so there the gate shows over a dark page with no attract, and the engine's own error overlay stays hidden.\n534\t- **No WebGPU, not touch:** a styled message saying which browsers have it (Chrome or Edge, recent Safari). No WebGL fallback.\n535\t- **Dialogue and cutscenes.** `createDialog`: `modal: false` with `auto` for radio, Tannoy and barks, so play goes on; modal for the shop patter and story talk. Cutscenes run in the world, with own cameras (`node x new camera`, `camera.set(code, { blend: true })`), `modal: () => true`, a letterbox through `post.combine`, and always skippable (hold Circle or Esc). Keep them short: 20 s at most, and most are under 10.\n536\t\n537\t**Screens:** splash (\"Pelham & Grice Mutual Assurance presents\") · title (New Claim, Continue, Last Stand, Settings, Controls, About) · pause (Resume, Case, Claim File, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, Retry from checkpoint, Main menu) · Case · Claim File (objective, a paper map drawn in SVG with pins, memos) · shop · Settings · Controls · About/Credits · dialogue and subtitles · game over · results · Dev Mode · touch gate · hub card.\n538\t\n539\t**Settings:** volume sliders with the music at **10% by default** (§13); difficulty; pad glyphs (PlayStation or Xbox); look sensitivity and invert for stick and mouse (`input.*`); aim assist; subtitle size; HUD scale; vibration (via `vibrationActuator` where present); quality (`auto`, `low`, `medium`, `high`); key and button rebinding. All kept in the store, and every setting's a row a pad can change with left and right.\n540\t\n541\t## 12. Art direction and animation\n542\t\n543\t**Base: the engine's native procedural style.** Everything is code and data: no image, model or sound files. What makes it ours is fog, dusk, silhouette and material.\n544\t\n545\t**Palette.** Slate, wet stone, tar black, oilskin yellow gone sour, rust. One warm accent, lantern amber. One cold accent, Lodger cyan-green (`#5ff0c4`), used for nothing else. Hero's tie is the only pure red on screen until the laser.\n546\t\n547\t**The look [verified as a start].** This took a foggy hamlet with a crowd closing in from nothing to moody in a few lines. Tune from here. Lower the sun's glare: at this setting its bloom whites out part of the sky.\n548\t\n549\t```ts\n550\tdefineSky('sky:skerry', {\n551\t  description: 'A sick, smoke-orange dusk with heavy ground fog.',\n552\t  background: '#6a5a4c', pointLights: 1.6,\n553\t  dome: { show: true, turbidity: 9, rayleigh: 3, mieCoefficient: 0.02, mieDirectionalG: 0.85, exposure: 0.35 },\n554\t  sun: { color: '#ff9a60', intensity: 1.1, azimuth: 2.4, elevation: 0.14 },\n555\t  ambient: { sky: '#8f8a90', ground: '#2a2a22', intensity: 0.75 },\n556\t  fog: { color: '#7b6f60', start: 7, end: 62, amount: 0.92, floor: 0, ceiling: 2.4, height: 0.35 },\n557\t  backdrop: { haze: '#8a7a6a', tint: '#6a6058', layers: [{ kind: 'mountains', color: '#4a4a48', height: 0.95 }] },\n558\t});\n559\tdefineLook('look:skerry', {\n560\t  description: 'The island at dusk.', sky: 'sky:skerry', resolution: 'full', textures: 'smooth',\n561\t  filters: {\n562\t    aa: { scope: 'all' },\n563\t    bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.18, threshold: 1.1, radius: 0.5 },\n564\t    air: { scope: 'all', haze: 0.5, height: 3, shafts: 1, halos: 0.5 },\n565\t    grade: { scope: 'all', saturation: 0.72, contrast: 1.12, temperature: 0.08, gamma: 0.95 },\n566\t    vignette: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.5, softness: 0.55 },\n567\t    grain: { scope: 'all', amount: 0.18 },\n568\t  },\n569\t});\n570\t```\n571\t\n572\tEach zone may lay its own grade on top (`post.combine`, view settings, never hashed): Marsh greener, thicker fog; Cannery tungsten amber and darker; Abbey cold moonlight (`sky:night` base); Causeway storm, then the last red dusk for the ending.\n573\t\n574\t**Make these** (engine library for generic crates, barrels, lanterns, benches):\n575\t\n576\t- **Characters (`defineBody`).** Start from the playground's `PLAYER_BODY` (§16.1 for where), a clothed human, and redress it; `body:humanoid`'s slot names are not what you'd guess. Quill: trench coat with the engine's `Cape` secondary motion (`secondary: { cape: true, color }`), red tie, briefcase in the off hand when not aiming. Parishioners: at least 6 dresses by seed with oilskin, sou'wester or cap; gaff, oar and knife as body parts on the hand bones. Netwife, Deacon, Hatchman (shield as a box part), Gutter (lobster-pot head of thin boxes, saw on a pole), Brack, Sedge, Goole, Salvor, Wren. Lodger eyes: unlit `eye` parts in the cold accent.\n577\t- **Bursting.** The view makes a puppet once and does not re-read `puppet.body` [verified]. So a Lodger burst replaces the actor: `removeActor`, then `spawnActor` on the spot with `body:parishionerBurst` (head parts removed, a neck stump, and for the lamprey the `secondary` component's hair chain, `{ hair: 'ponytail', color: '#5ff0c4' }`, the only chain that hangs at head height), with a splash of brine to hide the swap. Lash: a line of emitter bursts along the `telegraph:line`, 0.35 s.\n578\t- **World.** Materials: salt-stained stone, tarred planks, slate, rust iron, net. Slate-roofed cottages (level format 2, `roof: gable`, `pitch: 35`). Drying racks of herring, lobster pots, coiled rope, nets, rowboats on shingle, a bonfire, candles, Tannoy horns on poles (visible, always), stilted huts, cannery conveyors, rail hooks, boilers, fish-oil barrels and pools, abbey arches, shelves of ledgers, lighthouse with a lens beam (a long unlit transparent prop). Sea plane with `texture:water`, gulls by emitter. Check the ground up close: my grass looked streaky at grazing angles; a tighter `map` scale or another texture fixes it.\n579\t- **Light.** Lanterns and braziers (`prop:lantern`, `prop:brazier`, your own props with light spots) make the night; the engine's pool picks the nearest. Group them with `switchGroup` for scripted blackouts. Every interior needs an amber pool to walk toward.\n580\t- **Effects (`defineEmitter`).** Brine (a dark teal-black spray, no red blood), muzzle flash and tracer (free with the `gunshot` event, §16.3), rain and sea spray through `frame.emit`, fire, sparks on parry, paper storm in the Vault, Lodger mist.\n581\t\n582\t**Animation: the engine's animator, plus clips and new actions.** Clip ids below are real [verified with `node x anim find`]; register only the sets you use (§16.2).\n583\t\n584\t| Moment | Clip or engine feature |\n585\t|---|---|\n586\t| Parishioner shamble, idle | `quaternius/Zombie_Walk_Fwd_Loop`, `quaternius/Zombie_Idle_Loop`, variants in `mesh2motion/Zombie_Walk_2`, `cmu/Zombie_Walk_Loop` |\n587\t| Claw attack, roar | `quaternius/Zombie_Scratch`, `mesh2motion/Zombie Yell` |\n588\t| Thrower | `quaternius/OverhandThrow` |\n589\t| Kneel | `mesh2motion/Kneeling Tired` |\n590\t| Knocked flat, death, rise | `quaternius/Hit_Knockback`, `mesh2motion/Death_A` to `D`, `quaternius/LayToIdle`, `mesh2motion/Zombie_Rise`, ragdolls with `handOff` |\n591\t| Pistol | Engine hold and aim IK, `quaternius/Pistol_Reload`, `quaternius/Pistol_Shoot` |\n592\t| Kick | `move:roundhouse` through `Attack` and `states.body`, or `cmu/Roundhouse_Kick` trimmed |\n593\t| Door kick | `mesh2motion/Kick_Breach`, `move:breach` |\n594\t| Vault, ladder | `quaternius/ClimbUp_1m`, `mesh2motion/Climb Ladder` |\n595\t| Crawl (downed) | `mesh2motion/Crawl` |\n596\t| Carry Wren | `quaternius/Walk_Carry_Loop` |\n597\t| Stagger, grabs | Actions `action:dizzy`, `action:grab`, `action:grabbed`, `action:hurt` |\n598\t\n599\t**New animations you must make** (`node x new action`, or readable clips with `parseClip`), since they're the character: Quill straightening his tie; his knee-rub idle; reloading with the briefcase tucked under his arm; plank kick; foe reel (clutching its face); foe mid-sermon kneel and rise; Salvor rubbing hands and pointing with his pipe; Wren cranking, and her boost; Goole's sermon gestures; Brack's anchor wind-up and roar; Sedge's lunge and parried recoil.\n600\t\n601\t## 13. Audio\n602\t\n603\tAll code, no audio files. Engine: `defineSfx`, `defineSong`, `createAudio` (buses `effects`, `music`, `ui`, `ambience`; `play(id, { pitch, vol, when, position, bus, duck, loop })`; `room`; `music`, `intensity`, `stinger`).\n604\t\n605\t- **Music at 10% by default.** At startup, before any song: `audio.volume('music', 0.1)`, and the Settings slider shows 10%. A test reads it.\n606\t- **Music (`defineSong`, own tunes):** title (slow harmonium over wind); exploration (low drones, far foghorn); combat, built in `intensity` layers that join as foes close (low strings, anvil, frantic fiddle); filing-cabinet room (gentle harmonium, the safest sound in the game); the Salvor's stall (a sly squeezebox shanty, the theme people will hum); boss; finale; results jingle.\n607\t- **Effects:** every gun, reload, kick, slash and parry clang, body hits, saw engine (a loop with distance, heard long before seen), foghorn (huge, low, the game's signature sound), Tannoy crackle with hall reverb, gulls, sea, wind, rain, creaking hull, footsteps by surface (`footstepSound`), doors, glass, UI: typewriter clack for moves, stamp thud for picks.\n608\t- **Rooms:** `audio.room(...)` by zone. Walls muffle (`update(pose, queries)`).\n609\t- **Voices: Animalese style.** A phoneme kit of about 16 short `sfx:vo-*` entries (voiced formants with `saw` or `pulse` through bandpass filters; noise for consonants). A line's text maps to syllables: letter to phoneme, played in sequence with `when` from the context clock at 11 to 16 a second. Each speaker has a base `pitch`, a rate and a kit tweak: Quill low and dry; Wren quick and high; Thripp clipped; Goole slow, deep, on the `effects` bus with Tannoy filtering and hall reverb; Salvor bouncy, rising; Brack a growl; Parishioners a low mutter by position, three times out of ten with a subtitle (\"Bless the tide.\"). Duck music while speaking. A Voice slider scales `vol`.\n610\t- Every sound is presentation: sim events drive it from `frame.world.events.trace()`, never the reverse. `node x qa audio` must pass.\n611\t\n612\t## 14. Attract mode\n613\t\n614\tAfter **10 seconds with no input** on the title or any front-end menu (not in the pause menu or in a session), the game starts a looping AI-played demo. **Any input exits** back to the title: key, click, pointer moved past 8 px, pad button, stick past 0.4. On touch-only devices it runs regardless and a tap only shows the gate.\n615\t\n616\t- **It runs the real game.** `inspector.set('game.mode', 'attract')`, `inspector.seed(n)`. A page-side bot drives through `engine.input.virtual` (`axis`, `hold`, `press`), and cheats freely: dev actions for `god`, ammo and teleports. `modal` stays false so the virtual device reaches the sim. It writes no saves. On exit: `virtual.clear()`, back to `title` mode.\n617\t- **The loop, about 100 s, a beat each 10 to 15 s, with a slow camera cut between:** walking the Slip in fog; aim, knee, kick on Fish Lane; the trawler siege with a plank kick and a winch net; the Gutter; Case screen with items moving; Salvor stall; flare on a Whip in the Marsh; Wren carried off and shot free; Brack's lure; Sedge parry; Undertow in the beam; four players on the trawler.\n618\t- **On screen:** title in the corner, a stamped DEMO, \"Press any button\" in the current glyph style, pulsing.\n619\t\n620\t## 15. Dev mode\n621\t\n622\tFrom the pause menu, item **Dev Mode**. Not in hub sessions. Large panel, playable on a pad: left and right change a value, a mouse can drag.\n623\t\n624\t**Live sliders** (each a `defineSettings` entry read every step, so replays record them; each row with its default, and **Reset all to defaults**, plus one row's reset):\n625\t\n626\t| Area | Sliders |\n627\t|---|---|\n628\t| Player | Run speed (`movement.gaits.run`), sprint (`movement.gaits.sprint`), aim shuffle (`movement.gaits.walk`, default 0: planted), max HP, camera arm, field of view (`cam.fov`), laser wobble, aim assist |\n629\t| Guns | Damage ×, fire rate ×, reload time ×, recoil ×, head multiplier, leg multiplier, kick damage, kick radius, parry window |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"8ff6e4c8-d99b-4e62-bdb6-bde108523395","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:20:43.633Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/PLAN.md","content":"| **Bog Hound** (quadruped rig) | 60 | 5.5 | Leap bite 12 | Packs of 3 to 5. One shot staggers. | Marsh |\n| **Lodger Whip** (a burst Parishioner: headless, a lamprey lashing from the neck) | 140 | 1.4 | Lash 25 at 4.5 m, telegraphed | Body shots ×0.5. Flare or flash kills at once. | Chapel |\n| **Leech** (blob rig) | 8 | 3.0 | Latches on, 3 a second | Comes from dead Whips; mash to shake off. | Cannery |\n| **Deacon** (hooded robe, lantern) | 150 | 1.0 | Staff 12 | Chanting speeds foes within 12 m by 30%. Runs from you. Kill him first. | Chapel |\n| **Hatchman** (hatch-cover shield) | 130 | 1.1 | Shove 20 | Shield blocks the front torso. Knees and head are open; flank him. | Line Floor |\n\n### 7.2 Foe behaviour\n\nStates: `idle` (work or pray), `alert` (a shout, 0.5 s), `approach`, `windUp`, `strike`, `recover`, `reel`, `kneel`, `down` (ragdoll),\n`getUp`, `grabbing`, `carrying` (Wren), `vault`, `dead`.\n\n- **Pressure, not swarm.** A ring round the player (`approachRing`) with an assigned angle each, so they flank. At most 2\n  melee attackers at a time, through attack tokens (`takeToken`, `releaseToken`), scaled by `game.risk`. The others shuffle and\n  close, so the crowd looks hungry but the player stays fair.\n- **Add separation steering** (a spatial hash, repulsion within 0.9 m): actors do not push each other.\n- **Awareness** through `sense` and `Noise`: gunshots alert within 30 m; sight 25 m in a 110° cone; fog is no excuse.\n- **Paths** through `createSiteNav` flow fields (§16.5). Doors: foes bash and break them (`strikeDoor`). Windows and low walls:\n  scripted vaults with `ClimbUp_1m`.\n- **Telegraph everything that hurts:** an arm raised and a grunt at least 0.6 s before any swing. Big attacks also draw an\n  engine floor telegraph (`telegraph:arc`, `ring`, `line`).\n- **Corpses:** keep 30 ragdolls, then remove the oldest out of view (`removeActor`).\n\n### 7.3 Bosses and the duel\n\n**Harbourmaster Brack (The Gutting Floor).** 3,200 HP, a 30 × 30 m open floor under the sky. `build:giant`-style, 5 m tall\n(size 2.7 worked) [verified].\n- Attacks: anchor throw and drag along a line, 45; chain sweep in an arc, 45; slam in a ring, 35. All telegraphed.\n- Weak point: when he roars, the anglerfish lure on his chest opens for 2.5 s. Hits on it are ×3. Three hits and he kneels;\n  a kick prompt tears at it for 200.\n- Hazards: four hanging oil lamps. Shoot one when he stands under it: 300 damage and a stagger.\n- At 50% he summons four Parishioners and speeds up. At 30%, if you freed the seal, it bursts in and bites his leg for a\n  3 s stun (blob rig, grey). Reward: the gun you do not yet own, and \"Harbour dues. Paid.\"\n\n**Mr. Sedge (The Audit).** 1,100 HP in the Records Vault, a maze of shelf lanes, paper blowing. He deflects bullets with his cane\nunless stunned. He hides, lunges in 2 to 4 hit combos; each lunge is a parry prompt. Three clean parries stun him for\n2 s: shoot or kick now. Miss a parry: 22 damage. He also taunts on the Tannoy line, having cut in. It is the exam for the\nparry system, so make the parry feel wonderful.\n\n**Prior Goole, then the Undertow (The Causeway).**\n- *Phase 1, 1,500 HP, the Prior.* A long stone causeway with the tide rising to the ankles (slower run). He walks through fog\n  (vanishing and reappearing) and calls up Whips. Monologue over the Tannoy throughout.\n- *Phase 2, 5,000 HP, the Undertow.* He falls into the sea and rises 6 m tall, on a giant build with hanging tendril chains.\n  Wave slam (line telegraphs across the causeway), tendril sweep, brine spit (`SHOT_EMITTER` volleys). Wren turns the lighthouse\n  lens from the tower; the beam sweeps the causeway. When it hits him he recoils and his heart opens for 4 s (×2.5). Leeches\n  go for Wren: if she stops, the beam stops.\n- *Phase 3, below 25%.* The Salvor rows up mid-battle: \"Special offer, friend!\" He sells you the **Whaling Gun for 1 shilling**. It takes\n  a planted aim and one harpoon. Hit the open heart to finish, with a mash prompt to reel him in. Miss, and the next\n  harpoon costs twice as much. \"That'll be dear.\" Then the pun, the explosion, the rowboat.\n\n## 8. The briefcase economy\n\n### 8.1 The Case\n\nA grid inventory, played on a TV. The game pauses while it's open.\n\n- **Grid:** 10 × 6, buying 12 × 7, then 14 × 8. Items have footprints and rotate. Weapons, ammo, heals and throwables go in the grid.\n  Salvage and keys go in a separate File tab and take no room.\n- **Controls:** D-pad or left stick moves a big cursor. Cross lifts and places, Triangle rotates, Square uses or equips, Circle backs out.\n  **Mouse:** hover moves the cursor, click lifts and places, right click or wheel rotates. Keys: arrows or WASD, Enter, R, Esc.\n- **Combining:** lift one item and place it on another to mix. Rum + Kelp = Grog. Grog + Samphire = Tonic. Gems into salvage.\n- **Autosort** button. A pickup that doesn't fit opens the Case with the item on the cursor: fit it, or leave it.\n- **Cells are at least 64 px at 1080p.** One info pane, three lines, big type. Never a data table.\n\nKeep the grid logic in a pure, tested module (`labs/game/scenes/caseGrid.ts`). The state lives in a component on the player;\neach change is a scene dev action (`__engine.actions.run('case', op)`), so replays hold it.\n\n### 8.2 Items\n\n| Item | Cells | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| Rum | 1×2 | +25 HP |\n| Kelp | 1×1 | +35 HP |\n| Grog (Rum + Kelp) | 1×2 | Full heal |\n| Samphire | 1×1 | Alone, nothing. Mixed into Grog: Tonic |\n| Tonic | 1×2 | Full heal, max HP +10 |\n| Pistol rounds ×10, flare ×3, rifle ×5 | 1×1 | |\n| Shells ×6, trench rounds ×30 | 2×1 | |\n| Salvage | File tab | Sells for 300 to 5,000 shillings |\n\n### 8.3 The Salvor's stall\n\nA lantern-lit stall of crates and wreckage in three places (Shingle, Loading bay, Abbey steps), each with a filing cabinet near\nby. **Buy, Sell, Service, Organise.** Shows one item at a time with a large model-free card: name, price, one line of patter.\n\n- **Currency:** shillings. Income across a campaign should be about 25,000.\n- **Service (upgrades):** Firepower, Reload, Capacity, Handling, four levels a weapon, rising 800 to 5,000. Fully serviced\n  weapons earn one perk each (pistol: head shots sometimes crit ×5; pump gun: wider push; rifle: higher pierce; trench gun: no climb).\n- **Larger Case:** 2,500, 6,000. **Chart:** 500.\n\n### 8.4 Adaptive drops\n\nCrates and fallen foes drop what you lack. Each drop rolls an item or shillings, then weights by need: ammo for your equipped\ngun when under 1.5 mags, heals when HP is under 50%, shillings otherwise. Never drop ammo for a gun you don't own. Named stream\n`drops`. Keep one rule: the player should feel lucky, and always be one bad decision from ruin.\n\n### 8.5 Saves\n\n- **Filing cabinets** in each zone: \"File your report\" (three manual slots). The room is safe and quiet, with its own music.\n- **Autosave checkpoints** at zone gates and boss doors. Game over offers Retry from checkpoint, Last filed report, Main menu.\n- A save is compact JSON (version, beat, flags, HP, Case, shillings, service levels, collected sets, stats, seed), kept with\n  `createStore` (localStorage, which survives a reload on `file://` [verified]). Load is `inspector.seed(n)` and then a `load` dev action. Captures are\n  not saves: `restore` refuses foreign ones.\n\n**Results screen** at the end: big single numbers, one at a time: time, accuracy, kicks, head shots, deaths, salvage, rank (A to D,\nwith a stamp), Risk Rating.\n\n## 9. Wren\n\nAn actor with `player: false`, 60 HP, who follows at 2 m through the nav. Shots pass through her; she ducks when your laser\ncrosses her and says \"Oi.\" Hurt or carried, she shows on a small name bar top right.\n\n- **Commands (L1/G):** tap toggles *Stay close* and *Wait here*. Held near a locker, barrel or hatch: *Hide*, and she climbs in,\n  safe, muffled commentary. Tap to call her out. In waits and hides she's a problem you've parked, and you must come back.\n- **Grabbed and carried.** A foe near her lifts her (`Walk_Carry_Loop`) and walks toward the nearest exit or chute at 1.4 m/s.\n  A marker shows. Hit him enough and she drops. If he reaches it, or she dies: **CLAIM DENIED. Cause of loss: beneficiary mislaid.**\n- **She helps.** Calls flanks with odds and an on-screen ping. Boosts you up marked ledges (prompt for both). Cranks the hoist and\n  the lens. Reads the ledgers. She finds ammo sometimes: \"Ninety percent sure this is yours.\"\n- **Fair:** she must never stand in a doorway you need. When you back into her, swap places. Foes prefer her only if you've\n  left her alone over 10 m away.\n\n## 10. Last Stand: co-op and the hub\n\n**A 5-minute co-op survival round on the Mary Constance**, for 1 to 4 players, and the game's AI Hub session mode. It reuses the\nSquare. Menu entry \"Last Stand\" plays it solo in `game:world` with no reload, with up to 3 AI \"temps\" you may hire (a simple bot on the same\nreplica path, which also serves attract mode). There is no network outside a session: that's what \"the game on its own\" means in the hub's\nprotocol (`connect()` answers `null` and the game plays alone).\n\n### 10.1 The round\n\n- **Five waves over 300 s**, ending with the foghorn: everyone standing wins. Budgets: 14; 22 with Netwives; 26 with Hounds; 30 with Whips;\n  34 with the Gutter. Multiply by `0.7 + 0.3 × players`. At most `14 + 4 × players`, capped at 24 on the field.\n- **Loadout:** pistol, pump gun, 2 rum. Supply crates land in each 15 s lull. Planks and winch nets work as in the campaign.\n- **Downed, not dead:** at 0 HP you crawl for 30 s; a teammate holds Cross for 2.5 s to revive you at 40 HP. Bled out: back next wave at 50 HP. All down at\n  once: the round is lost. Solo gets one second wind.\n- **Score:** kill 100, head shot +50, kick kill +75, revive +150, multiplied by a streak (×1 + 0.1 a kill, lapsing after 6 s).\n- **Each player's coat trim and armband** take the seat's colour (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`), and a name label floats\n  over each. Names come from the hub and go in as text, never HTML.\n\n### 10.2 The hub protocol: exact requirements\n\nRead the protocol itself once: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`. Don't clone that\nrepository (it is over 5 GB). `curl -fsSO` what you need from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`:\n`harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into a folder under `out/`; `examples/arena.html`, a small shared-world game, to read; and\n`session.js`, saved as `labs/game/net/session.client.txt` so lint leaves it alone. (The hub replaces an unmodified client with each new version.)\n\n```html\n<!-- right after <meta charset>, first script in <head>, pasted unmodified: the bundler does this (§16.6) -->\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Hold the square together until the foghorn\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: stick/WASD. Aim: L2/RMB. Fire: R2/LMB. Kick: X/E. Reload: Square/R\">\n<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n```\n\n- `AIHub.active` true: **no title, menu or attract**. Straight into the round. `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`.\n- **Own card**, in the world: slow orbit of the trawler at dusk, the title, each player in their colour with a ready tick, how to win, this player's\n  controls, the countdown from the `card` event. Cross or Enter is `AIHub.answer('ready')`, Triangle or T is `AIHub.answer('more')`, and a tap or click on the card works too. It changes nothing in the round. **Listen for Enter with a plain `window` `keydown` listener added right after `connect()`, not through frame-sampled input:** the harness pokes Enter into the frame and allows 3 s, and frames are slow on the software renderer. Poll the pad in `requestAnimationFrame` here too.\n- `AIHub.ready()` once `createEngine` resolves, with no key press. **The harness waits only 20 s for this** (§16.7).\n- Play starts when `AIHub.time() >= 0`. A shared world finishes through the host: `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won, stats, awards })`, with a last reliable\n  snapshot first. `time-up` means finish now, within `graceMs`.\n- `end`: stop input, stop sound, stop the engine. `leave`: remove that player's actor. If no WebGPU: `AIHub.fail('WebGPU required')`.\n- **No** `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open`, navigation, sockets, `fetch` or chat. Options opens a small Settings overlay only; the round keeps running.\n- `AIHub.server` true (host with no player): run the world, no local player, input or card, and no heavy drawing beyond what the engine does.\n\n### 10.3 Netcode\n\nHost-authoritative for the world, client-authoritative for each player's own body. It is the pattern of the protocol's `examples/arena.html`.\n\n```text\nClient -> host  {t:'me', at, x,y,z, yaw,pitch, st, w}          12 Hz, unreliable, to the host\nClient -> host  {t:'shot'|'kick'|'use'|'rev', at, ...}         reliable, as they happen, at most 8/s\nHost  -> all    {t:'s', at, wave, left, p:[...], f:[...]}      10 Hz, unreliable, at most 1,200 bytes\nHost  -> all    {t:'e', ev:[[code, ...args], ...]}             reliable batches, at most 8/s\n```\n\n- **Budget:** at most 20 messages a second leave a copy, 16 KB each. An unreliable message over 1,200 bytes is lost whole if any packet is. A foe is about\n  28 bytes (`[nid, x·100, z·100, yaw·10, hp%, state, kind]`), so 24 foes fit. Past that, send alternate foes in alternate snapshots.\n- **Your controls never wait.** Your own actor moves locally. Your shot raycasts locally against what you see, with instant tracer, sound and hit marker; the host\n  applies damage from the `shot` message. In co-op, trust the client: no anti-cheat.\n- **Replicas are actors on both sides:** spawned from events, moved by steering. Each step: `move` toward the latest snapshot position, scaled by distance; a snap past 1.5 m. Foes' states\n  pick clips and reactions. Ragdolls may differ between copies; nobody will mind.\n- **Sim boundary [verified].** The sim never touches the network. Page code gathers each frame's messages and hands them over as a custom intent:\n  `engine.input.virtual.axis('game:net', { seq, msgs })`. A `net` system in phase `intents` applies each `seq` once (axes hold until changed). The same page reads\n  outgoing sim events from `frame.world.events.trace()` and sends them. This keeps \"the page never writes the sim\" and makes host runs replayable.\n- **Roles** come in as a setting: `game.role` = `solo`, `host`, `server` or `client`. On a client, AI, spawning and hazards do not run; `net` drives everything but the local player.\n- **Use a transport interface** (`send`, `on`, `me`, `players`, `isHost`, `time`), with `AIHub` behind one implementation and an in-memory one with seeded latency and loss behind another, so\n  host and client sims can be tested together in Vitest with no browser (§17).\n\n## 11. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n\nDesigned for a DualSense on a TV at 10 feet. Keyboard and mouse get the same screens and feel native on them.\n\n- **Look: a claims department in a storm.** Manila folders, carbon paper, typewriter text, red rubber stamps. Pause is a folder. Game over is a stamp. The shop is chalk on a crate lid.\n  Fonts are CSS stacks only: `\"Courier New\", monospace` for forms, `Georgia, serif` small caps for headings. No font files.\n- **Scale.** All UI sizes come from one scale, `min(innerWidth / 1920, innerHeight / 1080)`. At 1080p: body text at least 34 px, smallest text 28 px, subtitle 40 px, menu rows at least 56 px tall, at most 7 rows showing. 5% safe margin all round.\n- **No dense screens.** One column of choices, one detail pane, big single numbers. If a screen looks like a web page, redo it.\n- **HUD.** Bottom right: ammo as `10 / 42`, 96 px, with a weapon silhouette. Bottom left: health as a large stamped word and bar: **INSURED** (teal, 60%+), **UNDERINSURED** (amber), **UNINSURABLE** (red, pulsing, under 30%).\n  Top left: objective for 6 s when it changes. Centre: the prompt, at 64 px glyph and 44 px text. Top right: Wren. Direction arcs when hit. It fades in calm moments.\n- **Prompts follow the last input used.** PlayStation glyphs for a pad by default, with a Settings option for Xbox (A B X Y), keycaps and mouse icons otherwise. Draw the glyphs as inline SVG. Write `glyphFor(action)`: `input.bindings.codes(action)`, filtered with\n  `deviceOf`, by **your own** last-device tracker, from keydown, pointer and a poll of `navigator.getGamepads()`. Don't use `input.lastDevice`: it reads `virtual` whenever the game feeds the virtual device (netcode, attract), and prompts fall back to the keyboard [verified].\n- **Menus.** `createMenu` for lists (hover moves focus and a click picks, built in), themed with CSS over `.ui-panel` and `.ui-menu`. Add W and S to its arrows. `createPadCursor` is available for odd panels. While a menu is up: `inspector.pause()`, `modal: () => true`; the mouse cursor shows and pointer lock is released. Starting play shows \"Click to aim\" until the lock is taken.\n- **Touch-only devices** (`matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` with no pad connected): no touch controls at all. Always pass `touch=off` [verified: no touch UI appears]. Show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and a Settings button. Attract mode runs behind it. A pad connecting or a key pressed dismisses the gate. **Build the gate in plain DOM, created before `createEngine`,** since `engine.ui` is null when the renderer can't start. A Chromium phone profile on `file://` has WebGPU and runs attract [verified]; the WebKit iPhone profile has no WebGPU at all [verified], so there the gate shows over a dark page with no attract, and the engine's own error overlay stays hidden.\n- **No WebGPU, not touch:** a styled message saying which browsers have it (Chrome or Edge, recent Safari). No WebGL fallback.\n- **Dialogue and cutscenes.** `createDialog`: `modal: false` with `auto` for radio, Tannoy and barks, so play goes on; modal for the shop patter and story talk. Cutscenes run in the world, with own cameras (`node x new camera`, `camera.set(code, { blend: true })`), `modal: () => true`, a letterbox through `post.combine`, and always skippable (hold Circle or Esc). Keep them short: 20 s at most, and most are under 10.\n\n**Screens:** splash (\"Pelham & Grice Mutual Assurance presents\") · title (New Claim, Continue, Last Stand, Settings, Controls, About) · pause (Resume, Case, Claim File, Settings, Controls, Dev Mode, Retry from checkpoint, Main menu) · Case · Claim File (objective, a paper map drawn in SVG with pins, memos) · shop · Settings · Controls · About/Credits · dialogue and subtitles · game over · results · Dev Mode · touch gate · hub card.\n\n**Settings:** volume sliders with the music at **10% by default** (§13); difficulty; pad glyphs (PlayStation or Xbox); look sensitivity and invert for stick and mouse (`input.*`); aim assist; subtitle size; HUD scale; vibration (via `vibrationActuator` where present); quality (`auto`, `low`, `medium`, `high`); key and button rebinding. All kept in the store, and every setting's a row a pad can change with left and right.\n\n## 12. Art direction and animation\n\n**Base: the engine's native procedural style.** Everything is code and data: no image, model or sound files. What makes it ours is fog, dusk, silhouette and material.\n\n**Palette.** Slate, wet stone, tar black, oilskin yellow gone sour, rust. One warm accent, lantern amber. One cold accent, Lodger cyan-green (`#5ff0c4`), used for nothing else. Hero's tie is the only pure red on screen until the laser.\n\n**The look [verified as a start].** This took a foggy hamlet with a crowd closing in from nothing to moody in a few lines. Tune from here. Lower the sun's glare: at this setting its bloom whites out part of the sky.\n\n```ts\ndefineSky('sky:skerry', {\n  description: 'A sick, smoke-orange dusk with heavy ground fog.',\n  background: '#6a5a4c', pointLights: 1.6,\n  dome: { show: true, turbidity: 9, rayleigh: 3, mieCoefficient: 0.02, mieDirectionalG: 0.85, exposure: 0.35 },\n  sun: { color: '#ff9a60', intensity: 1.1, azimuth: 2.4, elevation: 0.14 },\n  ambient: { sky: '#8f8a90', ground: '#2a2a22', intensity: 0.75 },\n  fog: { color: '#7b6f60', start: 7, end: 62, amount: 0.92, floor: 0, ceiling: 2.4, height: 0.35 },\n  backdrop: { haze: '#8a7a6a', tint: '#6a6058', layers: [{ kind: 'mountains', color: '#4a4a48', height: 0.95 }] },\n});\ndefineLook('look:skerry', {\n  description: 'The island at dusk.', sky: 'sky:skerry', resolution: 'full', textures: 'smooth',\n  filters: {\n    aa: { scope: 'all' },\n    bloom: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.18, threshold: 1.1, radius: 0.5 },\n    air: { scope: 'all', haze: 0.5, height: 3, shafts: 1, halos: 0.5 },\n    grade: { scope: 'all', saturation: 0.72, contrast: 1.12, temperature: 0.08, gamma: 0.95 },\n    vignette: { scope: 'all', strength: 0.5, softness: 0.55 },\n    grain: { scope: 'all', amount: 0.18 },\n  },\n});\n```\n\nEach zone may lay its own grade on top (`post.combine`, view settings, never hashed): Marsh greener, thicker fog; Cannery tungsten amber and darker; Abbey cold moonlight (`sky:night` base); Causeway storm, then the last red dusk for the ending.\n\n**Make these** (engine library for generic crates, barrels, lanterns, benches):\n\n- **Characters (`defineBody`).** Start from the playground's `PLAYER_BODY` (§16.1 for where), a clothed human, and redress it; `body:humanoid`'s slot names are not what you'd guess. Quill: trench coat with the engine's `Cape` secondary motion (`secondary: { cape: true, color }`), red tie, briefcase in the off hand when not aiming. Parishioners: at least 6 dresses by seed with oilskin, sou'wester or cap; gaff, oar and knife as body parts on the hand bones. Netwife, Deacon, Hatchman (shield as a box part), Gutter (lobster-pot head of thin boxes, saw on a pole), Brack, Sedge, Goole, Salvor, Wren. Lodger eyes: unlit `eye` parts in the cold accent.\n- **Bursting.** The view makes a puppet once and does not re-read `puppet.body` [verified]. So a Lodger burst replaces the actor: `removeActor`, then `spawnActor` on the spot with `body:parishionerBurst` (head parts removed, a neck stump, and for the lamprey the `secondary` component's hair chain, `{ hair: 'ponytail', color: '#5ff0c4' }`, the only chain that hangs at head height), with a splash of brine to hide the swap. Lash: a line of emitter bursts along the `telegraph:line`, 0.35 s.\n- **World.** Materials: salt-stained stone, tarred planks, slate, rust iron, net. Slate-roofed cottages (level format 2, `roof: gable`, `pitch: 35`). Drying racks of herring, lobster pots, coiled rope, nets, rowboats on shingle, a bonfire, candles, Tannoy horns on poles (visible, always), stilted huts, cannery conveyors, rail hooks, boilers, fish-oil barrels and pools, abbey arches, shelves of ledgers, lighthouse with a lens beam (a long unlit transparent prop). Sea plane with `texture:water`, gulls by emitter. Check the ground up close: my grass looked streaky at grazing angles; a tighter `map` scale or another texture fixes it.\n- **Light.** Lanterns and braziers (`prop:lantern`, `prop:brazier`, your own props with light spots) make the night; the engine's pool picks the nearest. Group them with `switchGroup` for scripted blackouts. Every interior needs an amber pool to walk toward.\n- **Effects (`defineEmitter`).** Brine (a dark teal-black spray, no red blood), muzzle flash and tracer (free with the `gunshot` event, §16.3), rain and sea spray through `frame.emit`, fire, sparks on parry, paper storm in the Vault, Lodger mist.\n\n**Animation: the engine's animator, plus clips and new actions.** Clip ids below are real [verified with `node x anim find`]; register only the sets you use (§16.2).\n\n| Moment | Clip or engine feature |\n|---|---|\n| Parishioner shamble, idle | `quaternius/Zombie_Walk_Fwd_Loop`, `quaternius/Zombie_Idle_Loop`, variants in `mesh2motion/Zombie_Walk_2`, `cmu/Zombie_Walk_Loop` |\n| Claw attack, roar | `quaternius/Zombie_Scratch`, `mesh2motion/Zombie Yell` |\n| Thrower | `quaternius/OverhandThrow` |\n| Kneel | `mesh2motion/Kneeling Tired` |\n| Knocked flat, death, rise | `quaternius/Hit_Knockback`, `mesh2motion/Death_A` to `D`, `quaternius/LayToIdle`, `mesh2motion/Zombie_Rise`, ragdolls with `handOff` |\n| Pistol | Engine hold and aim IK, `quaternius/Pistol_Reload`, `quaternius/Pistol_Shoot` |\n| Kick | `move:roundhouse` through `Attack` and `states.body`, or `cmu/Roundhouse_Kick` trimmed |\n| Door kick | `mesh2motion/Kick_Breach`, `move:breach` |\n| Vault, ladder | `quaternius/ClimbUp_1m`, `mesh2motion/Climb Ladder` |\n| Crawl (downed) | `mesh2motion/Crawl` |\n| Carry Wren | `quaternius/Walk_Carry_Loop` |\n| Stagger, grabs | Actions `action:dizzy`, `action:grab`, `action:grabbed`, `action:hurt` |\n\n**New animations you must make** (`node x new action`, or readable clips with `parseClip`), since they're the character: Quill straightening his tie; his knee-rub idle; reloading with the briefcase tucked under his arm; plank kick; foe reel (clutching its face); foe mid-sermon kneel and rise; Salvor rubbing hands and pointing with his pipe; Wren cranking, and her boost; Goole's sermon gestures; Brack's anchor wind-up and roar; Sedge's lunge and parried recoil.\n\n## 13. Audio\n\nAll code, no audio files. Engine: `defineSfx`, `defineSong`, `createAudio` (buses `effects`, `music`, `ui`, `ambience`; `play(id, { pitch, vol, when, position, bus, duck, loop })`; `room`; `music`, `intensity`, `stinger`).\n\n- **Music at 10% by default.** At startup, before any song: `audio.volume('music', 0.1)`, and the Settings slider shows 10%. A test reads it.\n- **Music (`defineSong`, own tunes):** title (slow harmonium over wind); exploration (low drones, far foghorn); combat, built in `intensity` layers that join as foes close (low strings, anvil, frantic fiddle); filing-cabinet room (gentle harmonium, the safest sound in the game); the Salvor's stall (a sly squeezebox shanty, the theme people will hum); boss; finale; results jingle.\n- **Effects:** every gun, reload, kick, slash and parry clang, body hits, saw engine (a loop with distance, heard long before seen), foghorn (huge, low, the game's signature sound), Tannoy crackle with hall reverb, gulls, sea, wind, rain, creaking hull, footsteps by surface (`footstepSound`), doors, glass, UI: typewriter clack for moves, stamp thud for picks.\n- **Rooms:** `audio.room(...)` by zone. Walls muffle (`update(pose, queries)`).\n- **Voices: Animalese style.** A phoneme kit of about 16 short `sfx:vo-*` entries (voiced formants with `saw` or `pulse` through bandpass filters; noise for consonants). A line's text maps to syllables: letter to phoneme, played in sequence with `when` from the context clock at 11 to 16 a second. Each speaker has a base `pitch`, a rate and a kit tweak: Quill low and dry; Wren quick and high; Thripp clipped; Goole slow, deep, on the `effects` bus with Tannoy filtering and hall reverb; Salvor bouncy, rising; Brack a growl; Parishioners a low mutter by position, three times out of ten with a subtitle (\"Bless the tide.\"). Duck music while speaking. A Voice slider scales `vol`.\n- Every sound is presentation: sim events drive it from `frame.world.events.trace()`, never the reverse. `node x qa audio` must pass.\n\n## 14. Attract mode\n\nAfter **10 seconds with no input** on the title or any front-end menu (not in the pause menu or in a session), the game starts a looping AI-played demo. **Any input exits** back to the title: key, click, pointer moved past 8 px, pad button, stick past 0.4. On touch-only devices it runs regardless and a tap only shows the gate.\n\n- **It runs the real game.** `inspector.set('game.mode', 'attract')`, `inspector.seed(n)`. A page-side bot drives through `engine.input.virtual` (`axis`, `hold`, `press`), and cheats freely: dev actions for `god`, ammo and teleports. `modal` stays false so the virtual device reaches the sim. It writes no saves. On exit: `virtual.clear()`, back to `title` mode.\n- **The loop, about 100 s, a beat each 10 to 15 s, with a slow camera cut between:** walking the Slip in fog; aim, knee, kick on Fish Lane; the trawler siege with a plank kick and a winch net; the Gutter; Case screen with items moving; Salvor stall; flare on a Whip in the Marsh; Wren carried off and shot free; Brack's lure; Sedge parry; Undertow in the beam; four players on the trawler.\n- **On screen:** title in the corner, a stamped DEMO, \"Press any button\" in the current glyph style, pulsing.\n\n## 15. Dev mode\n\nFrom the pause menu, item **Dev Mode**. Not in hub sessions. Large panel, playable on a pad: left and right change a value, a mouse can drag.\n\n**Live sliders** (each a `defineSettings` entry read every step, so replays record them; each row with its default, and **Reset all to defaults**, plus one row's reset):\n\n| Area | Sliders |\n|---|---|\n| Player | Run speed (`movement.gaits.run`), sprint (`movement.gaits.sprint`), aim shuffle (`movement.gaits.walk`, default 0: planted), max HP, camera arm, field of view (`cam.fov`), laser wobble, aim assist |\n| Guns | Damage ×, fire rate ×, reload time ×, recoil ×, head multiplier, leg multiplier, kick damage, kick radius, parry window |","numLines":300,"startLine":330,"totalLines":913}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GThcTsHnkcXv2wk1Ps74KA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
