{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDeiVXYuW2tYKLKS3pn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018tZWxwhG5bbVYzYspZE3TY","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/PLAN.md","offset":629},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13503,"cache_read_input_tokens":632310,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13503},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"4ccee58c-091c-4fe6-beb0-de0930865cf7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:20:53.018Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDeiCRcdWywLnJZ3HrW","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018tZWxwhG5bbVYzYspZE3TY":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/PLAN.md","offset":629}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018tZWxwhG5bbVYzYspZE3TY","type":"tool_result","content":"629\t| Guns | Damage ×, fire rate ×, reload time ×, recoil ×, head multiplier, leg multiplier, kick damage, kick radius, parry window |\n630\t| Foes | HP ×, speed ×, damage ×, wind-up time ×, max attackers at once, max on field, sight range, burst chance |\n631\t| Economy | Drop rate, shillings ×, shop prices ×, Risk Rating lock |\n632\t| Partner, prompts | Wren HP, carry speed, follow distance, prompt window × |\n633\t| World (view) | Fog amount, grade strength, music level |\n634\t\n635\t**Tools:** god mode, freeze AI, time scale and hit-stop off (engine dev actions `god`, `freeze`, `timeScale`); infinite ammo, one-hit kills, give money, give all weapons, give all salvage; jump to any beat from a list; start or skip an encounter; kill all; spawn any foe at the laser's point; free camera (`cam3=fly`); labels over foes (state, HP, zones); a stats line (`__engine.stats()`, hash, tick, entities); **Copy balance as JSON** (`navigator.clipboard`, no dialog); **Record a replay** (`input.record()`).\n636\t\n637\t## 16. Technology\n638\t\n639\t### 16.1 Setup (exact, [verified])\n640\t\n641\tFrom the empty dev folder:\n642\t\n643\t```sh\n644\tsrc=$(mktemp -d) && git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge \"$src\" && node \"$src/tools/game/new-game.mjs\" . --name game\n645\tnpm ci   # 6 s. npm test then passes in 10 s, and npm run check in 13 s, on this machine.\n646\texport CHROMIUM_PATH=$(ls -d \"$HOME\"/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-*/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell | head -1)\n647\tnode x shot labs/game            # about 7 s\n648\tnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim   # about 17 s\n649\t```\n650\t\n651\t- **Don't run `scripts/setup.sh`.** It downloads Node and Chrome into your home folder. The machine's Node 24 satisfies the engine and `npm ci` is enough.\n652\t- **Use the headless shell for `CHROMIUM_PATH`, not the full `chrome`.** The full binary dies under this run's long temp path with `Socket path too long` [verified]; set the variable in every shell you use for `x shot`, `x film` or `x replay --browser`. `@playwright/test` from the workspace uses it through `executablePath`, no browser download.\n653\t- **Don't `git init` or commit.** The dev folder already sits inside the harness's repository. Skip the commit steps in AGENTS.md.\n654\t- **You share this machine.** Keep every file you make inside your folder, not in `/tmp` or a parent; don't read the folders beside yours. Prefer `file://` and the engine's headless tools. A server only for the hub harness (§17), on a port the OS picks. Stop only what you started, by PID: never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`.\n655\t- **Keep `$src`, read-only.** Its `labs/playground/` is the best worked example of this exact genre on this engine, and new-game does **not** copy it (the guide mentions it anyway). Read `cast/player.ts`, `controls.ts`, `weapons/`, `cast/neighbours.ts`, `cast/partners.ts`, `cast/ways.ts`, `bodies/player.ts`, `levels/plan.ts`, `levels/site.ts`, `scenes/site.ts`, `ui/`. Copy and adapt what you need into `labs/game/`. Never import from it.\n656\t- Read AGENTS.md (the game's) and `docs/GAME-GUIDE.md` once. Look things up in `docs/API.md`, the file comments, `node x describe`, `node x help`, `__engine.help()`. Write friction in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` as you go; TASK.md's Engine Feedback comes from it.\n657\t- **The engine is read-only** (`npm run check` compares every file). Everything below is achievable on top of it. Files stay under 400 lines with a `@file` comment.\n658\t\n659\t### 16.2 Folder layout\n660\t\n661\tLint treats `labs/*/scenes/**` and `labs/*/cast/**` as sim-side, importing only `engine/sim-api.ts`. `x qa` reads `labs/game/{geometry,props,textures,sounds}`. Everything else in `labs/game/` is page code, importing `engine/index.ts`.\n662\t\n663\t```text\n664\tlabs/game/\n665\t  index.html  main.ts  title.ts     page entry (keep the starter's error handling)\n666\t  data/          plain tables with no engine imports: items, weapons, foes, shop, waves, beats, dialogue, balance defaults\n667\t  scenes/        sim: world.ts (game:world), square.ts (game:square), systems as files: guns, melee, qte, foes, director,\n668\t                 story, drops, risk, caseGrid, partner, bosses/*, net, laststand, save\n669\t  cast/          sim: hero, wren, each foe, each boss\n670\t  levels/        defineLevel text (adapt the playground's Plan helper), site.ts (terrain, structures, zones)\n671\t  props/ geometry/ textures/ sounds/     data, read by x qa\n672\t  bodies/ looks/ materials.ts clips.ts   page registration (bodies, skies, looks, materials, clip sets)\n673\t  ui/            hud, prompts, glyphs, menus, case, shop, claimFile, dialogue, settings, controls, about, gameover, results, dev, gate, card\n674\t  audio/         page sound: events to sfx, music director, voice\n675\t  net/           hub.ts, transport, memory transport, session.client.txt\n676\t  attract/       attract.ts (bot and beats)\n677\t  bot/           campaign bot, its helpers\n678\t  tools/         bundle.mjs, verify.mjs\n679\t  replays/\n680\t```\n681\t\n682\t**Data-driven, so the rest of the game could be built with normal designer tools.** A new zone means: a level as text, an entry in the site, a beats table, an encounters table, dialogue lines. A new foe or weapon means a row of data and a body. No system needs editing for content. `node x new <kind>` scaffolds bodies, props, looks, levels, songs, sounds, actions.\n683\t\n684\t**Modes** are a setting, `game.mode` (`title`, `campaign`, `laststand`, `attract`, `gallery`), read in `setup`. Changing mode or loading a save: `inspector.set(...)`, then `inspector.seed(n)`, which restarts the scene and keeps changed settings [verified]. `frame.world` is a new object after a restart, so page code resets what it remembers (event `seq`, for one) when it changes.\n685\t\n686\t**Scenes.** `game:world` is everything. `game:square` is the same terrain and coordinates with only the Square's structures, for hub rounds to load fast; both share all systems.\n687\t\n688\t### 16.3 Engine map\n689\t\n690\t| Need | Use | Worked example |\n691\t|---|---|---|\n692\t| Hero | `createCharacter({ movement })`, `spawnActor`, `defineMovement` | §16.4; playground `cast/player.ts` |\n693\t| Camera | `cam3=shoulder,<yaw°>,<pitch°>,<arm>`, `__engine.camera.set(code, { blend: true })`; own cinematic cameras with `node x new camera` | engine `gfx/cameras/shoulder.ts` |\n694\t| Guns | Own system; `defineWeapon`, `weaponsFor`, `getWeapon`, `recoilStep`, `spreadOf`, `physicsOf(w).raycast`, `entityOfBody` | engine `sim/weapons.ts` |\n695\t| Melee | `Attack`, `getMove`, `meleeTargets`, `requestHitStop`, `damage` | engine `sim/melee.ts` |\n696\t| Foes | `spawnActor({ player: false })`, `actor.intents`, `reactTo`, `handOff`, `addRagdolls`, `standUp`, `playClip`, `actOn` | playground `cast/partners.ts`, `neighbours.ts` |\n697\t| Hounds, Leeches, seal | `addAgent`, `CROWD_BODY`, rigs `quadruped`, `blob` | playground `cast/dog.ts`; `labs/box/cast/slime.ts` |\n698\t| AI kit | `approachRing`, `followFlow`, `takeToken`, `sense`, `earshot`, `Noise`, `SpatialHash`, `defineTelegraph`, `inTelegraph` | `labs/box/cast/walker.ts`, `labs/box/scenes/fight-foes.ts` |\n699\t| World | `defineTerrain`, `defineSite`, `addSiteBodies`, `addSiteLadders`, `createSiteNav`, `propObstacles`, `siteFloorBelow`, `siteClearSight` | playground `levels/site.ts`, `scenes/site.ts`, `cast/ways.ts` |\n700\t| Doors, windows, breakables | `addLevelDoors`, `addDoor`, `strikeDoor`, `addLevelWindows`, `addBreakables`, `damageProp` | playground `scenes/site.ts` |\n701\t| Use prompts | `addInteraction`, `defineUsable`, `interactor.prompt` | `node x new interactable` |\n702\t| Moving platform | `driveMover`, `MOVER`, `moverPose` (phase `ai`) | engine `physics/bodies.ts` |\n703\t| Targets (gallery) | `defineThing`, `spawnThing` | playground `weapons/range.ts` |\n704\t| Triggers | `addSensor`, `updateTrigger` | engine `physics/bodies.ts` |\n705\t| Page → sim | Dev actions: `actions: { name(w, args) }` in the scene, `inspector.actions.run(name, args)`. Custom intents: `input.virtual.axis('game:x', data)` | §10.3 |\n706\t| Saves, prefs | `createStore`, `createEngine({ store })` | `labs/game/best.ts` |\n707\t\n708\t**Why a game-owned gun system.** The engine's `addWeapons` is for a range: its reload refills from nothing, it fires from the hip, and one set of intents drives every player. We need ammo from the Case, no hip fire, pellets, piercing, per-gun upgrades, and per-actor intents for co-op. Copy the logic of `stepOne` from `engine/sim/weapons.ts` into `scenes/guns.ts`, keeping the **component `weapons`** (`weaponsFor`) so the view still draws the gun in hand and the camera still reads `aim` and `kick`. **Emit the same `gunshot` event** `{ id, weapon, from, to, normal, body, target, hit }`, and you get tracer, muzzle flash, impact and bullet holes for free. Also set `animator.weapon` and `motion.holstered` as it does.\n709\t\n710\t### 16.4 Recipes that worked [verified]\n711\t\n712\t**Planted aim, with no fighting the controller.** On a movement profile, holding `aim` with a gun out sets the gait to `walk`. So make `walk` 0. Measured: 3.15 m in a second running, 0.135 m of slide while aiming.\n713\t\n714\t```ts\n715\tconst apex = getMovement('movement:apex');\n716\tdefineMovement('movement:quill', {\n717\t  description: 'Runs like a man of 51. Plants his feet to aim.',\n718\t  character: apex.character,\n719\t  model: { gaits: { walk: 0, run: 3.4, sprint: 5.2, holstered: 1 } },\n720\t});\n721\tspawnActor(w, {\n722\t  at, yaw, player: true, holstered: false,\n723\t  character: createCharacter({ movement: 'movement:quill' }),\n724\t  body: 'body:quill', anim: { build: 'build:adult', weapon: 'gun' },\n725\t  components: { weapons: weaponsFor(['weapon:deductible'], 0) },\n726\t});\n727\t```\n728\t\n729\tPass `input.sprint=hold` so run is a hold. The live slider for `movement.gaits.walk` gives the aim-shuffle option. Add no `jump` to the action map, and he never jumps, slides or mantles.\n730\t\n731\t**Action map.** `defineActionMap('actionMap:quill', { look: true, aimWith: 'centre', lock: true, actions: {...}, view: ['case', 'map', 'shoulder'] })`. Name the aim action `aim` and fire `fire`: the view keys off those. Read view actions through `createEngine({ onView })`.\n732\t\n733\t**Foe.**\n734\t\n735\t```ts\n736\tdefineComponent('health', { description: 'Hit points.', fields: HEALTH_FIELDS });\n737\tspawnActor(w, {\n738\t  at, player: false, character: createCharacter({ speed: 1.3 }),\n739\t  body: 'body:parishioner0', anim: { build: 'build:adult', weapon: 'none' },\n740\t  clips: { sets: ['clipset:quaternius'] },              // here, at spawn: see the traps\n741\t  components: { health: { hp: 100, hitAt: -1, hitBy: -1 }, foe: { kind: 'parishioner', state: 'idle' } },\n742\t});\n743\t// each step: f.actor.intents = { move: [dx, dz] };  from its first step: playClip(w, f.id, 'quaternius/Zombie_Walk_Fwd_Loop');\n744\t```\n745\t\n746\t**Hit zones.** `const y = shot.to[1] - foe.actor.y;` then the table in §6.1. Handle the event with `w.events.on('gunshot', ...)` or inside `game.guns` itself. Falling: `handOff(w, id, { push: [dx * 3, 1, dz * 3], dead: true })`. Flinching: `reactTo(w, id, (r) => r.hit(dirVector3, yaw, 1))`, as in the playground's partners.\n747\t\n748\t**Bodies and builds.** Copying a registry entry needs its `id` and `kind` removed: `const { id, kind, ...rest } = getBody('body:humanoid')`. A giant is `defineBuild('build:brack', { ...adultFields, size: 2.7 })` with `createCharacter({ speed, capsule: { radius: 0.9, height: 3.4 } })`, and it reads great. `defineBody`, `defineMaterial`, `defineSky` and `defineLook` are page-side, and the sim names them by id; `defineProp`, `defineLevel`, `defineTerrain`, `defineSite`, `defineWeapon`, `defineMovement` are sim-side.\n749\t\n750\t**Laser.** A page cannot add its own meshes through the public API. Draw the beam as a thin rotated CSS line in the overlay from the projected muzzle to the projected end, computing the end with `frame.queries.raycast` along the camera's centre. Add a 3D glow for the dot with a running emitter: `frame.emit('emitter:laserDot', at, 'laser')`. Project with `frame.camera` (position, yaw, pitch, fov). Note it in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\n751\t\n752\t**Clips in the page.** Register them in a statically imported module:\n753\t\n754\t```ts\n755\t// labs/game/clips.ts\n756\tconst TEXT = import.meta.glob<string>('../../data/anim/sets/quaternius/*.json', { query: '?raw', import: 'default', eager: true });\n757\tconst files = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(TEXT).map(([p, t]) => [p.split('/').pop()!, t]));\n758\tdefineClipSet(clipSetFromFiles(files, 'data/anim/sets/quaternius'));\n759\t```\n760\t\n761\tRegister `quaternius` and `mesh2motion`, and `cmu` if you use it. In Vitest, read the same files with `node:fs`.\n762\t\n763\t**Page boot order.**\n764\t\n765\t```ts\n766\timport './clips'; import './bodies'; import './looks'; /* every registration, static, first */\n767\tconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\n768\tfor (const key of [...search.keys()]) if (key.startsWith('aihub')) search.delete(key);   // see the traps\n769\tsearch.set('touch', 'off');\n770\tif (!search.has('cam3') && !search.has('cam')) search.set('cam3', 'shoulder,0,-4,2.8');\n771\tif (!search.has('post.look')) search.set('post.look', 'look:skerry');\n772\tif (!search.has('gfx.warmUp')) search.set('gfx.warmUp', 'asked');\n773\tconst hub = window.AIHub;\n774\tconst info = hub?.active ? await hub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\n775\t// with info: wire hub handlers NOW, set game.role, game.mode=laststand, seed=info.seed, ?scene=game:square (§16.7)\n776\tconst engine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['game:world', 'game:square'], search: `?${search}`, store, modal, onFrame, onView, actionMap: 'actionMap:quill' });\n777\t```\n778\t\n779\t### 16.5 Navigation\n780\t\n781\tCopy the idea of the playground's `cast/ways.ts`: `createSiteNav(site, { blocks: propObstacles(w) })`, one flow field per goal, flooded lazily, remade when a door or prop blocks the way. `nav.direction(field, x, y, z)` gives a foe its `move`. Make it on the first step, not in `setup`, since no query sees props in `setup`.\n782\t\n783\t### 16.6 Packaging [verified]\n784\t\n785\tThere's no game-side `x html`: the engine's `tools/lib/oneFile.ts` is hard-wired to the playground. Copy its method in `labs/game/tools/bundle.mjs`, run from the dev folder:\n786\t\n787\t```js\n788\tconst result = await build({\n789\t  root, configFile: false, logLevel: 'warn', base: './',\n790\t  resolve: { alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }] },\n791\t  build: {\n792\t    write: false, modulePreload: false, cssCodeSplit: false, assetsInlineLimit: () => true,\n793\t    chunkSizeWarningLimit: Infinity, target: 'esnext',\n794\t    rollupOptions: { input: { game: join(root, 'labs/game/index.html') }, output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } },\n795\t  },\n796\t});\n797\t// then: put each chunk and stylesheet inline, as oneFile.ts's inlineBuild does, using a replacer FUNCTION (the code holds $ signs):\n798\t//   script text with '</script' written as '<\\/script'; fail the build on '<!--' inside a script.\n799\t// then, right after <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />: <script>{session.client.txt, byte for byte}</script> and the hub:* tags.\n800\t// write to the deliverable's path one folder up, and set <title> from GAME_TITLE.\n801\t```\n802\t\n803\tThe starter came out at 6.7 MB and opened from `file://` with WebGPU, no errors, in 6 s on the software renderer. The hub checks that the pasted client is byte-identical to a release (SHA-256, banner to last line).\n804\t\n805\t### 16.7 Traps I hit, so you don't [all verified]\n806\t\n807\t1. **The hub's URL kills the engine.** The hub opens the page with `?aihub=1` (and `aihub-seed`). `createEngine` refuses any query key that isn't a declared setting (`CORE_BAD_SETTING`), so the engine never starts and the harness shows no traffic. **Strip `aihub*` before passing `search`.** Your own URL flags must be declared with `defineSettings`.\n808\t2. **`await import()` is eager in the one-file build.** With `inlineDynamicImports`, the imported module runs before the importer's body. Registering something then dynamically importing the page works in dev and fails in the bundle (`CORE_NO_ENTRY`). Register in static imports; put them first.\n809\t3. **The harness waits only 20 s for `ready()` from every copy,** and 4 WebGPU copies on the software renderer are slow. A hamlet-sized scene with 18 foes took 12.5 to 17 s at 4 players with these rules, and passed: `game:square` not the whole island; `gfx.warmUp=asked`; **on a software adapter in a session only**, `post.look=look:clean`, `quality=low`, `gfx.governor=false` (`adapter.info.isFallbackAdapter` or `architecture === 'swiftshader'`). Wire the `time-up` and `end` handlers before `createEngine`, so a slow copy still answers them. Spawn foes after start, not in `setup`.\n810\t4. **`spawnActor`'s entity isn't live in `setup`.** `addClips` and `playClip` right after it throw `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT`. Give `clips` at spawn, and play from the first step.\n811\t5. **`input.lastDevice` says `virtual`** after anything touches the virtual device, including net intents and attract. Track the last device yourself (§11).\n812\t6. **A bare `cam3=shoulder` faces +Z (south), ignoring the hero's yaw.** Name the yaw in the code, and call `camera.set` after any teleport.\n813\t7. **The governor lowers quality on slow frames** (`GFX_GOVERNOR`). Fine for players. For screenshots: `gfx.governor=false&quality=high`.\n814\t8. **The software renderer draws about one frame a second** with the full look at 1280×720 (800 ms GPU a frame), and the clock lags behind. Tests use `__engine.step(n)` and read state, at 480×270 with `post.look=look:clean&quality=low`. A WebGPU canvas may come out blank in a screenshot under some setups: check the state.\n815\t9. **`puppet.body` isn't re-read by the view.** Replace the actor (§12).\n816\t10. **Level text errors are good.** `LEVEL_BAD_ROOF` tells you a gable wants `pitch: 35`. Read them.\n817\t11. **`session.client.txt`, not `.js`:** as code it would fail the `@file` and line-count lint.\n818\t12. **Spare CPU, shared machine.** One or two browsers at a time. `earlyoom` may end the biggest browser: \"Target closed\" means memory, so run fewer.\n819\t\n820\t## 17. Testing\n821\t\n822\t**One command, `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs [sim|page|hub|all]`, prints only failures and a one-line count** (for example `verify: 214 checks, 0 failed`). Rerun only the part you changed. Screenshots only for what a script can't check. **No subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.**\n823\t\n824\t**Sim (Vitest, Node, no browser):**\n825\t- The four kinds the guide asks for: a golden replay, capture-and-restore continuing exactly, the bot winning across seeds, rule tests. Record goldens on purpose: `node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim --update`.\n826\t- Rules: damage table by zone; kick radius, i-frames, knockdowns; parry window; Case fit, rotate, autosort, combine (property-style with many seeds); shop math; adaptive drops favour what's lacking; save and load round-trip; every beat reachable; Wren carried to the chute loses; plank removal stops boarding.\n827\t- **The scripted playthrough of the whole game: `bot/campaign.ts` plays from Cold Open to the results screen through intents and dev-action menu picks**, including shop visits and every boss, on default difficulty, on 3 seeds (10 with `--full`). It's sim-only, about 3 to 5 ms a step, so a 10-minute bot run is under 3 minutes. If the bot can't win, find out whether it's the bot or the balance.\n828\t- Co-op: a host sim and 3 client sims joined by the memory transport at 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss: foes converge within 1.5 m; a client's shot kills; a client's revive works; host finish reaches all.\n829\t- Balance sanity: shots to kill per weapon, total shillings on a playthrough within 20,000 to 30,000.\n830\t\n831\t**Page, on the built deliverable from `file://`** (Playwright with `executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH` and args `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`; `window.__game` exposes `screen()` and `state()`; the UI is read through `[data-ui]` DOM queries):\n832\t- Boots with no errors or advice. Title shows `GAME_TITLE`. Enter and Space on the title behave (the hub opens the game alone and presses them).\n833\t- Attract starts after 10 s idle and exits on key, on click, on a stubbed pad button.\n834\t- Pause, then Dev Mode: a slider changes a live value; reset restores defaults. Settings persist through a reload.\n835\t- **Music volume is 0.1 by default**, and the Web Audio graph makes sound (`AnalyserNode` level, or an `OfflineAudioContext` render of a song and a voice line).\n836\t- Glyphs: a `navigator.getGamepads` stub in standard mapping switches prompts to PlayStation; the Xbox setting gives A B X Y; a key press switches to keycaps.\n837\t- Pad and mouse each work the title, the Case (lift, rotate, place) and the shop. Hover moves focus.\n838\t- A Chromium phone profile (`devices['Pixel 7']`) shows the gate with the Settings button, with attract running, and no touch controls. WebKit's iPhone profile shows the gate with no WebGPU and no error text.\n839\t- Font sizes at 1920×1080 meet §11's minimums; nothing overflows.\n840\t- About/Credits holds every field from TASK.md's Source Information and all the feedback answers. The exit interview parses, and has every key.\n841\t\n842\t**Hub:** serve a folder holding `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` and the deliverable, on a port the OS picks, from your test process (Node `listen(0, '127.0.0.1')`, or `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`). First confirm the page is your game by its `<title>`. Stop only what you started, by PID. Assert `window.__hubCheck.pass` once `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` for:\n843\t\n844\t```text\n845\t?game=<name>&players=2&auto=1&limit=40&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\n846\t?game=<name>&players=4&auto=1&limit=40&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\n847\t?game=<name>&players=4&auto=1&limit=40&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave\n848\t?game=<name>&players=2&auto=1&limit=40&scenario=server\n849\t```\n850\t\n851\tA minimal version of this passed all four here [verified], with the one-file build, in 17 to 34 s each. Also test your own card (\"Enter answers Ready\" is checked once you declare `card: true`).\n852\t\n853\t**Visual checks:** a few `--png` shots at 1920×1080 (the look, the Case, a boss, the HUD from far away), `node x gallery` for bodies and props, `node x qa geo tex audio`, `npm run check`.\n854\t\n855\t**Keep a tally as you go** in `labs/game/README.md`: issues testing caught, how many were critical, the most and least helpful tests. TASK.md's Testing Feedback asks for exactly that, and it's hard to reconstruct at the end.\n856\t\n857\t## 18. Build order\n858\t\n859\tEach milestone ends with a complete game you could ship, and `verify` green.\n860\t\n861\t| # | Build | Done when |\n862\t|---|---|---|\n863\t| M0 | Pick the title. Scaffold. `bundle.mjs`, `verify.mjs`, one-file smoke test, harness pass with an empty round. | The pipeline runs end to end before there's a game. |\n864\t| M1 | **Core loop in the Square:** hero, camera, laser, `game.guns`, zones, reactions, kick, parry, foes with tokens, HUD, glyphs, gibberish voice, the look. | It's fun with 10 foes and one gun. If it isn't, stay here. Spend real time on the kick. |\n865\t| M2 | **Last Stand and netcode:** waves, score, revive, transport, roles, card, finish. Solo menu entry. | All four harness runs pass with real play, and it's a game already. |\n866\t| M3 | **Front end:** title, pause, Settings, Controls, About, Dev Mode with sliders, attract (first loop), touch gate. | Every UI test in §17 passes. |\n867\t| M4 | **Economy:** Case, items, drops, shop, service, saves, game over, results. | Bot buys and sells; a save round-trips. |\n868\t| M5 | **World and first act:** site, Slip, Office, Lane, full trawler siege with the Gutter, foghorn, Shingle, Claims Practice. | 20 great minutes. Bot plays through. |\n869\t| M6 | **Marsh and Cannery:** Hounds, Netwives, Whips, Deacons, Hatchmen, Wren, Hoist, Brack. | Escort is tense, not annoying. |\n870\t| M7 | **The finish:** Funicular, Abbey, Vault, Sedge, Causeway, Goole, Undertow, ending. | Bot plays Cold Open to results. |\n871\t| M8 | **Polish:** all music, line-by-line script, animations in §12, effects, zone grades, full attract loop, data tidy. | Nothing on screen is a placeholder. |\n872\t| M9 | **Close:** §19. | Everything in §19 ticked. |\n873\t\n874\t**If you run short, cut content in this order, and leave what remains complete:** (1) Claims Practice gallery, (2) Funicular (a walk up the cliff path instead), (3) glass floats and memos, (4) trench gun, (5) Hatchmen, (6) the Audit (keep parries, make Sedge a cutscene), (7) Marsh length. **Never cut:** planted aim, zones, kick, parry, the Case, the shop, the trawler siege, Wren's escort, Brack, the Undertow, Last Stand and the hub round, attract, dev mode, glyphs, the touch gate, voices, About, the exit interview. \"No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features\" holds at every cut.\n875\t\n876\t## 19. Finishing: what done means\n877\t\n878\t**In-game About/Credits and your final chat reply both carry:** Source Information with every field TASK.md lists (take the date, model, environment and so on from *your* TASK.md; Plan is the file name of this plan as you received it; Usage is literally \"added on import\"), and your answers to Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback. Keep this in one data module so screen and file can't drift, and fill it from what really happened: \"unknown\" for what you can't confirm. Suggested facts: genre and perspective from §1; tech: my-3dge at the commit in `engine-lock.json` (three.js r182, WebGPU, Rapier, TypeScript, Vite), AI Hub session client 1.4.0 or current; art: engine-native procedural, fog and dusk; animation: the engine's animator, clip library, new actions; audio: synthesized music and effects, Animalese-style gibberish, music at 10% by default; online: AI Hub shared-world session, 1 to 4 players, none outside a session.\n879\t\n880\t**The exit interview:** the file and exact shape TASK.md gives, every value filled in, parsed by a test. For `aiHub`: `name` is `GAME_TITLE`; `type` Game; `genre` Horror; `source` and `series` from TASK.md's source; `players` \"1–4\"; tags such as `3d`, `third-person`, `co-op`, `horror`, `boss fights`, `story`.\n881\t\n882\t**Clean up:** stop anything you started, by PID. `labs/game/README.md` says what the game is now. `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` is filled in.\n883\t\n884\t**Coverage: every line of TASK.md, where it's handled, how it's proved.**\n885\t\n886\t| TASK.md | Plan | Proved by |\n887\t|---|---|---|\n888\t| Source; original game; its world, characters, themes, tone turned into mechanics, pacing, UX | §1, §2, §3, §4 to §9 | Playing it; campaign bot |\n889\t| Genre, perspective | §1 | About screen |\n890\t| Title by RNG from 50; deliverable name | §1, §16.6 | Title screen; file exists |\n891\t| Research | Your choice; this plan is enough. Report what you did | About screen |\n892\t| Single HTML, CDN allowed | §16.6 (everything inline) | Page tests run on the deliverable from `file://` |\n893\t| Engine's full workspace, read-only; own systems, art, animation on top | §16 | `npm run check` |\n894\t| Art direction | §12 | `x gallery`, screenshots |\n895\t| Animation | §12 | `x anim`, screenshots |\n896\t| Audio: all code, gibberish voices, music 10% | §13, §11 | Test reads 0.1; Analyser level; `x qa audio`; no binary (`x check`) |\n897\t| Online; multiplayer in the hub and on its own | §10 | Four harness runs; solo Last Stand; hub-style open with no session |\n898\t| Dev folder; shared machine rules; server and process rules | §16.1, §17 | Practice |\n899\t| Performance out of scope, unlimited budget | §4, §7, §12: detail freely; don't optimise | |\n900\t| Testing: one command, failures and count only; whole-game playthrough; no audit agents | §17 | `verify.mjs` |\n901\t| Effort | Spend it on the kick, the siege and the writing | |\n902\t| This computer: browsers, stand-ins for pad, touch, sound, second player, iPhone, TV | §16.1, §16.7, §17 | Stubs and profiles in page tests; 1080p shots |\n903\t| Feature-complete demo, polished vertical slice, infrastructure for the rest | §4, §16.2 (data-driven) | Campaign bot; data tables |\n904\t| Dev mode from pause, tools, live sliders, reset | §15 | Page test |\n905\t| Attract: 10 s idle, loop, any input exits, may cheat | §14 | Page test |\n906\t| Narrative tone | §3 | Reading the script |\n907\t| UI and UX, 10-foot, pad first; native keyboard and mouse; hover focus; last-input prompts; Xbox option; no dense screens | §5, §11 | Page tests; 1080p shots |\n908\t| Touch-only: no controls, message and settings, attract runs | §11, §14 | Phone-profile test |\n909\t| Done: no TODOs, placeholders, stubs | §18 | `grep` in `verify.mjs` for TODO, FIXME, placeholder in `labs/game/` |\n910\t| Source Information in reply and About | §19 | Page test |\n911\t| Exit interview | §19 | Parse test |\n912\t| Testing, Engine, Prompt Feedback | §16.1 (`ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`), §19 | Page test |\n913\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"ae3e5e53-939c-4316-a5c2-ea6d455eaf82","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:20:53.146Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/PLAN.md","content":"| Guns | Damage ×, fire rate ×, reload time ×, recoil ×, head multiplier, leg multiplier, kick damage, kick radius, parry window |\n| Foes | HP ×, speed ×, damage ×, wind-up time ×, max attackers at once, max on field, sight range, burst chance |\n| Economy | Drop rate, shillings ×, shop prices ×, Risk Rating lock |\n| Partner, prompts | Wren HP, carry speed, follow distance, prompt window × |\n| World (view) | Fog amount, grade strength, music level |\n\n**Tools:** god mode, freeze AI, time scale and hit-stop off (engine dev actions `god`, `freeze`, `timeScale`); infinite ammo, one-hit kills, give money, give all weapons, give all salvage; jump to any beat from a list; start or skip an encounter; kill all; spawn any foe at the laser's point; free camera (`cam3=fly`); labels over foes (state, HP, zones); a stats line (`__engine.stats()`, hash, tick, entities); **Copy balance as JSON** (`navigator.clipboard`, no dialog); **Record a replay** (`input.record()`).\n\n## 16. Technology\n\n### 16.1 Setup (exact, [verified])\n\nFrom the empty dev folder:\n\n```sh\nsrc=$(mktemp -d) && git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge \"$src\" && node \"$src/tools/game/new-game.mjs\" . --name game\nnpm ci   # 6 s. npm test then passes in 10 s, and npm run check in 13 s, on this machine.\nexport CHROMIUM_PATH=$(ls -d \"$HOME\"/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-*/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell | head -1)\nnode x shot labs/game            # about 7 s\nnode x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim   # about 17 s\n```\n\n- **Don't run `scripts/setup.sh`.** It downloads Node and Chrome into your home folder. The machine's Node 24 satisfies the engine and `npm ci` is enough.\n- **Use the headless shell for `CHROMIUM_PATH`, not the full `chrome`.** The full binary dies under this run's long temp path with `Socket path too long` [verified]; set the variable in every shell you use for `x shot`, `x film` or `x replay --browser`. `@playwright/test` from the workspace uses it through `executablePath`, no browser download.\n- **Don't `git init` or commit.** The dev folder already sits inside the harness's repository. Skip the commit steps in AGENTS.md.\n- **You share this machine.** Keep every file you make inside your folder, not in `/tmp` or a parent; don't read the folders beside yours. Prefer `file://` and the engine's headless tools. A server only for the hub harness (§17), on a port the OS picks. Stop only what you started, by PID: never `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`.\n- **Keep `$src`, read-only.** Its `labs/playground/` is the best worked example of this exact genre on this engine, and new-game does **not** copy it (the guide mentions it anyway). Read `cast/player.ts`, `controls.ts`, `weapons/`, `cast/neighbours.ts`, `cast/partners.ts`, `cast/ways.ts`, `bodies/player.ts`, `levels/plan.ts`, `levels/site.ts`, `scenes/site.ts`, `ui/`. Copy and adapt what you need into `labs/game/`. Never import from it.\n- Read AGENTS.md (the game's) and `docs/GAME-GUIDE.md` once. Look things up in `docs/API.md`, the file comments, `node x describe`, `node x help`, `__engine.help()`. Write friction in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` as you go; TASK.md's Engine Feedback comes from it.\n- **The engine is read-only** (`npm run check` compares every file). Everything below is achievable on top of it. Files stay under 400 lines with a `@file` comment.\n\n### 16.2 Folder layout\n\nLint treats `labs/*/scenes/**` and `labs/*/cast/**` as sim-side, importing only `engine/sim-api.ts`. `x qa` reads `labs/game/{geometry,props,textures,sounds}`. Everything else in `labs/game/` is page code, importing `engine/index.ts`.\n\n```text\nlabs/game/\n  index.html  main.ts  title.ts     page entry (keep the starter's error handling)\n  data/          plain tables with no engine imports: items, weapons, foes, shop, waves, beats, dialogue, balance defaults\n  scenes/        sim: world.ts (game:world), square.ts (game:square), systems as files: guns, melee, qte, foes, director,\n                 story, drops, risk, caseGrid, partner, bosses/*, net, laststand, save\n  cast/          sim: hero, wren, each foe, each boss\n  levels/        defineLevel text (adapt the playground's Plan helper), site.ts (terrain, structures, zones)\n  props/ geometry/ textures/ sounds/     data, read by x qa\n  bodies/ looks/ materials.ts clips.ts   page registration (bodies, skies, looks, materials, clip sets)\n  ui/            hud, prompts, glyphs, menus, case, shop, claimFile, dialogue, settings, controls, about, gameover, results, dev, gate, card\n  audio/         page sound: events to sfx, music director, voice\n  net/           hub.ts, transport, memory transport, session.client.txt\n  attract/       attract.ts (bot and beats)\n  bot/           campaign bot, its helpers\n  tools/         bundle.mjs, verify.mjs\n  replays/\n```\n\n**Data-driven, so the rest of the game could be built with normal designer tools.** A new zone means: a level as text, an entry in the site, a beats table, an encounters table, dialogue lines. A new foe or weapon means a row of data and a body. No system needs editing for content. `node x new <kind>` scaffolds bodies, props, looks, levels, songs, sounds, actions.\n\n**Modes** are a setting, `game.mode` (`title`, `campaign`, `laststand`, `attract`, `gallery`), read in `setup`. Changing mode or loading a save: `inspector.set(...)`, then `inspector.seed(n)`, which restarts the scene and keeps changed settings [verified]. `frame.world` is a new object after a restart, so page code resets what it remembers (event `seq`, for one) when it changes.\n\n**Scenes.** `game:world` is everything. `game:square` is the same terrain and coordinates with only the Square's structures, for hub rounds to load fast; both share all systems.\n\n### 16.3 Engine map\n\n| Need | Use | Worked example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Hero | `createCharacter({ movement })`, `spawnActor`, `defineMovement` | §16.4; playground `cast/player.ts` |\n| Camera | `cam3=shoulder,<yaw°>,<pitch°>,<arm>`, `__engine.camera.set(code, { blend: true })`; own cinematic cameras with `node x new camera` | engine `gfx/cameras/shoulder.ts` |\n| Guns | Own system; `defineWeapon`, `weaponsFor`, `getWeapon`, `recoilStep`, `spreadOf`, `physicsOf(w).raycast`, `entityOfBody` | engine `sim/weapons.ts` |\n| Melee | `Attack`, `getMove`, `meleeTargets`, `requestHitStop`, `damage` | engine `sim/melee.ts` |\n| Foes | `spawnActor({ player: false })`, `actor.intents`, `reactTo`, `handOff`, `addRagdolls`, `standUp`, `playClip`, `actOn` | playground `cast/partners.ts`, `neighbours.ts` |\n| Hounds, Leeches, seal | `addAgent`, `CROWD_BODY`, rigs `quadruped`, `blob` | playground `cast/dog.ts`; `labs/box/cast/slime.ts` |\n| AI kit | `approachRing`, `followFlow`, `takeToken`, `sense`, `earshot`, `Noise`, `SpatialHash`, `defineTelegraph`, `inTelegraph` | `labs/box/cast/walker.ts`, `labs/box/scenes/fight-foes.ts` |\n| World | `defineTerrain`, `defineSite`, `addSiteBodies`, `addSiteLadders`, `createSiteNav`, `propObstacles`, `siteFloorBelow`, `siteClearSight` | playground `levels/site.ts`, `scenes/site.ts`, `cast/ways.ts` |\n| Doors, windows, breakables | `addLevelDoors`, `addDoor`, `strikeDoor`, `addLevelWindows`, `addBreakables`, `damageProp` | playground `scenes/site.ts` |\n| Use prompts | `addInteraction`, `defineUsable`, `interactor.prompt` | `node x new interactable` |\n| Moving platform | `driveMover`, `MOVER`, `moverPose` (phase `ai`) | engine `physics/bodies.ts` |\n| Targets (gallery) | `defineThing`, `spawnThing` | playground `weapons/range.ts` |\n| Triggers | `addSensor`, `updateTrigger` | engine `physics/bodies.ts` |\n| Page → sim | Dev actions: `actions: { name(w, args) }` in the scene, `inspector.actions.run(name, args)`. Custom intents: `input.virtual.axis('game:x', data)` | §10.3 |\n| Saves, prefs | `createStore`, `createEngine({ store })` | `labs/game/best.ts` |\n\n**Why a game-owned gun system.** The engine's `addWeapons` is for a range: its reload refills from nothing, it fires from the hip, and one set of intents drives every player. We need ammo from the Case, no hip fire, pellets, piercing, per-gun upgrades, and per-actor intents for co-op. Copy the logic of `stepOne` from `engine/sim/weapons.ts` into `scenes/guns.ts`, keeping the **component `weapons`** (`weaponsFor`) so the view still draws the gun in hand and the camera still reads `aim` and `kick`. **Emit the same `gunshot` event** `{ id, weapon, from, to, normal, body, target, hit }`, and you get tracer, muzzle flash, impact and bullet holes for free. Also set `animator.weapon` and `motion.holstered` as it does.\n\n### 16.4 Recipes that worked [verified]\n\n**Planted aim, with no fighting the controller.** On a movement profile, holding `aim` with a gun out sets the gait to `walk`. So make `walk` 0. Measured: 3.15 m in a second running, 0.135 m of slide while aiming.\n\n```ts\nconst apex = getMovement('movement:apex');\ndefineMovement('movement:quill', {\n  description: 'Runs like a man of 51. Plants his feet to aim.',\n  character: apex.character,\n  model: { gaits: { walk: 0, run: 3.4, sprint: 5.2, holstered: 1 } },\n});\nspawnActor(w, {\n  at, yaw, player: true, holstered: false,\n  character: createCharacter({ movement: 'movement:quill' }),\n  body: 'body:quill', anim: { build: 'build:adult', weapon: 'gun' },\n  components: { weapons: weaponsFor(['weapon:deductible'], 0) },\n});\n```\n\nPass `input.sprint=hold` so run is a hold. The live slider for `movement.gaits.walk` gives the aim-shuffle option. Add no `jump` to the action map, and he never jumps, slides or mantles.\n\n**Action map.** `defineActionMap('actionMap:quill', { look: true, aimWith: 'centre', lock: true, actions: {...}, view: ['case', 'map', 'shoulder'] })`. Name the aim action `aim` and fire `fire`: the view keys off those. Read view actions through `createEngine({ onView })`.\n\n**Foe.**\n\n```ts\ndefineComponent('health', { description: 'Hit points.', fields: HEALTH_FIELDS });\nspawnActor(w, {\n  at, player: false, character: createCharacter({ speed: 1.3 }),\n  body: 'body:parishioner0', anim: { build: 'build:adult', weapon: 'none' },\n  clips: { sets: ['clipset:quaternius'] },              // here, at spawn: see the traps\n  components: { health: { hp: 100, hitAt: -1, hitBy: -1 }, foe: { kind: 'parishioner', state: 'idle' } },\n});\n// each step: f.actor.intents = { move: [dx, dz] };  from its first step: playClip(w, f.id, 'quaternius/Zombie_Walk_Fwd_Loop');\n```\n\n**Hit zones.** `const y = shot.to[1] - foe.actor.y;` then the table in §6.1. Handle the event with `w.events.on('gunshot', ...)` or inside `game.guns` itself. Falling: `handOff(w, id, { push: [dx * 3, 1, dz * 3], dead: true })`. Flinching: `reactTo(w, id, (r) => r.hit(dirVector3, yaw, 1))`, as in the playground's partners.\n\n**Bodies and builds.** Copying a registry entry needs its `id` and `kind` removed: `const { id, kind, ...rest } = getBody('body:humanoid')`. A giant is `defineBuild('build:brack', { ...adultFields, size: 2.7 })` with `createCharacter({ speed, capsule: { radius: 0.9, height: 3.4 } })`, and it reads great. `defineBody`, `defineMaterial`, `defineSky` and `defineLook` are page-side, and the sim names them by id; `defineProp`, `defineLevel`, `defineTerrain`, `defineSite`, `defineWeapon`, `defineMovement` are sim-side.\n\n**Laser.** A page cannot add its own meshes through the public API. Draw the beam as a thin rotated CSS line in the overlay from the projected muzzle to the projected end, computing the end with `frame.queries.raycast` along the camera's centre. Add a 3D glow for the dot with a running emitter: `frame.emit('emitter:laserDot', at, 'laser')`. Project with `frame.camera` (position, yaw, pitch, fov). Note it in `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`.\n\n**Clips in the page.** Register them in a statically imported module:\n\n```ts\n// labs/game/clips.ts\nconst TEXT = import.meta.glob<string>('../../data/anim/sets/quaternius/*.json', { query: '?raw', import: 'default', eager: true });\nconst files = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(TEXT).map(([p, t]) => [p.split('/').pop()!, t]));\ndefineClipSet(clipSetFromFiles(files, 'data/anim/sets/quaternius'));\n```\n\nRegister `quaternius` and `mesh2motion`, and `cmu` if you use it. In Vitest, read the same files with `node:fs`.\n\n**Page boot order.**\n\n```ts\nimport './clips'; import './bodies'; import './looks'; /* every registration, static, first */\nconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\nfor (const key of [...search.keys()]) if (key.startsWith('aihub')) search.delete(key);   // see the traps\nsearch.set('touch', 'off');\nif (!search.has('cam3') && !search.has('cam')) search.set('cam3', 'shoulder,0,-4,2.8');\nif (!search.has('post.look')) search.set('post.look', 'look:skerry');\nif (!search.has('gfx.warmUp')) search.set('gfx.warmUp', 'asked');\nconst hub = window.AIHub;\nconst info = hub?.active ? await hub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true }) : null;\n// with info: wire hub handlers NOW, set game.role, game.mode=laststand, seed=info.seed, ?scene=game:square (§16.7)\nconst engine = await createEngine({ canvas, scenes: ['game:world', 'game:square'], search: `?${search}`, store, modal, onFrame, onView, actionMap: 'actionMap:quill' });\n```\n\n### 16.5 Navigation\n\nCopy the idea of the playground's `cast/ways.ts`: `createSiteNav(site, { blocks: propObstacles(w) })`, one flow field per goal, flooded lazily, remade when a door or prop blocks the way. `nav.direction(field, x, y, z)` gives a foe its `move`. Make it on the first step, not in `setup`, since no query sees props in `setup`.\n\n### 16.6 Packaging [verified]\n\nThere's no game-side `x html`: the engine's `tools/lib/oneFile.ts` is hard-wired to the playground. Copy its method in `labs/game/tools/bundle.mjs`, run from the dev folder:\n\n```js\nconst result = await build({\n  root, configFile: false, logLevel: 'warn', base: './',\n  resolve: { alias: [{ find: /^three$/, replacement: 'three/webgpu' }] },\n  build: {\n    write: false, modulePreload: false, cssCodeSplit: false, assetsInlineLimit: () => true,\n    chunkSizeWarningLimit: Infinity, target: 'esnext',\n    rollupOptions: { input: { game: join(root, 'labs/game/index.html') }, output: { inlineDynamicImports: true } },\n  },\n});\n// then: put each chunk and stylesheet inline, as oneFile.ts's inlineBuild does, using a replacer FUNCTION (the code holds $ signs):\n//   script text with '</script' written as '<\\/script'; fail the build on '<!--' inside a script.\n// then, right after <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />: <script>{session.client.txt, byte for byte}</script> and the hub:* tags.\n// write to the deliverable's path one folder up, and set <title> from GAME_TITLE.\n```\n\nThe starter came out at 6.7 MB and opened from `file://` with WebGPU, no errors, in 6 s on the software renderer. The hub checks that the pasted client is byte-identical to a release (SHA-256, banner to last line).\n\n### 16.7 Traps I hit, so you don't [all verified]\n\n1. **The hub's URL kills the engine.** The hub opens the page with `?aihub=1` (and `aihub-seed`). `createEngine` refuses any query key that isn't a declared setting (`CORE_BAD_SETTING`), so the engine never starts and the harness shows no traffic. **Strip `aihub*` before passing `search`.** Your own URL flags must be declared with `defineSettings`.\n2. **`await import()` is eager in the one-file build.** With `inlineDynamicImports`, the imported module runs before the importer's body. Registering something then dynamically importing the page works in dev and fails in the bundle (`CORE_NO_ENTRY`). Register in static imports; put them first.\n3. **The harness waits only 20 s for `ready()` from every copy,** and 4 WebGPU copies on the software renderer are slow. A hamlet-sized scene with 18 foes took 12.5 to 17 s at 4 players with these rules, and passed: `game:square` not the whole island; `gfx.warmUp=asked`; **on a software adapter in a session only**, `post.look=look:clean`, `quality=low`, `gfx.governor=false` (`adapter.info.isFallbackAdapter` or `architecture === 'swiftshader'`). Wire the `time-up` and `end` handlers before `createEngine`, so a slow copy still answers them. Spawn foes after start, not in `setup`.\n4. **`spawnActor`'s entity isn't live in `setup`.** `addClips` and `playClip` right after it throw `SIM_BAD_ARGUMENT`. Give `clips` at spawn, and play from the first step.\n5. **`input.lastDevice` says `virtual`** after anything touches the virtual device, including net intents and attract. Track the last device yourself (§11).\n6. **A bare `cam3=shoulder` faces +Z (south), ignoring the hero's yaw.** Name the yaw in the code, and call `camera.set` after any teleport.\n7. **The governor lowers quality on slow frames** (`GFX_GOVERNOR`). Fine for players. For screenshots: `gfx.governor=false&quality=high`.\n8. **The software renderer draws about one frame a second** with the full look at 1280×720 (800 ms GPU a frame), and the clock lags behind. Tests use `__engine.step(n)` and read state, at 480×270 with `post.look=look:clean&quality=low`. A WebGPU canvas may come out blank in a screenshot under some setups: check the state.\n9. **`puppet.body` isn't re-read by the view.** Replace the actor (§12).\n10. **Level text errors are good.** `LEVEL_BAD_ROOF` tells you a gable wants `pitch: 35`. Read them.\n11. **`session.client.txt`, not `.js`:** as code it would fail the `@file` and line-count lint.\n12. **Spare CPU, shared machine.** One or two browsers at a time. `earlyoom` may end the biggest browser: \"Target closed\" means memory, so run fewer.\n\n## 17. Testing\n\n**One command, `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs [sim|page|hub|all]`, prints only failures and a one-line count** (for example `verify: 214 checks, 0 failed`). Rerun only the part you changed. Screenshots only for what a script can't check. **No subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.**\n\n**Sim (Vitest, Node, no browser):**\n- The four kinds the guide asks for: a golden replay, capture-and-restore continuing exactly, the bot winning across seeds, rule tests. Record goldens on purpose: `node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim --update`.\n- Rules: damage table by zone; kick radius, i-frames, knockdowns; parry window; Case fit, rotate, autosort, combine (property-style with many seeds); shop math; adaptive drops favour what's lacking; save and load round-trip; every beat reachable; Wren carried to the chute loses; plank removal stops boarding.\n- **The scripted playthrough of the whole game: `bot/campaign.ts` plays from Cold Open to the results screen through intents and dev-action menu picks**, including shop visits and every boss, on default difficulty, on 3 seeds (10 with `--full`). It's sim-only, about 3 to 5 ms a step, so a 10-minute bot run is under 3 minutes. If the bot can't win, find out whether it's the bot or the balance.\n- Co-op: a host sim and 3 client sims joined by the memory transport at 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss: foes converge within 1.5 m; a client's shot kills; a client's revive works; host finish reaches all.\n- Balance sanity: shots to kill per weapon, total shillings on a playthrough within 20,000 to 30,000.\n\n**Page, on the built deliverable from `file://`** (Playwright with `executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH` and args `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`; `window.__game` exposes `screen()` and `state()`; the UI is read through `[data-ui]` DOM queries):\n- Boots with no errors or advice. Title shows `GAME_TITLE`. Enter and Space on the title behave (the hub opens the game alone and presses them).\n- Attract starts after 10 s idle and exits on key, on click, on a stubbed pad button.\n- Pause, then Dev Mode: a slider changes a live value; reset restores defaults. Settings persist through a reload.\n- **Music volume is 0.1 by default**, and the Web Audio graph makes sound (`AnalyserNode` level, or an `OfflineAudioContext` render of a song and a voice line).\n- Glyphs: a `navigator.getGamepads` stub in standard mapping switches prompts to PlayStation; the Xbox setting gives A B X Y; a key press switches to keycaps.\n- Pad and mouse each work the title, the Case (lift, rotate, place) and the shop. Hover moves focus.\n- A Chromium phone profile (`devices['Pixel 7']`) shows the gate with the Settings button, with attract running, and no touch controls. WebKit's iPhone profile shows the gate with no WebGPU and no error text.\n- Font sizes at 1920×1080 meet §11's minimums; nothing overflows.\n- About/Credits holds every field from TASK.md's Source Information and all the feedback answers. The exit interview parses, and has every key.\n\n**Hub:** serve a folder holding `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` and the deliverable, on a port the OS picks, from your test process (Node `listen(0, '127.0.0.1')`, or `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`). First confirm the page is your game by its `<title>`. Stop only what you started, by PID. Assert `window.__hubCheck.pass` once `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` for:\n\n```text\n?game=<name>&players=2&auto=1&limit=40&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\n?game=<name>&players=4&auto=1&limit=40&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\n?game=<name>&players=4&auto=1&limit=40&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave\n?game=<name>&players=2&auto=1&limit=40&scenario=server\n```\n\nA minimal version of this passed all four here [verified], with the one-file build, in 17 to 34 s each. Also test your own card (\"Enter answers Ready\" is checked once you declare `card: true`).\n\n**Visual checks:** a few `--png` shots at 1920×1080 (the look, the Case, a boss, the HUD from far away), `node x gallery` for bodies and props, `node x qa geo tex audio`, `npm run check`.\n\n**Keep a tally as you go** in `labs/game/README.md`: issues testing caught, how many were critical, the most and least helpful tests. TASK.md's Testing Feedback asks for exactly that, and it's hard to reconstruct at the end.\n\n## 18. Build order\n\nEach milestone ends with a complete game you could ship, and `verify` green.\n\n| # | Build | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| M0 | Pick the title. Scaffold. `bundle.mjs`, `verify.mjs`, one-file smoke test, harness pass with an empty round. | The pipeline runs end to end before there's a game. |\n| M1 | **Core loop in the Square:** hero, camera, laser, `game.guns`, zones, reactions, kick, parry, foes with tokens, HUD, glyphs, gibberish voice, the look. | It's fun with 10 foes and one gun. If it isn't, stay here. Spend real time on the kick. |\n| M2 | **Last Stand and netcode:** waves, score, revive, transport, roles, card, finish. Solo menu entry. | All four harness runs pass with real play, and it's a game already. |\n| M3 | **Front end:** title, pause, Settings, Controls, About, Dev Mode with sliders, attract (first loop), touch gate. | Every UI test in §17 passes. |\n| M4 | **Economy:** Case, items, drops, shop, service, saves, game over, results. | Bot buys and sells; a save round-trips. |\n| M5 | **World and first act:** site, Slip, Office, Lane, full trawler siege with the Gutter, foghorn, Shingle, Claims Practice. | 20 great minutes. Bot plays through. |\n| M6 | **Marsh and Cannery:** Hounds, Netwives, Whips, Deacons, Hatchmen, Wren, Hoist, Brack. | Escort is tense, not annoying. |\n| M7 | **The finish:** Funicular, Abbey, Vault, Sedge, Causeway, Goole, Undertow, ending. | Bot plays Cold Open to results. |\n| M8 | **Polish:** all music, line-by-line script, animations in §12, effects, zone grades, full attract loop, data tidy. | Nothing on screen is a placeholder. |\n| M9 | **Close:** §19. | Everything in §19 ticked. |\n\n**If you run short, cut content in this order, and leave what remains complete:** (1) Claims Practice gallery, (2) Funicular (a walk up the cliff path instead), (3) glass floats and memos, (4) trench gun, (5) Hatchmen, (6) the Audit (keep parries, make Sedge a cutscene), (7) Marsh length. **Never cut:** planted aim, zones, kick, parry, the Case, the shop, the trawler siege, Wren's escort, Brack, the Undertow, Last Stand and the hub round, attract, dev mode, glyphs, the touch gate, voices, About, the exit interview. \"No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features\" holds at every cut.\n\n## 19. Finishing: what done means\n\n**In-game About/Credits and your final chat reply both carry:** Source Information with every field TASK.md lists (take the date, model, environment and so on from *your* TASK.md; Plan is the file name of this plan as you received it; Usage is literally \"added on import\"), and your answers to Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback. Keep this in one data module so screen and file can't drift, and fill it from what really happened: \"unknown\" for what you can't confirm. Suggested facts: genre and perspective from §1; tech: my-3dge at the commit in `engine-lock.json` (three.js r182, WebGPU, Rapier, TypeScript, Vite), AI Hub session client 1.4.0 or current; art: engine-native procedural, fog and dusk; animation: the engine's animator, clip library, new actions; audio: synthesized music and effects, Animalese-style gibberish, music at 10% by default; online: AI Hub shared-world session, 1 to 4 players, none outside a session.\n\n**The exit interview:** the file and exact shape TASK.md gives, every value filled in, parsed by a test. For `aiHub`: `name` is `GAME_TITLE`; `type` Game; `genre` Horror; `source` and `series` from TASK.md's source; `players` \"1–4\"; tags such as `3d`, `third-person`, `co-op`, `horror`, `boss fights`, `story`.\n\n**Clean up:** stop anything you started, by PID. `labs/game/README.md` says what the game is now. `ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md` is filled in.\n\n**Coverage: every line of TASK.md, where it's handled, how it's proved.**\n\n| TASK.md | Plan | Proved by |\n|---|---|---|\n| Source; original game; its world, characters, themes, tone turned into mechanics, pacing, UX | §1, §2, §3, §4 to §9 | Playing it; campaign bot |\n| Genre, perspective | §1 | About screen |\n| Title by RNG from 50; deliverable name | §1, §16.6 | Title screen; file exists |\n| Research | Your choice; this plan is enough. Report what you did | About screen |\n| Single HTML, CDN allowed | §16.6 (everything inline) | Page tests run on the deliverable from `file://` |\n| Engine's full workspace, read-only; own systems, art, animation on top | §16 | `npm run check` |\n| Art direction | §12 | `x gallery`, screenshots |\n| Animation | §12 | `x anim`, screenshots |\n| Audio: all code, gibberish voices, music 10% | §13, §11 | Test reads 0.1; Analyser level; `x qa audio`; no binary (`x check`) |\n| Online; multiplayer in the hub and on its own | §10 | Four harness runs; solo Last Stand; hub-style open with no session |\n| Dev folder; shared machine rules; server and process rules | §16.1, §17 | Practice |\n| Performance out of scope, unlimited budget | §4, §7, §12: detail freely; don't optimise | |\n| Testing: one command, failures and count only; whole-game playthrough; no audit agents | §17 | `verify.mjs` |\n| Effort | Spend it on the kick, the siege and the writing | |\n| This computer: browsers, stand-ins for pad, touch, sound, second player, iPhone, TV | §16.1, §16.7, §17 | Stubs and profiles in page tests; 1080p shots |\n| Feature-complete demo, polished vertical slice, infrastructure for the rest | §4, §16.2 (data-driven) | Campaign bot; data tables |\n| Dev mode from pause, tools, live sliders, reset | §15 | Page test |\n| Attract: 10 s idle, loop, any input exits, may cheat | §14 | Page test |\n| Narrative tone | §3 | Reading the script |\n| UI and UX, 10-foot, pad first; native keyboard and mouse; hover focus; last-input prompts; Xbox option; no dense screens | §5, §11 | Page tests; 1080p shots |\n| Touch-only: no controls, message and settings, attract runs | §11, §14 | Phone-profile test |\n| Done: no TODOs, placeholders, stubs | §18 | `grep` in `verify.mjs` for TODO, FIXME, placeholder in `labs/game/` |\n| Source Information in reply and About | §19 | Page test |\n| Exit interview | §19 | Parse test |\n| Testing, Engine, Prompt Feedback | §16.1 (`ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md`), §19 | Page test |\n","numLines":285,"startLine":629,"totalLines":913}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018tZWxwhG5bbVYzYspZE3TY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
