{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDfRDVGNNcNHGrgP3nS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The read-through flagged several fixes to make: the rifle scope conflicts with D-pad up, a section reference is wrong, the movement.* slider override needs a note, sprint-hold belongs in the boot snippet, and the Esc/pointer-lock trap plus a fullscreen option are missing. Next I'll confirm the hub's seed passes the engine's seed check.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13139,"cache_read_input_tokens":645813,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13139},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"29aaf4bf-bea6-4990-8057-49c34706f3f6","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:21:16.369Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDfQs9tPLFZ5kxXfTAH","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":1,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDfRDVGNNcNHGrgP3nS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018UbiWcNAybzkFFjTytUdEf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"R=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/.research; cd $R/proto2; grep -n \"export function checkSeed\" -A8 engine/sim/scene.ts | cut -c1-170; grep -n \"seed\" engine/app/routes.ts | sed -n 1,10p | cut -c1-170; cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nrep(\"| Scope (hold aim + D-pad up to zoom), pierces 2 |\",\"| Scoped: aiming zooms in (`zoom`), pierces 2 |\")\nrep(\"register only the sets you use (§16.2).\",\"register only the sets you use (§16.4).\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Tools:** god mode, freeze AI,\"\"\",\"\"\"The engine's `movement.*` settings override a profile only while off their own default, which is Apex's number. So those rows show the profile's value until moved, and their reset sets the setting back to its registered default, which removes the override.\n\n**Tools:** god mode, freeze AI,\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"search.set('touch', 'off');\n\"\"\",\"\"\"search.set('touch', 'off');\nsearch.set('input.sprint', 'hold');\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Pass `input.sprint=hold` so run is a hold. The live slider\"\"\",\"\"\"`input.sprint=hold` (in the boot code below) makes run a hold. The live slider\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"vibration (via `vibrationActuator` where present); quality\"\"\",\"\"\"vibration (via `vibrationActuator` where present); fullscreen (`requestFullscreen`, which the hub's client handles in a session); quality\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"12. **Spare CPU, shared machine.**\"\"\",\"\"\"12. **Esc under pointer lock.** The browser may spend the first Esc on releasing the lock, with no key event for you. Treat the lock lost during play as a pause, as the playground's `ui/frontEnd.ts` does (read from its comments, not run here).\n13. **Spare CPU, shared machine.**\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"### 16.7 Traps I hit, so you don't [all verified]\"\"\",\"\"\"### 16.7 Traps I hit, so you don't [verified unless noted]\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"seed=info.seed\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-120","description":"Check seed limits and apply review fixes to the plan","timeout":60000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13139,"cache_read_input_tokens":645813,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13139},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"a424006e-b597-4995-8269-71a6df2f42b2","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:21:24.287Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDfQs9tPLFZ5kxXfTAH","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018UbiWcNAybzkFFjTytUdEf":{"command":"R=/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work/.research; cd $R/proto2; grep -n \"export function checkSeed\" -A8 engine/sim/scene.ts | cut -c1-170; grep -n \"seed\" engine/app/routes.ts | sed -n 1,10p | cut -c1-170; cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-212002__x601dca/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'\ns=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nrep(\"| Scope (hold aim + D-pad up to zoom), pierces 2 |\",\"| Scoped: aiming zooms in (`zoom`), pierces 2 |\")\nrep(\"register only the sets you use (§16.2).\",\"register only the sets you use (§16.4).\")\nrep(\"\"\"**Tools:** god mode, freeze AI,\"\"\",\"\"\"The engine's `movement.*` settings override a profile only while off their own default, which is Apex's number. So those rows show the profile's value until moved, and their reset sets the setting back to its registered default, which removes the override.\n\n**Tools:** god mode, freeze AI,\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"search.set('touch', 'off');\n\"\"\",\"\"\"search.set('touch', 'off');\nsearch.set('input.sprint', 'hold');\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Pass `input.sprint=hold` so run is a hold. The live slider\"\"\",\"\"\"`input.sprint=hold` (in the boot code below) makes run a hold. The live slider\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"vibration (via `vibrationActuator` where present); quality\"\"\",\"\"\"vibration (via `vibrationActuator` where present); fullscreen (`requestFullscreen`, which the hub's client handles in a session); quality\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"12. **Spare CPU, shared machine.**\"\"\",\"\"\"12. **Esc under pointer lock.** The browser may spend the first Esc on releasing the lock, with no key event for you. Treat the lock lost during play as a pause, as the playground's `ui/frontEnd.ts` does (read from its comments, not run here).\n13. **Spare CPU, shared machine.**\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"### 16.7 Traps I hit, so you don't [all verified]\"\"\",\"\"\"### 16.7 Traps I hit, so you don't [verified unless noted]\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"seed=info.seed\" PLAN.md | cut -c1-120","description":"Check seed limits and apply review fixes to the plan","timeout":60000}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018UbiWcNAybzkFFjTytUdEf","type":"tool_result","content":"55:export function checkSeed(seed: unknown, where: string): number {\n56-  if (seed === undefined) return 1;\n57-  if (Number.isInteger(seed) && (seed as number) >= 0) return (seed as number) + 0; // -0 + 0 is 0\n58-  throw codeError('SIM_BAD_SEED', { where, value: show(seed) });\n59-}\n60-\n61-/** A dev action of a scene: runs between steps inside `w.run`, with plain-data `args`; recorded in replays. */\n62-export type SceneAction<W> = (w: W, args: unknown) => void;\n63-\n6: * - `?seed=<n>`: the seed, a whole number from 0 (1 when absent).\n27: * parseRoutes('?scene=room&seed=4&cam=topdown', { scenes: ['box:room'], registry }).scene; // 'box:room'\n49:export const ROUTE_KEYS = ['scene', 'seed', 'cam', 'cam3', 'replay'] as const;\n55:  seed: number;\n107:  const seedText = one('seed');\n108:  if (seedText !== null && !/^(0|[1-9]\\d*)$/.test(seedText)) {\n109:    bad('seed', seedText, 'is not a whole number from 0', 'write a seed as digits: ?seed=3');\n111:  const seed = seedText === null ? 1 : Number(seedText);\n112:  if (!Number.isSafeInteger(seed)) bad('seed', seedText ?? '', 'is too large', 'use a seed below 2^53');\n133:  return { scene, seed, ...(code ? { cam: code } : {}), ...(replay ? { replay } : {}), settings, ...(gallery ? { gallery } : {}) }; // prettier-ignore\n778:// with info: wire hub handlers NOW, set game.role, game.mode=laststand, seed=info.seed, ?scene=game:square (§16.7)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed5deb30-576e-4aa7-93e0-da5eaa4ce63e","uuid":"7f0764cd-fc6d-4bb9-a83d-87c47c154960","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:21:24.323Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"55:export function checkSeed(seed: unknown, where: string): number {\n56-  if (seed === undefined) return 1;\n57-  if (Number.isInteger(seed) && (seed as number) >= 0) return (seed as number) + 0; // -0 + 0 is 0\n58-  throw codeError('SIM_BAD